ithub.com/users/dankli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dankli/OspreyLoyalty/commits/27ce46540aee75ebec43e6f03eff66f4469f3407/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T12:38:40Z","email":"daniel.klingstedt@gmail.com","name":"Daniel Klingstedt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T12:38:40Z","email":"daniel.klingstedt@gmail.com","name":"Daniel Klingstedt"},"message":"ci(security): make Trivy scan offline and non-gating\n\nThe first devsecops run failed: Trivy''s Java analyzer hit Maven Central to\nresolve dependency versions and got a 429, aborting the scan (FATAL, so\n--exit-code 0 didn''t help) and leaving no SARIF for the upload step. Add\n--offline-scan so detection runs off the local vuln DB without external\ncalls, and make the step continue-on-error with a hashFiles-guarded upload\nso a scanner hiccup reports but never gates the build (visibility-first).","tree":{"sha":"b7ad4df3388bd4c2890e3f11748e63b4df8f000e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dankli/OspreyLoyalty/git/trees/b7ad4df3388bd4c2890e3f11748e63b4df8f000e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dankli/OspreyLoyalty/git/commits/27ce46540aee75ebec43e6f03eff66f4469f3407","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dankli","id":138536,"login":"dankli","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODUzNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dankli/received_events