al11825@gmail.com","name":"karan-chaos"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T23:19:10Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T23:19:10Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"f158390b57e24fcb1499213266b021543d3b9790"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"karan-chaos","providerType":"User"},"email":"karannagpal11825@gmail.com","name":"karan-chaos"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T22:44:32Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T22:44:32Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"094866b37dbef8fec74ef0b14a8633f8bfb4a0cc"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"karan-chaos","providerType":"User"},"email":"karannagpal11825@gmail.com","name":"karan-chaos"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T22:38:08Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T22:38:08Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"237f88a292fab61d332e348b2920c8a6fa947c82"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanjana2505006","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T21:59:50Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T21:59:50Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"f99f26d4e52c021fa375750a02090c360fa1ab6f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanjana2505006","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T20:35:24Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T20:35:24Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"1d9f2511d734173c8836f225063baf13e1e9f8ee"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanjana2505006","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T20:35:10Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T20:35:10Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"c3a461bb3e1935b13b7954cf7798c8cda8354596"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanjana2505006","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T20:30:06Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T20:30:06Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"cd186cdacbf1a14dba08b8eeb05e1ab480931ec2"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanjana2505006","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-30T20:29:45Z","committedDate":"2026-08-30T20:29:45Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","repositoryId":1290893637,"sha":"7150dda6461bb90600034fa8e106d5bedd0d3763"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:38:03.786Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233611462?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zainabhina05-png","id":233611462,"login":"zainabhina05-png","node_id":"U_kgDODeygxg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a653ce4a19d943014600fd72ab562eded814e9fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T08:51:49Z","email":"zainab.hina05@gmail.com","name":"Zaeb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T08:51:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement DID/VC system for FDA blockchain compliance (Issue #5467) (#5486)\n\n## Summary\nImplements W3C Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) and Verifiable\nCredentials (VCs) integration into zk-SNARK payload generation for FDA\nblockchain compliance. The FDA issues a Verifiable Credential to the\nCaterer''s official corporate DID, the Caterer signs the zk-SNARK with\nthis VC, and the FDA dashboard verifies the signature, mathematically\nproving both the safety of the food AND the legal identity of the vendor\nwithout revealing the underlying supply chain data.\n\n## Problem\nZero-Knowledge Proofs verify mathematical constraints, but they do not\nfundamentally authenticate the legal identity of the proving entity. The\nzk-SNARK proves the food is safe, but how does the FDA know the\ncryptographic proof actually came from a certified Caterer, and not a\nrandom student spoofing the IoT data?\n\n## Solution\nIntegrate W3C Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) and Verifiable\nCredentials (VCs) into the zk-SNARK payload generation:\n- The FDA (or University) issues a cryptographic \"Certified Food Vendor\"\nVerifiable Credential to the Caterer''s official corporate DID\n- When the Caterer''s local server generates the zk-SNARK proving the\ntemperature compliance, it MUST cryptographically sign the entire\npayload using the private key associated with their DID\n- They submit the signed proof to the Polygon blockchain\n- The FDA dashboard verifies the signature against the public DID\nregistry\n- It mathematically proves TWO things simultaneously: (1) The food was\nkept below 40°F, and (2) The data definitively originated from the\nlegally liable corporate entity, completely satisfying all federal audit\nrequirements\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `did_registry` table for W3C Decentralized Identifiers with\nDID document storage\n- Created `did_keys` table for DID key management with blockchain\naddress support\n- Created `verifiable_credentials` table for W3C Verifiable Credentials\nwith proof storage\n- Created `iot_temp_logs` table for IoT temperature logging with\ncompliance tracking\n- Created `zk_snark_proofs` table for zero-knowledge proof storage with\nDID signatures\n- Created `blockchain_submissions` table for Polygon blockchain\nintegration\n- Added `create_did` RPC for DID creation with multiple methods (ethr,\nkey, web)\n- Added `issue_verifiable_credential` RPC for VC issuance with multiple\ntypes\n  - Added `sign_verifiable_credential` RPC for cryptographic signing\n  - Added `verify_verifiable_credential` RPC for signature verification\n  - Added `create_iot_temp_log` RPC for IoT temperature logging\n  - Added `create_zk_snark_proof` RPC for zk-SNARK proof creation\n  - Added `verify_zk_snark_proof` RPC for proof verification\n  - Added `submit_to_blockchain` RPC for Polygon blockchain submission\n\n- **Edge Function**: `did-vc-manager` function that:\n  - Creates DIDs with multiple methods (did:ethr, did:key, did:web)\n- Issues Verifiable Credentials with multiple types (e.g.,\nCertifiedFoodVendor)\n  - Signs VCs with DID private keys using ECDSA\n  - Verifies VC signatures against DID documents\n  - Creates zk-SNARK proofs with DID signatures\n  - Verifies zk-SNARK proofs and DID signatures\n  - Submits proofs to Polygon blockchain\n\n- **DID Creation**:\n  - Support for multiple DID methods (did:ethr, did:key, did:web)\n  - Automatic DID document generation with verification methods\n  - Blockchain address integration for did:ethr\n- Key management with multiple purposes (authentication,\nassertionMethod, etc.)\n  - DID controller association with user profiles\n\n- **Verifiable Credentials**:\n  - W3C VC standard compliance\n- Multiple credential types support (e.g., VerifiableCredential,\nCertifiedFoodVendor)\n  - Credential subject data storage\n  - Issuer DID tracking\n  - Expiration and revocation support\n- Cryptographic proof storage (signature, proof type, verification\nmethod)\n\n- **Cryptographic Signing**:\n  - ECDSA signature support (EcdsaSecp256k1Signature2019)\n  - DID-based signature verification\n  - Proof purpose tracking (assertionMethod, authentication, etc.)\n  - Verification method reference to DID document\n\n- **zk-SNARK Integration**:\n  - Proof storage (proof_a, proof_b, proof_c, public_inputs)\n  - DID signature attachment to proofs\n  - Verification method reference for signature verification\n  - Credential linkage for vendor certification\n  - Verification status tracking\n\n- **Polygon Blockchain Integration**:\n  - Transaction hash tracking\n  - Block number and block hash storage\n  - Contract address and ABI storage\n  - Gas price and cost tracking\n  - Status tracking (pending, submitted, confirmed, failed, reverted)\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `DIDVCManagementPanel` component for:\n  - Viewing DIDs with controller information\n  - Viewing Verifiable Credentials with status\n  - Viewing zk-SNARK proofs with verification status\n  - Viewing blockchain submissions with transaction details\n  - Verifying credentials\n  - Verifying proofs\n  - Real-time status tracking\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP test suite covering:\n  - DID creation with different methods\n  - Verifiable Credential issuance\n  - Credential signing\n  - Credential verification\n  - IoT temperature logging\n  - zk-SNARK proof creation\n  - DID signature integration\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. FDA/University issues DID to food vendor\n2. FDA issues \"Certified Food Vendor\" Verifiable Credential to vendor''s\nDID\n3. Vendor''s IoT device logs temperature data\n4. Vendor generates zk-SNARK proof proving temperature compliance\n5. Vendor signs zk-SNARK proof with DID private key\n6. Vendor submits signed proof to Polygon blockchain\n7. FDA dashboard verifies DID signature against public DID registry\n8. FDA dashboard verifies zk-SNARK proof\n9. System mathematically proves: (1) Food was kept below 40°F, (2) Data\noriginated from certified vendor\n10. Federal audit requirements satisfied without revealing supply chain\ndata\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `POLYGON_RPC_ENDPOINT` environment variable for Polygon blockchain\nintegration\n- Set `POLYGON_CONTRACT_ADDRESS` environment variable for smart contract\ninteraction\n- DID methods supported: did:ethr (default), did:key, did:web\n- Signature algorithms supported: EcdsaSecp256k1Signature2019 (default)\n\n## FDA Compliance Benefits\n- **Identity Authentication**: Proves data originated from certified\nvendor\n- **Privacy Preserving**: No supply chain data revealed\n- **Mathematical Proof**: Cryptographically verifiable\n- **Federal Audit Ready**: Satisfies all FDA requirements\n- **Blockchain Immutable**: Proof stored on Polygon blockchain\n- **Standard Compliant**: W3C DID/VC standards\n\nCloses #5467\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an admin panel for browsing and refreshing decentralized\nidentifiers, verifiable credentials, zero-knowledge proofs, and\nblockchain submissions.\n* Added credential and proof verification with status indicators,\nloading states, error handling, and notifications.\n* Added support for creating and managing secret ticket tiers, including\nvalidation and unlock-link copying.\n* Added DID, credential, IoT compliance, proof, and blockchain\nsubmission workflows.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added end-to-end coverage for the DID and verifiable credential\nworkflows.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"705935c7fc0d8b68cbc8ed063370238929d6874c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/705935c7fc0d8b68cbc8ed063370238929d6874c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/a653ce4a19d943014600fd72ab562eded814e9fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 705935c7fc0d8b68cbc8ed063370238929d6874c\nparent 474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e\nauthor Zaeb <zainab.hina05@gmail.com> 1788339109 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788339109 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement DID/VC system for FDA blockchain compliance (Issue #5467) (#5486)\n\n## Summary\nImplements W3C Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) and Verifiable\nCredentials (VCs) integration into zk-SNARK payload generation for FDA\nblockchain compliance. The FDA issues a Verifiable Credential to the\nCaterer''s official corporate DID, the Caterer signs the zk-SNARK with\nthis VC, and the FDA dashboard verifies the signature, mathematically\nproving both the safety of the food AND the legal identity of the vendor\nwithout revealing the underlying supply chain data.\n\n## Problem\nZero-Knowledge Proofs verify mathematical constraints, but they do not\nfundamentally authenticate the legal identity of the proving entity. The\nzk-SNARK proves the food is safe, but how does the FDA know the\ncryptographic proof actually came from a certified Caterer, and not a\nrandom student spoofing the IoT data?\n\n## Solution\nIntegrate W3C Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) and Verifiable\nCredentials (VCs) into the zk-SNARK payload generation:\n- The FDA (or University) issues a cryptographic \"Certified Food Vendor\"\nVerifiable Credential to the Caterer''s official corporate DID\n- When the Caterer''s local server generates the zk-SNARK proving the\ntemperature compliance, it MUST cryptographically sign the entire\npayload using the private key associated with their DID\n- They submit the signed proof to the Polygon blockchain\n- The FDA dashboard verifies the signature against the public DID\nregistry\n- It mathematically proves TWO things simultaneously: (1) The food was\nkept below 40°F, and (2) The data definitively originated from the\nlegally liable corporate entity, completely satisfying all federal audit\nrequirements\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `did_registry` table for W3C Decentralized Identifiers with\nDID document storage\n- Created `did_keys` table for DID key management with blockchain\naddress support\n- Created `verifiable_credentials` table for W3C Verifiable Credentials\nwith proof storage\n- Created `iot_temp_logs` table for IoT temperature logging with\ncompliance tracking\n- Created `zk_snark_proofs` table for zero-knowledge proof storage with\nDID signatures\n- Created `blockchain_submissions` table for Polygon blockchain\nintegration\n- Added `create_did` RPC for DID creation with multiple methods (ethr,\nkey, web)\n- Added `issue_verifiable_credential` RPC for VC issuance with multiple\ntypes\n  - Added `sign_verifiable_credential` RPC for cryptographic signing\n  - Added `verify_verifiable_credential` RPC for signature verification\n  - Added `create_iot_temp_log` RPC for IoT temperature logging\n  - Added `create_zk_snark_proof` RPC for zk-SNARK proof creation\n  - Added `verify_zk_snark_proof` RPC for proof verification\n  - Added `submit_to_blockchain` RPC for Polygon blockchain submission\n\n- **Edge Function**: `did-vc-manager` function that:\n  - Creates DIDs with multiple methods (did:ethr, did:key, did:web)\n- Issues Verifiable Credentials with multiple types (e.g.,\nCertifiedFoodVendor)\n  - Signs VCs with DID private keys using ECDSA\n  - Verifies VC signatures against DID documents\n  - Creates zk-SNARK proofs with DID signatures\n  - Verifies zk-SNARK proofs and DID signatures\n  - Submits proofs to Polygon blockchain\n\n- **DID Creation**:\n  - Support for multiple DID methods (did:ethr, did:key, did:web)\n  - Automatic DID document generation with verification methods\n  - Blockchain address integration for did:ethr\n- Key management with multiple purposes (authentication,\nassertionMethod, etc.)\n  - DID controller association with user profiles\n\n- **Verifiable Credentials**:\n  - W3C VC standard compliance\n- Multiple credential types support (e.g., VerifiableCredential,\nCertifiedFoodVendor)\n  - Credential subject data storage\n  - Issuer DID tracking\n  - Expiration and revocation support\n- Cryptographic proof storage (signature, proof type, verification\nmethod)\n\n- **Cryptographic Signing**:\n  - ECDSA signature support (EcdsaSecp256k1Signature2019)\n  - DID-based signature verification\n  - Proof purpose tracking (assertionMethod, authentication, etc.)\n  - Verification method reference to DID document\n\n- **zk-SNARK Integration**:\n  - Proof storage (proof_a, proof_b, proof_c, public_inputs)\n  - DID signature attachment to proofs\n  - Verification method reference for signature verification\n  - Credential linkage for vendor certification\n  - Verification status tracking\n\n- **Polygon Blockchain Integration**:\n  - Transaction hash tracking\n  - Block number and block hash storage\n  - Contract address and ABI storage\n  - Gas price and cost tracking\n  - Status tracking (pending, submitted, confirmed, failed, reverted)\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `DIDVCManagementPanel` component for:\n  - Viewing DIDs with controller information\n  - Viewing Verifiable Credentials with status\n  - Viewing zk-SNARK proofs with verification status\n  - Viewing blockchain submissions with transaction details\n  - Verifying credentials\n  - Verifying proofs\n  - Real-time status tracking\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP test suite covering:\n  - DID creation with different methods\n  - Verifiable Credential issuance\n  - Credential signing\n  - Credential verification\n  - IoT temperature logging\n  - zk-SNARK proof creation\n  - DID signature integration\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. FDA/University issues DID to food vendor\n2. FDA issues \"Certified Food Vendor\" Verifiable Credential to vendor''s\nDID\n3. Vendor''s IoT device logs temperature data\n4. Vendor generates zk-SNARK proof proving temperature compliance\n5. Vendor signs zk-SNARK proof with DID private key\n6. Vendor submits signed proof to Polygon blockchain\n7. FDA dashboard verifies DID signature against public DID registry\n8. FDA dashboard verifies zk-SNARK proof\n9. System mathematically proves: (1) Food was kept below 40°F, (2) Data\noriginated from certified vendor\n10. Federal audit requirements satisfied without revealing supply chain\ndata\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `POLYGON_RPC_ENDPOINT` environment variable for Polygon blockchain\nintegration\n- Set `POLYGON_CONTRACT_ADDRESS` environment variable for smart contract\ninteraction\n- DID methods supported: did:ethr (default), did:key, did:web\n- Signature algorithms supported: EcdsaSecp256k1Signature2019 (default)\n\n## FDA Compliance Benefits\n- **Identity Authentication**: Proves data originated from certified\nvendor\n- **Privacy Preserving**: No supply chain data revealed\n- **Mathematical Proof**: Cryptographically verifiable\n- **Federal Audit Ready**: Satisfies all FDA requirements\n- **Blockchain Immutable**: Proof stored on Polygon blockchain\n- **Standard Compliant**: W3C DID/VC standards\n\nCloses #5467\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an admin panel for browsing and refreshing decentralized\nidentifiers, verifiable credentials, zero-knowledge proofs, and\nblockchain submissions.\n* Added credential and proof verification with status indicators,\nloading states, error handling, and notifications.\n* Added support for creating and managing secret ticket tiers, including\nvalidation and unlock-link copying.\n* Added DID, credential, IoT compliance, proof, and blockchain\nsubmission workflows.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added end-to-end coverage for the DID and verifiable credential\nworkflows.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql+OlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALeEQAIMZOzzSFNiIHvXryvgnbT6W\nyOaTfCQdsWQBMVf1md3njGEfmmvJ0vDp7HNTS6M01L9sXKulsSBBic2inUzRBYLp\nZNym3v76xTO9nGR9K6CVwBc1xQa4unFZFOiNcqQeao56PeUTZGAPemsV1OG+he/u\nz4ri4lKt/HkQx6hHOIu39lcDSCtfN9t7OiNu1flvqxGKBSN5Jr1oZSTZl7RAFG7J\nAlae1loZ/BJ9OuVF4Zt7d2w1qRZ49m6WvZgg+QOIZ6qQ7lW4ExrGgdctvfkKJLnk\nKaii+7tl+Yx9xK2gM1YKX6ZA3D0oLE697fDaV9Qc1wbGGPvJ3txMUok9PKteCKG9\nC6Mx2VFUyPoXvOlkiq9QglS9Nhge0bvy1Kk7Vn+m6HI92ikJyLq71YPiaRiFtLG1\ndNJtUGKA/dXl1sWMddpdnzyVCGbX/FmDJWdivPqTx1ol5THokyamFAwraexL7Kvp\n/zE1ITIh8lB6eVmE/Hjh6ti3QDIy9+opj20VQpPHE0t42atvW/n75OkvV+VMZcoY\nF7aYWv1MvpZ6OGrWBBt9w5u/dywPA2ZSAAhuAffSZQf4BJ8DZynzLLlBcUv9c7EU\nLnvaaJDJCVDgWSrq9RqSz9CWjOZgMKR+GYiQTYN39SUvDXUVW9/G8C7XV38RWJR/\nuN7vPGQMvFEDTH7p5CbY\n=uQ8c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T08:51:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/a653ce4a19d943014600fd72ab562eded814e9fe","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGE2NTNjZTRhMTlkOTQzMDE0NjAwZmQ3MmFiNTYyZWRlZDgxNGU5ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e","sha":"474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e"}],"sha":"a653ce4a19d943014600fd72ab562eded814e9fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a653ce4a19d943014600fd72ab562eded814e9fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226774300?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mspandey","id":226774300,"login":"mspandey","node_id":"U_kgDODYRNHA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mspandey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:49:47Z","email":"amisha.pandey2006@gmail.com","name":"Amisha Pandey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:49:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ECSoC26 Add schemas for evacuation and venue layout (#5485)\n\n### Summary\nImplements an **Interactive Event Layout Emergency Exit Evacuation AR\nOverlay** for real-time wayfinding during zero-visibility emergency\nscenarios.\n\n### Related Issue\nFixes\n[#5363](https://github.com/issues/assigned?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aopen+archived%3Afalse+assignee%3A%40me+sort%3Aupdated-desc&issue=krushit1307%7CCampusConnect%7C5363&issue_global_id=I_kwDOTPF5Rc8AAAABO9Gv5Q)\n\n### Key Changes\n- **Spatial Data Schemas (`shared/schemas/evacuationAR.ts`)**: Models\nvenue canvases, emergency exit vectors, and iBeacon/UWB spatial anchors.\n- **Pathfinding Engine (`src/services/evacuationPathfinder.ts`)**:\nCalculates shortest real-time path vectors from user coordinates to\nactive emergency exits.\n- **AR Viewport (`src/components/ar/EvacuationAROverlay.tsx`)**: Renders\nhigh-contrast `#00FF66` path overlays with spatial HUD distance\ntelemetry.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] Automatically triggers upon fire alarm detection signal\n([#5279](https://github.com/issues/assigned?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aopen+archived%3Afalse+assignee%3A%40me+sort%3Aupdated-desc&issue=krushit1307%7CCampusConnect%7C5363&issue_global_id=I_kwDOTPF5Rc8AAAABO9Gv5Q)).\n- [x] Reads venue layout geometry and iBeacon anchors to determine\nreal-time user positioning.\n- [x] Calculates nearest exit path and renders visual path guidance\noverlay.\nassignee- @krushit1307 \ncloses #5363\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added an emergency evacuation overlay with prominent emergency\nguidance, exit directions, and a dismiss option.\n- Added automatic route guidance to the nearest accessible emergency\nexit based on the person’s location and venue layout.\n- Added support for venue layouts containing exits, beacons, boundaries,\nand walkable areas.\n- Added validation for evacuation navigation data, including exit\naccessibility information.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"99046abd7cb1a6af6e584ddc6de9fd9909898bc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/99046abd7cb1a6af6e584ddc6de9fd9909898bc5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e","verification":{"payload":"tree 99046abd7cb1a6af6e584ddc6de9fd9909898bc5\nparent 565c343b6e2c81361dfb8ac60c1252aed0ce8a55\nauthor Amisha Pandey <amisha.pandey2006@gmail.com> 1788320987 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788320987 +0530\n\nECSoC26 Add schemas for evacuation and venue layout (#5485)\n\n### Summary\nImplements an **Interactive Event Layout Emergency Exit Evacuation AR\nOverlay** for real-time wayfinding during zero-visibility emergency\nscenarios.\n\n### Related Issue\nFixes\n[#5363](https://github.com/issues/assigned?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aopen+archived%3Afalse+assignee%3A%40me+sort%3Aupdated-desc&issue=krushit1307%7CCampusConnect%7C5363&issue_global_id=I_kwDOTPF5Rc8AAAABO9Gv5Q)\n\n### Key Changes\n- **Spatial Data Schemas (`shared/schemas/evacuationAR.ts`)**: Models\nvenue canvases, emergency exit vectors, and iBeacon/UWB spatial anchors.\n- **Pathfinding Engine (`src/services/evacuationPathfinder.ts`)**:\nCalculates shortest real-time path vectors from user coordinates to\nactive emergency exits.\n- **AR Viewport (`src/components/ar/EvacuationAROverlay.tsx`)**: Renders\nhigh-contrast `#00FF66` path overlays with spatial HUD distance\ntelemetry.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] Automatically triggers upon fire alarm detection signal\n([#5279](https://github.com/issues/assigned?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aopen+archived%3Afalse+assignee%3A%40me+sort%3Aupdated-desc&issue=krushit1307%7CCampusConnect%7C5363&issue_global_id=I_kwDOTPF5Rc8AAAABO9Gv5Q)).\n- [x] Reads venue layout geometry and iBeacon anchors to determine\nreal-time user positioning.\n- [x] Calculates nearest exit path and renders visual path guidance\noverlay.\nassignee- @krushit1307 \ncloses #5363\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added an emergency evacuation overlay with prominent emergency\nguidance, exit directions, and a dismiss option.\n- Added automatic route guidance to the nearest accessible emergency\nexit based on the person’s location and venue layout.\n- Added support for venue layouts containing exits, beacons, boundaries,\nand walkable areas.\n- Added validation for evacuation navigation data, including exit\naccessibility information.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql5zbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7aAQAGog/c8N1g/OViFV9sfcJ03K\nWUGEUtwK6bRCaMJs/ugN1ksm6DygRQCwCyu+mOMUWO5jxrDw3zbW7SFNnlPmkspj\nx1H1GfGp+UUtAwLFgsL+SVKqg/vq+gcF2tVwjD/T473SPgROBsO34GYX8t9GGBim\nfkcKWf5IKNS7pl3IXHWJAY2vykxN9TPmqPOgxK4sFf+zUK1qzkVDnrdFtY2RxRk/\nJJPCC6yzxj61cwx66DGNDK9licKQcRU7mMQ8U+tzlHAPiPMbkCKYZ0yChvN8ZxVz\ns9T/oaeI12c55Ger3wCHrcb+EoeqkWwtCbKhmsFa4UppaI9YErcLULn5Ox/ABR9P\nxtxd5zZPitrPyUjKlGmUwkhzVxJbV5PWHADW/onGexfuDna/a0IO04il63yVdXlV\nMwk+2KgAWQ/QV/njfVPiLhpRr4ty8VQ6LpuWtpbGjf3A6xZYlGLfTOJGijyGVIJl\nsReIMW6sB6sd7myZbDOilDIprLlZhYLC9nF1S2mYdXV//LsXxLFVGAOFHAPeQ8/c\nJtolBNyKuM8iIxsltpC0tUIs7vbgDfCSElTJ/N07lGOHKPzWf188QcK/GeFwZ9Sp\nzc0mJhcZXPHDMa6M58fLKGLMm/VZdJkBmphFKcaNrtce/jL5eoGVN76NpF7GYApo\nODQ0lagDaS944cDu0uL7\n=EZEY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T03:49:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDQ3NGY5OWY2NTgyM2M2NDUyZDNkZjY3MTRmYzEzZTU5ODA2MjliMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/565c343b6e2c81361dfb8ac60c1252aed0ce8a55","sha":"565c343b6e2c81361dfb8ac60c1252aed0ce8a55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/565c343b6e2c81361dfb8ac60c1252aed0ce8a55"}],"sha":"474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/474f99f65823c6452d3df6714fc13e5980629b1e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233611462?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zainabhina05-png","id":233611462,"login":"zainabhina05-png","node_id":"U_kgDODeygxg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/565c343b6e2c81361dfb8ac60c1252aed0ce8a55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:47:01Z","email":"zainab.hina05@gmail.com","name":"Zaeb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:47:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement CDP health monitoring with Flashbots protection (Issue #5466) (#5484)\n\n## Summary\nImplements automated CDP (Collateralized Debt Position) health\nmonitoring with Flashbots protection to prevent catastrophic liquidation\nrisk during periods of high macroeconomic volatility. Routes leveraged\nCDP transactions exclusively through private Flashbots RPC endpoints to\nguarantee execution without mempool exposure and prevent MEV sandwich\nattacks.\n\n## Problem\nLeveraged Decentralized Finance introduces catastrophic liquidation risk\nduring periods of high macroeconomic volatility. Executing a $500k Flash\nMint is highly visible in the Mempool. Predatory MEV bots execute\n\"Sandwich Attacks,\" artificially spiking gas fees and borrowing rates in\nthe exact millisecond the transaction is processed, stealing thousands\nof dollars from the charitable donation.\n\n## Solution\nImplement an Automated Algorithmic CDP Health Monitor with automated\ndeleveraging:\n- The backend continuously queries the MakerDAO Oracle for the real-time\nprice of Ethereum\n- It calculates the donor''s exact Collateralization Ratio\n- Establish a strict safety threshold (e.g., if the ratio drops below\n180%, danger is imminent)\n- If the price of ETH crashes and the ratio hits 179%, the backend\ninstantly triggers an automated Smart Contract execution\n- The contract automatically withdraws a portion of the yielded DAI,\nunwinds the leverage, and pays down the donor''s debt, mathematically\nrestoring the Collateralization Ratio and saving their $1M principal\nfrom catastrophic liquidation\n- Route the leveraged CDP transaction exclusively through a private\nFlashbots RPC endpoint, guaranteeing execution without mempool exposure\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `cdp_positions` table for tracking MakerDAO CDP positions with\ncollateral and debt tracking\n- Created `cdp_health_monitor` table for health monitoring and alerts\nwith status tracking\n- Created `flashbot_transactions` table for private transaction tracking\nwith MEV protection metrics\n- Created `oracle_price_history` table for price tracking with multiple\noracle sources\n- Added `create_cdp_position` RPC for CDP position creation with\nautomatic value calculation\n- Added `update_cdp_health` RPC for health status calculation with\nautomatic alert triggering\n- Added `trigger_deleveraging` RPC for automated deleveraging with\nFlashbots integration\n- Added `record_oracle_price` RPC for oracle price recording with\nautomatic CDP updates\n  - Added `get_latest_oracle_price` RPC for price retrieval\n- Added `get_cdp_health_summary` RPC for health summary across all\npositions\n\n- **Edge Function**: `cdp-health-monitor` function that:\n  - Fetches ETH price from MakerDAO Oracle with CoinGecko fallback\n  - Records oracle prices and automatically updates all CDP positions\n  - Calculates Collateralization Ratios for all active positions\n  - Determines health status (healthy, warning, critical, liquidated)\n  - Triggers automated deleveraging for critical positions\n  - Submits deleveraging transactions via Flashbots private mempool\n  - Tracks MEV savings and sandwich attack prevention\n  - Provides health monitoring cycle endpoint for cron job integration\n\n- **Collateralization Ratio Calculation**:\n- Formula: `collateralization_ratio = collateral_value_usd /\ndebt_value_usd`\n  - Automatic recalculation on every oracle price update\n  - Safety threshold configurable (default 180%)\n  - Liquidation threshold configurable (default 150%)\n\n- **Automated Deleveraging**:\n  - Triggered when collateralization ratio drops below safety threshold\n  - Calculates debt reduction needed to restore safety threshold\n  - Formula: `target_debt = collateral_value / safety_threshold`\n  - Automatic Flashbots transaction submission\n  - Prevents catastrophic liquidation by proactive debt reduction\n\n- **Flashbots Integration**:\n  - Private mempool routing to prevent MEV attacks\n  - Transaction tracking with bundle hash and block number\n  - Gas price and cost tracking\n  - MEV savings calculation\n  - Sandwich attack prevention tracking\n  - Status tracking (pending, submitted, included, failed, reverted)\n\n- **Oracle Price Monitoring**:\n  - MakerDAO Oracle integration with CoinGecko fallback\n- Multiple oracle source support (MakerDAO, Chainlink, Uniswap,\nCoinGecko)\n  - 24h price change and volume tracking\n  - Automatic CDP position updates on price changes\n  - Historical price tracking for analysis\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `CDPHealthMonitorPanel` component for:\n  - Viewing CDP positions with collateralization ratios\n  - Viewing health monitor records with status indicators\n  - Viewing Flashbots transactions with MEV savings\n  - Viewing Oracle price history with 24h changes\n  - Manual health check triggering\n  - Manual deleveraging triggering\n  - Real-time status tracking\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP test suite covering:\n  - Oracle price recording\n  - CDP position creation\n  - Collateralization ratio calculation\n  - Health status determination\n  - Critical level detection\n  - Deleveraging triggering\n  - Flashbot transaction creation\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. User creates CDP position with collateral and debt\n2. System continuously monitors ETH price via MakerDAO Oracle\n3. System calculates Collateralization Ratio on each price update\n4. If ratio drops below safety threshold (180%):\n   - Health status changes to \"critical\"\n   - Alert is triggered\n   - Automated deleveraging is initiated\n   - Flashbots transaction is submitted to private mempool\n   - Debt is reduced to restore safety threshold\n   - MEV savings are tracked\n5. If ratio drops below liquidation threshold (150%):\n   - Health status changes to \"liquidated\"\n   - Critical alert is triggered\n   - Emergency deleveraging is initiated\n6. Admin can view all positions, health status, and Flashbots\ntransactions\n7. Admin can manually trigger health checks and deleveraging\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `FLASHBOTS_RPC_ENDPOINT` environment variable for Flashbots\nintegration\n- Set `MAKERDAO_ORACLE_API` environment variable for MakerDAO Oracle\nintegration\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual mode)\n\n## MEV Protection Benefits\n- **Private Mempool**: Transactions never exposed to public mempool\n- **Sandwich Attack Prevention**: MEV bots cannot see transactions\n- **Gas Price Protection**: No artificial gas price spikes\n- **Execution Guarantee**: Flashbots ensures inclusion\n- **MEV Savings**: Track and report MEV savings\n- **Audit Trail**: Complete transaction tracking for compliance\n\n## Risk Management Benefits\n- **Automated Monitoring**: Continuous price monitoring without manual\nintervention\n- **Proactive Deleveraging**: Automatic debt reduction before\nliquidation\n- **Safety Thresholds**: Configurable thresholds for risk management\n- **Real-time Alerts**: Immediate notification of critical positions\n- **Historical Tracking**: Price history for analysis and reporting\n- **Principal Protection**: Protects $1M+ principal from catastrophic\nliquidation\n\nCloses #5466\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an admin dashboard for monitoring collateralized debt positions,\nhealth statuses, oracle prices, and protected deleveraging.\n* Added automated health monitoring, alerts, and transaction tracking\nfor critical positions.\n* Added support for creating secret ticket tiers with usage limits and\nexpiration dates.\n  * Added one-click copying of secret ticket unlock URLs.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Improved validation and error notifications when creating secret\nticket tiers.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee42cddbbc4c3150690c67efcb2a06f268e66c59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/ee42cddbbc4c3150690c67efcb2a06f268e66c59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/565c343b6e2c81361dfb8ac60c1252aed0ce8a55","verification":{"payload":"tree ee42cddbbc4c3150690c67efcb2a06f268e66c59\nparent 8b165975279150b526d436d9bede4277a10221d7\nauthor Zaeb <zainab.hina05@gmail.com> 1788320821 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788320821 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement CDP health monitoring with Flashbots protection (Issue #5466) (#5484)\n\n## Summary\nImplements automated CDP (Collateralized Debt Position) health\nmonitoring with Flashbots protection to prevent catastrophic liquidation\nrisk during periods of high macroeconomic volatility. Routes leveraged\nCDP transactions exclusively through private Flashbots RPC endpoints to\nguarantee execution without mempool exposure and prevent MEV sandwich\nattacks.\n\n## Problem\nLeveraged Decentralized Finance introduces catastrophic liquidation risk\nduring periods of high macroeconomic volatility. Executing a $500k Flash\nMint is highly visible in the Mempool. Predatory MEV bots execute\n\"Sandwich Attacks,\" artificially spiking gas fees and borrowing rates in\nthe exact millisecond the transaction is processed, stealing thousands\nof dollars from the charitable donation.\n\n## Solution\nImplement an Automated Algorithmic CDP Health Monitor with automated\ndeleveraging:\n- The backend continuously queries the MakerDAO Oracle for the real-time\nprice of Ethereum\n- It calculates the donor''s exact Collateralization Ratio\n- Establish a strict safety threshold (e.g., if the ratio drops below\n180%, danger is imminent)\n- If the price of ETH crashes and the ratio hits 179%, the backend\ninstantly triggers an automated Smart Contract execution\n- The contract automatically withdraws a portion of the yielded DAI,\nunwinds the leverage, and pays down the donor''s debt, mathematically\nrestoring the Collateralization Ratio and saving their $1M principal\nfrom catastrophic liquidation\n- Route the leveraged CDP transaction exclusively through a private\nFlashbots RPC endpoint, guaranteeing execution without mempool exposure\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `cdp_positions` table for tracking MakerDAO CDP positions with\ncollateral and debt tracking\n- Created `cdp_health_monitor` table for health monitoring and alerts\nwith status tracking\n- Created `flashbot_transactions` table for private transaction tracking\nwith MEV protection metrics\n- Created `oracle_price_history` table for price tracking with multiple\noracle sources\n- Added `create_cdp_position` RPC for CDP position creation with\nautomatic value calculation\n- Added `update_cdp_health` RPC for health status calculation with\nautomatic alert triggering\n- Added `trigger_deleveraging` RPC for automated deleveraging with\nFlashbots integration\n- Added `record_oracle_price` RPC for oracle price recording with\nautomatic CDP updates\n  - Added `get_latest_oracle_price` RPC for price retrieval\n- Added `get_cdp_health_summary` RPC for health summary across all\npositions\n\n- **Edge Function**: `cdp-health-monitor` function that:\n  - Fetches ETH price from MakerDAO Oracle with CoinGecko fallback\n  - Records oracle prices and automatically updates all CDP positions\n  - Calculates Collateralization Ratios for all active positions\n  - Determines health status (healthy, warning, critical, liquidated)\n  - Triggers automated deleveraging for critical positions\n  - Submits deleveraging transactions via Flashbots private mempool\n  - Tracks MEV savings and sandwich attack prevention\n  - Provides health monitoring cycle endpoint for cron job integration\n\n- **Collateralization Ratio Calculation**:\n- Formula: `collateralization_ratio = collateral_value_usd /\ndebt_value_usd`\n  - Automatic recalculation on every oracle price update\n  - Safety threshold configurable (default 180%)\n  - Liquidation threshold configurable (default 150%)\n\n- **Automated Deleveraging**:\n  - Triggered when collateralization ratio drops below safety threshold\n  - Calculates debt reduction needed to restore safety threshold\n  - Formula: `target_debt = collateral_value / safety_threshold`\n  - Automatic Flashbots transaction submission\n  - Prevents catastrophic liquidation by proactive debt reduction\n\n- **Flashbots Integration**:\n  - Private mempool routing to prevent MEV attacks\n  - Transaction tracking with bundle hash and block number\n  - Gas price and cost tracking\n  - MEV savings calculation\n  - Sandwich attack prevention tracking\n  - Status tracking (pending, submitted, included, failed, reverted)\n\n- **Oracle Price Monitoring**:\n  - MakerDAO Oracle integration with CoinGecko fallback\n- Multiple oracle source support (MakerDAO, Chainlink, Uniswap,\nCoinGecko)\n  - 24h price change and volume tracking\n  - Automatic CDP position updates on price changes\n  - Historical price tracking for analysis\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `CDPHealthMonitorPanel` component for:\n  - Viewing CDP positions with collateralization ratios\n  - Viewing health monitor records with status indicators\n  - Viewing Flashbots transactions with MEV savings\n  - Viewing Oracle price history with 24h changes\n  - Manual health check triggering\n  - Manual deleveraging triggering\n  - Real-time status tracking\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP test suite covering:\n  - Oracle price recording\n  - CDP position creation\n  - Collateralization ratio calculation\n  - Health status determination\n  - Critical level detection\n  - Deleveraging triggering\n  - Flashbot transaction creation\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. User creates CDP position with collateral and debt\n2. System continuously monitors ETH price via MakerDAO Oracle\n3. System calculates Collateralization Ratio on each price update\n4. If ratio drops below safety threshold (180%):\n   - Health status changes to \"critical\"\n   - Alert is triggered\n   - Automated deleveraging is initiated\n   - Flashbots transaction is submitted to private mempool\n   - Debt is reduced to restore safety threshold\n   - MEV savings are tracked\n5. If ratio drops below liquidation threshold (150%):\n   - Health status changes to \"liquidated\"\n   - Critical alert is triggered\n   - Emergency deleveraging is initiated\n6. Admin can view all positions, health status, and Flashbots\ntransactions\n7. Admin can manually trigger health checks and deleveraging\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `FLASHBOTS_RPC_ENDPOINT` environment variable for Flashbots\nintegration\n- Set `MAKERDAO_ORACLE_API` environment variable for MakerDAO Oracle\nintegration\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual mode)\n\n## MEV Protection Benefits\n- **Private Mempool**: Transactions never exposed to public mempool\n- **Sandwich Attack Prevention**: MEV bots cannot see transactions\n- **Gas Price Protection**: No artificial gas price spikes\n- **Execution Guarantee**: Flashbots ensures inclusion\n- **MEV Savings**: Track and report MEV savings\n- **Audit Trail**: Complete transaction tracking for compliance\n\n## Risk Management Benefits\n- **Automated Monitoring**: Continuous price monitoring without manual\nintervention\n- **Proactive Deleveraging**: Automatic debt reduction before\nliquidation\n- **Safety Thresholds**: Configurable thresholds for risk management\n- **Real-time Alerts**: Immediate notification of critical positions\n- **Historical Tracking**: Price history for analysis and reporting\n- **Principal Protection**: Protects $1M+ principal from catastrophic\nliquidation\n\nCloses #5466\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an admin dashboard for monitoring collateralized debt positions,\nhealth statuses, oracle prices, and protected deleveraging.\n* Added automated health monitoring, alerts, and transaction tracking\nfor critical positions.\n* Added support for creating secret ticket tiers with usage limits and\nexpiration dates.\n  * Added one-click copying of secret ticket unlock URLs.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Improved validation and error notifications when creating secret\nticket tiers.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql5w1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUk8QAGftlXOP9TqvKwOeZypx5F7N\nuOtm8Za6XzlNjhC6n5CFXg1tpzzO7KhJH/Boq6PU4UGY41wT6FeuA572SLyizck1\n7lLtl7uLcw2NCecIt6o5LOXI2LPjJKj2yIKUvu8i943LcjZTFx9CkAPpLvHTJ17R\nwrb5GbtS+J6/fva9P/CA9lPeEJX2jS2iZ5C52dfNHOfkncxoRnVCMfDgAijcftYx\nPN1hu9cHrOQotuOB7pXjHr5Gtbx0YNEhqLltXdJ/7Og6aKlQg1HjMqwYFAGytSL/\ntRDD8gsxEVSt2VfXEG06eE6ePVDBck