hub.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/c3effc426a7882e339caac55fea4ad58a0b73cb7","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGMzZWZmYzQyNmE3ODgyZTMzOWNhYWM1NWZlYTRhZDU4YTBiNzNjYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/c4efa32ed192e6be135060096fda5ceea4b9d808","sha":"c4efa32ed192e6be135060096fda5ceea4b9d808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/c4efa32ed192e6be135060096fda5ceea4b9d808"}],"sha":"c3effc426a7882e339caac55fea4ad58a0b73cb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/c3effc426a7882e339caac55fea4ad58a0b73cb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/231409700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nayanraj864-cmyk","id":231409700,"login":"nayanraj864-cmyk","node_id":"U_kgDODcsIJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/c4efa32ed192e6be135060096fda5ceea4b9d808/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:44:50Z","email":"nayanraj864@gmail.com","name":"nayanraj864-cmyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:44:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(catering): Build an ''Interactive \"Dietary Restriction\" Smart Refrigerator Lock'' (#4986) (#5480)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements the ''Interactive \"Dietary Restriction\" Smart\nRefrigerator Lock'' (`smart_refrigerator_locks`,\n`smart_fridge_access_logs`, `smartRefrigeratorLock.ts`, and\n`SmartRefrigeratorLockWidget`), protecting high-value specialized food\ndrop-offs (Halal/Kosher/Vegan catering) in communal staging zones by\nintegrating ESP32 IoT relays with cryptographic access control (Caterer\nQR deposit lock drop + Organizer 64-char SHA-256 Bluetooth BLE one-time\nunlock).\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Database Schema (`20260872000000_smart_refrigerator_lock.sql`)**:\nCreated `public.smart_refrigerator_locks` and\n`public.smart_fridge_access_logs` tables logging ESP32 device IDs,\none-time unlock hashes, and access logs.\n- **Cryptographic Access Control Engine (`smartRefrigeratorLock.ts`)**:\n`generateOneTimeUnlockHash` generates 64-char SHA-256 unlock hashes with\n4-hour expiry windows; `executeCatererQrDeposit` drops lock for caterer\nfood deposit; `executeOrganizerBleUnlock` verifies BLE unlock payloads\nto open staging fridges for event organizers.\n- **Smart Fridge Lock Dashboard UI\n(`SmartRefrigeratorLockWidget.tsx`)**: Features IoT lock status bar,\nprotected dietary staging details card, 1-click Caterer QR Deposit\nscanner, 64-char cryptographic unlock hash card, and 1-click Organizer\nBluetooth BLE unlock button.\n\n---\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [x] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] UI/UX Enhancement\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Other\n\n---\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #4986\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed:\n\n- [x] Tested locally via `npx vitest run\nsrc/lib/smartRefrigeratorLock.test.ts\nsrc/components/catering/SmartRefrigeratorLockWidget.test.tsx` (**6/6\npassed**)\n- [x] Verified 64-character SHA-256 one-time unlock hash generation with\n4-hour expiry window\n- [x] Verified Caterer QR deposit lock drop & 60s auto-lock\n- [x] Verified Organizer Bluetooth BLE unlock payload transmission\n(`BLE_ESP32_RELAY_UNLOCK`)\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n---\n\n## Screenshots\n\n*N/A — Interactive Dietary Restriction Smart Refrigerator Lock added to\nCatering & Event Staging view.*\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added smart refrigerator lock management for catering workflows.\n* Caterers can unlock refrigerators by scanning a QR code for food\ndeposits.\n* Organizers can unlock refrigerators using a one-time Bluetooth\nverification code.\n* Added lock status indicators, unlock expiration details,\nnotifications, and access activity records.\n* Added support for tracking refrigerator devices, locations, dietary\ntypes, events, and unlock history.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added coverage for hash generation, QR unlocks, Bluetooth unlocks,\ncallbacks, and displayed unlock states.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"d516e7261ca6cbf4901675df24b6e342d1e9cb89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/d516e7261ca6cbf4901675df24b6e342d1e9cb89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/c4efa32ed192e6be135060096fda5ceea4b9d808","verification":{"payload":"tree d516e7261ca6cbf4901675df24b6e342d1e9cb89\nparent 9ccf6df4c5aefd762c868d167387bc28e45aa1ca\nauthor nayanraj864-cmyk <nayanraj864@gmail.com> 1788320690 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788320690 +0530\n\nfeat(catering): Build an ''Interactive \"Dietary Restriction\" Smart Refrigerator Lock'' (#4986) (#5480)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements the ''Interactive \"Dietary Restriction\" Smart\nRefrigerator Lock'' (`smart_refrigerator_locks`,\n`smart_fridge_access_logs`, `smartRefrigeratorLock.ts`, and\n`SmartRefrigeratorLockWidget`), protecting high-value specialized food\ndrop-offs (Halal/Kosher/Vegan catering) in communal staging zones by\nintegrating ESP32 IoT relays with cryptographic access control (Caterer\nQR deposit lock drop + Organizer 64-char SHA-256 Bluetooth BLE one-time\nunlock).\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Database Schema (`20260872000000_smart_refrigerator_lock.sql`)**:\nCreated `public.smart_refrigerator_locks` and\n`public.smart_fridge_access_logs` tables logging ESP32 device IDs,\none-time unlock hashes, and access logs.\n- **Cryptographic Access Control Engine (`smartRefrigeratorLock.ts`)**:\n`generateOneTimeUnlockHash` generates 64-char SHA-256 unlock hashes with\n4-hour expiry windows; `executeCatererQrDeposit` drops lock for caterer\nfood deposit; `executeOrganizerBleUnlock` verifies BLE unlock payloads\nto open staging fridges for event organizers.\n- **Smart Fridge Lock Dashboard UI\n(`SmartRefrigeratorLockWidget.tsx`)**: Features IoT lock status bar,\nprotected dietary staging details card, 1-click Caterer QR Deposit\nscanner, 64-char cryptographic unlock hash card, and 1-click Organizer\nBluetooth BLE unlock button.\n\n---\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [x] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] UI/UX Enhancement\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Other\n\n---\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #4986\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed:\n\n- [x] Tested locally via `npx vitest run\nsrc/lib/smartRefrigeratorLock.test.ts\nsrc/components/catering/SmartRefrigeratorLockWidget.test.tsx` (**6/6\npassed**)\n- [x] Verified 64-character SHA-256 one-time unlock hash generation with\n4-hour expiry window\n- [x] Verified Caterer QR deposit lock drop & 60s auto-lock\n- [x] Verified Organizer Bluetooth BLE unlock payload transmission\n(`BLE_ESP32_RELAY_UNLOCK`)\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n---\n\n## Screenshots\n\n*N/A — Interactive Dietary Restriction Smart Refrigerator Lock added to\nCatering & Event Staging view.*\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added smart refrigerator lock management for catering workflows.\n* Caterers can unlock refrigerators by scanning a QR code for food\ndeposits.\n* Organizers can unlock refrigerators using a one-time Bluetooth\nverification code.\n* Added lock status indicators, unlock expiration details,\nnotifications, and access activity records.\n* Added support for tracking refrigerator devices, locations, dietary\ntypes, events, and unlock history.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added coverage for hash generation, QR unlocks, Bluetooth unlocks,\ncallbacks, and displayed unlock states.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql5uyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAutEQAIN342XVCbtfkHXn137j6sEx\ny4n2g31o7GfdNq2lTFGkmtJt0XYq/NiLdHBRVY5/Snern4nWnHLxgFC9eWcgm+XM\nwD//ENukfcZfqDp86CcP1fSRxZ9X8sdaBEcnmM3xBKOyhVMc95IHPNs8KzMXOXrJ\n6bJnMX6SkparTwyrNVZxa+9uTiNud3utnwb2+k03s7L0qBvxipuclAp23/52jKG+\nCDY3rziXxd//J2BszI7a8OCYtFwKfGgf1cXnrmwTBN6RB2vkdHhaQHCRZncASDXv\nrfXLXTd