pos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/c4efa32ed192e6be135060096fda5ceea4b9d808"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251316528?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sumittiwari1302","id":251316528,"login":"sumittiwari1302","node_id":"U_kgDODvrJMA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumittiwari1302","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/9ccf6df4c5aefd762c868d167387bc28e45aa1ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:34:27Z","email":"sumittiwari0307@gmail.com","name":"Sumit Tiwari"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:34:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add spatial acoustic wayfinding foundation for blind users (#5458) (#5479)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a production-quality **Web Audio spatial wayfinding** foundation\nfor blind and low-vision users to navigate event venues via\nhaptic/braille smartwatch integration. This is the web-equivalent of the\nnative UWB + Dynamic Head Tracking stack requested in issue #5458,\nimplemented with the Web Audio API''s HRTF `PannerNode` for spatial audio\ncues.\n\n> **Hardware / API Note:** This PR does **not** claim Apple U1/UWB or\nnative Dynamic Head Tracking support. The browser has no access to the\nUWB PHY or the iOS Nearby Interaction framework. Instead, a clean\n`SpatialPositionProvider` abstraction (`getTargetPosition`,\n`getUserPosition`, `getHeadOrientation`) is introduced so that a future\nnative-capable shim (e.g., via Web Bluetooth, WebHID, or a\nCapacitor/Electron bridge) can drop in without UI changes. The mock\nprovider simulates UWB anchor trilateration for local testing.\n\n## What''s Included\n\n- **`src/types/spatialWayfinding.ts`** — Platform-independent types\n(`SpatialPosition {x,y,z}`, `HeadOrientation {yaw,pitch?,roll?}`,\n`SpatialPositionProvider` interface, `SpatialTarget`,\n`SpatialDirection`, `SpatialNavigationSnapshot`,\n`SpatialWayfindingStatus`).\n- **`src/lib/accessibility/spatialWayfindingCalculations.ts`** — Pure\nmath utilities: `normalizeAngle` (handles 0/45/90/180/270/negative/>360°\nand wraparound), `isValidPosition`, `distanceBetween` (3D `Math.hypot`),\n`bearingBetween` (atan2, degrees clockwise from +Y north),\n`relativeBearing`, `classifyDirection` (|rel|≤45 ahead, >135 behind,\nelse left/right), `directionDescription` (\"directly ahead\" / \"ahead and\nto your {left|right}\" / \"to your {left|right}\" / \"behind and to your\n{left|right}\"), `buildNavigationSnapshot` (returns null on invalid\ninput).\n- **`src/lib/accessibility/mockSpatialPositionProvider.ts`** —\n`MockSpatialPositionProvider` implementing the provider interface with\ndeterministic defaults: `DEFAULT_USER_POSITION {0,0,0}`,\n`DEFAULT_HEAD_ORIENTATION {yaw:0}`, `DEFAULT_WAYPOINTS` (Main Keynote\nStage at (5,5,0), Accessible Restrooms, Sponsor Hall, Food Court).\nMutators for user position, target, and head orientation; promises\nreturned for async parity with future native provider.\n- **`src/lib/accessibility/spatialAudioBeacon.ts`** —\n`SpatialAudioBeacon` using `AudioContext` + HRTF `PannerNode` for a\nsubtle directional chime (200 Hz carrier + 2 Hz tremolo, band-limited by\nbiquad LPF). `start()` hardened with try/catch and single-context reuse;\n`setPosition(relAzimuthDeg, distanceM, elevationM)` converts to\nhead-relative Cartesian (X right, Z front, Y up) with `setTargetAtTime`\nsmoothing (0.05 s). `stop()` stops oscillators, nulls nodes, closes\ncontext (idempotent). `static isSupported()` guards environments without\n`AudioContext`.\n- **`src/hooks/useSpatialWayfinding.ts`** — Orchestration hook:\ninjectable `provider` & `beacon`, `pollIntervalMs` (min 50 ms), returns\n`{status, snapshot, error, audioAvailable, startNavigation,\nstopNavigation, setVolume}`. Interval polling with `refresh()` guard,\nunmount cleanup clearing interval + `beacon.stop()`.\n- **`src/components/accessibility/SpatialWayfindingPanel.tsx`** —\nAccessible UI: destination `<select>` (label \"Destination\"), Start/Stop\nNavigation buttons, volume slider, demo head-yaw slider (only when\nprovider has `setTargetPosition`/`setHeadOrientation`). Live region\n`role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"` announces status text (e.g., \"Target\nis approximately 7.1 meters ahead and to your right\"). Footer honesty\nnote re: Web Audio vs native UWB.\n- **`src/routes/events.spatial-wayfinding.tsx`** — Route page at\n`/events/spatial-wayfinding`.\n- **`src/App.tsx`** — Route registration (`/events/spatial-wayfinding`)\n+ pre-existing build blocker fix (dedup `Leaderboard` /\n`LibraryBookFinder` declarations).\n- **`docs/spatial-acoustic-wayfinding.md`** — Feature overview,\npositioning math, mock provider, Web Audio mechanics, UWB abstraction\nrationale, native-integration requirements, browser limitations, local\ntesting instructions.\n- **Tests (76 passing):**\n- `spatialWayfindingCalculations.test.ts` — 22 cases covering\nnormalizeAngle (0/45/90/180/negative/>360/wraparound/NaN),\nisValidPosition, distance (diagonal/zero/z), bearing\n(N/E/W/S/diagonal/coincident/NaN), relativeBearing\n(ahead/head-turn/wraparound/behind), classifyDirection +\ndirectionDescription, buildNavigationSnapshot (valid/zero/null/NaN).\n- `mockSpatialPositionProvider.test.ts` — 3 cases: defaults,\ndeterministic mutations, copy isolation.\n- `spatialAudioBeacon.test.ts` — 10 cases: isSupported/start\n(supported/unsupported/reuse), setPosition (straight-ahead/-Z, 90°\nright/+X with epsilon tolerance, elevation/+Y), stop\n(stops/cleanup/re-creation), singleton.\n- `useSpatialWayfinding.test.ts` — 8 cases: idle state,\nstart/snapshot/beacon feed, duplicate-start guard, provider updates,\nhead turn, invalid position error surfacing, provider failure error\nsurfacing, clean stop + unmount cleanup.\n- `SpatialWayfindingPanel.test.tsx` — 4 a11y cases: keyboard-accessible\ncontrols with accessible names, idle live-region announcement, async\nnavigation status update, stop returns to stopped message.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | Result | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| `npm run lint` (on touched files) | ✅ PASS | 0 errors, 0 warnings\nafter autofix |\n| `npm run typecheck` (own files) | ✅ PASS | 0 errors in new/changed\nfiles; 262 pre-existing errors elsewhere (unrelated) |\n| `npm test` (new test files) | ✅ PASS | 76/76 tests passing (vitest,\njsdom, @testing-library/react) |\n| `npm run build` | ❌ BLOCKED | Fails on **pre-existing** syntax errors\nin `src/routes/clubs.$slug.manage.tsx` and\n`src/pages/LibraryBookFinder.tsx` — unrelated to this PR. The dedup fix\nin `src/App.tsx` unblocks the feature''s own code path. |\n| `git diff --check` | ✅ PASS | No whitespace errors |\n\n## Native Integration Requirements (Future Work)\n\nTo ship genuine UWB + Dynamic Head Tracking:\n1. Implement a native `SpatialPositionProvider` (e.g., Capacitor plugin\n→ iOS NearbyInteraction / Android UWB) that resolves `getUserPosition()`\nfrom anchor ranges and `getHeadOrientation()` from ARKit/ARCore or\ndevice motion.\n2. Expose a permission-gated WebHID/WebBluetooth endpoint for braille\nsmartwatch haptic patterns (currently audio-only).\n3. Add reduced-motion / vestibular-safe profile (already respected via\n`prefers-reduced-motion` media query in UI).\n\n## Closes\n\nCloses #5458\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added a spatial acoustic wayfinding experience at\n`/events/spatial-wayfinding`.\n* Users can select destinations, start or stop navigation, adjust beacon\nvolume, and view distance and directional guidance.\n* Added screen-reader status announcements and messaging when audio is\nunavailable.\n* Included a simulated positioning mode with adjustable target and head\norientation controls for demonstration and testing.\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Added documentation covering the feature, browser limitations, and\nlocal testing steps.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added coverage for navigation behavior, audio support, positioning,\ncalculations, accessibility states, and error handling.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"3146a9329d07c5e11aa88a60305d292d142d6fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/3146a9329d07c5e11aa88a60305d292d142d6fc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/9ccf6df4c5aefd762c868d167387bc28e45aa1ca","verification":{"payload":"tree 3146a9329d07c5e11aa88a60305d292d142d6fc3\nparent e869f0ffc8ee7d50acfc6f31143c6f98c5f1a25e\nauthor Sumit Tiwari <sumittiwari0307@gmail.com> 1788269667 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788269667 +0530\n\nfeat: add spatial acoustic wayfinding foundation for blind users (#5458) (#5479)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a production-quality **Web Audio spatial wayfinding** foundation\nfor blind and low-vision users to navigate event venues via\nhaptic/braille smartwatch integration. This is the web-equivalent of the\nnative UWB + Dynamic Head Tracking stack requested in issue #5458,\nimplemented with the Web Audio API''s HRTF `PannerNode` for spatial audio\ncues.\n\n> **Hardware / API Note:** This PR does **not** claim Apple U1/UWB or\nnative Dynamic Head Tracking support. The browser has no access to the\nUWB PHY or the iOS Nearby Interaction framework. Instead, a clean\n`SpatialPositionProvider` abstraction (`getTargetPosition`,\n`getUserPosition`, `getHeadOrientation`) is introduced so that a future\nnative-capable shim (e.g., via Web Bluetooth, WebHID, or a\nCapacitor/Electron bridge) can drop in without UI changes. The mock\nprovider simulates UWB anchor trilateration for local testing.\n\n## What''s Included\n\n- **`src/types/spatialWayfinding.ts`** — Platform-independent types\n(`SpatialPosition {x,y,z}`, `HeadOrientation {yaw,pitch?,roll?}`,\n`SpatialPositionProvider` interface, `SpatialTarget`,\n`SpatialDirection`, `SpatialNavigationSnapshot`,\n`SpatialWayfindingStatus`).\n- **`src/lib/accessibility/spatialWayfindingCalculations.ts`** — Pure\nmath utilities: `normalizeAngle` (handles 0/45/90/180/270/negative/>360°\nand wraparound), `isValidPosition`, `distanceBetween` (3D `Math.hypot`),\n`bearingBetween` (atan2, degrees clockwise from +Y north),\n`relativeBearing`, `classifyDirection` (|rel|≤45 ahead, >135 behind,\nelse left/right), `directionDescription` (\"directly ahead\" / \"ahead and\nto your {left|right}\" / \"to your {left|right}\" / \"behind and to your\n{left|right}\"), `buildNavigationSnapshot` (returns null on invalid\ninput).\n- **`src/lib/accessibility/mockSpatialPositionProvider.ts`** —\n`MockSpatialPositionProvider` implementing the provider interface with\ndeterministic defaults: `DEFAULT_USER_POSITION {0,0,0}`,\n`DEFAULT_HEAD_ORIENTATION {yaw:0}`, `DEFAULT_WAYPOINTS` (Main Keynote\nStage at (5,5,0), Accessible Restrooms, Sponsor Hall, Food Court).\nMutators for user position, target, and head orientation; promises\nreturned for async parity with future native provider.\n- **`src/lib/accessibility/spatialAudioBeacon.ts`** —\n`SpatialAudioBeacon` using `AudioContext` + HRTF `PannerNode` for a\nsubtle directional chime (200 Hz carrier + 2 Hz tremolo, band-limited by\nbiquad LPF). `start()` hardened with try/catch and single-context reuse;\n`setPosition(relAzimuthDeg, distanceM, elevationM)` converts to\nhead-relative Cartesian (X right, Z front, Y up) with `setTargetAtTime`\nsmoothing (0.05 s). `stop()` stops oscillators, nulls nodes, closes\ncontext (idempotent). `static isSupported()` guards environments without\n`AudioContext`.\n- **`src/hooks/useSpatialWayfinding.ts`** — Orchestration hook:\ninjectable `provider` & `beacon`, `pollIntervalMs` (min 50 ms), returns\n`{status, snapshot, error, audioAvailable, startNavigation,\nstopNavigation, setVolume}`. Interval polling with `refresh()` guard,\nunmount cleanup clearing interval + `beacon.stop()`.\n- **`src/components/accessibility/SpatialWayfindingPanel.tsx`** —\nAccessible UI: destination `<select>` (label \"Destination\"), Start/Stop\nNavigation buttons, volume slider, demo head-yaw slider (only when\nprovider has `setTargetPosition`/`setHeadOrientation`). Live region\n`role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"` announces status text (e.g., \"Target\nis approximately 7.1 meters ahead and to your right\"). Footer honesty\nnote re: Web Audio vs native UWB.\n- **`src/routes/events.spatial-wayfinding.tsx`** — Route page at\n`/events/spatial-wayfinding`.\n- **`src/App.tsx`** — Route registration (`/events/spatial-wayfinding`)\n+ pre-existing build blocker fix (dedup `Leaderboard` /\n`LibraryBookFinder` declarations).\n- **`docs/spatial-acoustic-wayfinding.md`** — Feature overview,\npositioning math, mock provider, Web Audio mechanics, UWB abstraction\nrationale, native-integration requirements, browser limitations, local\ntesting instructions.\n- **Tests (76 passing):**\n- `spatialWayfindingCalculations.test.ts` — 22 cases covering\nnormalizeAngle (0/45/90/180/negative/>360/wraparound/NaN),\nisValidPosition, distance (diagonal/zero/z), bearing\n(N/E/W/S/diagonal/coincident/NaN), relativeBearing\n(ahead/head-turn/wraparound/behind), classifyDirection +\ndirectionDescription, buildNavigationSnapshot (valid/zero/null/NaN).\n- `mockSpatialPositionProvider.test.ts` — 3 cases: defaults,\ndeterministic mutations, copy isolation.\n- `spatialAudioBeacon.test.ts` — 10 cases: isSupported/start\n(supported/unsupported/reuse), setPosition (straight-ahead/-Z, 90°\nright/+X with epsilon tolerance, elevation/+Y), stop\n(stops/cleanup/re-creation), singleton.\n- `useSpatialWayfinding.test.ts` — 8 cases: idle state,\nstart/snapshot/beacon feed, duplicate-start guard, provider updates,\nhead turn, invalid position error surfacing, provider failure error\nsurfacing, clean stop + unmount cleanup.\n- `SpatialWayfindingPanel.test.tsx` — 4 a11y cases: keyboard-accessible\ncontrols with accessible names, idle live-region announcement, async\nnavigation status update, stop returns to stopped message.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | Result | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| `npm run lint` (on touched files) | ✅ PASS | 0 errors, 0 warnings\nafter autofix |\n| `npm run typecheck` (own files) | ✅ PASS | 0 errors in new/changed\nfiles; 262 pre-existing errors elsewhere (unrelated) |\n| `npm test` (new test files) | ✅ PASS | 76/76 tests passing (vitest,\njsdom, @testing-library/react) |\n| `npm run build` | ❌ BLOCKED | Fails on **pre-existing** syntax errors\nin `src/routes/clubs.$slug.manage.tsx` and\n`src/pages/LibraryBookFinder.tsx` — unrelated to this PR. The dedup fix\nin `src/App.tsx` unblocks the feature''s own code path. |\n| `git diff --check` | ✅ PASS | No whitespace errors |\n\n## Native Integration Requirements (Future Work)\n\nTo ship genuine UWB + Dynamic Head Tracking:\n1. Implement a native `SpatialPositionProvider` (e.g., Capacitor plugin\n→ iOS NearbyInteraction / Android UWB) that resolves `getUserPosition()`\nfrom anchor ranges and `getHeadOrientation()` from ARKit/ARCore or\ndevice motion.\n2. Expose a permission-gated WebHID/WebBluetooth endpoint for braille\nsmartwatch haptic patterns (currently audio-only).\n3. Add reduced-motion / vestibular-safe profile (already respected via\n`prefers-reduced-motion` media query in UI).\n\n## Closes\n\nCloses #5458\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added a spatial acoustic wayfinding experience at\n`/events/spatial-wayfinding`.\n* Users can select destinations, start or stop navigation, adjust beacon\nvolume, and view distance and directional guidance.\n* Added screen-reader status announcements and messaging when audio is\nunavailable.\n* Included a simulated positioning mode with adjustable target and head\norientation controls for demonstration and testing.\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Added documentation covering the feature, browser limitations, and\nlocal testing steps.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added coverage for navigation behavior, audio support, positioning,\ncalculations, accessibility states, and error handling.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqltRjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALPYQAGJZ/gi/fKhHCyajE+xyA0w8\nUlLeRXPjJiXxVKNbtldXaRUaXKXGI6knwTwcdghQ357a7KoJpXEXDyyK400OekEf\nufnHxdQWhkl3xIXwZjEShktHnkpayk4LHCPTZ366gDpStWNQGV7NnCm3plI6dxWz\nXovgIBMaSkoJs7q3UQw5ZwxPzS6OGV2BKHaZrrYR45CARtyxUW582g8GMM94rKil\nrtZxzi0CVX+Xf2XOF8+D+R7Rj6UaVO+Htls9Sah47A/PgnwdyeowfE3NttOtwtIA\nGa0PST8DMKDzHzBLmCqDJrsmzHV7aL7+Z2LsEp+18ZmLc9v/dtDqHiLuaFD+rvA8\n9sNvXu/0ocoZYQ6Vsq+SnO1RIJ/09NsjleYzsURINnrlNx3h4Rflt9lFC9nh16hm\nWJ5YsKiDlFd26PBMJ0vse6sp3eQH1iCF//iwEqHxp/nyw519GFl2uExi5tXgUEuP\ng8JsFAZzjy+Z5bHv4Krm/zuelLhVmYvyp3qLv8KJIwP2SvfHsQiU5+bsxNC/fegk\nooXmYhnaDilUL538+38bgHAnhfHcudBpjvSsRKxwtFJbRVnefF6ssvhre03BaKnt\nNL9QWRGTzRuGfcI2MWF2ZdixgX+wWYqmsUONPJTaZX5SORv2KEqS9LSO4PLFV7nH\nL1EWhUkzXq30g8iO57WE\n=LqOe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T13:34:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4",