url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/c92b4427a662c94c1b46a4cfb362889c03405fea","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGM5MmI0NDI3YTY2MmM5NGMxYjQ2YTRjZmIzNjI4ODljMDM0MDVmZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377","sha":"d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377"}],"sha":"c92b4427a662c94c1b46a4cfb362889c03405fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/c92b4427a662c94c1b46a4cfb362889c03405fea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/202644253?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sukhmanpreetkaur18","id":202644253,"login":"Sukhmanpreetkaur18","node_id":"U_kgDODBQbHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:13:01Z","email":"jasmeetkaurchwl@gmail.com","name":"Sukhmanpreet Kaur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:13:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Automated Event Feedback Linguistic Sentiment Drift w… (#5475)\n\n### 📝 Description\nThis PR implements Canvas/WebGL fingerprinting to detect headless\nbrowser botnets. By rendering complex 3D WebGL shapes and hashing pixel\noutputs, the system can mathematically distinguish between consumer\ndevices and server-grade GPU instances (AWS/DigitalOcean), exposing\nsophisticated headless automation.\n\n### 🚀 Features Added\n\n#### 1. Canvas Analyzer (500+ lines)\n- **Canvas Fingerprinting**: Hash canvas pixel data\n- **WebGL Fingerprinting**: Hash WebGL renderer properties\n- **Headless Detection**: Identify headless patterns\n- **Device Classification**: Desktop, Mobile, Tablet, Headless\n- **Risk Assessment**: Low, Medium, High, Critical\n\n#### 2. Hash Comparator (300+ lines)\n- **Hash Comparison**: Compare against known patterns\n- **Device Matching**: Match desktop/mobile/headless hashes\n- **Confidence Scoring**: Calculate confidence levels\n- **Pattern Detection**: Identify renderer patterns\n\n#### 3. Detection Rules (300+ lines)\n- **Rule Engine**: Apply detection rules\n- **Rule Conditions**: Headless, software rendering, virtual GPU\n- **Action Types**: Block, Flag, Allow\n- **Severity Levels**: Critical, High, Medium, Low\n\n#### 4. Fingerprint Service (500+ lines)\n- **Analysis Management**: Store and retrieve analyses\n- **Session Tracking**: Track multiple fingerprints per session\n- **Risk Assessment**: Aggregate risk scoring\n- **Statistics**: Detection statistics\n- **Cleanup**: Old data cleanup\n\n#### 5. Middleware (300+ lines)\n- **Header Validation**: Validate fingerprint headers\n- **Automatic Analysis**: Analyze on request\n- **Blocking Logic**: Block based on risk level\n- **Exempt Paths**: Skip certain paths\n\n#### 6. API Endpoints (300+ lines)\n| Endpoint | Method | Description |\n|----------|--------|-------------|\n| `/api/fingerprint/collect` | POST | Collect fingerprint |\n| `/api/fingerprint/analysis/{id}` | GET | Get analysis |\n| `/api/fingerprint/session/{id}` | GET | Get session fingerprints |\n| `/api/fingerprint/session/{id}/risk` | GET | Get risk assessment |\n| `/api/fingerprint/block/{id}` | POST | Block fingerprint |\n| `/api/fingerprint/statistics` | GET | Get stats |\n\nfixes #5465","tree":{"sha":"1eae9eb8a53055dfd38e5e56cb037cd50fa29a01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/1eae9eb8a53055dfd38e5e56cb037cd50fa29a01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377","verification":{"payload":"tree 1eae9eb8a53055dfd38e5e56cb037cd50fa29a01\nparent 10fa4f62fa05536743beb2ba63958be479f34c50\nauthor Sukhmanpreet Kaur <jasmeetkaurchwl@gmail.com> 1788239581 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788239581 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement Automated Event Feedback Linguistic Sentiment Drift w… (#5475)\n\n### 📝 Description\nThis PR implements Canvas/WebGL fingerprinting to detect headless\nbrowser botnets. By rendering complex 3D WebGL shapes and hashing pixel\noutputs, the system can mathematically distinguish between consumer\ndevices and server-grade GPU instances (AWS/DigitalOcean), exposing\nsophisticated headless automation.\n\n### 🚀 Features Added\n\n#### 1. Canvas Analyzer (500+ lines)\n- **Canvas Fingerprinting**: Hash canvas pixel data\n- **WebGL Fingerprinting**: Hash WebGL renderer properties\n- **Headless Detection**: Identify headless patterns\n- **Device Classification**: Desktop, Mobile, Tablet, Headless\n- **Risk Assessment**: Low, Medium, High, Critical\n\n#### 2. Hash Comparator (300+ lines)\n- **Hash Comparison**: Compare against known patterns\n- **Device Matching**: Match desktop/mobile/headless hashes\n- **Confidence Scoring**: Calculate confidence levels\n- **Pattern Detection**: Identify renderer patterns\n\n#### 3. Detection Rules (300+ lines)\n- **Rule Engine**: Apply detection rules\n- **Rule Conditions**: Headless, software rendering, virtual GPU\n- **Action Types**: Block, Flag, Allow\n- **Severity Levels**: Critical, High, Medium, Low\n\n#### 4. Fingerprint Service (500+ lines)\n- **Analysis Management**: Store and retrieve analyses\n- **Session Tracking**: Track multiple fingerprints per session\n- **Risk Assessment**: Aggregate risk scoring\n- **Statistics**: Detection statistics\n- **Cleanup**: Old data cleanup\n\n#### 5. Middleware (300+ lines)\n- **Header Validation**: Validate fingerprint headers\n- **Automatic Analysis**: Analyze on request\n- **Blocking Logic**: Block based on risk level\n- **Exempt Paths**: Skip certain paths\n\n#### 6. API Endpoints (300+ lines)\n| Endpoint | Method | Description |\n|----------|--------|-------------|\n| `/api/fingerprint/collect` | POST | Collect fingerprint |\n| `/api/fingerprint/analysis/{id}` | GET | Get analysis |\n| `/api/fingerprint/session/{id}` | GET | Get session fingerprints |\n| `/api/fingerprint/session/{id}/risk` | GET | Get risk assessment |\n| `/api/fingerprint/block/{id}` | POST | Block fingerprint |\n| `/api/fingerprint/statistics` | GET | Get stats |\n\nfixes #5465","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqll7dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3sUQAGQZPt701GEaChO61xA9ZxHN\nFDO0DYA/X1+PGvmgt06Jogqpniz16jEISKK/ITLwhiL99IozP5OcACBSCKeNS5B4\nNt86M13g6GSZD6CXOzPQZXarPZrD17e44wu0rstky+CDGs6y37aClOwjVEr8Zy49\ndy7Q2qpuMrWQFq5S2seOfgfimqMW6m4oeRXnFQ52NOCyH2K/WqPTgkC7hYuHrj14\nB6CxZEctuRvPE6iyElp5FsX9OZnmePdmNhC8zAXnKIzdPLnYPzBQ3etv7J/e2iki\nzPQJXY9GZLWxRQYYCA8UgHenehRVZmbpjT5i3Sm1oMMzYU+oQD5lRtseS1WOp0C7\nquNKAD6bSqcw325Ont1lDesKy9sxeBHDMypjtF91MmwzbV463u0y1ETyE6VeucRk\nUvtwHwSqu5iXbB0UZwmC0JRlKAYLBzZJYZh68xZ1whwM0gkYVN/9wcjymXLrVnp6\nyXUaW5HKSMXGK3ZwVNk4fGIAHx3dOUzcZFqzMNVWBgkZU897u8ojvTGA7ipO8MY7\nACjO84huGyoRggGFw+Z97INjxNcYkGPNWI5WrMZp9XTfff6m9OTSq2mU47zcXD3o\nOtuCUq1Sja9tkV4wZxm71+HzAwcOSjSffk1t2ujL28/DiyTbmM81Y3LpT6Ct+T3u\nstYvmw+7U4f/Rt6qAhqg\n=EzQZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:13:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGQyZDNkOGIwMmJkNzFmODI0NTQzODM0ZmI4ODg5NTI5Y2NjNzAzNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/10fa4f62fa05536743beb2ba63958be479f34c50","sha":"10fa4f62fa05536743beb2ba63958be479f34c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/10fa4f62fa05536743beb2ba63958be479f34c50"}],"sha":"d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/d2d3d8b02bd71f824543834fb8889529ccc70377"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/202644253?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sukhmanpreetkaur18","id":202644253,"login":"Sukhmanpreetkaur18","node_id":"U_kgDODBQbHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/10fa4f62fa05536743beb2ba63958be479f34c50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:10:08Z","email":"jasmeetkaurchwl@gmail.com","name":"Sukhmanpreet Kaur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:10:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Interactive Vendor Bidding Escrow Slashing with Multi… (#5470)\n\n### 📝 Description\nThis PR implements a comprehensive escrow slashing system with\nmulti-modal oracle consensus combining IoT temperature logs, computer\nvision, and time verification. The system ensures vendors are only paid\nwhen ALL three conditions are met: (1) on-time delivery, (2) temperature\n> 140°F, AND (3) food structural integrity score > 90.\n\n### 🚀 Features Added\n\n#### 1. Escrow Contract Models (400+ lines)\n- **EscrowContract**: Full escrow contract with all conditions\n- **EscrowStatus**: Pending, Active, Completed, Disputed, Slashed,\nRefunded\n- **TemperatureReading**: IoT temperature sensor data\n- **VisionAnalysis**: Computer vision food integrity analysis\n- **TimeVerification**: Delivery time validation\n- **OracleConsensus**: Multi-modal consensus result\n- **EscrowSlashEvent**: Slash event tracking\n- **EscrowTransaction**: Transaction history\n\n#### 2. Temperature Oracle (300+ lines)\n- **Validation**: Check temperature against threshold (140°F)\n- **Tolerance**: ±5°F tolerance for margin of error\n- **Stability**: Check temperature consistency over time\n- **Batch Validation**: Validate multiple readings\n- **Sensor Integration**: IoT sensor data processing\n\n#### 3. Vision Oracle (600+ lines)\n- **Food Integrity Classification**: Intact, Slightly Damaged,\nModerately Damaged, Severely Damaged, Destroyed\n- **Confidence Scoring**: 0-1 confidence in classification\n- **Integrity Score**: 0-100 structural integrity score\n- **Damage Detection**: Detect and classify damage types\n- **Damage Severity**: Minimal, Moderate, Severe, Critical\n- **Batch Analysis**: Process multiple images\n- **Image Validation**: Validate image quality\n\n#### 4. Time Oracle (300+ lines)\n- **Delivery Validation**: Check on-time delivery\n- **Delay Calculation**: Calculate delay in minutes\n- **Penalty Calculation**: Calculate delay penalties\n- **Time Window**: Validate within acceptable window\n- **Grace Period**: Configurable grace period\n\n#### 5. Consensus Oracle (500+ lines)\n- **Multi-modal Consensus**: ALL three oracles must approve\n- **Status Aggregation**: Combine individual oracle statuses\n- **Rejection Reasons**: Detailed rejection reasons\n- **Manual Review**: Flag for manual review when needed\n- **Simulation**: Simulate consensus scenarios\n- **Statistics**: Track approval/rejection rates\n\n#### 6. Escrow Smart Contract Integration (500+ lines)\n- **Contract Creation**: Create and activate escrow contracts\n- **Fund Release**: Release funds when all oracles approve\n- **Fund Slashing**: Slash funds when any oracle rejects\n- **Transaction Tracking**: Track all transactions\n- **Slash Events**: Record all slash events\n- **Statistics**: Contract statistics\n\n#### 7. API Endpoints (400+ lines)\n| Endpoint | Method | Description |\n|----------|--------|-------------|\n| `/api/escrow/contract` | POST | Create escrow contract |\n| `/api/escrow/contract/{id}/activate` | POST | Activate contract |\n| `/api/escrow/contract/{id}/evaluate` | POST | Evaluate with oracles |\n| `/api/escrow/contract/{id}` | GET | Get contract details |\n| `/api/escrow/contracts/vendor/{id}` | GET | Get vendor contracts |\n| `/api/escrow/contracts/client/{id}` | GET | Get client contracts |\n| `/api/escrow/consensus/simulate` | POST | Simulate consensus |\n| `/api/escrow/statistics` | GET | Get statistics |\n\n\nfixes #5643\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added escrow contract management, including creation, activation,\nevaluation, lookup, and statistics.\n* Added automated validation of delivery temperature, timing, and\nproduct integrity from images.\n  * Added consensus-based fund release when all validation checks pass.\n* Added protection against failed conditions through escrow slashing and\nrecorded evidence.\n  * Added consensus simulation and reporting capabilities.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\nfixes #5463","tree":{"sha":"ae8e5412a5ad3402d1982f4a5390c80e0691a212","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/ae8e5412a5ad3402d1982f4a5390c80e0691a212"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/10fa4f62fa05536743beb2ba63958be479f34c50","verification":{"payload":"tree ae8e5412a5ad3402d1982f4a5390c80e0691a212\nparent 5580267a842f6199c895094125a4fcd8ee64b099\nauthor Sukhmanpreet Kaur <jasmeetkaurchwl@gmail.com> 1788239408 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788239408 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement Interactive Vendor Bidding Escrow Slashing with Multi… (#5470)\n\n### 📝 Description\nThis PR implements a comprehensive escrow slashing system with\nmulti-modal oracle consensus combining IoT temperature logs,