acy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/annukumar123","id":220594134,"login":"annukumar123","node_id":"U_kgDODSX_1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/annukumar123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/5f60cb50cce0c716ceb5f334338836554015942f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T04:05:51Z","email":"annu83175@gmail.com","name":"Annu Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T04:05:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(safety): build interactive event layout evacuation bottleneck simulator (#4815) (#5437)\n\n### **Overview & Summary**\nCloses #4815 by building an Interactive \"Event Layout\" Evacuation\nBottleneck Simulator. Integrates a particle flocking simulation engine\ninto the Venue Canvas editor, spawning $N$ particles (`max_capacity`)\nmoving towards exits. Calculates doorway congestion densities\n(persons/foot); if thresholds are breached, highlights the doorway in\nflashing red (`\"CRITICAL BOTTLENECK DETECTED\"`), withholding Fire\nMarshal event approval until secondary exits are provided.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Changes**\n* **Database Schema Migration & Stored Procedure**: Created\n`supabase/migrations/20260896000000_create_evacuation_simulations.sql`\nestablishing `venue_evacuation_simulations` and\n`record_evacuation_simulation_run` RPC procedure.\n* **Evacuation Simulator Module**: Created\n`src/lib/evacuationSimulator.ts` providing `spawnCrowdParticles` and\n`stepEvacuationSimulation`.\n* **Automated Unit Tests**: Created\n`src/lib/evacuationSimulator.test.ts` testing capacity particle\nspawning, critical bottleneck density detection, and exit node\nevacuation mechanics.\n\n---\n\n### **Linked Issues**\n* /Closes #4815\n* /Resolves #4815\n* /Fixes #4815\n\n---\n\n### **Testing & Verification**\nRan `npx vitest run src/lib/evacuationSimulator.test.ts`:\n* ✅ `spawns particles equal to max_capacity within room boundaries`\n(Passed)\n* ✅ `detects CRITICAL BOTTLENECK when exit doorway density exceeds\nthreshold` (Passed)\n* ✅ `evacuates particles when they reach exit node coordinates` (Passed)","tree":{"sha":"af7e8e4f246e4a6915b3ef1265ff143b58b57318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/af7e8e4f246e4a6915b3ef1265ff143b58b57318"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/5f60cb50cce0c716ceb5f334338836554015942f","verification":{"payload":"tree af7e8e4f246e4a6915b3ef1265ff143b58b57318\nparent 79ab60982525fa1fc8ee0af759fb8b76d767c887\nauthor Annu Kumar <annu83175@gmail.com> 1788235551 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788235551 +0530\n\nfeat(safety): build interactive event layout evacuation bottleneck simulator (#4815) (#5437)\n\n### **Overview & Summary**\nCloses #4815 by building an Interactive \"Event Layout\" Evacuation\nBottleneck Simulator. Integrates a particle flocking simulation engine\ninto the Venue Canvas editor, spawning $N$ particles (`max_capacity`)\nmoving towards exits. Calculates doorway congestion densities\n(persons/foot); if thresholds are breached, highlights the doorway in\nflashing red (`\"CRITICAL BOTTLENECK DETECTED\"`), withholding Fire\nMarshal event approval until secondary exits are provided.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Changes**\n* **Database Schema Migration & Stored Procedure**: Created\n`supabase/migrations/20260896000000_create_evacuation_simulations.sql`\nestablishing `venue_evacuation_simulations` and\n`record_evacuation_simulation_run` RPC procedure.\n* **Evacuation Simulator Module**: Created\n`src/lib/evacuationSimulator.ts` providing `spawnCrowdParticles` and\n`stepEvacuationSimulation`.\n* **Automated Unit Tests**: Created\n`src/lib/evacuationSimulator.test.ts` testing capacity particle\nspawning, critical bottleneck density detection, and exit node\nevacuation mechanics.\n\n---\n\n### **Linked Issues**\n* /Closes #4815\n* /Resolves #4815\n* /Fixes #4815\n\n---\n\n### **Testing & Verification**\nRan `npx vitest run src/lib/evacuationSimulator.test.ts`:\n* ✅ `spawns particles equal to max_capacity within room boundaries`\n(Passed)\n* ✅ `detects CRITICAL BOTTLENECK when exit doorway density exceeds\nthreshold` (Passed)\n* ✅ `evacuates particles when they reach exit node coordinates` (Passed)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlk8fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAybgQAGDQilbFaCqMwcfgTRwh3u8W\nWbeCcf+Bq6F+4+NJeurjReYeMJRcy4bFF8DBp9AfmMDnU75J3GhcWBT6li3icmIv\nKRN2KvBwiid55xOVOQU4Adk+Ri+vr/WXhpXaBFRrI2RaB+Xmjyc+D4T9W+x+x/ju\ncPChQ+lobk9t2n1FwsncOACl1oPG2EN8Tzg41gXvepzz9FJw7v8mevwj/o53lcJX\nEz+wSbzpaqeu4ZAWfdj5ak6ixsHmxr+5Axpru8GGbDL93L83fmij4yg/uGf3jGHx\nVwNXZCjSOyqp+hPgTd4/rboIIGm/jWQN9cFdCoW/6F+u/2tzTL+qbDKv3uGAh6Q3\nVAAkBdjtPINKtxFI8gxNC5Z/ipgM7rU6OyZEicGW55VzulD+UuKZnLqv4x4m1+e/\neS5z4eIKjGe/5Dxr9WZCqRT3T5K7evxDAEPAu4ph2SXotaLRrjZc3pnxESh84Gzr\nmRT8npeVt7dknnUIyJBHOEepaxwRRXj5KO3Adj9iE3rm6IKPhtdD9ErQgP9EOhnB\n1SA/uzhicd6XO/OdaXMUQEbnUOKi1iZUuCSbyoV1/y+sFQ1DOWkqWHwA9H4Oqp/P\n9wKESqwvRJcrCU47e7rLbTx/6AyKEiucakgWCvlEj3scTLd/Z0i4rDnGk8a4PauV\nnUAPp1RgM4XN7PWtkDeP\n=KcWz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T04:05:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/5f60cb50cce0c716ceb5f334338836554015942f","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDVmNjBjYjUwY2NlMGM3MTZjZWI1ZjMzNDMzODgzNjU1NDAxNTk0MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/79ab60982525fa1fc8ee0af759fb8b76d767c887","sha":"79ab60982525fa1fc8ee0af759fb8b76d767c887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/79ab60982525fa1fc8ee0af759fb8b76d767c887"}],"sha":"5f60cb50cce0c716ceb5f334338836554015942f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/5f60cb50cce0c716ceb5f334338836554015942f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/202644253?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sukhmanpreetkaur18","id":202644253,"login":"Sukhmanpreetkaur18","node_id":"U_kgDODBQbHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sukhmanpreetkaur18","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/79ab60982525fa1fc8ee0af759fb8b76d767c887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T03:54:50Z","email":"jasmeetkaurchwl@gmail.com","name":"Sukhmanpreet Kaur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T03:54:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Proof-of-Skill (PoS) Merkle Trees for blockchain-veri… (#5436)\n\n### 📝 Description\nThis PR implements a complete Proof-of-Skill (PoS) system that\ncryptographically verifies technical skills by hashing GitHub Classroom\nactivity into immutable Merkle Trees anchored to the Polygon blockchain.\nThis eliminates resume fraud by providing verifiable proof of actual\ncoding ability.\n\n### 🚀 Features Added\n\n#### 1. AST Hashing System (600+ lines)\n- **Multi-Language Support**: Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, C++,\nRust\n- **AST Parsing**: Extracts Abstract Syntax Trees from code\n- **Code Normalization**: Language-specific normalization for consistent\nhashing\n- **Feature Extraction**: Node count, complexity, function count, class\ncount\n- **File Hashing**: Hash individual files and entire repositories\n- **Combined Hashing**: Generate a single hash for multiple files\n\n#### 2. Merkle Tree Implementation (700+ lines)\n- **Tree Building**: Build Merkle trees from leaf data\n- **Proof Generation**: Generate Merkle proofs for any leaf\n- **Proof Verification**: Verify Merkle proofs\n- **Batch Verification**: Verify multiple proofs at once\n- **Tree Statistics**: Get tree depth, node count, leaf count\n- **JSON Export**: Export tree data as JSON\n\n#### 3. Blockchain Client (1000+ lines)\n- **Multi-Chain Support**: Polygon, Ethereum, BSC, Arbitrum, Optimism\n- **RPC Connection**: Web3 integration with automatic middleware\n- **Smart Contract Interaction**: Store and verify Merkle roots\n- **Transaction Management**: Anchor, verify, and revoke Merkle roots\n- **Gas Estimation**: Calculate transaction costs\n- **Balance Checking**: Get account balances\n- **Contract Deployment**: Deploy Merkle root storage contracts\n\n#### 4. Proof-of-Skill Service (800+ lines)\n- **Code Verification**: Hash code and generate Merkle proofs\n- **Proof Management**: Create, store, and verify skill proofs\n- **User Skills**: Get verified skills for a user\n- **Skill Badges**: Generate cryptographically verified skill badges\n- **Proof Revocation**: Revoke skill proofs\n- **Verification Reports**: Generate comprehensive reports\n- **Statistics**: Track verification success rates\n\n#### 5. API Endpoints (500+ lines)\n| Endpoint | Method | Description |\n|----------|--------|-------------|\n| `/api/pos/verify` | POST | Verify a skill |\n| `/api/pos/verify/{proof_id}` | GET | Verify a proof |\n| `/api/pos/proofs/{proof_id}` | GET | Get proof details |\n| `/api/pos/user/{user_id}/skills` | GET | Get user skills |\n| `/api/pos/user/{user_id}/badge/{skill_name}` | GET | Get skill badge |\n| `/api/pos/revoke/{proof_id}` | POST | Revoke a proof |\n| `/api/pos/stats` | GET | Get statistics |\n| `/api/pos/merkle-tree/{proof_id}` | GET | Get Merkle tree |\n| `/api/pos/report/{user_id}` | GET | Generate report |\n| `/api/pos/chains` | GET | Get supported chains |\n| `/api/pos/deploy-contract` | POST | Deploy contract |\n\n\nfixes #5356\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added Proof-of-Skill verification for code and repositories.\n* Added skill proofs, verification badges, reports, statistics, and\nrevocation.\n  * Added Merkle-tree-based proof generation and validation.\n* Added blockchain anchoring and verification across supported networks.\n* Added APIs to retrieve user skills, badges, proof details, and\nverification data.\n  * Added support for hashing code in multiple programming languages.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"f65b74cb619f8685e07baf04fe96644685974119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/f65b74cb619f8685e07baf04fe96644685974119"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/79ab60982525fa1fc8ee0af759fb8b76d767c887","verification":{"payload":"tree f65b74cb619f8685e07baf04fe96644685974119\nparent ae377fd9ab3856bf1cb8b79794b6df3ab74081fe\nauthor Sukhmanpreet Kaur <jasmeetkaurchwl@gmail.com> 1788234890 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788234890 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement Proof-of-Skill (PoS) Merkle Trees for blockchain-veri… (#5436)\n\n### 📝 Description\nThis PR implements a complete Proof-of-Skill (PoS) system that\ncryptographically verifies technical skills by hashing GitHub Classroom\nactivity into immutable Merkle Trees anchored to the Polygon blockchain.\nThis eliminates resume fraud by providing verifiable proof of actual\ncoding ability.\n\n### 🚀 Features Added\n\n#### 1. AST Hashing System (600+ lines)\n- **Multi-Language Support**: Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, C++,\nRust\n- **AST Parsing**: Extracts Abstract Syntax Trees from code\n- **Code Normalization**: Language-specific normalization for consistent\nhashing\n- **Feature Extraction**: Node count, complexity, function count, class\ncount\n- **File Hashing**: Hash individual files and entire repositories\n- **Combined Hashing**: Generate a single hash for multiple files\n\n#### 2. Merkle Tree Implementation (700+ lines)\n- **Tree Building**: Build Merkle trees from leaf data\n- **Proof Generation**: Generate Merkle proofs for any leaf\n- **Proof Verification**: Verify Merkle proofs\n- **Batch Verification**: Verify multiple proofs at once\n- **Tree Statistics**: Get tree depth, node count, leaf count\n- **JSON Export**: Export tree data as JSON\n\n#### 3. Blockchain Client (1000+ lines)\n- **Multi-Chain Support**: Polygon, Ethereum, BSC, Arbitrum, Optimism\n- **RPC Connection**: Web3 integration with automatic middleware\n- **Smart Contract Interaction**: Store and verify Merkle roots\n- **Transaction Management**: Anchor, verify, and revoke Merkle roots\n- **Gas Estimation**: Calculate transaction costs\n- **Balance Checking**: Get account balances\n- **Contract Deployment**: Deploy Merkle root storage contracts\n\n#### 4. Proof-of-Skill Service (800+ lines)\n- **Code Verification**: Hash code and generate Merkle proofs\n- **Proof Management**: Create, store, and verify skill proofs\n- **User Skills**: Get verified skills for a user\n- **Skill Badges**: Generate cryptographically verified skill badges\n- **Proof Revocation**: Revoke skill proofs\n- **Verification Reports**: Generate comprehensive reports\n- **Statistics**: Track verification success rates\n\n#### 5. API Endpoints (500+ lines)\n| Endpoint | Method | Description |\n|----------|--------|-------------|\n| `/api/pos/verify` | POST | Verify a skill |\n| `/api/pos/verify/{proof_id}` | GET | Verify a proof |\n| `/api/pos/proofs/{proof_id}` | GET | Get proof details |\n| `/api/pos/user/{user_id}/skills` | GET | Get user skills |\n| `/api/pos/user/{user_id}/badge/{skill_name}` | GET | Get skill badge |\n| `/api/pos/revoke/{proof_id}` | POST | Revoke a proof |\n| `/api/pos/stats` | GET | Get statistics |\n| `/api/pos/merkle-tree/{proof_id}` | GET | Get Merkle tree |\n| `/api/pos/report/{user_id}` | GET | Generate report |\n| `/api/pos/chains` | GET | Get supported chains |\n| `/api/pos/deploy-contract` | POST | Deploy contract |\n\n\nfixes #5356\n\n<!-- 