Connect/commits/fbff457bf4dd5aae23b2ca42c6147efdcebf02a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:49:59Z","email":"sushmitakoti661@gmail.com","name":"Sushmita K"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:49:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(telepresence): implement dynamic alumni speaker holographic 3D r… (#5433)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements a real-time volumetric 3D video and holographic telepresence\nrendering pipeline for keynote presentations (Issue #5358).\n\nThis system captures real-time 3D point cloud data of a speaker (e.g.,\nvia iPhone LiDAR/TrueDepth or stereoscopic camera array), compresses and\nstreams the volumetric data over low-latency WebRTC `RTCDataChannel`\nconnections, and renders a life-size 3D hologram of the speaker on an\ninvisible stage HoloGauze projection mesh using Three.js / WebGL.\n\nKey additions include:\n* **WebRTC Signaling & Stream Management (`hologramWebRTCService.js`):**\nHandles room creation, SDP offer/answer exchanges, ICE candidate\nrelaying, 16-bit coordinate quantization packing for 25,000-point\nframes, and live bandwidth/latency telemetry.\n* **Hologram REST API (`hologramController.js`):** Exposes session\ncreation (`POST /api/hologram/session/create`), signaling endpoints\n(`POST /api/hologram/signal`), and room status tracking (`GET\n/api/hologram/session/:sessionId`).\n* **Holographic Stage & Telemetry UI (`HolographicTelepresence.tsx`):**\nInteractive Three.js WebGL venue renderer featuring HoloGauze mesh\nprojections, customizable GLSL holographic shaders (scanlines,\ncyan/magenta Fresnel rim glow, chromatic jitter), stage camera presets,\nand real-time performance HUD readouts.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5358\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed.\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n### Test Details:\n* **Automated Integration Test Suite\n(`backend/services/hologramPipeline.test.js`):** Executed `node\nbackend/services/hologramPipeline.test.js` with **7/7 tests passing**\n(verifying WebRTC room creation, point cloud packing/unpacking routines,\nand API endpoints).\n* **TypeScript Compilation:** Typechecked\n`components/HolographicTelepresence.tsx` with `npx tsc` with **0\nerrors**.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nDetailed visual interaction states, component layouts, shader controls,\nand test logs are documented in `walkthrough.md`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added an interactive holographic telepresence experience with animated\n3D speaker visuals.\n- Added venue, capture, and split-view modes with camera presets and\norbit controls.\n- Added controls for walking, scanlines, visual effects, and screen\nopacity.\n- Added session management, WebRTC signaling, telemetry, and 3D\npoint-cloud streaming support.\n  - Added a default keynote session for demonstration purposes.\n\n- **Tests**\n- Added coverage for session creation, signaling, telemetry, point-cloud\nprocessing, REST handlers, and failure handling.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"ae0a34547417b6d9914264a2a2bf9ecb7d27d423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/ae0a34547417b6d9914264a2a2bf9ecb7d27d423"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/fbff457bf4dd5aae23b2ca42c6147efdcebf02a2","verification":{"payload":"tree ae0a34547417b6d9914264a2a2bf9ecb7d27d423\nparent 373c9a627da31eb07e47b1944f7e37401db57276\nauthor Sushmita K <sushmitakoti661@gmail.com> 1788202199 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788202199 +0530\n\nfeat(telepresence): implement dynamic alumni speaker holographic 3D r… (#5433)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements a real-time volumetric 3D video and holographic telepresence\nrendering pipeline for keynote presentations (Issue #5358).\n\nThis system captures real-time 3D point cloud data of a speaker (e.g.,\nvia iPhone LiDAR/TrueDepth or stereoscopic camera array), compresses and\nstreams the volumetric data over low-latency WebRTC `RTCDataChannel`\nconnections, and renders a life-size 3D hologram of the speaker on an\ninvisible stage HoloGauze projection mesh using Three.js / WebGL.\n\nKey additions include:\n* **WebRTC Signaling & Stream Management (`hologramWebRTCService.js`):**\nHandles room creation, SDP offer/answer exchanges, ICE candidate\nrelaying, 16-bit coordinate quantization packing for 25,000-point\nframes, and live bandwidth/latency telemetry.\n* **Hologram REST API (`hologramController.js`):** Exposes session\ncreation (`POST /api/hologram/session/create`), signaling endpoints\n(`POST /api/hologram/signal`), and room status tracking (`GET\n/api/hologram/session/:sessionId`).\n* **Holographic Stage & Telemetry UI (`HolographicTelepresence.tsx`):**\nInteractive Three.js WebGL venue renderer featuring HoloGauze mesh\nprojections, customizable GLSL holographic shaders (scanlines,\ncyan/magenta Fresnel rim glow, chromatic jitter), stage camera presets,\nand real-time performance HUD readouts.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5358\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed.\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n### Test Details:\n* **Automated Integration Test Suite\n(`backend/services/hologramPipeline.test.js`):** Executed `node\nbackend/services/hologramPipeline.test.js` with **7/7 tests passing**\n(verifying WebRTC room creation, point cloud packing/unpacking routines,\nand API endpoints).\n* **TypeScript Compilation:** Typechecked\n`components/HolographicTelepresence.tsx` with `npx tsc` with **0\nerrors**.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nDetailed visual interaction states, component layouts, shader controls,\nand test logs are documented in `walkthrough.md`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added an interactive holographic telepresence experience with animated\n3D speaker visuals.\n- Added venue, capture, and split-view modes with camera presets and\norbit controls.\n- Added controls for walking, scanlines, visual effects, and screen\nopacity.\n- Added session management, WebRTC signaling, telemetry, and 3D\npoint-cloud streaming support.\n  - Added a default keynote session for demonstration purposes.\n\n- **Tests**\n- Added coverage for session creation, signaling, telemetry, point-cloud\nprocessing, REST handlers, and failure handling.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlczXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8PQQAJ1qbB/jgAK4KkbKRjcKhzD2\n9bXO8J4tDtJfF9Y96RbPijS27Bf+kK8vaTgS8InbrQz/LjSuMIPuEQ+Kx4CSx/cb\nWmdZSfyyzM/L2Wu2IjfEOgm86LNyYMgWGrn4JhOBsYS5tD/apMsVYz07psqG+WDZ\nqzARxgnYx34sDbbNNE98gxq7mfjztXHsjIN21S6Qe4J3oyZ2uEYaOB1GjK968hJB\n/7EB3sXT9k/UQG8AmWbUZuY5iqDO/iBua2ssHA1NZblXEeotd2cj9nvEy2JCTbyB\nQ8OK4ZCPjh7dVwIcXDBatPpAEL+qJ0NB3fpFSeK8+um0cnXtDQzF0MUh5rqTucl2\nBt7DgEfHMyXiMzLacg0n5AqdFZYBgij5iSDp0iHHIYsBAocUkC8sb9Jtw0atlVAA\nOP3V5XfbSIbPAkivZE/LNf7LqX