31T17:36:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"security: implement dynamic ML-WAF honeypot trap with automated AWS e… (#5424)\n\n…dge block rules #5293\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nProvide a brief description of the changes introduced in this pull\nrequest.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed.\n\n- [ ] Tested locally\n- [ ] Existing functionality verified\n- [ ] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nIf applicable, add screenshots of the changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [ ] No unnecessary files included\n- [ ] Changes have been tested\n- [ ] Ready for review\n## Description\nImplements an automated ML-driven Web Application Firewall (WAF) Honey\nPot trap designed to stop highly adaptive ticket-scraping networks. When\nan entity hits the hidden \"Early Bird\" link, the application extracts\nstructural TCP/TLS telemetry profiles and dynamically provisions IP\nrestriction parameters at the AWS network edge.\n\n## Changes\n- Created `waf_honeypot.py` implementing header fingerprinting\nextraction rules.\n- Integrated `boto3` client handlers to update global AWS WAF IPSet\nrulesets dynamically.\n- Formulated isolated validation tests checking edge blocking triggers\nfor suspicious endpoints.\n\nCloses #5293","tree":{"sha":"43637f2505aef913e66df73b01a623b7a26ae203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/43637f2505aef913e66df73b01a623b7a26ae203"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/18a9fcb036489db306f3dd948aebd4eda2b1d5e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 43637f2505aef913e66df73b01a623b7a26ae203\nparent 5b2d5a9dd2e76cdf1e576647872aa79fcff4d40a\nauthor Milan <milanrathod5