applicable, add screenshots of the changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [ ] No unnecessary files included\n- [ ] Changes have been tested\n- [ ] Ready for review\n## Description\nImplements an automated real-time secondary audio track generator for\nVOD assets to assist visually impaired students. The service uploads\nvideo tracks to a multimodal AI engine to extract contextual visual\nshifts, compiles descriptions via AWS Polly neural text-to-speech, and\nsplices them back into an MP4 wrapper on a secondary audio track using\nan FFmpeg filter graph.\n\n## Changes\n- Created `audio_description_generator.py` integrating Google Gemini and\nAWS Polly clients.\n- Configured dynamic `ffmpeg` multi-channel delay shifting filters via\nexplicit subprocess executions.\n- Added comprehensive pipeline testing scripts using isolated mock\nframework mocks.\n\nCloses #5292","tree":{"sha":"35502e85a7bfdd456a9e15ad3e1070ff2879bc62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/35502e85a7bfdd456a9e15ad3e1070ff2879bc62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/5b2d5a9dd2e76cdf1e576647872aa79fcff4d40a","verification":{"payload":"tree 35502e85a7bfdd456a9e15ad3e1070ff2879bc62\nparent 9ffc30ed6892d3d3bb214f5364a01b7f0129549e\nauthor Milan <milanrathod5201@gmail.com> 1788197816 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788197816 +0530\n\nfeat: implement multimodal AI video description mapping with automate… (#5425)\n\n…d Polly TTS splicing #5292\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nProvide a brief description of the changes introduced in this pull\nrequest.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed.\n\n- [ ] Tested locally\n- [ ] Existing functionality verified\n- [ ] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nIf applicable, add screenshots of the changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [ ] No unnecessary files included\n- [ ] Changes have been tested\n- [ ] Ready for review\n## Description\nImplements an automated real-time secondary audio track generator for\nVOD assets to assist visually impaired students. The service uploads\nvideo tracks to a multimodal AI engine to extract contextual visual\nshifts, compiles descriptions via AWS Polly neural text-to-speech, and\nsplices them back into an MP4 wrapper on a secondary audio track using\nan FFmpeg filter graph.\n\n## Changes\n- Created `audio_description_generator.py` integrating Google Gemini and\nAWS Polly clients.\n- Configured dynamic `ffmpeg` multi-channel delay shifting filters via\nexplicit subprocess executions.\n- Added comprehensive pipeline testing scripts using isolated mock\nframework mocks.\n\nCloses #5292","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlbu4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeN8QADT9StCIBFWiZWeCrlB84wOJ\nz5dBF8076GpOiIxjQXciCcFUvjJaC4EWZfNxom0Joxt7xK4khqkCl2ZuFX4na99f\nhJ6KRzUuw6N/tCpUZwnU8VdVAfcDvylimrJ6xj/HpvVXV0dyRh+O6Btodf5UqIK5\nHKZ+eOuLoMt1KNIFKR+zAJwsHvayyQKpCCO088IVjKPI0exQzRCRfsj1f4aShB7G\nwqSMnh3ijP4aT74qEd8q/NY7V4ej4aucq+yZ3lzqjMTgyF6uAj5exb9mb7l0KBq3\nNKRQySJK86DSfFmd3w91G4+1/utdxwoLLrLGqmXxOG/pNXtSuL7lyFzLLguBdRHw\nXZsqRbDnK75T2oegfg2lVKvHQwhdjV/VM54iyI5BZhxn9OAYOCJ8EXfvepy7Uw9J\nn35e6B1LfVWzl/1HwUzrsRLSejtfSQEpcaqLhfpfAVnUDkweMZqQZiiX2KszayCS\nV3iyFJiGU1oqk0SGrvsmhD1VH1lFwiSvaEMTb+E1U9HmmC6PHWqjnYDqxJhGolMa\nxMH5YFiyo+8whW5CxGXvq/uUtNoNEVsePAbjxVVmk9NUHouFAeuVGR7m3qqOiNbG\n7sxiNk0FZH1OmZ6mPUj6lwiFmzWiULCtDHLflgBx/gRBcOrShkP5gBJxDZAnL4lJ\nxnYfs7gro7jDmjNmY0iS\n=olK9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T17:36:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1