307/CampusConnect/commits/24a0db0688966b333ae6e7bdae89e9f9260ae6da"}],"sha":"d7c599440bf2dc165aea3f79d0a49fd2843cb101","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/d7c599440bf2dc165aea3f79d0a49fd2843cb101"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265290994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Babin123456","id":265290994,"login":"Babin123456","node_id":"U_kgDOD9AE8g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/24a0db0688966b333ae6e7bdae89e9f9260ae6da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:47:15Z","email":"265290994+Babin123456@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Babin Bid"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:47:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Build Real-Time Dynamic Pricing Dutch Auction RL Yield Management Agent (#5419)\n\n# feat: Build Real-Time Dynamic Pricing Dutch Auction RL Yield\nManagement Agent (#5145)\n\n## Summary\nResolves #5145\n\nDeploys a Reinforcement Learning (RL) Yield Management AI Agent for\nDutch Auctions that dynamically manipulates the auction clock and ticket\npricing based on real-time purchase velocity streams\n(`Purchase_Velocity`), optimizing revenue extraction during high-demand\nbursts.\n\n## Problem\nLinear time-based Dutch auctions drop prices blindly at fixed intervals\n(e.g. $50 -> $49 -> $48). During high-demand events (e.g. headliner DJ\nperformance), 50 tickets sell out in 2 seconds at a discounted rate,\nleaving thousands of dollars in uncaptured willingness-to-pay on the\ntable.\n\n## Solution & Architecture\n- **Real-Time Velocity Stream Monitoring**: The RL agent ingests\nreal-time ticket purchase velocity (tickets / second) and inventory\nscarcity ratio.\n- **Dynamic Clock & Micro-Boost Manipulation**:\n- **High Demand Spike (>= 5 t/s)**: Autonomously pauses the downward\ndecay clock to let high-demand buyers settle at the higher price.\n- **Explosive Burst (>= 15 t/s)**: Triggers a hybrid Dutch/English\nauction response, micro-boosting the ticket price slightly upward back\ntoward peak demand.\n\n## Key Changes\n1. **RL Yield Management Agent Service\n(`src/services/dutchAuctionRlYieldAgent.ts`)**:\n- Evaluates auction state space `[purchaseVelocity, inventoryRatio,\ntimeRatio]`.\n- Computes actions `DECAY_PRICE_NORMAL`, `PAUSE_CLOCK`,\n`MICRO_BOOST_PRICE`, `STABILIZE_FLOOR`.\n   - Calculates Demand Elasticity Index and estimated revenue lift.\n- Includes full simulation benchmark comparing static linear Dutch\nauctions vs RL dynamic pricing.\n\n2. **Database Migration\n(`supabase/migrations/20280908000000_dynamic_dutch_auction_yield_agent.sql`)**:\n- Created `dutch_auctions`, `auction_velocity_metrics`, and\n`rl_agent_decisions` tables.\n- Added stored procedure `evaluate_auction_rl_yield_step` to execute\nreal-time RL decision steps in PostgreSQL.\n\n3. **React Dashboard\n(`src/components/auctions/DynamicDutchAuctionDashboard.tsx`)**:\n- Interactive UI displaying current price, real-time purchase velocity,\nelasticity index, price adjustment banner, demand velocity triggers, and\nrevenue lift benchmark.\n\n4. **Unit Tests\n(`src/components/auctions/DynamicDutchAuctionDashboard.test.tsx`)**:\n- Vitest suite testing velocity threshold triggers, clock pausing,\nhybrid micro-boost execution, revenue comparison benchmarks, and UI\ncomponent actions.\n\n## Tests\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/components/auctions/DynamicDutchAuctionDashboard.test.tsx","tree":{"sha":"77248fabdee4f38f28e65b2f3f004ac17cdbd744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/77248fabdee4f38f28e65b2f3f004ac17cdbd744"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/24a0db0688966b333ae6e7bdae89e9f9260ae6da","verification":{"payload":"tree 77248fabdee4f38f28e65b2f3f004ac17cdbd744\nparent 4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998\nauthor Babin Bid <265290994+Babin123456@users.noreply.github.com> 1788194835 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788194835 +0530\n\nfeat: Build Real-Time Dynamic Pricing Dutch Auction RL Yield Management Agent (#5419)\n\n# feat: Build Real-Time Dynamic Pricing Dutch Auction RL Yield\nManagement Agent (#5145)\n\n## Summary\nResolves #5145\n\nDeploys a Reinforcement Learning (RL) Yield Management AI Agent for\nDutch Auctions that dynamically manipulates the auction clock and ticket\npricing based on real-time purchase velocity streams\n(`Purchase_Velocity`), optimizing revenue extraction during high-demand\nbursts.\n\n## Problem\nLinear time-based Dutch auctions drop prices blindly at fixed intervals\n(e.g. $50 -> $49 -> $48). During high-demand events (e.g. headliner DJ\nperformance), 50 tickets sell out in 2 seconds at a discounted rate,\nleaving thousands of dollars in uncaptured willingness-to-pay on the\ntable.\n\n## Solution & Architecture\n- **Real-Time Velocity Stream Monitoring**: The RL agent ingests\nreal-time ticket purchase velocity (tickets / second) and inventory\nscarcity ratio.\n- **Dynamic Clock & Micro-Boost Manipulation**:\n- **High Demand Spike (>= 5 t/s)**: Autonomously pauses the downward\ndecay clock to let high-demand buyers settle at the higher price.\n- **Explosive Burst (>= 15 t/s)**: Triggers a hybrid Dutch/English\nauction response, micro-boosting the ticket price slightly upward back\ntoward peak demand.\n\n## Key Changes\n1. **RL Yield Management Agent Service\n(`src/services/dutchAuctionRlYieldAgent.ts`)**:\n- Evaluates auction state space `[purchaseVelocity, inventoryRatio,\ntimeRatio]`.\n- Computes actions `DECAY_PRICE_NORMAL`, `PAUSE_CLOCK`,\n`MICRO_BOOST_PRICE`, `STABILIZE_FLOOR`.\n   - Calculates Demand Elasticity Index and estimated revenue lift.\n- Includes full simulation benchmark comparing static linear Dutch\nauctions vs RL dynamic pricing.\n\n2. **Database Migration\n(`supabase/migrations/20280908000000_dynamic_dutch_auction_yield_agent.sql`)**:\n- Created `dutch_auctions`, `auction_velocity_metrics`, and\n`rl_agent_decisions` tables.\n- Added stored procedure `evaluate_auction_rl_yield_step` to execute\nreal-time RL decision steps in PostgreSQL.\n\n3. **React Dashboard\n(`src/components/auctions/DynamicDutchAuctionDashboard.tsx`)**:\n- Interactive UI displaying current price, real-time purchase velocity,\nelasticity index, price adjustment banner, demand velocity triggers, and\nrevenue lift benchmark.\n\n4. **Unit Tests\n(`src/components/auctions/DynamicDutchAuctionDashboard.test.tsx`)**:\n- Vitest suite testing velocity threshold triggers, clock pausing,\nhybrid micro-boost execution, revenue comparison benchmarks, and UI\ncomponent actions.\n\n## Tests\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/components/auctions/DynamicDutchAuctionDashboard.test.tsx","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlbATCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8U0QABZZ1Issh9kvoMFLOs2zq6w/\n8buOm4dutm4kzWVEl6vZ3tBbZBaBNJ3kayKIUjDZBHsShIBJVRqL+jJHgiBiTncr\n54WIZUXd/P84AzOQW9sghgR4984lNEf2noe7fyixUdaEDaCwGgZu3m1Xup3rQNe6\nAUz7yqpiUXGDxdIE2eegl1gezyjkjjbwAXfcA0On8DzNvtATy8loJ+rWRkPAS+0/\n0fiZwZ72Oepl36IOFZ+lkInVcy/T9L92FbEuDC2l+Xt1r2EouA5ibRiQrPO2Xkx9\nXaqzuUmgHagLu22Vr5vWGBozD+xU9Wh0iwXj/YUr5q4S/LmZxf9WBIf9+ipBK+nm\nd8KLQT1u3S3gKE2Kpj1jOumy7mFYGci+QIsoBzKTsuHmfny3oh4txP3kP3TYAwZL\nil81xr1cCava+NoH0s2GF0g0CuzjRPoyrnhNs9bHQUK1b1+RoeusRHRDzhSF+7Uu\ns8rzaADU1MDDjL2+sQQ6xHPbrsymEo8tdvZ2x/yOEE4Arm5KZfvvzf2G2O/t8KIj\n6aa5/1VOr0kgI+A+y/UDndM0cpkm00AMcT6SKORgR+nEyNpEFAe+2q9CFA04kjDm\ny/twNtX6u/bsoAE0ZUJayrVaXhRyslCvAACNLY2Sv+pvfsB5iBmCa4Od0q+LzRQp\nhaASTjtTY4WBqQNk8IxF\n=eCYO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T16:47:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/24a0db0688966b333ae6e7bdae89e9f9260ae6da","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDI0YTBkYjA2ODg5NjZiMzMzYWU2ZTdiZGFlODllOWY5MjYwYWU2ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998","sha":"4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998"}],"sha":"24a0db0688966b333ae6e7bdae89e9f9260ae6da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/24a0db0688966b333ae6e7bdae89e9f9260ae6da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265290994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Babin123456","id":265290994,"login":"Babin123456","node_id":"U_kgDOD9AE8g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:46:59Z","email":"265290994+Babin123456@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Babin Bid"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:46:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Automated Event Cancellation Decentralized Insurance Pool (#5418)\n\n# feat: Implement Automated Event Cancellation Decentralized Insurance\nPool (#5144)\n\n## Summary\nResolves #5144\n\nImplements an automated Decentralized Insurance Pool integrated with\nPrediction Market hedging (Polymarket CTF interface) to eliminate\ncatastrophe risk and prevent smart contract bankruptcy when correlated\nevent cancellation claims hit simultaneously (e.g. 50 clubs claiming\nrainouts at once).\n\n## Problem\nDecentralized insurance pools without dynamic external hedging\nmechanisms are vulnerable to catastrophic correlated failures. For\nexample, if a hurricane hits and 50 campus clubs claim rainout insurance\nsimultaneously ($100,000 total payout demand) against a $20,000 pool\nreserve, the smart contract goes bankrupt and clubs lose their payouts.\n\n## Solution & Architecture\n- **Polymarket Prediction Market Hedging**: When a policy is\nunderwritten (e.g. $100 premium for $5,000 payout), 90% of the premium\nis immediately deployed to buy \"YES\" shares on a Polymarket event\ncontract (e.g., *\"Will it rain > 1 inch in Austin on 2026-09-15?\"*).\n- **Correlated Risk Liquidity Inflow**: Traders worldwide bet \"NO\",\nproviding global external liquidity. If a catastrophe occurs, the smart\ncontract wins the bet, instantly liquidating the prediction market\npayout back into the liquidity pool to cover all 50 club claims.\n\n## Key Changes\n1. **Solidity Smart Contract\n(`contracts/EventCancellationInsurancePool.sol`)**:\n- Implemented `purchasePolicy` with automatic 90% premium deployment\ninto Polymarket CTF YES shares.\n- Implemented `processEventCancellationClaim` to redeem prediction\nmarket winnings into pool reserves before executing club payouts.\n- Added `getPoolMetrics` for reserve, hedged asset, and solvency ratio\ntracking.\n\n2. **Database Migration\n(`supabase/migrations/20280907000000_event_insurance_prediction_hedging.sql`)**:\n- Added `event_insurance_pools`, `event_insurance_policies`, and\n`prediction_market_positions` tables.\n- Added `underwrite_event_insurance_policy` and\n`execute_correlated_event_claim` RPC functions.\n\n3. **TypeScript Service\n(`src/services/eventInsuranceHedgingService.ts`)**:\n- Underwriting service, Polymarket position tracking, claim settlement\nengine, and `simulateMassCatastrophe` algorithm (testing 50 simultaneous\n$5,000 claims).\n\n4. **React Dashboard\n(`src/components/insurance/EventInsuranceHedgingDashboard.tsx`)**:\n- Visualizes pool reserve, Polymarket hedged liquidity, solvency ratio,\npolicy underwriting form, and an interactive **Catastrophe Hedge Test**\nsimulator.\n\n5. **Unit Tests\n(`src/components/insurance/EventInsuranceHedgingDashboard.test.tsx`)**:\n- Comprehensive Vitest suite verifying 90% capital allocation, 50-club\ncatastrophe solvency preservation, and UI components.\n\n## Tests\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/components/insurance/EventInsuranceHedgingDashboard.test.tsx","tree":{"sha":"344014fc67675ccb672ea9e2d1c96d5f5b712c3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/344014fc67675ccb672ea9e2d1c96d5f5b712c3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998","verification":{"payload":"tree 344014fc67675ccb672ea9e2d1c96d5f5b712c3c\nparent e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389\nauthor Babin Bid <265290994+Babin123456@users.noreply.github.com> 1788194819 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788194819 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement Automated Event Cancellation Decentralized Insurance Pool (#5418)\n\n# feat: Implement Automated Event Cancellation Decentralized Insurance\nPool (#5144)\n\n## Summary\nResolves #5144\n\nImplements an automated Decentralized Insurance Pool integrated with\nPrediction Market hedging (Polymarket CTF interface) to eliminate\ncatastrophe risk and prevent smart contract bankruptcy when correlated\nevent cancellation claims hit simultaneously (e.g. 50 clubs claiming\nrainouts at once).\n\n## Problem\nDecentralized insurance pools without dynamic external hedging\nmechanisms are vulnerable to catastrophic correlated failures. For\nexample, if a hurricane hits and 50 campus clubs claim rainout insurance\nsimultaneously ($100,000 total payout demand) against a $20,000 pool\nreserve, the smart contract goes bankrupt and clubs lose their payouts.\n\n## Solution & Architecture\n- **Polymarket Prediction Market Hedging**: When a policy is\nunderwritten (e.g. $100 premium for $5,000 payout), 90% of the premium\nis immediately deployed to buy \"YES\" shares on a Polymarket event\ncontract (e.g., *\"Will it rain > 1 inch in Austin on 2026-09-15?\"*).\n- **Correlated Risk Liquidity Inflow**: Traders worldwide bet \"NO\",\nproviding global external liquidity. If a catastrophe occurs, the smart\ncontract wins the bet, instantly liquidating the prediction market\npayout back into the liquidity pool to cover all 50 club claims.\n\n## Key Changes\n1. **Solidity Smart Contract\n(`contracts/EventCancellationInsurancePool.sol`)**:\n- Implemented `purchasePolicy` with automatic 90% premium deployment\ninto Polymarket CTF YES shares.\n- Implemented `processEventCancellationClaim` to redeem prediction\nmarket winnings into pool reserves before executing club payouts.\n- Added `getPoolMetrics` for reserve, hedged asset, and solvency ratio\ntracking.\n\n2. **Database Migration\n(`supabase/migrations/20280907000000_event_insurance_prediction_hedging.sql`)**:\n- Added `event_insurance_pools`, `event_insurance_policies`, and\n`prediction_market_positions` tables.\n- Added `underwrite_event_insurance_policy` and\n`execute_correlated_event_claim` RPC functions.\n\n3. **TypeScript Service\n(`src/services/eventInsuranceHedgingService.ts`)**:\n- Underwriting service, Polymarket position tracking, claim settlement\nengine, and `simulateMassCatastrophe` algorithm (testing 50 simultaneous\n$5,000 claims).\n\n4. **React Dashboard\n(`src/components/insurance/EventInsuranceHedgingDashboard.tsx`)**:\n- Visualizes pool reserve, Polymarket hedged liquidity, solvency ratio,\npolicy underwriting form, and an interactive **Catastrophe Hedge Test**\nsimulator.\n\n5. **Unit Tests\n(`src/components/insurance/EventInsuranceHedgingDashboard.test.tsx`)**:\n- Comprehensive Vitest suite verifying 90% capital allocation, 50-club\ncatastrophe solvency preservation, and UI components.\n\n## Tests\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/components/insurance/EventInsuranceHedgingDashboard.test.tsx","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlbADCR