hit1307/CampusConnect/commit/e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389","sha":"e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389"}],"sha":"4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/4922d2d94770c28d71ec28169165ac9e1ca86998"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233611462?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zainabhina05-png","id":233611462,"login":"zainabhina05-png","node_id":"U_kgDODeygxg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:09:27Z","email":"zainab.hina05@gmail.com","name":"Zaeb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:09:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement hash-based content screening for CSAM/NCII detection (Issue #5359) (#5417)\n\n## Summary\nImplements hash-based content screening for CSAM and non-consensual\nintimate imagery (NCII) detection before files are written to S3,\npreventing the initial distribution of illegal material and eliminating\nthe need for human moderators to view traumatic content.\n\n## Problem\nStandard content moderation requires humans to view the content, which\ntraumatizes moderators and fails to stop the initial distribution of\nillegal material. A deeply malicious user generates non-consensual\ndeepfake pornography of a female Club President and uploads it to the\nEvent Gallery. If this is distributed, it will cause catastrophic\npsychological harm and massive legal liability for the University.\n\n## Solution\nIntegrate specialized Deepfake/CSAM hash matching databases directly\ninto the upload pipeline:\n- Before any image or video is written to the S3 bucket, it is held in a\nsecure, ephemeral memory buffer\n- Generate a robust perceptual hash (e.g., PhotoDNA or a custom\nCNN-based hash) of the media\n- Query this hash against established industry databases (e.g., NCMEC\nfor CSAM, or StopNCII.org for non-consensual intimate imagery)\n- If a match is detected, instantly purge the buffer. The file NEVER\nhits the disk\n- Automatically freeze the user''s account, preserve their IP/telemetry\ndata, and generate a high-priority forensic report for Campus Police and\nfederal authorities\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `content_moderation_queue` table for upload screening workflow\nwith telemetry tracking\n- Created `content_hashes` table for perceptual hash storage (MD5,\nSHA256, pHash, dHash)\n- Created `forensic_reports` table for law enforcement reporting with\ncase tracking\n- Created `user_suspensions` table for account freezing with permanent\nsuspension support\n  - Added `create_moderation_queue_entry` RPC for queue management\n  - Added `store_content_hash` RPC for hash storage\n- Added `reject_content` RPC for content rejection with automatic\nforensic report generation\n  - Added `approve_content` RPC for approved content\n- Added `suspend_user` RPC for account freezing with permanent\nsuspension support\n  - Added `is_user_suspension` RPC for suspension status checking\n\n- **Edge Function**: `content-screening` function that:\n  - Receives file data in memory buffer (base64 encoded)\n- Generates perceptual hashes (MD5, SHA256 for integrity; pHash, dHash\nfor perceptual matching)\n  - Screens hashes against NCMEC database for CSAM detection\n- Screens hashes against StopNCII database for non-consensual intimate\nimagery detection\n  - Automatically rejects content and purges buffer if match detected\n- Automatically freezes user account (permanent for CSAM, temporary for\nNCII)\n- Generates forensic reports with IP telemetry, user agent, and match\ndetails\n  - Links forensic reports to user suspensions for audit trail\n\n- **Perceptual Hashing**:\n  - MD5 and SHA256 for basic integrity checks\n  - pHash (perceptual hash) placeholder for robust image matching\n  - dHash (difference hash) placeholder for faster image matching\n- Note: Production implementation should integrate with PhotoDNA API or\nCNN-based hashing for more accurate perceptual matching\n\n- **Database Integrations**:\n  - NCMEC API integration for CSAM hash matching\n- StopNCII API integration for non-consensual intimate imagery detection\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual review mode)\n\n- **Account Freezing**:\n  - Automatic permanent suspension for CSAM matches\n  - Automatic temporary suspension for NCII matches\n- Preserves IP address, user agent, and device fingerprint for forensic\nanalysis\n  - Links suspension to forensic report for legal documentation\n\n- **Forensic Reporting**:\n- Automatic report generation for critical violations (CSAM, NCII,\ndeepfake)\n  - Includes user telemetry (IP, user agent, device fingerprint)\n  - Includes content information (file name, size, type, hashes)\n  - Includes match details from database queries\n  - Tracks report submission to authorities (NCMEC, Campus Police, FBI)\n  - Case number tracking for legal follow-up\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `ContentModerationPanel` component for:\n  - Viewing moderation queue with screening status\n  - Viewing forensic reports with severity indicators\n  - Managing user suspensions with lift functionality\n  - Updating forensic reports with resolution notes\n  - Real-time status tracking (pending, screening, approved, rejected)\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP and Vitest test suites covering:\n  - Moderation queue creation and management\n  - Content hash generation and storage\n  - Content rejection with forensic report generation\n  - User suspension (temporary and permanent)\n  - Hash generation (MD5, SHA256)\n  - Hash matching logic\n  - Database match detection (NCMEC, StopNCII)\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. User attempts to upload image/video to event gallery\n2. File is held in memory buffer (not written to S3 yet)\n3. System generates perceptual hashes (MD5, SHA256, pHash, dHash)\n4. System screens hashes against NCMEC and StopNCII databases\n5. If no match found:\n   - Content approved\n   - File uploaded to S3\n   - Moderation queue entry marked as approved\n6. If match found:\n   - Buffer purged (file never hits disk)\n   - Content rejected\n   - User account frozen (permanent for CSAM, temporary for NCII)\n   - Forensic report generated with IP telemetry and match details\n   - Admin notified via ContentModerationPanel\n   - Legal counsel can review forensic report and submit to authorities\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `NCMEC_API_KEY` environment variable for CSAM database integration\n- Set `STOPNCII_API_KEY` environment variable for NCII database\nintegration\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual review mode)\n\n## Legal Compliance Benefits\n- **Zero Human Exposure**: Moderators never view illegal content\n- **Prevent Distribution**: Files purged before hitting disk\n- **Forensic Evidence**: IP telemetry preserved for law enforcement\n- **Automatic Reporting**: High-priority reports generated for\nauthorities\n- **Audit Trail**: Complete documentation of screening process\n- **Legal Protection**: University protected from liability through\nproactive screening\n\nCloses #5359\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e305b8e898d6cbf8bb0b727ca7ebea31e73fabfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/e305b8e898d6cbf8bb0b727ca7ebea31e73fabfd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389","verification":{"payload":"tree e305b8e898d6cbf8bb0b727ca7ebea31e73fabfd\nparent 1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6\nauthor Zaeb <zainab.hina05@gmail.com> 1788192567 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788192567 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement hash-based content screening for CSAM/NCII detection (Issue #5359) (#5417)\n\n## Summary\nImplements hash-based content screening for CSAM and non-consensual\nintimate imagery (NCII) detection before files are written to S3,\npreventing the initial distribution of illegal material and eliminating\nthe need for human moderators to view traumatic content.\n\n## Problem\nStandard content moderation requires humans to view the content, which\ntraumatizes moderators and fails to stop the initial distribution of\nillegal material. A deeply malicious user generates non-consensual\ndeepfake pornography of a female Club President and uploads it to the\nEvent Gallery. If this is distributed, it will cause catastrophic\npsychological harm and massive legal liability for the University.\n\n## Solution\nIntegrate specialized Deepfake/CSAM hash matching databases directly\ninto the upload pipeline:\n- Before any image or video is written to the S3 bucket, it is held in a\nsecure, ephemeral memory buffer\n- Generate a robust perceptual hash (e.g., PhotoDNA or a custom\nCNN-based hash) of the media\n- Query this hash against established industry databases (e.g., NCMEC\nfor CSAM, or StopNCII.org for non-consensual intimate imagery)\n- If a match is detected, instantly purge the buffer. The file NEVER\nhits the disk\n- Automatically freeze the user''s account, preserve their IP/telemetry\ndata, and generate a high-priority forensic report for Campus Police and\nfederal authorities\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `content_moderation_queue` table for upload screening workflow\nwith telemetry tracking\n- Created `content_hashes` table for perceptual hash storage (MD5,\nSHA256, pHash, dHash)\n- Created `forensic_reports` table for law enforcement reporting with\ncase tracking\n- Created `user_suspensions` table for account freezing with permanent\nsuspension support\n  - Added `create_moderation_queue_entry` RPC for queue management\n  - Added `store_content_hash` RPC for hash storage\n- Added `reject_content` RPC for content rejection with automatic\nforensic report generation\n  - Added `approve_content` RPC for approved content\n- Added `suspend_user` RPC for account freezing with permanent\nsuspension support\n  - Added `is_user_suspension` RPC for suspension status checking\n\n- **Edge Function**: `content-screening` function that:\n  - Receives file data in memory buffer (base64 encoded)\n- Generates perceptual hashes (MD5, SHA256 for integrity; pHash, dHash\nfor perceptual matching)\n  - Screens hashes against NCMEC database for CSAM detection\n- Screens hashes against StopNCII database for non-consensual intimate\nimagery detection\n  - Automatically rejects content and purges buffer if match detected\n- Automatically freezes user account (permanent for CSAM, temporary for\nNCII)\n- Generates forensic reports with IP telemetry, user agent, and match\ndetails\n  - Links forensic reports to user suspensions for audit trail\n\n- **Perceptual Hashing**:\n  - MD5 and SHA256 for basic integrity checks\n  - pHash (perceptual hash) placeholder for robust image matching\n  - dHash (difference hash) placeholder for faster image matching\n- Note: Production implementation should integrate with PhotoDNA API or\nCNN-based hashing for more accurate perceptual matching\n\n- **Database Integrations**:\n  - NCMEC API integration for CSAM hash matching\n- StopNCII API integration for non-consensual intimate imagery detection\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual review mode)\n\n- **Account Freezing**:\n  - Automatic permanent suspension for CSAM matches\n  - Automatic temporary suspension for NCII matches\n- Preserves IP address, user agent, and device fingerprint for forensic\nanalysis\n  - Links suspension to forensic report for legal documentation\n\n- **Forensic Reporting**:\n- Automatic report generation for critical violations (CSAM, NCII,\ndeepfake)\n  - Includes user telemetry (IP, user agent, device fingerprint)\n  - Includes content information (file name, size, type, hashes)\n  - Includes match details from database queries\n  - Tracks report submission to authorities (NCMEC, Campus Police, FBI)\n  - Case number tracking for legal follow-up\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `ContentModerationPanel` component for:\n  - Viewing moderation queue with screening status\n  - Viewing forensic reports with severity indicators\n  - Managing user suspensions with lift functionality\n  - Updating forensic reports with resolution notes\n  - Real-time status tracking (pending, screening, approved, rejected)\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP and Vitest test suites covering:\n  - Moderation queue creation and management\n  - Content hash generation and storage\n  - Content rejection with forensic report generation\n  - User suspension (temporary and permanent)\n  - Hash generation (MD5, SHA256)\n  - Hash matching logic\n  - Database match detection (NCMEC, StopNCII)\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. User attempts to upload image/video to event gallery\n2. File is held in memory buffer (not written to S3 yet)\n3. System generates perceptual hashes (MD5, SHA256, pHash, dHash)\n4. System screens hashes against NCMEC and StopNCII databases\n5. If no match found:\n   - Content approved\n   - File uploaded to S3\n   - Moderation queue entry marked as approved\n6. If match found:\n   - Buffer purged (file never hits disk)\n   - Content rejected\n   - User account frozen (permanent for CSAM, temporary for NCII)\n   - Forensic report generated with IP telemetry and match details\n   - Admin notified via ContentModerationPanel\n   - Legal counsel can review forensic report and submit to authorities\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `NCMEC_API_KEY` environment variable for CSAM database integration\n- Set `STOPNCII_API_KEY` environment variable for NCII database\nintegration\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual review mode)\n\n## Legal Compliance Benefits\n- **Zero Human Exposure**: Moderators never view illegal content\n- **Prevent Distribution**: Files purged before hitting disk\n- **Forensic Evidence**: IP telemetry preserved for law enforcement\n- **Automatic Reporting**: High-priority reports generated for\nauthorities\n- **Audit Trail**: Complete documentation of screening process\n- **Legal Protection**: University protected from liability through\nproactive screening\n\nCloses #5359\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlac3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAISEQAJA7WNPBzrMdnoESw2wj7+Oz\nsziYhqHpffygedPHvBG2E5W1jr7gy+9NSjOFM/YctVHIbkK7X9EK2WnwHKZw5Pd6\njHDUnElgcwiN+hksORn5VwEdMXBubCqVyl6nalXQ+bfrVxKc+CWitIYyzAOrgAH2\njEFebNI5/D6CqQ9be+21JKXLwZNN5mBw4mv5TjMvMAdVFJ4tdtedBzehuqN1vKcZ\ntzna61CAlO8KET9SztF6H1MVKPb91hue+ByLQig7mzSOOUioMC6KxJCB4kIQRpnt\nlC8OEY2WLA87CODHV65elh3RWOdcctTTut7p/TWzWVtAlmi9EIoiAzz5gWzmUyaz\n/Sfx1BJDUqTmaXCieRz5rQMadTqfHPVZ9ynHJHiLx0cx6RWydJb6gQwsNiaPLwBr\nzqN16xm4G1XBtHnyUpKdDDPLobN1AiKSrvdJpYmqJAkLwCVX7XlQBH9WnzXUpkL8\n8AUjWEsSo9sisd2nVIJezI4H3a1VUB88eXDP5VKNOuZg9jqsWAK0DJC7KkVrqRRM\nTBkIaC4B32h44cxuQqjDX4S5jYi/K7HjbiQMIYKMgyPjdvk4TlNCkqSzl3bWG2bm\nL3h1UyNqNxZnyj6PBTRe9jCDH+z+EadRLGdpqluFrZLsZr48SMFP5p+OcXZFyWuK\nZMAqIZYQAJ4d6Y+LJrIZ\n=v+P9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T16:09:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGU4YmIzMmZlNWMxMDBkOGZmYWM1MDQ0MTllZDFmYzU2ODE4NDIzODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6","sha":"1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6"}],"sha":"e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/e8bb32fe5c100d8ffac504419ed1fc5681842389"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265290994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Babin123456","id":265290994,"login":"Babin123456","node_id":"U_kgDOD9AE8g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Babin123456","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:07:38Z","email":"265290994+Babin123456@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Babin Bid"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:07:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: implement Zero-Knowledge Multi-Campus MAC Randomization Supporter (#5416)\n\nCloses #5143\n\n### Description\nResolves cross-institutional privacy leakage during Eduroam and\nfederated campus Wi-Fi roaming (Issue #5143). Standard federated\nidentity protocols (RADIUS / Eduroam) leak the user''s permanent identity\nand home institution to host network operators (e.g., logging every\nwebsite visited by a visiting student and attributing it to their\npermanent identity).\n\nThis PR introduces **Zero-Knowledge Identity Federation & Dynamic MAC\nRandomization**, enabling fully anonymous, cryptographically verifiable\nnetwork roaming across host university campuses.\n\n### Key Changes\n1. **Zero-Knowledge Proof Generator & Manager\n(`src/lib/network/zkFederatedMacManager.ts`)**:\n- `generateZkRoamingProof`: Generates a zero-knowledge proof proving\nvalid student credential ownership without disclosing student ID, name,\nor home institution.\n- `verifyZkRoamingProof`: Verifies Groth16 zk-SNARK proof statements at\nthe host university authentication server.\n- `createAnonymousMacSession`: Provisions dynamic isolated guest VLAN\nnetwork sessions bound to ephemeral, randomized MAC addresses.\n- `rotateAnonymousMacSession`: Allows dynamic on-demand MAC rotation\nwhile preserving active session state without tracking correlation.\n- `generateRandomLocallyAdministeredMac`: Generates RFC 7042 compliant\nlocally administered MAC addresses.\n\n2. **Types & Interfaces (`src/types/zkFederatedMac.ts`)**:\n- Data interfaces for ZK Trust Anchors, Proof Payloads, Nullifier\nHashes, and Anonymous RADIUS Session configurations.\n\n3. **Database Schema & RLS\n(`supabase/migrations/20280923000000_zk_federated_mac_randomization.sql`)**:\n- `zk_federation_trust_anchors`: Stores verified university commitment\nroots and public key parameters.\n- `zk_anonymous_mac_sessions`: Manages dynamic randomized MAC mappings\nand isolated VLAN IDs.\n- `zk_proof_audit_ledger`: Nullifier hash ledger preventing double-spend\n/ replay attacks without compromising user identity.\n\n4. **Host Authentication Edge Function\n(`supabase/functions/verify-zk-roaming-proof/index.ts`)**:\n- Edge function for host RADIUS servers to verify incoming ZKP payloads,\ncheck nullifiers against double-spending, and authorize dynamic MAC\nsessions.\n\n5. **UI Component\n(`src/components/network/ZkMacRandomizationPanel.tsx`)**:\n- User panel to toggle ZK anonymous network roaming, select target host\nuniversities, trigger dynamic MAC address rotations, and view session\ntelemetry isolation.\n\n6. **Unit Tests (`tests/zkFederatedMacRandomization.test.ts`)**:\n- Comprehensive unit test suite validating proof generation, host\nverification, nullifier double-spend rejection, MAC normalization, and\nsession lifecycle.\n\n### LOC Modifications\n- **Total LOC Added**: ~776 LOC across 6 files (Exceeds minimum\nrequirement of 350 LOC).\n\n### Verification\n- Executed unit test suite via Vitest:\n  ```bash\n  npx vitest run tests/zkFederatedMacRandomization.test.ts\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added anonymous cross-campus network roaming with zero-knowledge\nauthentication.\n* Added automatic locally administered MAC address randomization and\nsession rotation.\n* Added session details including expiration, isolated VLAN, and\nrotation history.\n  * Added host-campus verification and protection against proof replay.\n* Added support for managing trust anchors, active sessions, and session\nrevocation.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Added clear error handling for invalid credentials, expired proofs,\nmismatched campuses, and failed session operations.\n* **Tests**\n* Added coverage for roaming proofs, MAC generation, session lifecycle,\nrotation, revocation, and privacy settings.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"04cbed98ebd983587eb2f175e5d57f2184d74358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/04cbed98ebd983587eb2f175e5d57f2184d74358"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6","verification":{"payload":"tree 04cbed98ebd983587eb2f175e5d57f2184d74358\nparent a74bf48e77176f496f5aa41fa3cf934cdd1b38a4\nauthor Babin Bid <265290994+Babin123456@users.noreply.github.com> 1788192458 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788192458 +0530\n\nfeat: implement Zero-Knowledge Multi-Campus MAC Randomization Supporter (#5416)\n\nCloses #5143\n\n### Description\nResolves cross-institutional privacy leakage during Eduroam and\nfederated campus Wi-Fi roaming (Issue #5143). Standard federated\nidentity protocols (RADIUS / Eduroam) leak the user''s permanent identity\nand home institution to host network operators (e.g., logging every\nwebsite visited by a visiting student and attributing it to their\npermanent identity).\n\nThis PR introduces **Zero-Knowledge Identity Federation & Dynamic MAC\nRandomization**, enabling fully anonymous, cryptographically verifiable\nnetwork roaming across host university campuses.\n\n### Key Changes\n1. **Zero-Knowledge Proof Generator & Manager\n(`src/lib/network/zkFederatedMacManager.ts`)**:\n- `generateZkRoamingProof`: Generates a zero-knowledge proof proving\nvalid student credential ownership without disclosing student ID, name,\nor home institution.\n- `verifyZkRoamingProof`: Verifies Groth16 zk-SNARK proof statements at\nthe host university authentication server.\n- `createAnonymousMacSession`: Provisions dynamic isolated guest VLAN\nnetwork sessions bound to ephemeral, randomized MAC addresses.\n- `rotateAnonymousMacSession`: Allows dynamic on-demand MAC rotation\nwhile preserving active session state without tracking correlation.\n- `generateRandomLocallyAdministeredMac`: Generates RFC 7042 compliant\nlocally administered MAC addresses.\n\n2. **Types & Interfaces (`src/types/zkFederatedMac.ts`)**:\n- Data interfaces for ZK Trust Anchors, Proof Payloads, Nullifier\nHashes, and Anonymous RADIUS Session configurations.\n\n3. **Database Schema & RLS\n(`supabase/migrations/20280923000000_zk_federated_mac_randomization.sql`)**:\n- `zk_federation_trust_anchors`: Stores verified university commitment\nroots and public key parameters.\n- `zk_anonymous_mac_sessions`: Manages dynamic randomized MAC mappings\nand isolated VLAN IDs.\n- `zk_proof_audit_ledger`: Nullifier hash ledger preventing double-spend\n/ replay attacks without compromising user identity.\n\n4. **Host Authentication Edge Function\n(`supabase/functions/verify-zk-roaming-proof/index.ts`)**:\n- Edge function for host RADIUS servers to verify incoming ZKP payloads,\ncheck nullifiers against double-spending, and authorize dynamic MAC\nsessions.\n\n5. **UI Component\n(`src/components/network/ZkMacRandomizationPanel.tsx`)**:\n- User panel to toggle ZK anonymous network roaming, select target host\nuniversities, trigger dynamic MAC address rotations, and view session\ntelemetry isolation.\n\n6. **Unit Tests (`tests/zkFederatedMacRandomization.test.ts`)**:\n- Comprehensive unit test suite validating proof generation, host\nverification, nullifier double-spend rejection, MAC normalization, and\nsession lifecycle.\n\n### LOC Modifications\n- **Total LOC Added**: ~776 LOC across 6 files (Exceeds minimum\nrequirement of 350 LOC).\n\n### Verification\n- Executed unit test suite via Vitest:\n  ```bash\n  npx vitest run tests/zkFederatedMacRandomization.test.ts\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added anonymous cross-campus network roaming with zero-knowledge\nauthentication.\n* Added automatic locally administered MAC address randomization and\nsession rotation.\n* Added session details including expiration, isolated VLAN, and\nrotation history.\n  * Added host-campus verification and protection against proof replay.\n* Added support for managing trust anchors, active sessions, and session\nrevocation.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Added clear error handling for invalid credentials, expired proofs,\nmismatched campuses, and failed session operations.\n* **Tests**\n* Added coverage for roaming proofs, MAC generation, session lifecycle,\nrotation, revocation, and privacy settings.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlabKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKnQQAAZG7DpGsaAeE9Uc+mHCsWqO\nr2bsuN96aT31OX3kklk4PzqhBy6mAU2+HvN9o3pcwPc+z0RgFG42HBX3dnU3QY2/\nsqqv66WpZzE5uEPx0bqbH++wkFebXJklHI9H2H8kbvMdOcVhBsx3kJ68VnD6FFUN\nRopt5qMR7U8glJW8ZHf2Dy7F/SQ6Rw49vyb2WpnZoJG4ROJWfMEZQc