"}],"sha":"1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/1caca4cdd2a3cf1c0a5f311b771f3df3ebded7b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233611462?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zainabhina05-png","id":233611462,"login":"zainabhina05-png","node_id":"U_kgDODeygxg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zainabhina05-png","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a74bf48e77176f496f5aa41fa3cf934cdd1b38a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:59:59Z","email":"zainab.hina05@gmail.com","name":"Zaeb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:59:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement UBO screening with OFAC sanctions checking (Issue #5364) (#5415)\n\n## Summary\nImplements corporate veil piercing for OFAC sanctions screening by\nintegrating with corporate registry APIs to extract Ultimate Beneficial\nOwners (UBOs) and checking them against sanctions lists, blocking escrow\npayouts if any UBO is flagged.\n\n## Problem\nEntity-level sanctions screening is trivially bypassed via nested\ncorporate structures and shell companies. The OFAC checker (Issue #5065)\nclears the Catering Company because the company name itself is clean.\nHowever, the Catering Company is actually a Delaware Shell Corporation.\nThe actual human who owns the shell corporation is an internationally\nsanctioned oligarch. The University is still liable for laundering\nmoney.\n\n## Solution\nIntegrate with FinCEN Beneficial Ownership Information (BOI) APIs to\npierce the corporate veil during vendor onboarding:\n- During Vendor contract signing, the API does not just check the\n''Vendor_Name''\n- It queries an advanced corporate registry API (OpenCorporates or\nspecialized FinCEN integrators) to traverse the corporate hierarchy\n- Extract the names of the Ultimate Beneficial Owners (UBOs) — the\nactual humans who own >25% of the entity\n- Run the OFAC Sanctions check against these specific individuals\n- If a UBO is flagged, instantly block the Escrow payout and alert the\nUniversity General Counsel that a sanctioned individual is attempting to\noperate via a proxy entity\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `vendors` table for vendor management with tax ID and\njurisdiction\n- Created `vendor_contracts` table for contract tracking with escrow\nblocking\n- Created `corporate_ownership` table for UBO tracking with >25%\nownership threshold\n- Created `sanctions_screenings` table for OFAC sanctions check results\n  - Created `legal_alerts` table for legal counsel alert system\n  - Added `create_vendor` RPC for vendor creation\n- Added `add_corporate_ownership` RPC for tracking ownership with\nautomatic UBO detection\n- Added `screen_vendor_sanctions` RPC for entity and UBO sanctions\nscreening\n- Added `block_vendor_escrow` RPC for blocking payouts when sanctions\nfound\n\n- **Edge Function**: `ubo-screening` function that:\n  - Integrates with OpenCorporates API to fetch corporate ownership data\n- Traverses corporate hierarchy to extract officers, directors, and\nshareholders\n  - Implements UBO extraction logic (>25% ownership threshold)\n  - Screens both the entity and all UBOs against OFAC sanctions lists\n  - Automatically blocks escrow payouts if any sanctions match is found\n  - Creates legal alerts for University General Counsel review\n\n- **UBO Extraction Logic**:\n  - Filters owners with >25% ownership as Ultimate Beneficial Owners\n- Falls back to screening all individuals if ownership percentages\nunavailable\n  - Tracks source (OpenCorporates, FinCEN BOI, manual) for audit trail\n  - Stores raw API response for compliance documentation\n\n- **Escrow Blocking**:\n  - Automatically blocks all active contracts for sanctioned vendors\n  - Updates contract status to ''blocked'' with reason and timestamp\n  - Creates critical legal alert for immediate review\n  - Prevents payout until legal counsel resolves the alert\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `UBOScreeningPanel` component for:\n  - Creating and managing vendors\n  - Triggering UBO screening via OpenCorporates API\n  - Viewing corporate ownership hierarchy\n  - Viewing sanctions screening results with match scores\n  - Managing legal alerts and resolution workflow\n  - Adding manual ownership data when API unavailable\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP and Vitest test suites covering:\n  - Vendor creation and management\n  - Corporate ownership tracking with UBO detection\n  - Sanctions screening for entities and UBOs\n  - Escrow blocking for sanctioned vendors\n  - Legal alert creation and resolution\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. Admin creates vendor with tax ID and jurisdiction\n2. System triggers UBO screening via OpenCorporates API\n3. API returns corporate ownership data (officers, directors,\nshareholders)\n4. System extracts UBOs (>25% ownership)\n5. System screens entity and all UBOs against OFAC sanctions lists\n6. If sanctions match found:\n   - Vendor marked as sanctioned\n   - All active contracts blocked from escrow payout\n   - Critical legal alert created for University General Counsel\n   - Legal counsel reviews and resolves alert\n7. If no sanctions match:\n   - Vendor cleared for normal operations\n   - Contracts proceed normally\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `OPENCORPORATES_API_KEY` environment variable for corporate\nregistry integration\n- Set `OFAC_API_KEY` environment variable for sanctions checking\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual entry mode)\n\n## Legal Compliance Benefits\n- **Corporate Veil Piercing**: Identifies actual human owners behind\nshell companies\n- **UBO Detection**: Automatically identifies individuals with >25%\nownership\n- **Sanctions Compliance**: Screens actual individuals against OFAC\nlists, not just entity names\n- **Escrow Protection**: Automatically blocks payouts to sanctioned\nentities\n- **Legal Alert System**: Immediate notification to University General\nCounsel\n- **Audit Trail**: Complete documentation of screening process for\ncompliance audits\n\nCloses #5364\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"778db7c2164c9a6baa485f415e0b0bcf474b9a64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/778db7c2164c9a6baa485f415e0b0bcf474b9a64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/a74bf48e77176f496f5aa41fa3cf934cdd1b38a4","verification":{"payload":"tree 778db7c2164c9a6baa485f415e0b0bcf474b9a64\nparent 97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d\nauthor Zaeb <zainab.hina05@gmail.com> 1788191999 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788191999 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement UBO screening with OFAC sanctions checking (Issue #5364) (#5415)\n\n## Summary\nImplements corporate veil piercing for OFAC sanctions screening by\nintegrating with corporate registry APIs to extract Ultimate Beneficial\nOwners (UBOs) and checking them against sanctions lists, blocking escrow\npayouts if any UBO is flagged.\n\n## Problem\nEntity-level sanctions screening is trivially bypassed via nested\ncorporate structures and shell companies. The OFAC checker (Issue #5065)\nclears the Catering Company because the company name itself is clean.\nHowever, the Catering Company is actually a Delaware Shell Corporation.\nThe actual human who owns the shell corporation is an internationally\nsanctioned oligarch. The University is still liable for laundering\nmoney.\n\n## Solution\nIntegrate with FinCEN Beneficial Ownership Information (BOI) APIs to\npierce the corporate veil during vendor onboarding:\n- During Vendor contract signing, the API does not just check the\n''Vendor_Name''\n- It queries an advanced corporate registry API (OpenCorporates or\nspecialized FinCEN integrators) to traverse the corporate hierarchy\n- Extract the names of the Ultimate Beneficial Owners (UBOs) — the\nactual humans who own >25% of the entity\n- Run the OFAC Sanctions check against these specific individuals\n- If a UBO is flagged, instantly block the Escrow payout and alert the\nUniversity General Counsel that a sanctioned individual is attempting to\noperate via a proxy entity\n\n## Technical Implementation\n- **Database Changes**:\n- Created `vendors` table for vendor management with tax ID and\njurisdiction\n- Created `vendor_contracts` table for contract tracking with escrow\nblocking\n- Created `corporate_ownership` table for UBO tracking with >25%\nownership threshold\n- Created `sanctions_screenings` table for OFAC sanctions check results\n  - Created `legal_alerts` table for legal counsel alert system\n  - Added `create_vendor` RPC for vendor creation\n- Added `add_corporate_ownership` RPC for tracking ownership with\nautomatic UBO detection\n- Added `screen_vendor_sanctions` RPC for entity and UBO sanctions\nscreening\n- Added `block_vendor_escrow` RPC for blocking payouts when sanctions\nfound\n\n- **Edge Function**: `ubo-screening` function that:\n  - Integrates with OpenCorporates API to fetch corporate ownership data\n- Traverses corporate hierarchy to extract officers, directors, and\nshareholders\n  - Implements UBO extraction logic (>25% ownership threshold)\n  - Screens both the entity and all UBOs against OFAC sanctions lists\n  - Automatically blocks escrow payouts if any sanctions match is found\n  - Creates legal alerts for University General Counsel review\n\n- **UBO Extraction Logic**:\n  - Filters owners with >25% ownership as Ultimate Beneficial Owners\n- Falls back to screening all individuals if ownership percentages\nunavailable\n  - Tracks source (OpenCorporates, FinCEN BOI, manual) for audit trail\n  - Stores raw API response for compliance documentation\n\n- **Escrow Blocking**:\n  - Automatically blocks all active contracts for sanctioned vendors\n  - Updates contract status to ''blocked'' with reason and timestamp\n  - Creates critical legal alert for immediate review\n  - Prevents payout until legal counsel resolves the alert\n\n- **Admin Interface**: `UBOScreeningPanel` component for:\n  - Creating and managing vendors\n  - Triggering UBO screening via OpenCorporates API\n  - Viewing corporate ownership hierarchy\n  - Viewing sanctions screening results with match scores\n  - Managing legal alerts and resolution workflow\n  - Adding manual ownership data when API unavailable\n\n- **Tests**: Comprehensive pgTAP and Vitest test suites covering:\n  - Vendor creation and management\n  - Corporate ownership tracking with UBO detection\n  - Sanctions screening for entities and UBOs\n  - Escrow blocking for sanctioned vendors\n  - Legal alert creation and resolution\n\n## Expected Behavior\n1. Admin creates vendor with tax ID and jurisdiction\n2. System triggers UBO screening via OpenCorporates API\n3. API returns corporate ownership data (officers, directors,\nshareholders)\n4. System extracts UBOs (>25% ownership)\n5. System screens entity and all UBOs against OFAC sanctions lists\n6. If sanctions match found:\n   - Vendor marked as sanctioned\n   - All active contracts blocked from escrow payout\n   - Critical legal alert created for University General Counsel\n   - Legal counsel reviews and resolves alert\n7. If no sanctions match:\n   - Vendor cleared for normal operations\n   - Contracts proceed normally\n\n## Configuration\n- Set `OPENCORPORATES_API_KEY` environment variable for corporate\nregistry integration\n- Set `OFAC_API_KEY` environment variable for sanctions checking\n- Both APIs have fallbacks when keys not available (manual entry mode)\n\n## Legal Compliance Benefits\n- **Corporate Veil Piercing**: Identifies actual human owners behind\nshell companies\n- **UBO Detection**: Automatically identifies individuals with >25%\nownership\n- **Sanctions Compliance**: Screens actual individuals against OFAC\nlists, not just entity names\n- **Escrow Protection**: Automatically blocks payouts to sanctioned\nentities\n- **Legal Alert System**: Immediate notification to University General\nCounsel\n- **Audit Trail**: Complete documentation of screening process for\ncompliance audits\n\nCloses #5364\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zainabhina05-png <2.33611462e+08+zainabhina05-png@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlaT/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7cIQAHdBLFk+hfkYb8YLETk8ilsl\nebfH9URNj4vTIj22l1hgQXhG7gwyaJl4RIIHCcuHnSO5IWsfdR8s7CXHF84HGPXR\ncJcgxJ4Z5FWnvQvGZs5WdluVr29pvI+DqaKL5yTCBg8KycnFXHW3vO/XfMf+FdNN\n60lUNTi6PwNG27k9XQW+CgzjGDbCU+6Eiv7oKoiE3+3qj+WLrfoZoaDTOVurQOet\nxmgTccXVf7SwS1DLgijy5c0vcNZVHAEzISgu4tOnBrOZ3DfLjqTC1R3vEv3V/suw\nha/pk8jtaZArXOw4gs+cINSMB7zw53Po+Hn0r+IMgSnJHr4u0BQsVRznRadKt7kC\ncm5Bvar1nz5+wqWUhiX7ejKuF3ba5ASRcnuy0xo41DnKh4nwSF3DLYBj4XyH46zR\njIFAXNdToCuCVyhEzHFu6oweUis+/Y6mPcb4Z8saTzOsrXEMJRiP4XZEcY/Yiupv\nK8L7VOAG3OaVmPqsrNx41ZbMX+G0hFALVFg3YPMyzEsjt3RHvE3s/ERP/7uhdGUx\nzYw1CBqjS/GkxLYLjTMJ0RqMIqNbflbV5C4i7jWi/DUte1nfvV0BrNonEi+53lrR\n9M9BwKSlxNXtkGE4xDTdaI0rv843NcN5Ae1RscK3xhw1M1Lhr3l+U7hws+3u2cNn\nrJ7IOz4u1Ofi3QPj/46s\n=dXNA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T15:59:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/a74bf48e77176f496f5aa41fa3cf934cdd1b38a4","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGE3NGJmNDhlNzcxNzZmNDk2ZjVhYTQxZmEzY2Y5MzRjZGQxYjM4YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d","sha":"97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d"}],"sha":"a74bf48e77176f496f5aa41fa3cf934cdd1b38a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a74bf48e77176f496f5aa41fa3cf934cdd1b38a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204190294?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dhruvi2006-source","id":204190294,"login":"Dhruvi2006-source","node_id":"U_kgDODCuyVg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:22:54Z","email":"2006dhruvi@gmail.com","name":"Technical-Dhruvi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:22:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Multi-Oracle Consensus for Decentralized Event Cancellation Insurance (#5075) (#5406)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5075\n\nImplements a multi-oracle consensus mechanism for the decentralized\nevent cancellation insurance workflow. The system removes the single\ncentralized weather oracle dependency by requiring independent\nprecipitation data from NOAA, AccuWeather, and a cryptographically\nsigned campus IoT rain gauge. Insurance payouts are triggered only when\nthe required oracle consensus is reached.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Multi-Oracle Data Integration**:\n\n   * Added support for three independent precipitation data sources\n   * Integrated NOAA weather data as the first external oracle\n   * Integrated AccuWeather data as the second external oracle\n* Added support for cryptographically signed campus IoT rain gauge\nmeasurements\n* Normalizes precipitation data from all sources for consensus\nevaluation\n\n2. **Cryptographically Signed IoT Oracle**:\n\n   * Added validation for signed rain gauge payloads\n* Verifies the authenticity and integrity of campus sensor measurements\n   * Prevents unauthorized or modified sensor data from being accepted\n* Associates IoT precipitation readings with the relevant insured event\n\n3. **2-of-3 Oracle Consensus**:\n\n   * Added threshold-based oracle consensus evaluation\n* Requires at least 2 of 3 independent sources to confirm the qualifying\ncondition\n   * Uses `precipitation > 1.0 inches` as the payout trigger\n* Prevents a single unreliable or manipulated data source from\ntriggering a claim\n* Rejects payout conditions when oracle responses do not reach the\nrequired threshold\n\n4. **Polygon Smart Contract Integration**:\n\n* Updated the insurance smart contract to support multiple oracle inputs\n   * Added consensus validation before executing insurance payouts\n   * Prevents direct payout decisions based on a single centralized API\n   * Records oracle responses and consensus results for each event\n   * Keeps payout execution dependent on validated oracle agreement\n\n5. **Event Cancellation Payout Workflow**:\n\n   * Queries all configured oracle sources when the insured event begins\n   * Collects precipitation measurements from each source\n   * Evaluates the measurements against the configured threshold\n   * Executes payout only after successful 2-of-3 consensus\n* Rejects or holds claims when sufficient oracle agreement is\nunavailable\n\n6. **Oracle Failure & Manipulation Handling**:\n\n   * Handles unavailable or invalid oracle responses\n* Prevents failed oracle requests from being treated as positive\nconfirmations\n   * Isolates inconsistent readings from the final consensus decision\n   * Reduces the impact of a compromised individual oracle\n* Provides a resilient alternative to single-source weather verification\n\n7. **Auditability & Claim Integrity**:\n\n   * Records oracle responses used for each insurance decision\n   * Tracks the final consensus result\n* Associates payout decisions with the underlying precipitation evidence\n   * Provides traceability for successful and rejected claims\n   * Strengthens protection of the shared student insurance pool\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash id=\"j6v4pt\"\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* NOAA oracle response handling\n* AccuWeather oracle response handling\n* Cryptographically signed IoT rain gauge payloads\n* IoT signature validation\n* Precipitation threshold evaluation\n* 2-of-3 oracle consensus\n* Single-oracle failure scenarios\n* Conflicting oracle responses\n* Invalid oracle data rejection\n* Payout prevention without sufficient consensus\n* Payout execution after valid 2-of-3 confirmation\n* Polygon smart contract consensus integration\n* Event cancellation insurance claim workflow\n* Oracle manipulation and failure scenarios\n\nCo-authored-by: Prajapati Krushit Bipinbhai <kp7802829544@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"7570824de44acd806f7021a584acd22ae8e3fd71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/7570824de44acd806f7021a584acd22ae8e3fd71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d","verification":{"payload":"tree 7570824de44acd806f7021a584acd22ae8e3fd71\nparent e40516ae458691d72779f0f0816ddbceaebb9dce\nauthor Technical-Dhruvi <2006dhruvi@gmail.com> 1788189774 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788189774 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement Multi-Oracle Consensus for Decentralized Event Cancellation Insurance (#5075) (#5406)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5075\n\nImplements a multi-oracle consensus mechanism for the decentralized\nevent cancellation insurance workflow. The system removes the single\ncentralized weather oracle dependency by requiring independent\nprecipitation data from NOAA, AccuWeather, and a cryptographically\nsigned campus IoT rain gauge. Insurance payouts are triggered only when\nthe required oracle consensus is reached.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Multi-Oracle Data Integration**:\n\n   * Added support for three independent precipitation data sources\n   * Integrated NOAA weather data as the first external oracle\n   * Integrated AccuWeather data as the second external oracle\n* Added support for cryptographically signed campus IoT rain gauge\nmeasurements\n* Normalizes precipitation data from all sources for consensus\nevaluation\n\n2. **Cryptographically Signed IoT Oracle**:\n\n   * Added validation for signed rain gauge payloads\n* Verifies the authenticity and integrity of campus sensor measurements\n   * Prevents unauthorized or modified sensor data from being accepted\n* Associates IoT precipitation readings with the relevant insured event\n\n3. **2-of-3 Oracle Consensus**:\n\n   * Added threshold-based oracle consensus evaluation\n* Requires at least 2 of 3 independent sources to confirm the qualifying\ncondition\n   * Uses `precipitation > 1.0 inches` as the payout trigger\n* Prevents a single unreliable or manipulated data source from\ntriggering a claim\n* Rejects payout conditions when oracle responses do not reach the\nrequired threshold\n\n4. **Polygon Smart Contract Integration**:\n\n* Updated the insurance smart contract to support multiple oracle inputs\n   * Added consensus validation before executing insurance payouts\n   * Prevents direct payout decisions based on a single centralized API\n   * Records oracle responses and consensus results for each event\n   * Keeps payout execution dependent on validated oracle agreement\n\n5. **Event Cancellation Payout Workflow**:\n\n   * Queries all configured oracle sources when the insured event begins\n   * Collects precipitation measurements from each source\n   * Evaluates the measurements against the configured threshold\n   * Executes payout only after successful 2-of-3 consensus\n* Rejects or holds claims when sufficient oracle agreement is\nunavailable\n\n6. **Oracle Failure & Manipulation Handling**:\n\n   * Handles unavailable or invalid oracle responses\n* Prevents failed oracle requests from being treated as positive\nconfirmations\n   * Isolates inconsistent readings from the final consensus decision\n   * Reduces the impact of a compromised individual oracle\n* Provides a resilient alternative to single-source weather verification\n\n7. **Auditability & Claim Integrity**:\n\n   * Records oracle responses used for each insurance decision\n   * Tracks the final consensus result\n* Associates payout decisions with the underlying precipitation evidence\n   * Provides traceability for successful and rejected claims\n   * Strengthens protection of the shared student insurance pool\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash id=\"j6v4pt\"\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* NOAA oracle response handling\n* AccuWeather oracle response handling\n* Cryptographically signed IoT rain gauge payloads\n* IoT signature validation\n* Precipitation threshold evaluation\n* 2-of-3 oracle consensus\n* Single-oracle failure scenarios\n* Conflicting oracle responses\n* Invalid oracle data rejection\n* Payout prevention without sufficient consensus\n* Payout execution after valid 2-of-3 confirmation\n* Polygon smart contract consensus integration\n* Event cancellation insurance claim workflow\n* Oracle manipulation and failure scenarios\n\nCo-authored-by: Prajapati Krushit Bipinbhai <kp7802829544@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlZxOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfpkQAAsH0G7ivk1RVmPMtBPWUUwu\n1nUwOKbR0UJKPDOK9iooqQ/YKbYp5Ce1TwIKuU/5ExKGkYXh6i0olh981PgZ1hue\nuYR+rzuyk952aeCNiE1oyJaFTPQQRfLQeO/6az5uWM8kYRkawKy3ZRGhQeqvbB0t\n4MymXrWszrUdGFsw0hxFHLHfsznXFwCs8aKHwW/ycgrZjQ7udEgnG76szY+KA19l\n//0exmyt+BlASPyYb4FEWE3lCUreZrSBV5w5iIRrebA/gvIHr3mKHeT0W8f8DZZ/\nOUHbYCrRd7yPU9pYEOSjRL5c0RBZUzuKIe+J58SrTKj/GalXphXza1AQKflD51Gx\ncr8mD5DhcatM62DsClH0RzQiHEKTXN3uLwS7c9rxg99ebx3VA5XSsxDO7+ZK0DHt\niuuGP+CIrlDpiPInDpF8J4oHTOwA5qZDQ8Cr2VkJNWtBEaYTBQzt0QhEby7L2/+6\nhA+1giVVorC14qCA+LUpozVEI8PLANu3oSb6QDh7IFIsYwS8cKba+IrSAu3415Sr\nJtNS1lASyaVEXG0862G5V0cDkT4gd03MnVLGmHVFNK4Yg6Ky2Y89aeUeYZBWlfLl\naIxS6QeVcSKxt/rXxE1/xoat1ogYyKAEmZai/PIZC8DyEOLf9525B9pnIbp1RsBq\nfcXJBuJKwbPw5qv3oT0o\n=Zdj2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T15:22:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDk3ODI4YmY0YzI0ODI5ZTI0ZmNhODYzYzkyM2U0MDhjZWFkYTBlMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/e40516ae458691d72779f0f0816ddbceaebb9dce","sha":"e40516ae458691d72779f0f0816ddbceaebb9dce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/e40516ae458691d72779f0f0816ddbceaebb9dce"}],"sha":"97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/97828bf4c24829e24fca863c923e408ceada0e0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204190294?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dhruvi2006-source","id":204190294,"login":"Dhruvi2006-source","node_id":"U_kgDODCuyVg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/e40516ae458691d72779f0f0816ddbceaebb9dce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:21:55Z","email":"2006dhruvi@gmail.com","name":"Technical-Dhruvi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:21:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Multi-Campus Eduroam EAP-TLS Certificate Auto-Provisioning (#5074) (#5407)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5074\n\nImplements a multi-campus Wi-Fi provisioning workflow that removes\ndependency on device MAC address tracking by provisioning time-bound\nWPA2-Enterprise EAP-TLS credentials. The system connects eligible event\nRSVPs with university PKI provisioning, generates platform-specific\nWi-Fi configuration profiles, and allows supported devices to\nauthenticate through certificates even when MAC randomization is\nenabled.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Multi-Campus Wi-Fi Provisioning Workflow**:\n\n   * Added event RSVP validation for cross-campus attendees\n* Associates eligible student accounts with the destination campus Wi-Fi\nprovisioning flow\n   * Supports campus-specific network and certificate configuration\n   * Keeps Wi-Fi credentials scoped to the relevant event and campus\n* Replaces MAC-address-dependent access with certificate-based\nauthentication\n\n2. **University PKI Integration**:\n\n* Added backend integration with the university Public Key\nInfrastructure\n   * Generates unique client certificates for eligible devices\n   * Configures certificates with time-bound validity\n* Associates issued certificates with the corresponding student and\ncampus\n   * Supports certificate lifecycle and provisioning status tracking\n\n3. **EAP-TLS Credential Provisioning**:\n\n   * Added WPA2-Enterprise EAP-TLS configuration support\n   * Uses client certificates for network authentication\n* Enables network authentication independent of the device''s MAC address\n* Supports secure certificate-based authentication for participating\nstudents\n   * Handles invalid, expired, or unavailable certificates safely\n\n4. **iOS & macOS Configuration Profiles**:\n\n   * Added generation of Apple `.mobileconfig` Wi-Fi profiles\n* Configures the destination enterprise network and EAP-TLS credentials\n* Associates the provisioned client certificate with the appropriate\nnetwork configuration\n* Provides a user-facing installation workflow for supported Apple\ndevices\n\n5. **Android Passpoint / Hotspot 2.0 Support**:\n\n* Added support for generating Android-compatible Passpoint\nconfiguration\n   * Configures supported devices for enterprise Wi-Fi authentication\n* Allows the operating system to manage EAP-TLS authentication natively\n* Reduces repeated captive portal interactions caused by MAC address\nrotation\n\n6. **Certificate Installation Experience**:\n\n   * Added user-facing Wi-Fi profile provisioning flow\n   * Displays an installation prompt for eligible students\n* Provides the appropriate profile based on the user''s device platform\n   * Tracks provisioning and installation status\n   * Handles failed or incomplete profile installation gracefully\n\n7. **MAC Randomization Compatibility**:\n\n* Removed reliance on persistent MAC address identification for\nprovisioned devices\n* Allows devices to continue enterprise Wi-Fi authentication while MAC\nrandomization is enabled\n   * Uses certificate-based identity instead of MAC address persistence\n* Improves cross-campus connectivity for privacy-preserving mobile\noperating systems\n\n8. **Security & Certificate Lifecycle Management**:\n\n   * Uses time-bound client certificates to limit credential lifetime\n* Prevents expired credentials from being treated as active network\nidentities\n* Keeps certificate issuance associated with authorized RSVP and campus\ncontext\n* Adds validation around certificate provisioning and network\nconfiguration\n* Prevents unauthorized users from obtaining destination-campus\ncredentials\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash id=\"p4x8ns\"\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* Multi-campus RSVP eligibility\n* University PKI certificate provisioning\n* Time-bound certificate generation\n* EAP-TLS credential configuration\n* Certificate expiration handling\n* iOS/macOS `.mobileconfig` generation\n* Android Passpoint configuration\n* Device platform detection\n* Wi-Fi profile installation workflow\n* Certificate provisioning failures\n* MAC randomization compatibility\n* Certificate-based network authentication\n* Unauthorized provisioning prevention\n* Certificate lifecycle and provisioning status tracking\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added Wi-Fi provisioning for supported campuses using secure\ncertificate-based authentication.\n- Users can view their certificate status and download an Apple\n`.mobileconfig` profile for connecting to the `eduroam` network.\n- Added clear loading and error feedback during profile generation and\ncertificate updates.\n- Certificates automatically expire after 30 days and are securely\nassociated with the requesting user.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Prajapati Krushit Bipinbhai <kp7802829544@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c10b97b0c3941c955910658c568ac7d787c30954","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/c10b97b0c3941c955910658c568ac7d787c30954"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/e40516ae458691d72779f0f0816ddbceaebb9dce","verification":{"payload":"tree c10b97b0c3941c955910658c568ac7d787c30954\nparent eb29810b3d07d3a4fa93c22518656929bf617523\nauthor Technical-Dhruvi <2006dhruvi@gmail.com> 1788189715 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788189715 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement Multi-Campus Eduroam EAP-TLS Certificate Auto-Provisioning (#5074) (#5407)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5074\n\nImplements a multi-campus Wi-Fi provisioning workflow that removes\ndependency on device MAC address tracking by provisioning time-bound\nWPA2-Enterprise EAP-TLS credentials. The system connects eligible event\nRSVPs with university PKI provisioning, generates platform-specific\nWi-Fi configuration profiles, and allows supported devices to\nauthenticate through certificates even when MAC randomization is\nenabled.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Multi-Campus Wi-Fi Provisioning Workflow**:\n\n   * Added event RSVP validation for cross-campus attendees\n* Associates eligible student accounts with the destination campus Wi-Fi\nprovisioning flow\n   * Supports campus-specific network and certificate configuration\n   * Keeps Wi-Fi credentials scoped to the relevant event and campus\n* Replaces MAC-address-dependent access with certificate-based\nauthentication\n\n2. **University PKI Integration**:\n\n* Added backend integration with the university Public Key\nInfrastructure\n   * Generates unique client certificates for eligible devices\n   * Configures certificates with time-bound validity\n* Associates issued certificates with the corresponding student and\ncampus\n   * Supports certificate lifecycle and provisioning status tracking\n\n3. **EAP-TLS Credential Provisioning**:\n\n   * Added WPA2-Enterprise EAP-TLS configuration support\n   * Uses client certificates for network authentication\n* Enables network authentication independent of the device''s MAC address\n* Supports secure certificate-based authentication for participating\nstudents\n   * Handles invalid, expired, or unavailable certificates safely\n\n4. **iOS & macOS Configuration Profiles**:\n\n   * Added generation of Apple `.mobileconfig` Wi-Fi profiles\n* Configures the destination enterprise network and EAP-TLS credentials\n* Associates the provisioned client certificate with the appropriate\nnetwork configuration\n* Provides a user-facing installation workflow for supported Apple\ndevices\n\n5. **Android Passpoint / Hotspot 2.0 Support**:\n\n* Added support for generating Android-compatible Passpoint\nconfiguration\n   * Configures supported devices for enterprise Wi-Fi authentication\n* Allows the operating system to manage EAP-TLS authentication natively\n* Reduces repeated captive portal interactions caused by MAC address\nrotation\n\n6. **Certificate Installation Experience**:\n\n   * Added user-facing Wi-Fi profile provisioning flow\n   * Displays an installation prompt for eligible students\n* Provides the appropriate profile based on the user''s device platform\n   * Tracks provisioning and installation status\n   * Handles failed or incomplete profile installation gracefully\n\n7. **MAC Randomization Compatibility**:\n\n* Removed reliance on persistent MAC address identification for\nprovisioned devices\n* Allows devices to continue enterprise Wi-Fi authentication while MAC\nrandomization is enabled\n   * Uses certificate-based identity instead of MAC address persistence\n* Improves cross-campus connectivity for privacy-preserving mobile\noperating systems\n\n8. **Security & Certificate Lifecycle Management**:\n\n   * Uses time-bound client certificates to limit credential lifetime\n* Prevents expired credentials from being treated as active network\nidentities\n* Keeps certificate issuance associated with authorized RSVP and campus\ncontext\n* Adds validation around certificate provisioning and network\nconfiguration\n* Prevents unauthorized users from obtaining destination-campus\ncredentials\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash id=\"p4x8ns\"\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* Multi-campus RSVP eligibility\n* University PKI certificate provisioning\n* Time-bound certificate generation\n* EAP-TLS credential configuration\n* Certificate expiration handling\n* iOS/macOS `.mobileconfig` generation\n* Android Passpoint configuration\n* Device platform detection\n* Wi-Fi profile installation workflow\n* Certificate provisioning failures\n* MAC randomization compatibility\n* Certificate-based network authentication\n* Unauthorized provisioning prevention\n* Certificate lifecycle and provisioning status tracking\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added Wi-Fi provisioning for supported campuses using secure\ncertificate-based authentication.\n- Users can view their certificate status and download an Apple\n`.mobileconfig` profile for connecting to the `eduroam` network.\n- Added clear loading and error feedback during profile generation and\ncertificate updates.\n- Certificates automatically expire after 30 days and are securely\nassociated with the requesting user.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Prajapati Krushit Bipinbhai <kp7802829544@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlZwTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1jQQABOtP7FfRL45cIh5DCEWQvuT\ncI7hBCd8gTzANBdL8cNdSfLWl0KAW02WWMVmZ//DAoS+xahaxu2vch1BJIGPpeO2\n7XyyzJY/i3ypCtf19PquRnfb+lAbSBT4Y