ived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/3219ceb0846b254cb45ac685430138e0b4f6dfe3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:18:17Z","email":"aryan.buha89@gmail.com","name":"Aryan Buha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:18:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(finances): #5377 Implement Multi-Oracle SLA Vendor Escrow Slashing (#5404)\n\n📝 Summary\nThis PR implements a multi-oracle Smart Contract SLA validation and\nslashing engine. Releasing contracted escrow funds requires synchronized\nconsensus on both GPS arrival time and cargo bay temperature. If the\ncryptographically signed temperature log falls below 140°F, an automatic\n50% slashing penalty is executed, paying half to the vendor and\nrefunding the remaining half back to the club''s ledger balance.\n\n🏷️ Type of Change\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] New feature\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Performance improvement\n- [ ] Refactoring\n- [x] Test improvement\n- [ ] CI/CD or build change\n\n🔗 Related Issue\nCloses #5377\n\n✨ Changes Made\n- **Database Schema & Oracle RPC\n(`20270926000000_vendor_sla_escrow_slashing.sql`)**:\n- Upgraded the `vendor_contracts` table with SLA parameters (deadlines,\ntemperature constraints, actual sensor logs, signatures, and statuses).\n- Implemented `execute_vendor_sla_payout` RPC. It evaluates oracle\ninputs and executes a 50% slash on temperature drops (< 140°F),\nreleasing the remaining amount and refunding the slashed 50% back into\n`club_transactions` as a positive ledger refund.\n- **Client Service Wrapper (`vendorSlaService.ts`)**:\n- Mapped SLA configuration settings and simulated oracle execution\npings.\n- **SLA Oracle Tracker Panel (`VendorEscrowViewer.tsx`)**:\n- Upgraded the escrow details view to display delivery deadlines and\ntemperature rules.\n- Embedded an interactive Multi-Oracle Payout Simulator to mock actual\nGPS timestamps, recorded probe temperatures, and consensus signatures.\n- Renders Polygon settlement records detailing payout sums, penalty\nrefunds, and cryptographic hashes.\n- **Unit Test Suites**:\n- **pgTAP database tests (`vendor_sla_escrow_slashing.test.sql`)**:\nVerifies column schemas, temperature constraint validations, 50% slash\nmath, and positive ledger refunds.\n- **React component tests (`vendorSla.test.tsx`)**: Verifies SLA\nconfiguration badges, temperature input fields, and simulated cold\ntemperature slashed triggers.\n\n🧪 Testing\n- [x] Tests pass\n- [x] Linters run successfully\n- [x] Tested locally\n\nTesting Details:\nRun Vitest unit tests:\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/routes/vendorSla.test.tsx","tree":{"sha":"8066abc381392d0f4696d7701b7043ddf87e94d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/8066abc381392d0f4696d7701b7043ddf87e94d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/3219ceb0846b254cb45ac685430138e0b4f6dfe3","verification":{"payload":"tree 8066abc381392d0f4696d7701b7043ddf87e94d4\nparent 105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288\nauthor Aryan Buha <aryan.buha89@gmail.com> 1788189497 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788189497 +0530\n\nfeat(finances): #5377 Implement Multi-Oracle SLA Vendor Escrow Slashing (#5404)\n\n📝 Summary\nThis PR implements a multi-oracle Smart Contract SLA validation and\nslashing engine. Releasing contracted escrow funds requires synchronized\nconsensus on both GPS arrival time and cargo bay temperature. If the\ncryptographically signed temperature log falls below 140°F, an automatic\n50% slashing penalty is executed, paying half to the vendor and\nrefunding the remaining half back to the club''s ledger balance.\n\n🏷️ Type of Change\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] New feature\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Performance improvement\n- [ ] Refactoring\n- [x] Test improvement\n- [ ] CI/CD or build change\n\n🔗 Related Issue\nCloses #5377\n\n✨ Changes Made\n- **Database Schema & Oracle RPC\n(`20270926000000_vendor_sla_escrow_slashing.sql`)**:\n- Upgraded the `vendor_contracts` table with SLA parameters (deadlines,\ntemperature constraints, actual sensor logs, signatures, and statuses).\n- Implemented `execute_vendor_sla_payout` RPC. It evaluates oracle\ninputs and executes a 50% slash on temperature drops (< 140°F),\nreleasing the remaining amount and refunding the slashed 50% back into\n`club_transactions` as a positive ledger refund.\n- **Client Service Wrapper (`vendorSlaService.ts`)**:\n- Mapped SLA configuration settings and simulated oracle execution\npings.\n- **SLA Oracle Tracker Panel (`VendorEscrowViewer.tsx`)**:\n- Upgraded the escrow details view to display delivery deadlines and\ntemperature rules.\n- Embedded an interactive Multi-Oracle Payout Simulator to mock actual\nGPS timestamps, recorded probe temperatures, and consensus signatures.\n- Renders Polygon settlement records detailing payout sums, penalty\nrefunds, and cryptographic hashes.\n- **Unit Test Suites**:\n- **pgTAP database tests (`vendor_sla_escrow_slashing.test.sql`)**:\nVerifies column schemas, temperature constraint validations, 50% slash\nmath, and positive ledger refunds.\n- **React component tests (`vendorSla.test.tsx`)**: Verifies SLA\nconfiguration badges, temperature input fields, and simulated cold\ntemperature slashed triggers.\n\n🧪 Testing\n- [x] Tests pass\n- [x] Linters run successfully\n- [x] Tested locally\n\nTesting Details:\nRun Vitest unit tests:\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/routes/vendorSla.test.tsx","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABC