thub.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288","sha":"105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288"}],"sha":"3219ceb0846b254cb45ac685430138e0b4f6dfe3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/3219ceb0846b254cb45ac685430138e0b4f6dfe3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/273169945?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aryanbuha890","id":273169945,"login":"Aryanbuha890","node_id":"U_kgDOEEg-GQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aryanbuha890","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:18:14Z","email":"aryan.buha89@gmail.com","name":"Aryan Buha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:18:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(telemetry): #5378 Implement Edge ML Acoustic Density Overcrowding Detection (#5405)\n\n📝 Summary\nThis PR implements a privacy-preserving acoustic crowd density\novercrowding detection system. Audio waveforms are analyzed locally\ninside IoT microphone arrays (Edge TinyML), instantly wiped from RAM,\nand only anonymized density scores are broadcasted over MQTT. If density\nscore matches exceed 85%, security overcrowding alerts are dispatched to\nsystem administrators.\n\n🏷️ Type of Change\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] New feature\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Performance improvement\n- [ ] Refactoring\n- [x] Test improvement\n- [ ] CI/CD or build change\n\n🔗 Related Issue\nCloses #5378\n\n✨ Changes Made\n- **Database Schema & Ingest RPC\n(`20270928000000_acoustic_density_edge_ml.sql`)**:\n- Created the `acoustic_microphones`, `acoustic_density_telemetry`, and\n`acoustic_overcrowding_alerts` tables.\n  - Enabled RLS policies for database tables.\n- Implemented `ingest_acoustic_density` RPC, which validates incoming\nMQTT logs, creates overcrowding alerts if threshold score &ge; 85%, and\ndispatches security warnings to system administrators.\n- **Client Service Wrapper (`acousticDensityService.ts`)**:\n- Implements device listings, telemetry logs queries, simulated MQTT\nscore publishes, and local TinyML binary firmware flashing.\n- **Acoustic Density Panel (`AcousticDensityTelemetry.tsx` /\n`facility-dashboard.tsx`)**:\n- Added a dashboard panel displaying arrays, firmware statuses, and\nrecent MQTT feeds inside the HVAC facility manager board.\n- Provides a Firmware Flasher tool to simulate flashing local TFLite\nmodels.\n- Embeds an MQTT simulation broadcaster with raw wave RAM-wipe\nconfirmations.\n- **Unit Test Suites**:\n- **pgTAP database tests (`acoustic_density_edge_ml.test.sql`)**:\nVerifies table schemas, RLS rules, MQTT logs ingestion, threshold\nalerts, and admin warnings.\n- **React component tests (`acousticDensity.test.tsx`)**: Verifies\ndevice grids, flashing sequences, and MQTT publishing alerts.\n\n🧪 Testing\n- [x] Tests pass\n- [x] Linters run successfully\n- [x] Tested locally\n\nTesting Details:\nRun Vitest unit tests:\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/routes/acousticDensity.test.tsx\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added acoustic density monitoring to facility dashboards.\n  * View microphone inventory, firmware status, privacy assurances, telemetry scores, and live updates.\n  * Flash machine-learning firmware to supported microphones.\n  * Simulate and publish density readings with MQTT topics.\n  * Automatically generate overcrowding alerts and security notifications for high-density readings.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for microphone display, firmware flashing, telemetry publishing, and alert handling.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"f2ac2d1475759affc5487819c705f3de8b911bbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/f2ac2d1475759affc5487819c705f3de8b911bbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288","verification":{"payload":"tree f2ac2d1475759affc5487819c705f3de8b911bbb\nparent f2bc5d79c9de5b964db65051a4a07e25251466fd\nauthor Aryan Buha <aryan.buha89@gmail.com> 1788189494 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788189494 +0530\n\nfeat(telemetry): #5378 Implement Edge ML Acoustic Density Overcrowding Detection (#5405)\n\n📝 Summary\nThis PR implements a privacy-preserving acoustic crowd density\novercrowding detection system. Audio waveforms are analyzed locally\ninside IoT microphone arrays (Edge TinyML), instantly wiped from RAM,\nand only anonymized density scores are broadcasted over MQTT. If density\nscore matches exceed 85%, security overcrowding alerts are dispatched to\nsystem administrators.\n\n🏷️ Type of Change\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] New feature\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Performance improvement\n- [ ] Refactoring\n- [x] Test improvement\n- [ ] CI/CD or build change\n\n🔗 Related Issue\nCloses #5378\n\n✨ Changes Made\n- **Database Schema & Ingest RPC\n(`20270928000