com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDEwNWY0NGY3YTBlYTYwOTlmOTYxODUxZDI0NjA4ZWM1OGM5ZmUyODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/f2bc5d79c9de5b964db65051a4a07e25251466fd","sha":"f2bc5d79c9de5b964db65051a4a07e25251466fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/f2bc5d79c9de5b964db65051a4a07e25251466fd"}],"sha":"105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/105f44f7a0ea6099f961851d24608ec58c9fe288"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204190294?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dhruvi2006-source","id":204190294,"login":"Dhruvi2006-source","node_id":"U_kgDODCuyVg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/f2bc5d79c9de5b964db65051a4a07e25251466fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:18:05Z","email":"2006dhruvi@gmail.com","name":"Technical-Dhruvi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:18:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement Multimodal Deepfake Detection with Video Lip-Sync Analysis (#5068) (#5408)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5068\n\nImplements multimodal deepfake detection for uploaded videos by\nanalyzing both visual lip movements and audio speech patterns. The\nsystem extracts video and audio streams, evaluates their synchronization\nusing a dedicated lip-sync verification model, and quarantines\nsuspicious content when significant audio-visual inconsistencies are\ndetected.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Video & Audio Stream Extraction**:\n\n   * Added processing for uploaded MP4 video files\n   * Extracts the visual frame sequence from the video\n   * Separates the corresponding audio track for analysis\n   * Validates that both media streams are available before detection\n\n2. **Lip-Sync Verification Engine**:\n\n* Added integration with a specialized deepfake detection service or\nSyncNet-based analysis pipeline\n   * Analyzes facial and lip movement across video frames\n* Compares observed lip movements against speech phonemes from the audio\ntrack\n   * Calculates an audio-visual synchronization confidence score\n* Detects abnormal synchronization patterns associated with synthetic\nvideo generation\n\n3. **Multimodal Deepfake Detection**:\n\n* Combines visual and audio analysis instead of relying exclusively on\naudio deepfake detection\n* Identifies cases where authentic speech has been combined with\nmanipulated facial footage\n   * Applies configurable confidence thresholds for suspicious content\n* Distinguishes normal synchronization variance from potentially\nmanipulated media\n\n4. **Video Quarantine Workflow**:\n\n* Automatically quarantines videos that fall below the configured\nsynchronization threshold\n* Prevents suspicious media from being published or distributed normally\n   * Stores detection results and analysis metadata for further review\n* Provides clear processing states for pending, approved, and\nquarantined videos\n\n5. **Fraud & Account Flagging**:\n\n   * Flags accounts associated with high-confidence deepfake detections\n   * Records the detection event for platform security review\n* Integrates suspicious media events with existing fraud and moderation\nworkflows\n   * Prevents repeated suspicious uploads from bypassing detection\n\n6. **Detection Result Handling**:\n\n   * Stores synchronization scores and detection status\n   * Provides structured results for moderation and security interfaces\n   * Handles failed model requests and malformed media safely\n* Avoids automatically treating uncertain model results as confirmed\nfraud\n\n7. **Security & Privacy Controls**:\n\n   * Processes uploaded media through controlled detection workflows\n* Restricts detection metadata to authorized moderation and security\ncontexts\n* Prevents untrusted media from directly influencing platform trust\ndecisions without validation\n* Keeps detection thresholds configurable for future model improvements\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* MP4 video upload processing\n* Video frame extraction\n* Audio track extraction\n* Lip-sync analysis\n* Audio-visual correlation scoring\n* Natural synchronization handling\n* Low synchronization detection\n* Deepfake detection threshold evaluation\n* Suspicious video quarantine\n* Detection result persistence\n* Fraud account flagging\n* Invalid or incomplete media handling\n* Detection service failures\n* Existing audio-only deepfake detection compatibility\n* End-to-end video moderation workflow","tree":{"sha":"0282b9ff723734cb629626d025cfb18ea429a0bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/0282b9ff723734cb629626d025cfb18ea429a0bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/f2bc5d79c9de5b964db65051a4a07e25251466fd","verification":{"payload":"tree 0282b9ff723734cb629626d025cfb18ea429a0bf\nparent 09a8