:"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dhruvi2006-source","id":204190294,"login":"Dhruvi2006-source","node_id":"U_kgDODCuyVg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dhruvi2006-source","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/601aa8cd7b085473c97b2ba48dbff36c79f5fc77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T14:10:35Z","email":"2006dhruvi@gmail.com","name":"Technical-Dhruvi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T14:10:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement IoT Temperature Compliance & Automated Escrow Refund Workflow (#5082) (#5402)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5082\n\nImplements an automated environmental compliance workflow that connects\nsigned IoT temperature telemetry with the vendor payment settlement\nprocess. The system keeps vendor payouts pending until environmental\nclearance is completed, validates cryptographically signed temperature\ndata, evaluates continuous temperature violations, and automatically\ntriggers a refund when contractual food safety conditions are breached.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Environmental Clearance Payment State**:\n\n* Added `Pending_Environmental_Clearance` state for vendor escrow\npayouts\n* Holds vendor payment after arrival until environmental compliance is\nverified\n   * Prevents successful vendor arrival from immediately releasing funds\n* Connects physical compliance verification with the payment settlement\nlifecycle\n\n2. **Cryptographically Signed IoT Payload Handling**:\n\n   * Added backend support for TempTale temperature logger payloads\n   * Accepts signed JSON temperature timeseries data\n* Validates payload authenticity before processing environmental\nreadings\n* Protects temperature compliance decisions against tampered telemetry\n* Associates environmental readings with the relevant vendor order and\npayment workflow\n\n3. **Temperature Compliance Evaluation**:\n\n   * Added backend processing for IoT temperature timeseries\n* Evaluates temperature readings against configured food safety\nrequirements\n   * Detects continuous exposure above the configured `40°F` threshold\n   * Tracks the duration of non-compliant temperature exposure\n   * Identifies violations exceeding `120 continuous minutes`\n   * Produces a compliance decision for the associated payment state\n\n4. **Automated Stripe Refund Workflow**:\n\n* Connects environmental compliance results to the Stripe payment\nlifecycle\n* Automatically initiates a refund when a qualifying temperature\nviolation is detected\n   * Prevents non-compliant vendor payments from being finalized\n* Returns the payment amount to the Club through the configured Stripe\nworkflow\n   * Keeps payment and environmental compliance states synchronized\n\n5. **Contractual Health & Safety Enforcement**:\n\n   * Treats environmental compliance as a blocking settlement condition\n* Ensures payment decisions are based on verified IoT telemetry rather\nthan arrival time alone\n* Creates a programmatic link between food safety violations and\nfinancial settlement\n* Prevents vendors from receiving final payment when defined\nenvironmental requirements are violated\n\n6. **Automated Vendor Notification**:\n\n   * Added automated notification for payment void/refund events\n* Notifies vendors when environmental compliance requirements cause\nsettlement reversal\n* Includes the applicable contractual health and safety violation in the\nnotification\n   * Provides a clear explanation of why the payment was voided\n\n7. **Compliance & Audit Handling**:\n\n* Records environmental compliance decisions associated with payment\ntransactions\n* Preserves the relationship between IoT telemetry, compliance\nevaluation, and settlement action\n   * Supports traceability of automated refund decisions\n* Helps prevent disputes caused by disconnected physical compliance and\nfinancial records\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash id=\"m8q4zs\"\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* `Pending_Environmental_Clearance` payment state\n* Signed IoT JSON payload validation\n* Invalid or tampered telemetry rejection\n* Temperature timeseries processing\n* Continuous exposure duration calculation\n* `40°F` temperature threshold validation\n* `120 continuous minutes` violation detection\n* Compliant temperature payload handling\n* Automated Stripe refund workflow\n* Payment state transitions after environmental violations\n* Vendor payment notification\n* Environmental compliance and payment state synchronization\n* Auditability of automated compliance decisions","tree":{"sha":"602647a2f1169eba543822681665d1612292ac3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/602647a2f1169eba543822681665d1612292ac3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/601aa8cd7b085473c97b2ba48dbff36c79f5fc77","verification":{"payload":"tree 602647a2f1169eba543822681665d1612292ac3c\nparent 781a53783b40bd4c23a324f4ae040deb61426163\nauthor Technical-Dhruvi <2006dhruvi@gmail.com> 1788185435 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788185435 +0530\n\nfeat: Implement IoT Temperature Compliance & Automated Escrow Refund Workflow (#5082) (#5402)\n\n## Description\n\nResolves #5082\n\nImplements an automated environmental compliance workflow that connects\nsigned IoT temperature telemetry with the vendor payment settlement\nprocess. The system keeps vendor payouts pending until environmental\nclearance is completed, validates cryptographically signed temperature\ndata, evaluates continuous temperature violations, and automatically\ntriggers a refund when contractual food safety conditions are breached.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Environmental Clearance Payment State**:\n\n* Added `Pending_Environmental_Clearance` state for vendor escrow\npayouts\n* Holds vendor payment after arrival until environmental compliance is\nverified\n   * Prevents successful vendor arrival from immediately releasing funds\n* Connects physical compliance verification with the payment settlement\nlifecycle\n\n2. **Cryptographically Signed IoT Payload Handling**:\n\n   * Added backend support for TempTale temperature logger payloads\n   * Accepts signed JSON temperature timeseries data\n* Validates payload authenticity before processing environmental\nreadings\n* Protects temperature compliance decisions against tampered telemetry\n* Associates environmental readings with the relevant vendor order and\npayment workflow\n\n3. **Temperature Compliance Evaluation**:\n\n   * Added backend processing for IoT temperature timeseries\n* Evaluates temperature readings against configured food safety\nrequirements\n   * Detects continuous exposure above the configured `40°F` threshold\n   * Tracks the duration of non-compliant temperature exposure\n   * Identifies violations exceeding `120 continuous minutes`\n   * Produces a compliance decision for the associated payment state\n\n4. **Automated Stripe Refund Workflow**:\n\n* Connects environmental compliance results to the Stripe payment\nlifecycle\n* Automatically initiates a refund when a qualifying temperature\nviolation is detected\n   * Prevents non-compliant vendor payments from being finalized\n* Returns the payment amount to the Club through the configured Stripe\nworkflow\n   * Keeps payment and environmental compliance states synchronized\n\n5. **Contractual Health & Safety Enforcement**:\n\n   * Treats environmental compliance as a blocking settlement condition\n* Ensures payment decisions are based on verified IoT telemetry rather\nthan arrival time alone\n* Creates a programmatic link between food safety violations and\nfinancial settlement\n* Prevents vendors from receiving final payment when defined\nenvironmental requirements are violated\n\n6. **Automated Vendor Notification**:\n\n   * Added automated notification for payment void/refund events\n* Notifies vendors when environmental compliance requirements cause\nsettlement reversal\n* Includes the applicable contractual health and safety violation in the\nnotification\n   * Provides a clear explanation of why the payment was voided\n\n7. **Compliance & Audit Handling**:\n\n* Records environmental compliance decisions associated with payment\ntransactions\n* Preserves the relationship between IoT telemetry, compliance\nevaluation, and settlement action\n   * Supports traceability of automated refund decisions\n* Helps prevent disputes caused by disconnected physical compliance and\nfinancial records\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash id=\"m8q4zs\"\nnpm test\n```\n\nAdded coverage for:\n\n* `Pending_Environmental_Clearance` payment state\n* Signed IoT JSON payload validation\n* Invalid or tampered telemetry rejection\n* Temperature timeseries processing\n* Continuous exposure duration calculation\n* `40°F` temperature threshold validation\n* `120 continuous minutes` violation detection\n* Compliant temperature payload handling\n* Automated Stripe refund workflow\n* Payment state transitions after environmental violations\n* Vendor payment notification\n* Environmental compliance and payment state synchronization\n* Auditability of automated compliance decisions","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlYtbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP3IQABjiK4TqzVtGQpg5/Y+J3x9