with\ndyslexia keep pace with fast-paced lecture captions. When enabled via a\nnew toggle in the CC/subtitles menu, the player intercepts VTT cue text\n(via `cuechange`) instead of relying on native browser-rendered\ncaptions, bolds roughly the first 45% of each word''s letters as a\nreading anchor, and renders the result in a custom overlay above the\ncontrol bar. Disabling the toggle hands rendering back to the native\n`<track>` element with no change in existing behavior.\n\nProvide a brief description of the changes introduced in this pull\nrequest.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [X] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5365 \n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed.\n\n- [X] Tested locally\n- [X] Existing functionality verified\n- [X] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nIf applicable, add screenshots of the changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [X] Code follows project conventions\n- [X] Documentation updated where required\n- [X]  No unnecessary files included\n- [X] Changes have been tested\n- [X] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Added an optional dyslexia-optimized subtitle mode that emphasizes\nword beginnings for easier reading.\n- Added a toggle in the closed captions menu to enable or disable the\noptimized subtitle display.\n- Preserved standard subtitle rendering when the feature is turned off.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"a53b5ab80773b5ac612b5ee06b249b0a345df315","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/a53b5ab80773b5ac612b5ee06b249b0a345df315"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/781a53783b40bd4c23a324f4ae040deb61426163","verification":{"payload":"tree a53b5ab80773b5a