:"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDc4MWE1Mzc4M2I0MGJkNGMyM2EzMjRmNGFlMDQwZGViNjE0MjYxNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6","sha":"ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6"}],"sha":"781a53783b40bd4c23a324f4ae040deb61426163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/781a53783b40bd4c23a324f4ae040deb61426163"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183577111?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sanjana2505006","id":183577111,"login":"sanjana2505006","node_id":"U_kgDOCvEqFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:18:18Z","email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:18:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: MWBE supplier diversity tracking and federal compliance reporting (#5400)\n\nCloses #5291\n\n## Summary\n\nThe platform had no supplier demographic metadata, so the 15% MWBE spend\ncondition on the federal grant could not be answered at all. This adds a\nstate-directory lookup at vendor onboarding, a verified badge, search\nboosting for certified vendors, and the aggregate spend report the Dean\nasked for.\n\n## Technical requirements\n\n1. **Directory lookup at onboarding** — `verify-mwbe-certification`\nqueries the state MWBE directory by EIN, falling back to legal name. EIN\nwins outright: two businesses can share a trading name, but an EIN\nidentifies one taxpayer, and a badge on the wrong vendor is a false\ncompliance claim. An ambiguous name match is treated as no match.\n2. **Verified badge on the profile** — the outcome is upserted into\n`mwbe_vendor_certifications` with the certificate number, ownership\nclass, issuing registry, expiry, how it was matched, and an evidence\nsentence an auditor can read.\n3. **Search boosting** — `MwbeVendorSearch` sorts certified vendors\nabove uncertified ones, ties broken by relevance, then rating, then\nname, so the list is stable between renders.\n4. **Super Admin aggregate** — `SupplierDiversityComplianceDashboard`\nrenders the sentence from the issue verbatim: `Total Spend: $1,000,000.\nMWBE Spend: $180,000 (18%). Federal Compliance: Achieved.`\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/lib/supplierDiversity.ts` | EIN/name canonicalization, directory\nmatching, badge issuance with expiry, search ranking, spend report |\n| `src/lib/supplierDiversity.test.ts` | 22 unit tests |\n| `supabase/migrations/20260920000000_mwbe_supplier_diversity.sql` |\n`mwbe_vendor_certifications`, `vendor_contracts.vendor_ein`,\n`mwbe_escrow_payouts` and `mwbe_compliance_summary` views, RLS |\n| `supabase/functions/verify-mwbe-certification/index.ts` | State\nregistry call and badge persistence |\n| `src/components/vendors/MwbeVendorSearch.tsx` | Organizer search with\nboosting and badges |\n| `src/components/admin/SupplierDiversityComplianceDashboard.tsx` |\nCampus-wide compliance report |\n\nFive decisions worth review, because each is the difference between a\nreport and a defensible report:\n\n- **Only released escrow payouts count.** `mwbe_escrow_payouts` filters\non `released_at IS NOT NULL`. Contracted-but-unpaid money would let the\nuniversity report compliance on spending it has not made, which is the\nfirst thing a grant audit tests.\n- **Expiry is evaluated against the payout date, not today.** A lapsed\ncertificate yields `EXPIRED` and stops counting; the view requires the\nbadge to have been in force when the money moved.\n- **A miss is stored as `NOT_FOUND`.** \"We checked and the state has no\nrecord\" and \"we never checked\" are indistinguishable in a report unless\nthe negative result is persisted.\n- **Boosting reorders, never filters.** The mandate is a spending\ntarget, not a procurement ban, so uncertified vendors stay visible and\nselectable; an optional \"certified only\" toggle is the organizer''s\nchoice rather than the default.\n- **`vendor_contracts` gained a nullable `vendor_ein`.** The table\nidentified vendors by trading name only, which cannot be attributed to a\ndirectory record reliably; the view joins on EIN when present and falls\nback to normalized legal name for pre-existing rows. RLS grants no write\npolicy on certifications to any client role — only the Edge Function''s\nservice role writes them, so a vendor cannot award itself a badge the\nstate never issued.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/supplierDiversity.test.ts` — 22 passed: EIN\nnormalization from raw digits, suffix/punctuation-insensitive name\ncanonicalization (\"Rivera & Daughters Catering, LLC.\" ≡ \"Rivera and\nDaughters Catering LLC\"), EIN match beating a differing trading name,\nname fallback, ambiguous-name refusal,\nverified/expired/not-found/invalid-EIN badges with their evidence text,\ncertified vendors outranking more relevant uncertified ones, boosting\nnot dropping anyone, deterministic tie-breaks, no mutation of the\ncaller''s array, the issue''s exact headline at 18%, the dollar shortfall\nat 10%, the AT_RISK band at 15.2%, zero-amount payouts excluded,\nper-category splits, an empty ledger not dividing by zero, and a\nstricter 25% mandate.\n- Both components were smoke-rendered through jsdom: the certified\nvendor listed first with its badge, the certified-only toggle, the\nissue''s headline verbatim with no shortfall line, and the `$100,000`\nshortfall when the mandate is missed. The scaffold was not committed.\n- `tsc` against the repo tsconfig reports no errors in any new file;\n`eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on all of them.","tree":{"sha":"0315215904cd1f6669ce84ee9649905d2ae4ab7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/0315215904cd1f6669ce84ee9649905d2ae4ab7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 0315215904cd1f6669ce84ee9649905d2ae4ab7d\nparent 34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8\nauthor Sanjana <sanju250506@gmail.com> 1788182298 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788182298 +0530\n\nfeat: MWBE supplier diversity tracking and federal compliance reporting (#5400)\n\nCloses #5291\n\n## Summary\n\nThe platform had no supplier demographic metadata, so the 15% MWBE spend\ncondition on the federal grant could not be answered at all. This adds a\nstate-directory lookup at vendor onboarding, a verified badge, search\nboosting for certified vendors, and the aggregate spend report the Dean\nasked for.\n\n## Technical requirements\n\n1. **Directory lookup at onboarding** — `verify-mwbe-certification`\nqueries the state MWBE directory by EIN, falling back to legal name. EIN\nwins outright: two businesses can share a trading name, but an EIN\nidentifies one taxpayer, and a badge on the wrong vendor is a false\ncompliance claim. An ambiguous name match is treated as no match.\n2. **Verified badge on the profile** — the outcome is upserted into\n`mwbe_vendor_certifications` with the certificate number, ownership\nclass, issuing registry, expiry, how it was matched, and an evidence\nsentence an auditor can read.\n3. **Search boosting** — `MwbeVendorSearch` sorts certified vendors\nabove uncertified ones, ties broken by relevance, then rating, then\nname, so the list is stable between renders.\n4. **Super Admin aggregate** — `SupplierDiversityComplianceDashboard`\nrenders the sentence from the issue verbatim: `Total Spend: $1,000,000.\nMWBE Spend: $180,000 (18%). Federal Compliance: Achieved.`\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/lib/supplierDiversity.ts` | EIN/name canonicalization, directory\nmatching, badge issuance with expiry, search ranking, spend report |\n| `src/lib/supplierDiversity.test.ts` | 22 unit tests |\n| `supabase/migrations/20260920000000_mwbe_supplier_diversity.sql` |\n`mwbe_vendor_certifications`, `vendor_contracts.vendor_ein`,\n`mwbe_escrow_payouts` and `mwbe_compliance_summary` views, RLS |\n| `supabase/functions/verify-mwbe-certification/index.ts` | State\nregistry call and badge persistence |\n| `src/components/vendors/MwbeVendorSearch.tsx` | Organizer search with\nboosting and badges |\n| `src/components/admin/SupplierDiversityComplianceDashboard.tsx` |\nCampus-wide compliance report |\n\nFive decisions worth review, because each is the difference between a\nreport and a defensible report:\n\n- **Only released escrow payouts count.** `mwbe_escrow_payouts` filters\non `released_at IS NOT NULL`. Contracted-but-unpaid money would let the\nuniversity report compliance on spending it has not made, which is the\nfirst thing a grant audit tests.\n- **Expiry is evaluated against the payout date, not today.** A lapsed\ncertificate yields `EXPIRED` and stops counting; the view requires the\nbadge to have been in force when the money moved.\n- **A miss is stored as `NOT_FOUND`.** \"We checked and the state has no\nrecord\" and \"we never checked\" are indistinguishable in a report unless\nthe negative result is persisted.\n- **Boosting reorders, never filters.** The mandate is a spending\ntarget, not a procurement ban, so uncertified vendors stay visible and\nselectable; an optional \"certified only\" toggle is the organizer''s\nchoice rather than the default.\n- **`vendor_contracts` gained a nullable `vendor_ein`.** The table\nidentified vendors by trading name only, which cannot be attributed to a\ndirectory record reliably; the view joins on EIN when present and falls\nback to normalized legal name for pre-existing rows. RLS grants no write\npolicy on certifications to any client role — only the Edge Function''s\nservice role writes them, so a vendor cannot award itself a badge the\nstate never issued.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/supplierDiversity.test.ts` — 22 passed: EIN\nnormalization from raw digits, suffix/punctuation-insensitive name\ncanonicalization (\"Rivera & Daughters Catering, LLC.\" ≡ \"Rivera and\nDaughters Catering LLC\"), EIN match beating a differing trading name,\nname fallback, ambiguous-name refusal,\nverified/expired/not-found/invalid-EIN badges with their evidence text,\ncertified vendors outranking more relevant uncertified ones, boosting\nnot dropping anyone, deterministic tie-breaks, no mutation of the\ncaller''s array, the issue''s exact headline at 18%, the dollar shortfall\nat 10%, the AT_RISK band at 15.2%, zero-amount payouts excluded,\nper-category splits, an empty ledger not dividing by zero, and a\nstricter 25% mandate.\n- Both components were smoke-rendered through jsdom: the certified\nvendor listed first with its badge, the certified-only toggle, the\nissue''s headline verbatim with no shortfall line, and the `$100,000`\nshortfall when the mandate is missed. The scaffold was not committed.\n- `tsc` against the repo tsconfig reports no errors in any new file;\n`eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on all of them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlX8aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPfMQAEsrad0bPc1NVJs9QSOJS1Je\n1/TO4OKL9AAlir/92K6ppx2gn8s1GnrQYejOdHePTA2WDvoeHTzo0Dade4Ak83aV\nA9UyWk7Yvwc6ctnNhNIItdNZndL7U9+eU3ShYIXbTS4BxGe2kvMcHT4Gb2gNDJ4G\nW4Nlxm2j56tZLh+ip3uzwOKdvOKzT/W+4PxC+CoWRnKb7ilK6JtKbib5XFYaQS6B\nMS+GJODDmDj0A+Qz2xddoRm0S0+DfEEDz5XXxo5iaqdEKQKs4NgkPCnA8JvSkFtF\nBYJQQWOe0qV+BJ9l+FK9jcwj4nSEmtK6PW2cayMxytMQs4BoMtxgQV5KTclLFwNL\nlaK3Oba/aADbZGcadoZ524eLsXi4Men5bT9yZ+lmtyAqDVqungsYXIn8JUOqtM3m\nU9U0hScsTEFLLMpewNkOTqH8Odkyb+0D3uyzuvDrX786zh5TDKc0g+2cKTvT1b/L\ntruPk8KwJgVmn3DvIZrXf8x5sMFQluxiol6yq7jYk5ueIaxIjMdiRF/WQ4okaGFf\n/ltuIQZY2LVbyXBEuOuKmDidJHZALiiUzC1CKVkFi2LU8mdksq10qFFXbl+5u4g5\njFMG1VCv8teuqPY7dsNvVsWHUas4rGelTLFexyJA6a5xpYTRFCNMzlctN8Zy4VOZ\nkqsXlAwa5AbwOw0AtUKW\n=st0X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:18:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGJhNThjMDgwYzA5NjI5NDQxNjhjYmYxMzQ4MWVjNTQ4Nzg2MzcyZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8","sha":"34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8"}],"sha":"ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/ba58c080c0962944168cbf13481ec548786372f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183577111?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sanjana2505006","id":183577111,"login":"sanjana2505006","node_id":"U_kgDOCvEqFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:17:55Z","email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:17:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: hard-block layout saves that fail evacuation simulation (#5399)\n\nCloses #5290\n\n## Summary\n\nThe floorplan editor already painted fire-lane warnings; an organizer\ncould still click \"Save layout\" past them, which is how a hall ends up\nneeding 7 minutes to clear a single door. This adds an evacuation\nsimulation that runs on every layout change and hard-blocks the save\nwhen the Time To Evacuate exceeds the fire marshal''s limit.\n\n## Technical requirements\n\n1. **Mandatory simulation before saving** — the gate lives in\n`saveFloorplan`, the single choke point every save passes through, and\nis mirrored in the editor so the organizer reads seconds rather than a\nfailure. The editor also re-simulates on every drag, so the number moves\nwhile the layout is being edited.\n2. **N particles routed to the exit doors** — one particle per unit of\nevent capacity (`events.max_attendees`), spread over the walkable floor,\nrouted by a multi-source BFS from every door across a 1 ft furniture\ngrid. One pass yields both each cell''s walking distance and its nearest\ndoor, so occupants queue the way a crowd does instead of being split\nevenly across doors that are not equally close.\n3. **TTE from physical door width** — `0.5` occupants per foot of door\nper second, which is the 2-per-second figure in the issue for a standard\n4 ft door. A door''s clearance time is `max(last arrival, first arrival +\nqueue drain)`, and the venue TTE is the slowest door''s clearance. Exit\nassets dropped on the plan count as doors sized by the asset, so\nwidening an aisle actually improves the result.\n4. **Checked against the regulatory limit** —\n`FIRE_MARSHAL_TTE_LIMIT_SEC = 180`, overridable per call for a stricter\nlocal code.\n5. **Hard validation error** — `EvacuationComplianceError` carries the\nmessage from the issue verbatim, with the computed numbers: `CRITICAL\nSAFETY VIOLATION: Current layout requires 250 seconds to evacuate.\nMaximum allowed is 180 seconds. You must add another exit aisle or\nreduce capacity before saving.` The Save button is disabled and\nrelabelled \"Save blocked\" while the layout violates.\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/lib/floorplan/evacuation.ts` | New: door inventory and flow, BFS\nrouting, per-door queue model, TTE, `assertEvacuationCompliance`,\nviolation message |\n| `src/lib/floorplan/evacuation.test.ts` | New: 17 unit tests |\n|\n`src/components/events/floorplan/FloorplanEditorEvacuationGate.test.tsx`\n| New: 3 tests that the Save control is actually blocked |\n| `src/lib/floorplan/service.ts` | `loadFloorplan` also returns\ncapacity; `saveFloorplan` runs the gate before writing |\n| `src/hooks/useFloorplan.ts` | Holds capacity, exposes the live\nsimulation and the blocking message |\n| `src/components/events/floorplan/FloorplanEditor.tsx` | Simulation\npanel (TTE, limit, bottleneck, per-door queue), violation banner,\nblocked Save |\n| `src/routes/events.$eventId.floorplan.tsx` | Passes the simulation\nthrough |\n\nThree decisions worth review:\n\n- **Trapped occupants get their own message.** Furniture can wall a\nsection off entirely, and \"requires Infinity seconds\" is not actionable\n— the remedy is clearing a route, not widening a door, so that case\nreads `N of M occupants have no path to an exit`.\n- **`saveFloorplan` simulates what is about to be written**, by parsing\nthe outgoing document rather than trusting the editor''s in-memory copy.\n- **Occupants are spread evenly over reachable floor.** Clustering them\nnear a door would flatter the layout, and the pool of assumptions should\nnot be the thing that passes a fire code check. This is a client-side\ngate, matching where the issue places it (\"before allowing the Organizer\nto Save\"); enforcing it in Postgres would mean running pathfinding in\nplpgsql on a JSON column.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/floorplan/evacuation.test.ts` — 17 passed: 4\nft door yields exactly 2 occupants/second, exit assets counted and\nsized, the 500-occupant single-door hall from the issue blocked at 250 s\nwith `queueDrainSec` 500/2, a 60-occupant hall passing, the\nwalking-distance-limited case, occupants routed to their nearest door\nrather than split evenly, a second exit reducing the TTE, capacity\nreduction clearing the violation at the arithmetic boundary, occupants\nwalled off by a vendor table detected, a layout with no doors flagged,\nthe thrown message matching the issue''s wording exactly, and a stricter\nlocal limit honoured.\n- `npx vitest run\nsrc/components/events/floorplan/FloorplanEditorEvacuationGate.test.tsx`\n— 3 passed: Save disabled and relabelled with `onSave` never called, the\nbanner text, TTE shown as `250s`, the compliant case reaching `onSave`,\nand a service-side violation surfaced.\n- `src/lib/floorplan` suite: 52 of 53 pass. The one failure\n(`floorplan.test.ts` expecting no `base_price` key) fails identically on\nunmodified `main` — verified by re-running it against a stashed tree.\n- `tsc` over the touched files reports 105 errors before and after this\nchange, differing only by line numbers shifted in `FloorplanEditor.tsx`;\nno new errors. `eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on every\nfile touched.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added live evacuation simulations to floorplan editing.\n* Displays evacuation times, bottlenecks, trapped occupants, and safety\nviolations.\n  * Uses event capacity to assess layout compliance.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Prevents saving layouts that exceed evacuation safety limits.\n  * Displays clear messages for evacuation and save failures.\n  * Allows compliant layouts to save normally.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"42d3f1a0583a800cef4368f602f3295aeda9377f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/42d3f1a0583a800cef4368f602f3295aeda9377f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 42