eError` carries the\nmessage from the issue verbatim, with the computed numbers: `CRITICAL\nSAFETY VIOLATION: Current layout requires 250 seconds to evacuate.\nMaximum allowed is 180 seconds. You must add another exit aisle or\nreduce capacity before saving.` The Save button is disabled and\nrelabelled \"Save blocked\" while the layout violates.\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/lib/floorplan/evacuation.ts` | New: door inventory and flow, BFS\nrouting, per-door queue model, TTE, `assertEvacuationCompliance`,\nviolation message |\n| `src/lib/floorplan/evacuation.test.ts` | New: 17 unit tests |\n|\n`src/components/events/floorplan/FloorplanEditorEvacuationGate.test.tsx`\n| New: 3 tests that the Save control is actually blocked |\n| `src/lib/floorplan/service.ts` | `loadFloorplan` also returns\ncapacity; `saveFloorplan` runs the gate before writing |\n| `src/hooks/useFloorplan.ts` | Holds capacity, exposes the live\nsimulation and the blocking message |\n| `src/components/events/floorplan/FloorplanEditor.tsx` | Simulation\npanel (TTE, limit, bottleneck, per-door queue), violation banner,\nblocked Save |\n| `src/routes/events.$eventId.floorplan.tsx` | Passes the simulation\nthrough |\n\nThree decisions worth review:\n\n- **Trapped occupants get their own message.** Furniture can wall a\nsection off entirely, and \"requires Infinity seconds\" is not actionable\n— the remedy is clearing a route, not widening a door, so that case\nreads `N of M occupants have no path to an exit`.\n- **`saveFloorplan` simulates what is about to be written**, by parsing\nthe outgoing document rather than trusting the editor''s in-memory copy.\n- **Occupants are spread evenly over reachable floor.** Clustering them\nnear a door would flatter the layout, and the pool of assumptions should\nnot be the thing that passes a fire code check. This is a client-side\ngate, matching where the issue places it (\"before allowing the Organizer\nto Save\"); enforcing it in Postgres would mean running pathfinding in\nplpgsql on a JSON column.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/floorplan/evacuation.test.ts` — 17 passed: 4\nft door yields exactly 2 occupants/second, exit assets counted and\nsized, the 500-occupant single-door hall from the issue blocked at 250 s\nwith `queueDrainSec` 500/2, a 60-occupant hall passing, the\nwalking-distance-limited case, occupants routed to their nearest door\nrather than split evenly, a second exit reducing the TTE, capacity\nreduction clearing the violation at the arithmetic boundary, occupants\nwalled off by a vendor table detected, a layout with no doors flagged,\nthe thrown message matching the issue''s wording exactly, and a stricter\nlocal limit honoured.\n- `npx vitest run\nsrc/components/events/floorplan/FloorplanEditorEvacuationGate.test.tsx`\n— 3 passed: Save disabled and relabelled with `onSave` never called, the\nbanner text, TTE shown as `250s`, the compliant case reaching `onSave`,\nand a service-side violation surfaced.\n- `src/lib/floorplan` suite: 52 of 53 pass. The one failure\n(`floorplan.test.ts` expecting no `base_price` key) fails identically on\nunmodified `main` — verified by re-running it against a stashed tree.\n- `tsc` over the touched files reports 105 errors before and after this\nchange, differing only by line numbers shifted in `FloorplanEditor.tsx`;\nno new errors. `eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on every\nfile touched.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added live evacuation simulations to floorplan editing.\n* Displays evacuation times, bottlenecks, trapped occupants, and safety\nviolations.\n  * Uses event capacity to assess layout compliance.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Prevents saving layouts that exceed evacuation safety limits.\n  * Displays clear messages for evacuation and save failures.\n  * Allows compliant layouts to save normally.\n\n<!-- end of auto-genera