2e8","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDM0NDA3YThkYWEwZmFiOThhMjFlNzY2MTQ1ZTRmMWNlM2JjMDAyZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/d3980cc0db1db9d99d1e39c7028eba25b2e1c46d","sha":"d3980cc0db1db9d99d1e39c7028eba25b2e1c46d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/d3980cc0db1db9d99d1e39c7028eba25b2e1c46d"}],"sha":"34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/34407a8daa0fab98a21e766145e4f1ce3bc002e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183577111?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sanjana2505006","id":183577111,"login":"sanjana2505006","node_id":"U_kgDOCvEqFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/d3980cc0db1db9d99d1e39c7028eba25b2e1c46d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:58:24Z","email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:58:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: risk-priced insurance micro-premiums for hardware checkouts (#5398)\n\nCloses #5289\n\n## Summary\n\nThe hardware library lends $2,000 drones to untrained students with no\nfinancial backstop, so one lake landing permanently removes an asset\nfrom inventory. This adds a mandatory, algorithmically priced\nmicro-premium on every hardware checkout, funds a university\nself-insurance pool from it via Stripe, and routes replacement money out\nof that pool to purchasing when an admin declares an asset destroyed.\n\n## Technical requirements\n\n1. **Risk multipliers per asset category** — `hardware_risk_tiers` seeds\neight categories from `drone` at HIGH (×3.0) down to `projector` at LOW\n(×0.5), each with the reason it sits there. The multiplier encodes how\noften a category is *destroyed*, not what it costs, because replacement\nvalue is already priced in separately.\n2. **Checkout mandates a non-refundable premium** —\n`HardwareInsurancePremiumCheckout` prices the booking, shows the\narithmetic, and keeps the confirm button disabled until the club ticks\nan explicit non-refundable acknowledgement. It also blocks a booking\nwhose premium exceeds the club''s escrow balance instead of letting the\ncharge fail later.\n3. **Premium moves from club escrow into the pool** — the\n`charge_premium` action creates a Stripe transfer from the club''s\nconnected account to the pool account and writes a `PREMIUM` row to the\nledger.\n4. **The pool accumulates** — `hardware_insurance_ledger` is append-only\nand the balance is derived from it, never stored. A running total that\ndrifts from the movements behind it is how a self-insurance pool ends up\nunderwriting claims it cannot pay.\n5. **\"Asset Destroyed\" routes a replacement** —\n`HardwareInsurancePoolAdmin` previews the settlement, and\n`settle_destruction` records the claim, transfers to the purchasing\ndepartment, writes the negative ledger entry, and takes the asset out of\nthe bookable inventory.\n\nThe premium is calibrated so the case in the issue lands exactly on its\nnumber: a $2,000 drone at ×3.0 for a 24-hour booking costs **$15.00**\n(`valuation × 0.25% × multiplier × duration factor`), with a $1 floor so\nnothing is insured free and a $50 ceiling so a survey drone''s premium\nstays a micro-payment. Bookings longer than a day add 25% per extra day,\ncapped at ×2.\n\n## Solvency is explicit, not assumed\n\nA payout never exceeds the pool balance. Routing more than the pool\nholds would overdraw the real Stripe balance and bury the gap the\nuniversity has to fund from another budget, so a short pool yields\n`PARTIALLY_FUNDED` with the shortfall recorded, and an empty one yields\n`DECLINED_INSOLVENT` — surfaced in the admin preview *before* the claim\nis committed, so nobody promises a club a new drone the pool cannot buy.\n`bookingsToFundReplacement` states the underwriting reality plainly: 134\ndrone checkouts fund one drone.\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `supabase/migrations/20260919000000_hardware_insurance_pool.sql` |\nRisk tiers (seeded), append-only ledger, destruction claims, derived\n`hardware_insurance_pool_state` view, RLS |\n| `supabase/functions/hardware-insurance-settlement/index.ts` |\n`charge_premium` and `settle_destruction` Stripe movements |\n| `src/lib/hardwareInsurancePremium.ts` | Pricing, duration surcharge,\npool derivation, settlement arithmetic |\n| `src/types/hardwareInsurance.ts` | Domain types |\n| `src/components/hardware/HardwareInsurancePremiumCheckout.tsx` |\nMandatory premium step in checkout |\n| `src/components/admin/HardwareInsurancePoolAdmin.tsx` | Pool position,\nrisk tiers, \"Asset Destroyed\" |\n| `src/lib/__tests__/hardwareInsurancePremium.test.ts` | 23 unit tests |\n\nThree details worth a reviewer''s attention:\n\n- **The Edge Function re-prices server-side and ignores any client\namount.** The caller is the party being charged, so a client-supplied\npremium is a self-assessed bill. The UI figure is a quote.\n- **RLS grants no INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE to any client role**, and a\n`UNIQUE (booking_id, entry_type)` constraint makes a retried checkout\nidempotent rather than double-charging the club. Check constraints keep\npayout signs consistent with entry type and force `shortfall = claimed −\npayout` to reconcile.\n- **Assets are tiered by data, not code.** Adding a category is a row in\n`hardware_risk_tiers`; an untiered category deliberately falls back to\nMODERATE (×1.5) rather than the cheapest tier, because underpricing is\nthe failure mode that empties the pool.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/__tests__/hardwareInsurancePremium.test.ts` —\n23 passed, covering the $15 drone case and its derivation from base rate\n× multiplier, projector-versus-drone ordering, the floor and ceiling\nclamps, duration surcharge and its cap, untiered fallback, balance\nderivation across premiums/subsidies/payouts, premium and payout ledger\nentry shapes, and all three settlement decisions including a claim\nagainst an already drained pool.\n- Both components were smoke-rendered locally through jsdom: the confirm\nbutton staying disabled until the non-refundable box is ticked, the\nescrow-shortfall block, a fully funded payout reaching the callback at\n$2,000, and the partially funded warning. The scaffold was not\ncommitted.\n- `tsc` against the repo tsconfig reports no errors in any new file;\n`eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on all of them.","tree":{"sha":"9e30cc1c384deb8c9a54a9c6fd9b409da88a4c57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/9e30cc1c384deb8c9a54a9c6fd9b409da88a4c57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/d3980cc0db1db9d99d1e39c7028eba25b2e1c46d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e30cc1c384deb8c9a54a9c6fd9b409da88a4c57\nparent 78087521e474b540532f9b4c046e62a18ba16ae9\nauthor Sanjana <sanju250506@gmail.com> 1788181104 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788181104 +0530\n\nfeat: risk-priced insurance micro-premiums for hardware checkouts (#5398)\n\nCloses #5289\n\n## Summary\n\nThe hardware