00**\n(`valuation × 0.25% × multiplier × duration factor`), with a $1 floor so\nnothing is insured free and a $50 ceiling so a survey drone''s premium\nstays a micro-payment. Bookings longer than a day add 25% per extra day,\ncapped at ×2.\n\n## Solvency is explicit, not assumed\n\nA payout never exceeds the pool balance. Routing more than the pool\nholds would overdraw the real Stripe balance and bury the gap the\nuniversity has to fund from another budget, so a short pool yields\n`PARTIALLY_FUNDED` with the shortfall recorded, and an empty one yields\n`DECLINED_INSOLVENT` — surfaced in the admin preview *before* the claim\nis committed, so nobody promises a club a new drone the pool cannot buy.\n`bookingsToFundReplacement` states the underwriting reality plainly: 134\ndrone checkouts fund one drone.\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `supabase/migrations/20260919000000_hardware_insurance_pool.sql` |\nRisk tiers (seeded), append-only ledger, destruction claims, derived\n`hardware_insurance_pool_state` view, RLS |\n| `supabase/functions/hardware-insurance-settlement/index.ts` |\n`charge_premium` and `settle_destruction` Stripe movements |\n| `src/lib/hardwareInsurancePremium.ts` | Pricing, duration surcharge,\npool derivation, settlement arithmetic |\n| `src/types/hardwareInsurance.ts` | Domain types |\n| `src/components/hardware/HardwareInsurancePremiumCheckout.tsx` |\nMandatory premium step in checkout |\n| `src/components/admin/HardwareInsurancePoolAdmin.tsx` | Pool position,\nrisk tiers, \"Asset Destroyed\" |\n| `src/lib/__tests__/hardwareInsurancePremium.test.ts` | 23 unit tests |\n\nThree details worth a reviewer''s attention:\n\n- **The Edge Function re-prices server-side and ignores any client\namount.** The caller is the party being charged, so a client-supplied\npremium is a self-assessed bill. The UI figure is a quote.\n- **RLS grants no INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE to any client role**, and a\n`UNIQUE (booking_id, entry_type)` constraint makes a retried checkout\nidempotent rather than double-charging the club. Check constraints keep\npayout signs consistent with entry type and force `shortfall = claimed −\npayout` to reconcile.\n- **Assets are tiered by data, not code.** Adding a category is a row in\n`hardware_risk_tiers`; an untiered category deliberately falls back to\nMODERATE (×1.5) rather than the cheapest tier, because underpricing is\nthe failure mode that empties the pool.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/__tests__/hardwareInsurancePremium.test.ts` —\n23 passed, covering the $15 drone case and its derivation from base rate\n× multiplier, projector-versus-drone ordering, the floor and ceiling\nclamps, duration surcharge and its cap, untiered fallback, balance\nderivation across premiums/subsidies/payouts, premium and payout ledger\nentry shapes, and all three settlement decisions including a claim\nagainst an already drained pool.\n- Both components were smoke-rendered locally through jsdom: the confirm\nbutton staying disabled until the non-refundable box is ticked, the\nescrow-shortfall block, a fully funded payout reaching the callback at\n$2,000, and the partially funded warning. The scaffold was not\ncommitted.\n- `tsc` against the repo tsconfig reports no errors in any new file;\n`eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on all of them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXpwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhvAQAD5Qm3W/DWkK9hhm0MNFSuye\nZO10nfzPgALEMifjJi8P7G2OCYyS7crSobRE0p83dHFE5n+agwmVebQBr6uYD7bh\nwEpkXmEZMH5muU/bFMyO5mBHpG9F4RcqM0Pa2EDub5kozcD2WMoVjGGm2qONDAeO\nMfYn8lDsmvcgUYlyAclYQPleUJTrS55fbVOl4xGYfTzgw7GxsP7mmeuautfvDmnA\nBgixkIhBDB1YAGLUUWOrrxKUfos4dI27czcK6nAceVnNxUmDNWbGMkesPwOfOKTA\nzt3JXmxx9ZTmMVHyf+hGceIJyznotMEEpvVcmQBaHx50BlKLqYnFHnInU49u2pPz\nDTi5STqlqJHpRRfjXUUItfBLor1okM2aSaX84pqfQzzxd5SYEFhpSoL9wNRQEvxN\n75PyYUT4maUdt+WSlgIlACHAdMkO4LJu+u6Ii4ttOglqEKMFuKCLl+w9dKjLf2oV\nZMoNtrcKlbDU8C0vkc4sAnptYjXvuFyHjAmDdR9dFimWWDIPruAlROeMFgG2x