:"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sanjana2505006","id":183577111,"login":"sanjana2505006","node_id":"U_kgDOCvEqFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanjana2505006","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/78087521e474b540532f9b4c046e62a18ba16ae9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:46:32Z","email":"sanju250506@gmail.com","name":"Sanjana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:46:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: blockchain provenance for Halal/Kosher catering certification (#5397)\n\nCloses #5284\n\n## Summary\n\nDietary compliance for Halal and Kosher events rested on trusting the\ncaterer. This adds lot-level cryptographic provenance: a caterer\npublishes each carton''s lot number plus the certificate and signature of\nan accredited board, the record is chained by digest and anchored on\nPolygon, and a QR code on the food table lets an attendee trace the\nchicken on their plate back to the certified slaughterhouse.\n\n## Technical requirements\n\n1. **Lot number + slaughterhouse certificate signature upload** — the\ncaterer console takes the carton lot number (`LOT-YYYY-MMDD-BATCH`),\nprocessing facility, issuing board, slaughter date, the board''s\ncertificate document, and its signature. The document is hashed, never\npublished: putting a vendor''s paperwork on a public ledger leaks\ncontract data, while the digest is enough to prove the document shown\nlater is the one committed to before service.\n2. **Written to the Polygon blockchain** — `HalalProvenanceLedger.sol`\nstores one immutable record per lot, keyed by its own entry digest and\nlinked to the event''s previous entry. There is no update or delete path;\n`anchorLot` reverts on a chain-head mismatch rather than appending out\nof order, because a record the attendee cannot replay is worse than a\nsubmission the caterer has to retry. The Edge Function verifies the\nsignature and submits the digest.\n3. **QR code for the food table** — printed from the console, encoding\nthe event and the current chain head. The head means the code never\nneeds reprinting when a lot is added, and a scanner can still detect a\nsubstituted ledger.\n4. **Attendees scan to view the immutable trail** — the scan view\nrenders plate → lot → certificate → facility → board → Polygon anchor,\neach hop showing the digest behind it, and replays the hash chain in the\nbrowser.\n\n## Verification that is not just display\n\nA claim is only anchored if the board''s signature verifies over the\ncanonical payload (standard, lot, facility, board, slaughter date,\ncertificate digest). Anything else is stored as `REJECTED` and never\nreaches the chain — an unverifiable claim carrying a QR code is worse\nthan no claim, because the code lends it credibility. Specifically\nrejected: an unregistered board, a Kosher board vouching for a Halal\nclaim, a malformed signature, a signature that does not cover the\nsubmitted certificate, and a signature lifted from another lot.\n\nThe attendee''s replay distinguishes two failures, because the causes\ndiffer: a broken hash chain (a record was edited or spliced out) and a\nchain-head mismatch (the ledger being served is not the one the printed\ncode committed to).\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `contracts/HalalProvenanceLedger.sol` | Append-only Polygon ledger:\nboard accreditation, caterer authorization, `anchorLot`, per-event chain\nand head reads |\n| `supabase/migrations/20260918000000_halal_provenance_ledger.sql` |\nBoard and facility registries, `halal_provenance_records`, RLS |\n| `supabase/functions/anchor-halal-provenance/index.ts` | Verifies the\nsignature, links the chain, anchors the digest, attaches the transaction\n|\n| `src/lib/halalProvenance.ts` | `HalalProvenanceEngine`:\ncanonicalization, certificate hashing, signature verification, chain\nbuild/replay, QR payload, trail assembly |\n| `src/types/halalProvenance.ts` | Domain types |\n| `src/components/events/HalalProvenanceDashboard.tsx` | Caterer\nconsole: lot submission, anchor status, table QR code |\n| `src/components/events/HalalProvenanceTrail.tsx` | Attendee scan view\n|\n| `src/lib/__tests__/halalProvenance.test.ts` | 23 unit tests |\n\nTwo details worth flagging for review:\n\n- **RLS grants no UPDATE or DELETE to any client role.** Only the\nservice role used by the anchoring function attaches the transaction\nhash, and a `CHECK` constraint prevents a row from claiming `ANCHORED`\nwithout one. Revoking a board''s accreditation deliberately leaves\nalready-anchored records readable: an attendee who ate that food is\nentitled to see what was claimed at the time, and rewriting history is\nwhat this ledger exists to prevent.\n- **The digest function is duplicated between\n`src/lib/halalProvenance.ts` and the Edge Function on purpose.** The\nattendee''s browser recomputes digests to check the trail, so both sides\nmust produce identical output; it is synchronous FNV-1a rather than Web\nCrypto so the same code path runs in the browser, in Deno, and in tests.\nSwapping in a real SHA-256 and real Ed25519 verification against\nIFANCA''s published keys touches `digest`, `expectedSignature`, and the\nanchoring block only.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/__tests__/halalProvenance.test.ts` — 23\npassed, covering lot canonicalization and format rejection, certificate\ndigest determinism and single-character sensitivity, all five signature\nverdicts including cross-standard and replayed signatures, `REJECTED`\nrecords refusing to anchor, chain replay detecting an edited body and a\nspliced-out record, QR payload and URL construction, and the trail\n(including the Polygon hop and the unregistered-facility/board wording).\n- Both components were smoke-rendered locally through jsdom — render,\nsignature retrieval, the anchor transition to `ANCHORED`, the `REJECTED`\npath leaving the chain untouched, and the head-mismatch warning. The\nscaffold was not committed.\n- `tsc` against the repo tsconfig reports no errors in any of the new\nfiles; `eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on all of them.","tree":{"sha":"73a44f062ce1bdc94e42afe9c53b15a7d5f5260e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/73a44f062ce1bdc94e42afe9c53b15a7d5f5260e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/78087521e474b540532f9b4c046e62a18ba16ae9","verification":{"payload":"tree 73a44f062ce1bdc94e42afe9c53b15a7d5f5260e\nparent 5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384\nauthor Sanjana <sanju250506@gmail.com> 1788180392 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788180392 +0530\n\nfeat: blockchain provenance for Halal/Kosher catering certification (#5397)\n\nCloses #5284\n\n## Summary\n\nDietary compliance for Halal and Kosher events rested on trusting the\ncaterer. This adds lot-level cryptographic provenance: a caterer\npublishes each carton''s lot number plus the certificate and signature of\nan accredited board, the record is chained by digest and anchored on\nPolygon, and a QR code on the food table lets an attendee trace the\nchicken on their plate back to the certified slaughterhouse.\n\n## Technical requirements\n\n1. **Lot number + slaughterhouse certificate signature upload** — the\ncaterer console takes the carton lot number (`LOT-YYYY-MMDD-BATCH`),\nprocessing facility, issuing board, slaughter date, the board''s\ncertificate document, and its signature. The document is hashed, never\npublished: putting a vendor''s paperwork on a public ledger leaks\ncontract data, while the digest is enough to prove the document shown\nlater is the one committed to before service.\n2. **Written to the Polygon blockchain** — `HalalProvenanceLedger.sol`\nstores one immutable record per lot, keyed by its own entry digest and\nlinked to the event''s previous entry. There is no update or delete path;\n`anchorLot` reverts on a chain-head mismatch rather than appending out\nof order, because a record the attendee cannot replay is worse than a\nsubmission the caterer has to retry. The Edge Function verifies the\nsignature and submits the digest.\n3. **QR code for the food table** — printed from the console, encoding\nthe event and the current chain head. The head means the code never\nneeds reprinting when a lot is added, and a scanner can still detect a\nsubstituted ledger.\n4. **Attendees scan to view the immutable trail** — the scan view\nrenders plate → lot → certificate → facility → board → Polygon anchor,\neach hop showing the digest behind it, and replays the hash chain in the\nbrowser.\n\n## Verification that is not just display\n\nA claim is only anchored if the board''s signature verifies over the\ncanonical payload (standard, lot, facility, board, slaughter date,\ncertificate digest). Anything else is stored as `REJECTED` and never\nreaches the chain — an unverifiable claim carrying a QR code is worse\nthan no claim, because the code lends it credibility. Specifically\nrejected: an unregistered board, a Kosher board vouching for a Halal\nclaim, a malformed signature, a signature that does not cover the\nsubmitted certificate, and a signature lifted from another lot.\n\nThe attendee''s replay distinguishes two failures, because the causes\ndiffer: a broken hash chain (a record was edited or spliced out) and a\nchain-head mismatch (the ledger being served is not the one the printed\ncode committed to).\n\n## Files\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `contracts/HalalProvenanceLedger.sol` | Append-only Polygon ledger:\nboard accreditation, caterer authorization, `anchorLot`, per-event chain\nand head reads |\n| `supabase/migrations/20260918000000_halal_provenance_ledger.sql` |\nBoard and facility registries, `halal_provenance_records`, RLS |\n| `supabase/functions/anchor-halal-provenance/index.ts` | Verifies the\nsignature, links the chain, anchors the digest, attaches the transaction\n|\n| `src/lib/halalProvenance.ts` | `HalalProvenanceEngine`:\ncanonicalization, certificate hashing, signature verification, chain\nbuild/replay, QR payload, trail assembly |\n| `src/types/halalProvenance.ts` | Domain types |\n| `src/components/events/HalalProvenanceDashboard.tsx` | Caterer\nconsole: lot submission, anchor status, table QR code |\n| `src/components/events/HalalProvenanceTrail.tsx` | Attendee scan view\n|\n| `src/lib/__tests__/halalProvenance.test.ts` | 23 unit tests |\n\nTwo details worth flagging for review:\n\n- **RLS grants no UPDATE or DELETE to any client role.** Only the\nservice role used by the anchoring function attaches the transaction\nhash, and a `CHECK` constraint prevents a row from claiming `ANCHORED`\nwithout one. Revoking a board''s accreditation deliberately leaves\nalready-anchored records readable: an attendee who ate that food is\nentitled to see what was claimed at the time, and rewriting history is\nwhat this ledger exists to prevent.\n- **The digest function is duplicated between\n`src/lib/halalProvenance.ts` and the Edge Function on purpose.** The\nattendee''s browser recomputes digests to check the trail, so both sides\nmust produce identical output; it is synchronous FNV-1a rather than Web\nCrypto so the same code path runs in the browser, in Deno, and in tests.\nSwapping in a real SHA-256 and real Ed25519 verification against\nIFANCA''s published keys touches `digest`, `expectedSignature`, and the\nanchoring block only.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/__tests__/halalProvenance.test.ts` — 23\npassed, covering lot canonicalization and format rejection, certificate\ndigest determinism and single-character sensitivity, all five signature\nverdicts including cross-standard and replayed signatures, `REJECTED`\nrecords refusing to anchor, chain replay detecting an edited body and a\nspliced-out record, QR payload and URL construction, and the trail\n(including the Polygon hop and the unregistered-facility/board wording).\n- Both components were smoke-rendered locally through jsdom — render,\nsignature retrieval, the anchor transition to `ANCHORED`, the `REJECTED`\npath leaving the chain untouched, and the head-mismatch warning. The\nscaffold was not committed.\n- `tsc` against the repo tsconfig reports no errors in any of the new\nfiles; `eslint` (with the prettier plugin) is clean on all of them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXeoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWjAQAHIj4Hkjyp+hYqNA3mDddfeP\nwv6T55laLol/Njoc5xqCWg4ur9Ngwngv/nSkUzIXrn00QCLPRDN9ep0INSu+hLb3\nLOoG0N/huMAKSfxI6Zfb6WfBrNLUXM0fOUx1Ps894U9e9XIKfEuczskO1fV/kngT\nsBrn8TY5rJHHDj/hHeVQ1lYWo7eJuHFiE8YH1L8v7Zqn1k3mNOZnaGa90Ru+PWj1\n4Gck32pdATG762zfgBsYIw4Fi8cfC34BV+0hgI+/L6aTowZayScL9MQISltX6c4Y\ndUIqe/nIljF768g7tQdVmGKny9FNNocbWae9X6NSCe9U+HQN0YRni/nj4UMg0U55\nEZA1EDXuZYk4FB1H1QAbxicIhbFC+LxKtaQK1EKB8LXL+LZf59cBxvpBwZhC066+\nJ/qaxI8COSwrDCP8hsdD1iEmobWuHW+RVrars0JslfE0zyM0kquAoRKkRIBhikJN\nOEW/fEKdLBf8u9bMuqrlVjLQUc+r8+n+1cWTD7E1PuoUqXeNI0GLcX44/bUCe8hj\nX1TsG3a5rYVH7LdaIUo6xd2iBYt8tE3Cqc2/ivfWf/WK5gxGzQaxG4RImkbY3RiQ\nHh656R1RXXPwWsf/IITuGE7UTfqdo1RmEQPDKVFAxNIGozv6vLa8BerHny76E15E\nuZbCO3OJtg4vWfmv0x4t\n=j8gV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:46:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/78087521e474b540532f9b4c046e62a18ba16ae9","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDc4MDg3NTIxZTQ3NGI1NDA1MzJmOWI0YzA0NmU2MmExOGJhMTZhZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384","sha":"5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384"}],"sha":"78087521e474b540532f9b4c046e62a18ba16ae9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/78087521e474b540532f9b4c046e62a18ba16ae9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178648745?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/XYR05","id":178648745,"login":"XYR05","node_id":"U_kgDOCqX2qQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:32:34Z","email":"pctarvis@gmail.com","name":"XYR0$"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:32:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5307 defi yield endowment (#5396)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR solves a major roadblock in high-level fundraising:\nUltra-High-Net-Worth individuals refuse to surrender principal capital\ndue to mismanagement risks. Traditional endowments require the donor to\npart with their liquidity.\n\nWe are solving this by introducing a **Lossless DeFi Yield Endowment\nArchitecture**. This allows a donor to lock $1,000,000 USDC in a smart\ncontract that they exclusively control, generate 5% APY in Aave V3, and\nautomatically route *only* the accrued interest ($50k/year) directly to\na student club treasury.\n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Engineered `contracts/LosslessYieldDonation.sol`:\n- Interacts directly with the Aave V3 Pool and aUSDC minimal interfaces.\n- Features strict `onlyDonor` modifiers on `withdrawPrincipal()`. The\nsmart contract structurally forbids anyone, including the university,\nfrom touching the core principal.\n- Implements a mathematically precise `getAvailableYield()` function\nthat cleanly separates the dynamically growing aUSDC balance from the\nlocked principal.\n- Anyone can call `harvestYield()`, which cleanly routes the extracted\nAPY directly to the Club Treasury wallet without touching the principal.\n- Added database migration `20260910000000_lossless_yield_donation.sql`\nto map the Club IDs to the deployed Smart Contract addresses for\ntracking the lifetime yield impact.\n- Built the `LosslessYieldDonationDashboard.tsx` Web3 UI:\n  - An ultra-premium, real-time dashboard for the HNW donor.\n- Visualizes the locked USDC liquidity and the real-time continuous\nstreaming of yield (using a visual `setInterval` approximation of\nblockchain blocks).\n- Includes an active \"Harvest to Club\" button and an \"Emergency Withdraw\nPrincipal\" button that illustrates the absolute control the donor\nretains.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed local Hardhat simulation of the Aave V3 `supply()` and\n`withdraw()` lifecycle.\n- Confirmed that calling `harvestYield()` strictly transfers the surplus\naUSDC to the club, while leaving exactly the `principalAmount`\nuntouched.\n- Confirmed that `withdrawPrincipal()` safely unwinds the Aave position,\npays out any remaining yield to the club, and returns 100% of the USDC\nstrictly to the `donorWallet`.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\nCloses #5307","tree":{"sha":"f1ddc80427e43db5041419b4bc0f00693dc52cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/f1ddc80427e43db5041419b4bc0f00693dc52cef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384","verification":{"payload":"tree f1ddc80427e43db5041419b4bc0f00693dc52cef\nparent bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499\nauthor XYR0$ <pctarvis@gmail.com> 1788179554 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788179554 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5307 defi yield endowment (#5396)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR solves a major roadblock in high-level fundraising:\nUltra-High-Net-Worth individuals refuse to surrender principal capital\ndue to mismanagement risks. Traditional endowments require the donor to\npart with their liquidity.\n\nWe are solving this by introducing a **Lossless DeFi Yield Endowment\nArchitecture**. This allows a donor to lock $1,000,000 USDC in a smart\ncontract that they exclusively control, generate 5% APY in Aave V3, and\nautomatically route *only* the accrued interest ($50k/year) directly to\na student club treasury.\n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Engineered `contracts/LosslessYieldDonation.sol`:\n- Interacts directly with the Aave V3 Pool and aUSDC minimal interfaces.\n- Features strict `onlyDonor` modifiers on `withdrawPrincipal()`. The\nsmart contract structurally forbids anyone, including the university,\nfrom touching the core principal.\n- Implements a mathematically precise `getAvailableYield()` function\nthat cleanly separates the dynamically growing aUSDC balance from the\nlocked principal.\n- Anyone can call `harvestYield()`, which cleanly routes the extracted\nAPY directly to the Club Treasury wallet without touching the principal.\n- Added database migration `20260910000000_lossless_yield_donation.sql`\nto map the Club IDs to the deployed Smart Contract addresses for\ntracking the lifetime yield impact.\n- Built the `LosslessYieldDonationDashboard.tsx` Web3 UI:\n  - An ultra-premium, real-time dashboard for the HNW donor.\n- Visualizes the locked USDC liquidity and the real-time continuous\nstreaming of yield (using a visual `setInterval` approximation of\nblockchain blocks).\n- Includes an active \"Harvest to Club\" button and an \"Emergency Withdraw\nPrincipal\" button that illustrates the absolute control the donor\nretains.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed local Hardhat simulation of the Aave V3 `supply()` and\n`withdraw()` lifecycle.\n- Confirmed that calling `harvestYield()` strictly transfers the surplus\naUSDC to the club, while leaving exactly the `principalAmount`\nuntouched.\n- Confirmed that `withdrawPrincipal()` safely unwinds the Aave position,\npays out any remaining yield to the club, and returns 100% of the USDC\nstrictly to the `donorWallet`.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\nCloses #5307","reason":"valid","signature":"-----B