","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499","sha":"bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499"}],"sha":"5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/5311c575fb950b8acc6639ec169a7c80581d6384"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178648745?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/XYR05","id":178648745,"login":"XYR05","node_id":"U_kgDOCqX2qQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:28:50Z","email":"pctarvis@gmail.com","name":"XYR0$"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:28:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5306 botnet review bombing (#5395)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR mitigates a critical weakness in our Graph Database collusion\nalgorithms: highly fragmented, distributed Sybil attacks (Botnets). When\na malicious organizer purchases 5,000 fake reviews routed through 5,000\ndistinct IP addresses, relational mapping fails because the nodes do not\nintersect.\n\nTo combat this, we are deploying **Volumetric IP-to-ASN\nFingerprinting**. This fundamentally shifts the defense from analyzing\n*identities* to analyzing *physical infrastructure*.\n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Added database migration `20260909000000_botnet_asn_tracking.sql` to\nexplicitly map the `event_review_telemetry` to known Threat Intelligence\nASN registries.\n- Built the `detect-review-bombing` Edge Function:\n  - Intercepts all incoming event feedback.\n- Resolves the origin IP to its physical Autonomous System Number (e.g.\ntracking it to AWS, Hetzner, or DigitalOcean).\n- Performs real-time volumetric analysis against the last 100 reviews.\nIf >80% of recent traffic originates from commercial Server/Datacenter\nASNs rather than residential ISPs (Comcast, AT&T), the algorithm\nmathematically proves the traffic is synthetic.\n- Automatically overrides the database to quarantine the fake reviews\nand shadowbans the offending ASNs.\n- Built the `BotnetReviewRadar.tsx` Security UI:\n  - Provides a real-time table of incoming review ingress.\n- Color-codes traffic by Infrastructure Type (Residential vs\nDatacenter).\n- Features a simulation toggle that blasts the system with an 95%\nDatacenter botnet attack. The UI correctly calculates the velocity ratio\nand instantly engages the WAF Shadowban state, retroactively\nquarantining the fake reviews.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed the Edge Function locally. Passed mock IP payloads. Verified\nthe mathematical aggregation triggered the `QUARANTINED` status\nprecisely when the datacenter ratio breached the 0.80 threshold.\n- Interacted with the React component simulation. Verified the React\nstate correctly mapped AWS/DigitalOcean ASNs to the \"Datacenter\"\nclassification and correctly updated the WAF UI.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\nCloses #5306","tree":{"sha":"ece243de9d211d913575b31d77c992128d45b1f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/ece243de9d211d913575b31d77c992128d45b1f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499","verification":{"payload":"tree ece243de9d211d913575b31d77c992128d45b1f2\nparent 3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904\nauthor XYR0$ <pctarvis@gmail.com> 1788179330 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788179330 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5306 botnet review bombing (#5395)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR mitigates a critical weakness in our Graph Database collusion\nalgorithms: highly fragmented, distributed Sybil attacks (Botnets). When\na malicious organizer purchases 5,000 fake reviews routed through 5,000\ndistinct IP addresses, relational mapping fails because the nodes do not\nintersect.\n\nTo combat this, we are deploying **Volumetric IP-to-ASN\nFingerprinting**. This fundamentally shifts the defense from analyzing\n*identities* to analyzing *physical infrastructure*.\n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Added database migration `20260909000000_botnet_asn_tracking.sql` to\nexplicitly map the `event_review_telemetry` to known Threat Intelligence\nASN registries.\n- Built the `detect-review-bombing` Edge Function:\n  - Intercepts all incoming event feedback.\n- Resolves the origin IP to its physical Autonomous System Number (e.g.\ntracking it to AWS, Hetzner, or DigitalOcean).\n- Performs real-time volumetric analysis against the last 100 reviews.\nIf >80% of recent traffic originates from commercial Server/Datacenter\nASNs rather than residential ISPs (Comcast, AT&T), the algorithm\nmathematically proves the traffic is synthetic.\n- Automatically overrides the database to quarantine the fake reviews\nand shadowbans the offending ASNs.\n- Built the `BotnetReviewRadar.tsx` Security UI:\n  - Provides a real-time table of incoming review ingress.\n- Color-codes traffic by Infrastructure Type (Residential vs\nDatacenter).\n- Features a simulation toggle that blasts the system with an 95%\nDatacenter botnet attack. The UI correctly calculates the velocity ratio\nand instantly engages the WAF Shadowban state, retroactively\nquarantining the fake reviews.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed the Edge Function locally. Passed mock IP payloads. Verified\nthe mathematical aggregation triggered the `QUARANTINED` status\nprecisely when the datacenter ratio breached the 0.80 threshold.\n- Interacted with the React component simulation. Verified the React\nstate correctly mapped AWS/DigitalOcean ASNs to the \"Datacenter\"\nclassification and correctly updated the WAF UI.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\nCloses #5306","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXOCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE4AQAIPjn5i3gRO/WpZxbXDysc3l\n7Lo8CdutZWlcTegLR4/GTpGDgAQxTr/ZaynJ3jJnJEJ+fMxwYp26wttGSVnH6eAb\nuJruKK8rbBsTvsQ3Wxazcn6lVK6ysgJ2VZwbqbi0YvcpAFNVsjl1s61u//IfzIj8\neJg0da5o+atu2CyQydJc5a2t7FqyJoHHkyD5/26O6l4KuswVhc7y+ANc68g6muag\n6S1mEcEd1kHyVBR8kRDL98wJk/nDTvhE8/sdKSkph3m3UnBUjDQZ1yrmDlnFvCgk\n5qlMn5a3vXHE2SCjsKXA5d+HtGnp+WKblMlqkOduOcwgoozC8ynxS6YnlnALuhW1\nlNNzskDMsFQMeCBM2+vjYFCkM6WDoNxOhLbgdUYTCWn/jwVbv167hBbgQFyqmEbe\nCHuhGDf8glDBjSEZftpoawkwzmjkjLj9XViQZCnH59prYKGB8jCe+vdhLTvDZDRB\nLRrVrLoM+knt9OJVJkB+VNnunfM093lTLOG0de8fW8yy9yTn3hJFGkuyy0sCE8rp\nU9+K8j7If/r0pgzsEQMsshGakfNj2W3k8SmsN2YvntcGrviBZvUasD2umPvB6cE4\nujeHlJsQYPozrX3CUAOYy6sAao10EMq0U8PJKJSg3wh6q8VZqVE0tT+f5jg8jXeS\n8pEkbWhRMdhjilY7izPa\n=YOPK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:28:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGJjYTQ0YTY1ZGRlMTk5MTMwNjc4NTExNTJjNjlhNGNhZmIyYTA0OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904","sha":"3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904"}],"sha":"bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/bca44a65dde19913067851152c69a4cafb2a0499"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225343394?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vachhani-Tapan","id":225343394,"login":"Vachhani-Tapan","node_id":"U_kgDODW53og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:23:34Z","email":"tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com","name":"Vachhani Tapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:23:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5371 gait analysis redaction (#5393)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements an advanced \"Data Privacy\" Video Face Blurring\nPipeline upgrade targeting biometric evasion. Specifically, it combats\nmalicious Gait Analysis surveillance algorithms that can identify a\nstudent based on their kinetic movement even after facial redaction.\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Kinematic Pose Extrapolation (`gaitRedactionService.ts`)**: \n- Created a robust companion service that geographically extrapolates\nthe skeletal keypoints of the subject''s lower body (hips, knees, ankles)\nbased on the detected facial bounding box.\n- **Biometric Disturbance Matrix**: \n- Implemented an algorithmic FFmpeg `geq` (generic equation) filter\ndesigned to target the extrapolated lower body region.\n- Generates microscopic, randomized pixel displacement (jitter) on a\nper-frame basis, perfectly timed to the subject''s appearance on-screen.\n- **Orchestrator Integration (`videoFaceBlurringService.ts`)**: \n- Injected the kinematic distortion specs into the core AWS MediaConvert\npipeline, running synchronously with standard facial box blurring.\n- The resulting microscopic warp shatters the mathematical tracking\ncontinuity required by Gait Analysis neural networks without noticeably\ndegrading video quality for human viewers.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5371\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified geometric extrapolation accurately covers lower body bounding\nregions. Confirmed that FFmpeg equation filters map correctly inside the\nAWS MediaConvert `IMAGE_INSERTER` orchestrator payload.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"954211d17e7bf1205c78986e9f13ba2f6b331cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/954211d17e7bf1205c78986e9f13ba2f6b331cc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904","verification":{"payload":"tree 954211d17e7bf1205c78986e9f13ba2f6b331cc6\nparent 2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7\nauthor Vachhani Tapan <tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com> 1788179014 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788179014 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5371 gait analysis redaction (#5393)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements an advanced \"Data Privacy\" Video Face Blurring\nPipeline upgrade targeting biometric evasion. Specifically, it combats\nmalicious Gait Analysis surveillance algorithms that can identify a\nstudent based on their kinetic movement even after facial redaction.\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Kinematic Pose Extrapolation (`gaitRedactionService.ts`)**: \n- Created a robust companion service that geographically extrapolates\nthe skeletal keypoints of the subject''s lower body (hips, knees, ankles)\nbased on the detected facial bounding box.\n- **Biometric Disturbance Matrix**: \n- Implemented an algorithmic FFmpeg `geq` (generic equation) filter\ndesigned to target the extrapolated lower body region.\n- Generates microscopic, randomized pixel displacement (jitter) on a\nper-frame basis, perfectly timed to the subject''s appearance on-screen.\n- **Orchestrator Integration (`videoFaceBlurringService.ts`)**: \n- Injected the kinematic distortion specs into the core AWS MediaConvert\npipeline, running synchronously with standard facial box blurring.\n- The resulting microscopic warp shatters the mathematical tracking\ncontinuity required by Gait Analysis neural networks without noticeably\ndegrading video quality for human viewers.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5371\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified geometric extrapolation accurately covers lower body bounding\nregions. Confirmed that FFmpeg equation filters map correctly inside the\nAWS MediaConvert `IMAGE_INSERTER` orchestrator payload.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXJGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzacQAEsB7xbsLSr13GpwgaGqU1V0\nrybvEOb5Fo8f2kYU2x4+9kimRJt4vxgQYlajV6lYQp+dL5boclJ1SOvw06ebxRuT\nYz6ONk4yx4Tqldtn4Fi7dLpa0vUP+f7jF4uB356NCS6B4EgYG0QGAaJHCzq/y69N\nLVwzX6NZQljnZmi1BNbQ+eEKuJqRdIhD4hq5eZiyqDOzvjG51EpjUnD2/kKT3/2f\nMu1c+v81T5v5TT9RD404i+91jWsCzGqT4s2gVaoE4W5z/S780DfiVDQ69JKOmanQ\nB99Ettn7gKnPgS9rc5/YpcvRynK5/lW1Ybr7674hUXEAHZKv0V3/U884NeBZcIto\n8jZRb54FY/A0IoQwGvxjZLHfnWsLZ7epDlTBGvJ85MWLj9zb+bqThYvlHF4YFrQ3\nzj6Pz+K6k3IvkMvPN4wXQ6TutioZoVrKS/pBy7bM/nOK0P5CJ7fOZ/vF4xcI289e\n/iR08A3saCrCJZvXflyWI2tUo0MaqngUs58Hc5eX2A1vGLmabqhSPkJIon6PhfQa\n9rnBkjdVRgi6e81Q/XTgkoLOAW2sDWpvYGD/6i8o0TDTxXO5wX5pA/OAd7TaKWoM\n5YisRLv25gXoO0fOWutKTF1VtrP7gnyG+W9erj4BPsRBxwGYiaI0mJPtWkJ3yX8r\nf9F30qlW5jtktqN6FK0r\n=ZvZM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:23:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDNjZDZmMWE5YjIzZmViZDQ5ZDEwZTA0OWQzM2Y0ZjI2ODgyY2Q5MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7","sha":"2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7"}],"sha":"3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/3cd6f1a9b23febd49d10e049d33f4f26882cd904"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178648745?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/XYR05","id":178648745,"login":"XYR05","node_id":"U_kgDOCqX2qQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:23:29Z","email":"pctarvis@gmail.com","name":"XYR0$"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:23:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5305 acoustic dsp radar (#5394)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR solves a highly dangerous failure mode in our crowd density\nanalytics: intentional digital evasion. When students collectively place\ntheir devices in Airplane Mode to hide from Wi-Fi triangulation, the\nnetwork falsely reports an empty room, enabling extreme crush hazards\n(e.g., 500 people packing into a 100-capacity basement for an\nunderground rave).\n\nTo solve this, we are deploying a secondary layer of **Physical Acoustic\nTriangulation** using directional microphone arrays and Digital Signal\nProcessing (DSP).\n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Added database migration `20260908000000_acoustic_crowd_sensors.sql`\nto formally track acoustic density logs and `CRITICAL_CRUSH_HAZARD`\nalarms.\n- Built a standalone Python DSP Microservice (`worker.py`):\n- Uses `numpy` and `scipy.fft` to execute Fast Fourier Transforms on raw\nmicrophone audio buffers.\n- Extracts the 300Hz-3000Hz \"Pink Noise\" band (the exact frequency range\nof human vocal overlapping).\n- Algorithmically calculates total acoustic energy in this specific band\nto mathematically estimate the physical number of human bodies in a\nroom, independent of any digital network.\n- Automatically triggers database alarms if the acoustic density\nviolently contradicts the Wi-Fi telemetry and exceeds fire code\ncapacity.\n- Engineered the `AcousticCrowdRadar.tsx` UI:\n  - An interactive React dashboard for campus security.\n- Features an animated FFT visualizer and real-time comparison between\nthe Wi-Fi telemetry (\"0 devices\") and the Acoustic Truth (\"550 bodies\").\n- Includes a prominent simulation toggle to demonstrate how the system\ninstantaneously detects an underground rave evasion scenario.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed the `worker.py` script locally, passing in mathematically\ngenerated raw audio buffers of 100, 400, and 550 overlapping sine waves\nmimicking the vocal pink noise spectrum.\n- Verified that the FFT algorithm correctly isolated the 300Hz-3000Hz\nenergy block and accurately converted it back to an estimated crowd\nsize, successfully triggering the `CRITICAL_CRUSH_HAZARD` state.\n- Activated the simulation inside the React component and verified the\nvisual alarm states trigger flawlessly when discrepancies between Wi-Fi\nand Acoustic truths occur.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\n\nCloses #5305","tree":{"sha":"eb0deabc532a3c5c1d0dc312469d2d5acc9a88ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/eb0deabc532a3c5c1d0dc312469d2d5acc9a88ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7","verification":{"payload":"tree eb0deabc532a3c5c1d0dc312469d2d5acc9a88ba\nparent fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef\nauthor XYR0$ <pctarvis@gmail.com> 1788179009 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788179009 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5305 acoustic dsp radar (#5394)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR solves a highly dangerous failure mode in our crowd density\nanalytics: intentional digital evasion. When students collectively place\ntheir devices in Airplane Mode to hide from Wi-Fi triangulation, the\nnetwork falsely reports an empty room, enabling extreme crush hazards\n(e.g., 500 people packing into a 100-capacity basement for an\nunderground rave).\n\nTo solve this, we are deploying a secondary layer of **Physical Acoustic\nTriangulation** using directional microphone arrays and Digital Signal\nProcessing (DSP).\n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Added database migration `20260908000000_acoustic_crowd_sensors.sql`\nto formally track acoustic density logs and `CRITICAL_CRUSH_HAZARD`\nalarms.\n- Built a standalone Python DSP Microservice (`worker.py`):\n- Uses `numpy` and `scipy.fft` to execute Fast Fourier Transforms on raw\nmicrophone audio buffers.\n- Extracts the 300Hz-3000Hz \"Pink Noise\" band (the exact frequency range\nof human vocal overlapping).\n- Algorithmically calculates total acoustic energy in this specific band\nto mathematically estimate the physical number of human bodies in a\nroom, independent of any digital network.\n- Automatically triggers database alarms if the acoustic density\nviolently contradicts the Wi-Fi telemetry and exceeds fire code\ncapacity.\n- Engineered the `AcousticCrowdRadar.tsx` UI:\n  - An interactive React dashboard for campus security.\n- Features an animated FFT visualizer and real-time comparison between\nthe Wi-Fi telemetry (\"0 devices\") and the Acoustic Truth (\"550 bodies\").\n- Includes a prominent simulation toggle to demonstrate how the system\ninstantaneously detects an underground rave evasion scenario.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed the `worker.py` script locally, passing in mathematically\ngenerated raw audio buffers of 100, 400, and 550 overlapping sine waves\nmimicking the vocal pink noise spectrum.\n- Verified that the FFT algorithm correctly isolated the 300Hz-3000Hz\nenergy block and accurately converted it back to an estimated crowd\nsize, successfully triggering the `CRITICAL_CRUSH_HAZARD` state.\n- Activated the simulation inside the React component and verified the\nvisual alarm states trigger flawlessly when discrepancies between Wi-Fi\nand Acoustic truths occur.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\n\nCloses #5305","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXJBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIbkQAHHGmWFKpEJ+NldKXD1I2Qxm\nVNmTylgMqZnrO654sm2EnXSN3RSmfAaELNP07Kl00vc5G7JNJbKl2JV+Rkc96LfA\nyxWn82mwJjZwT2IGpdH0EdT8IHoO1bfWk+mxrj+rwSyVWWzXGK6vuST6BKBXEPRs\nfALNaHgg1ACAv00wsAcDELdhLIgWdH4yVoX0W2BreWNsNWd4pEhBuk8gNOVIfEp4\nAxwvMJ8OtG5Dnsn7XDybCgS8WxvtQKHRLiwWQHnpNr1opiDgZILZqlmcRQOuQ5fi\nOtpSGV3rAlMso4v1axELsLwqNKvXNOF/t7cuYit6ztFukeeFAFf4y5hhF1VIFyFn\nIa71Atb1eWoyZOqhyL1W1Ml03vc5RK3jReNoil4HFnXa5jKrt5KA4ZHkaHmKMrcK\n951AaJ9oRmzWgBEG+Rz1ys+Ut5e+Lbyo1enxDX8/vgS+MazjzPZjoGhuFc0TQkGJ\n7qJjvQXI3V+VyZBIiNerC5I5+SG0S537nSZpMpuGqZ1el3ptcnDaKFFAi19FdRQf\nVlQXclcQAk7L/XvfyEw1Q4cFHsBrahJHFAB1hLnZtQB89FHP0IwLAzTbZkjzBbHp\nskVPh1fNcpbdCnJXg7N7mOlM6Kgofl5PkVb26P8pfUj+sJEGCi1MIjQItY3h20O8\nLEI91J0YCRzc6KOmK654\n=kA/S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:23:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDJlMGMwY2M2OGJiYTQ2MzAyMWUxZTk4NTQ3NTk3ZDU5YTM2N2E2ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef","sha":"fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef"}],"sha":"2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/2e0c0cc68bba463021e1e98547597d59a367a6d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178648745?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/XYR05","id":178648745,"login":"XYR05","node_id":"U_kgDOCqX2qQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:20:07Z","email":"pctarvis@gmail.com","name":"XYR0$"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:20:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5304 vendor escrow slashing (#5392)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR fundamentally solves the massive counterparty risk associated\nwith centralized fiat banking rails (e.g. Stripe chargebacks/frozen\naccounts) when attempting to enforce programmatic penalties on\nunreliable vendors. By migrating our Service Level Agreement (SLA)\nescrows to the Polygon blockchain, we can use Decentralized Oracle\nNetworks (DONs) to deterministically and irreversibly execute financial\nslashing the exact millisecond a vendor breaches their contract.\n\nfixes #5304 \n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Authored and compiled `contracts/VendorSlaEscrow.sol`:\n- A robust Solidity Smart Contract that locks Event USDC funds in\nescrow.\n  - Integrates `@chainlink/contracts` to build secure Oracle requests.\n- Contains immutable SLA math: if the fetched drone arrival timestamp\nexceeds the SLA deadline, the contract mathematically slashes the vendor\npayout by 10% and refunds the club instantly.\n- Built the `chainlink-drone-oracle` Edge Function:\n  - Serves as the external REST API Adapter for the Chainlink nodes.\n- Securely exposes the precise arrival timestamp from our internal Drone\nTelemetry logs, allowing the blockchain to reach consensus on physical\nworld events.\n- Added database migration `20260907000000_vendor_sla_escrow.sql` to\nlink Postgres Event IDs to the Polygon Contract mapping hashes.\n- Built the `VendorEscrowDashboard.tsx` UI:\n- An interactive React dashboard allowing clubs to monitor their locked\nUSDC.\n- Visualizes the Chainlink Oracle fetching sequence and the\ndeterministic settlement matrix that splits the payout across wallets\natomically.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Simulated the Chainlink `fulfillSlaResolution` callback locally.\n- Verified that providing an `_arrivalTimestamp` past the deadline\ncorrectly executes two ERC20 `transfer()` calls (90% to Vendor, 10% to\nClub).\n- Verified the `VendorEscrowDashboard` UI correctly animates the Oracle\nconsensus delay before rendering the slashed payout matrix.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\n\nCloses #5304","tree":{"sha":"1a2b888b9987adf31ba6a29616eac3769b664f1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/1a2b888b9987adf31ba6a29616eac3769b664f1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a2b888b9987adf31ba6a29616eac3769b664f1b\nparent 93a1ce74ca8729698d523fcbf2e58fa02f796cef\nauthor XYR0$ <pctarvis@gmail.com> 1788178807 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788178807 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5304 vendor escrow slashing (#5392)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR fundamentally solves the massive counterparty risk associated\nwith centralized fiat banking rails (e.g. Stripe chargebacks/frozen\naccounts) when attempting to enforce programmatic penalties on\nunreliable vendors. By migrating our Service Level Agreement (SLA)\nescrows to the Polygon blockchain, we can use Decentralized Oracle\nNetworks (DONs) to deterministically and irreversibly execute financial\nslashing the exact millisecond a vendor breaches their contract.\n\nfixes #5304 \n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Authored and compiled `contracts/VendorSlaEscrow.sol`:\n- A robust Solidity Smart Contract that locks Event USDC funds in\nescrow.\n  - Integrates `@chainlink/contracts` to build secure Oracle requests.\n- Contains immutable SLA math: if the fetched drone arrival timestamp\nexceeds the SLA deadline, the contract mathematically slashes the vendor\npayout by 10% and refunds the club instantly.\n- Built the `chainlink-drone-oracle` Edge Function:\n  - Serves as the external REST API Adapter for the Chainlink nodes.\n- Securely exposes the precise arrival timestamp from our internal Drone\nTelemetry logs, allowing the blockchain to reach consensus on physical\nworld events.\n- Added database migration `20260907000000_vendor_sla_escrow.sql` to\nlink Postgres Event IDs to the Polygon Contract mapping hashes.\n- Built the `VendorEscrowDashboard.tsx` UI:\n- An interactive React dashboard allowing clubs to monitor their locked\nUSDC.\n- Visualizes the Chainlink Oracle fetching sequence and the\ndeterministic settlement matrix that splits the payout across wallets\natomically.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Simulated the Chainlink `fulfillSlaResolution` callback locally.\n- Verified that providing an `_arrivalTimestamp` past the deadline\ncorrectly executes two ERC20 `transfer()` calls (90% to Vendor, 10% to\nClub).\n- Verified the `VendorEscrowDashboard` UI correctly animates the Oracle\nconsensus delay before rendering the slashed payout matrix.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\n\nCloses #5304","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXF3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANfgQAFuYzl5cuK1cbbIK1Jd3JDK2\n5v0m58dX9FeSKgXVOBRIVOF1c/l2/pXM49+q07RAfFyxl0AnbEkASVUh4AODwyJt\n7bn+AZQLFFIRItJyn4trtJN/TTUkwMpsAyWd6kFnSUDDu/pFJyI7adOiLFK1oLPQ\neZhY/X5H9uJNunVRBNNIyX+hwzm7g0ZoEgL4t36uMsMAzz4SDZohibq3dg4CzDGf\nc+I3+bM9If4Zuy837AFGqKowwC52Jt/zTVUgc3E2E09PF18FMOW+1sCXcqRt5ttf\n76qctlooOP4noGM2fc/ZuTC+R7jUM5UIwEUcliZoouofWKnLgiFdn+fHasY15Jkj\nMIAfX/UA9FLlYUjWnhb9m2jjp7LB9Ti07AmWv8Xpy85PVFZ+3aJJeVeMBBchIpSo\nH7ZJ0pjlP8HYCzxOdshOkmK6I+/wtVskO7z4+RvhC8vuU5kGuxgmYOJys5BRzIxF\nOpHdsmbtoiOVfnzBpEzMatYOZcqyrNliXVV+AOxK4ttSS7+zu4fV7CCpJ1cW1yRs\nGGbXaSLuzBdWnxKLcITP8jJSFdq4RWGQytsyUdUFo9WTE78hsYp3t57d1S9DpZyR\nohDouS1KvNmpA7cnRLXFZySaJNhi/bjcjz/hokJ0Dn4zX3EK3d3YLY8MgqJth0bT\nag9DeROQcEl9NET+h9gd\n=7Yie\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:20:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGZjOGZjMGYzZTRiNjI5ZjVlMTZiMDgzNDhlMTQxMmE5ODc2NDU3ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/93a1ce74ca8729698d523fcbf2e58fa02f796cef","sha":"93a1ce74ca8729698d523fcbf2e58fa02f796cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/93a1ce74ca8729698d523fcbf2e58fa02f796cef"}],"sha":"fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/fc8fc0f3e4b629f5e16b08348e1412a9876457ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225343394?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vachhani-Tapan","id":225343394,"login":"Vachhani-Tapan","node_id":"U_kgDODW53og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/93a1ce74ca8729698d523fcbf2e58fa02f796cef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:17:10Z","email":"tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com","name":"Vachhani Tapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:17:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5372 smartwatch haptic wayfinding (#5391)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements an Interactive \"Event Layout\" Acoustic Wayfinding\nmodule using Smartwatch Haptic Integration. It enables visually impaired\nusers to navigate chaotic, high-decibel acoustic environments (e.g.,\nloud concerts) where standard audio guidance via screen readers or\nearbuds fails.\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Web Bluetooth BLE Wrapper (`smartwatchHaptics.ts`)**: \n- Created a robust adapter utilizing the Web Bluetooth API to connect\ndirectly to the companion Apple Watch / WearOS app via standard GATT\ncharacteristics.\n- Standardized single-byte telemetry commands (`TURN_LEFT`,\n`TURN_RIGHT`, `STOP_OBSTACLE`, `CLEAR`) for ultra-low latency\ntransmission.\n- **Controller Interception (`acousticWayfindingController.ts`)**: \n- Intercepted the LiDAR spatial routing engine. Text-based instructions\n(\"Turn Right\", \"Turn Left\") are instantly mirrored as BLE payloads,\nenabling continuous Morse-code-like pulsing on the specific side of the\nwrist.\n- Linked the `triggerAggressiveStopHaptics` and `handleObstacleCleared`\nevents to broadcast real-time physical stops when obstacles are in the\nuser''s path (translating to sharp double-taps).\n- **User Configuration (`lidarWayfinding.ts`)**: \n- Added `smartwatchHapticsEnabled` toggle in `WayfindingAudioConfig`,\nempowering users to seamlessly fallback to wrist navigation.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [x] Accessibility (a11y) Improvement\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5372\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified GATT characteristic payloads are correctly translating and\ndispatching. Graceful mocking is active when Bluetooth permissions are\ndenied or unsupported.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"627f16aa6c241d9fdc925908ed6a97183bdcac02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/627f16aa6c241d9fdc925908ed6a97183bdcac02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/93a1ce74ca8729698d523fcbf2e58fa02f796cef","verification":{"payload":"tree 627f16aa6c241d9fdc925908ed6a97183bdcac02\nparent 4a8d1dc0cc1dd5d48aa59547d37a58907da3ac0f\nauthor Vachhani Tapan <tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com> 1788178630 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788178630 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5372 smartwatch haptic wayfinding (#5391)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements an Interactive \"Event Layout\" Acoustic Wayfinding\nmodule using Smartwatch Haptic Integration. It enables visually impaired\nusers to navigate chaotic, high-decibel acoustic environments (e.g.,\nloud concerts) where standard audio guidance via screen readers or\nearbuds fails.\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Web Bluetooth BLE Wrapper (`smartwatchHaptics.ts`)**: \n- Created a robust adapter utilizing the Web Bluetooth API to connect\ndirectly to the companion Apple Watch / WearOS app via standard GATT\ncharacteristics.\n- Standardized single-byte telemetry commands (`TURN_LEFT`,\n`TURN_RIGHT`, `STOP_OBSTACLE`, `CLEAR`) for ultra-low latency\ntransmission.\n- **Controller Interception (`acousticWayfindingController.ts`)**: \n- Intercepted the LiDAR spatial routing engine. Text-based instructions\n(\"Turn Right\", \"Turn Left\") are instantly mirrored as BLE payloads,\nenabling continuous Morse-code-like pulsing on the specific side of the\nwrist.\n- Linked the `triggerAggressiveStopHaptics` and `handleObstacleCleared`\nevents to broadcast real-time physical stops when obstacles are in the\nuser''s path (translating to sharp double-taps).\n- **User Configuration (`lidarWayfinding.ts`)**: \n- Added `smartwatchHapticsEnabled` toggle in `WayfindingAudioConfig`,\nempowering users to seamlessly fallback to wrist navigation.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [x] Accessibility (a11y) Improvement\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5372\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified GATT characteristic payloads are correctly translating and\ndispatching. Graceful mocking is active when Bluetooth permissions are\ndenied or unsupported.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXDGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWNkQAHBKYsG3BCQJQCarOgPY9UJq\nZJeAGoO2juRFap+vVvHGeXLUiBZ2NoM/RAaeYopKQiCx+1FJGblhCSr0PLwLCkuP\nrfw8A1miKq64xEom+fngp2g5GntKAPAoZJMC14F8krLGYuPG9GhgwzE6QCrf8/aU\n/6ProzA5qvB1GTqE6YJi/S7Gy8zIS6+Itx/zK8z49kEJoZIhgXH8EQncQS9BSRnj\nO5iyG/Yfm0/z/SLrdnPpv4zC0hKU0CVYdka141Hh3RgwuV/K/8FTgVp0sYmQTFQ6\ncZPc5uCAkN/VtsCXqrd3oWppByyF/wNkvc/UQZxBm3ortIl2KShV41eZVlBjNQGj\n/j5dfOTrg+bthMiTK5fNRg/9yFyBTnF1rKSWtCdd61f7W58j0RP05yZYr14UFjHq\nNLB5Ouos90V1zQ9PqVhhsJgHLdgA