94?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vachhani-Tapan","id":225343394,"login":"Vachhani-Tapan","node_id":"U_kgDODW53og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/4a8d1dc0cc1dd5d48aa59547d37a58907da3ac0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:16:55Z","email":"tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com","name":"Vachhani Tapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:16:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5373 radius anomaly engine (#5390)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR introduces the `radiusAnomalyEngine.js` service, implementing\nVolumetric Behavioral Anomaly Detection on federated RADIUS accounting\nlogs to prevent commercial/illicit arbitrage (such as illicit VPN\nrouting on the Eduroam network).\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Mathematical Baseline Tracking**: Utilizes an Exponential Moving\nAverage (EMA) to establish a continuous throughput baseline for each\ncryptographic session.\n- **Volumetric Anomaly Detection**: Actively monitors time-series RADIUS\nAccounting-Request streams. It mathematically flags sessions exhibiting\ndata-center throughput (>100 MB/s sustained) alongside massive\nconcurrent connections (>500 flows) indicative of commercial arbitrage.\n- **RADIUS Packet of Disconnect (PoD)**: Once anomalous behavior is\nclassified, the engine issues a simulated `RADIUS Disconnect-Message\n(PoD)` via Axios to the MIT core switch controller to terminate the\nsession instantly, preventing massive federated network billing\nliabilities.\n- **Garbage Collection**: Includes an automated memory cleanup routine\nfor stale sessions to ensure robust continuous operation.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5373\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified the Time-Series mathematical triggers (Exponential Moving\nAverages) and throughput calculations. Confirmed garbage collection\nlogic properly prunes inactive sessions.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added behavioral monitoring for unusually high-throughput,\nhigh-concurrency network sessions, with automated connection\ndisconnection when thresholds are exceeded.\n* Replaced precipitation-based insurance payouts with 24-hour\ntime-weighted rain probability.\n  * Added dynamic policy premiums based on weather probability.\n* Added weather probability updates and visibility into recorded weather\nconditions.\n* **Updates**\n  * Payouts now trigger when the 24-hour rain probability exceeds 60%.\n  * Insurance status messages now report rain probability percentages.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"176a67388b5d7802613407efffc50c979cdd8a00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/176a67388b5d7802613407efffc50c979cdd8a00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/4a8d1dc0cc1dd5d48aa59547d37a58907da3ac0f","verification":{"payload":"tree 176a67388b5d7802613407efffc50c979cdd8a00\nparent af6b547b4aa29add7a5ad0e4bf48e0c828f3108e\nauthor Vachhani Tapan <tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com> 1788178615 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788178615 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5373 radius anomaly engine (#5390)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR introduces the `radiusAnomalyEngine.js` service, implementing\nVolumetric Behavioral Anomaly Detection on federated RADIUS accounting\nlogs to prevent commercial/illicit arbitrage (such as illicit VPN\nrouting on the Eduroam network).\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Mathematical Baseline Tracking**: Utilizes an Exponential Moving\nAverage (EMA) to establish a continuous throughput baseline for each\ncryptographic session.\n- **Volumetric Anomaly Detection**: Actively monitors time-series RADIUS\nAccounting-Request streams. It mathematically flags sessions exhibiting\ndata-center throughput (>100 MB/s sustained) alongside massive\nconcurrent connections (>500 flows) indicative of commercial arbitrage.\n- **RADIUS Packet of Disconnect (PoD)**: Once anomalous behavior is\nclassified, the engine issues a simulated `RADIUS Disconnect-Message\n(PoD)` via Axios to the MIT core switch controller to terminate the\nsession instantly, preventing massive federated network billing\nliabilities.\n- **Garbage Collection**: Includes an automated memory cleanup routine\nfor stale sessions to ensure robust continuous operation.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5373\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified the Time-Series mathematical triggers (Exponential Moving\nAverages) and throughput calculations. Confirmed garbage collection\nlogic properly prunes inactive sessions.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added behavioral monitoring for unusually high-throughput,\nhigh-concurrency network sessions, with automated connection\ndisconnection when thresholds are exceeded.\n* Replaced precipitation-based insurance payouts with 24-hour\ntime-weighted rain probability.\n  * Added dynamic policy premiums based on weather probability.\n* Added weather probability updates and visibility into recorded weather\nconditions.\n* **Updates**\n  * Payouts now trigger when the 24-hour rain probability exceeds 60%.\n  * Insurance status messages now report rain probability percentages.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXC3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE4MQAJ+D91Sxzk+dN+3OD/jO8Rad\ndCWu3DTHo1lT2X+UKzAq+wWkhUjPdH6/RNrY8pRchSLrZZ/7zfKI6fgFylckQfGe\nw/gVtN1Mjs5r6wF9OKYeNkgCmWdgDJSEOg4lsW6n88GmPbHCWWs+GP3tbIIl6oXt\n93eL8cIXRLSEsn65UduaGQQeTn5K6eI7zsFHwj7Nuuh7ErEv3YC5xfh/9p4kN2nn\nL0UgCpKUDRajxa4muFyn6ksR6oeb6lU3qhmQEfzzr8VVTfWuDj6yGXpPxY3YKIe9\n7BynnMn8WtctnrpZKkynd97xSAg03zQ3TdXjGUtIUSnOGyblhb0gAiQJvPZStN3b\n1iQGh18xE9OoJBGEblbRvc64D1bGx9TCufqojGWhv11gtwn+eBkS/EwZzDWB6S+A\nbGsguxlsxQLYoBI0XTpFAwrBx9BoQ3aOvLmpD8z/cxL/FzjleCsGN2lUJv5bh58s\n23//UKpFCVdqGcX4sYYP6vi6/UpIQrpmmNPKIbj8KMkrd7TLH5ljpDY/FEnE6UkO\nLToub/hDK7Okn9G+6rllac5/G6MQAYgp1f9kFMYhxXmjgAhizNOp/Do