s://api.github.com/users/XYR05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/XYR05","id":178648745,"login":"XYR05","node_id":"U_kgDOCqX2qQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XYR05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/af6b547b4aa29add7a5ad0e4bf48e0c828f3108e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:06:16Z","email":"pctarvis@gmail.com","name":"XYR0$"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:06:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/issue 5308 fda blockchain audit (#5388)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR solves a critical institutional liability issue where Computer\nVision and IoT temperature safety systems were running successfully, but\nthe raw data was inaccessible during unexpected Health Department\naudits. We have introduced a 1-click **FDA HACCP Compliance Audit\nExport** tool. By querying our underlying Web3 infrastructure, it\nretrieves immutably signed safety logs and packages them into a highly\nprofessional, legally admissible PDF report for inspectors.\n\nfixes #5308 \n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Installed `jspdf` and `jspdf-autotable` to enable complex, client-side\nPDF document generation.\n- Added a new migration (`20260906000000_fda_audit_logs.sql`) to track\n`fda_haccp_audit_logs`. Every time an admin runs a report, it securely\nlogs the targeted Vendor, the Polygon TX Hash, and the Computer Vision\nMerkle root for internal accountability.\n- Built the `generate-fda-audit-report` Edge Function:\n  - Validates Admin MFA / Authorization logic.\n- Queries the underlying Web3 RPC nodes (mocked) to extract the\nimmutable IoT Cold Storage temperature arrays and the Computer Vision\nSpoilage Intervention records.\n- Built the `FdaHealthAuditExport.tsx` frontend component:\n- A highly professional UI for Super Admins to input Vendor Contract\nIDs.\n- Generates a fully formatted FDA HACCP-compliant PDF document instantly\nin the browser.\n- Mathematically stamps the PDF footer with the cryptographically\nverified Transaction Hashes, proving absolute chain-of-custody to the\nHealth Inspector.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed the `generate-fda-audit-report` function to verify the mock\nRPC latency and data payload structure.\n- Generated the PDF through the UI. Verified that `jspdf-autotable`\ncorrectly rendered both the IoT Table and the Computer Vision Action\nTable, and confirmed the Polygon cryptographic hashes were prominently\ndisplayed for legal verification.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\n\nCloses #5308 \n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an FDA/HACCP audit export tool for compiling vendor audit data.\n* Added blockchain verification, temperature monitoring, and spoilage\ndetails to audit reports.\n* Added PDF report downloads with formatted audit tables and\nverification information.\n* Added secure audit record storage and access controls for authorized\nadministrators.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"40d7d6d0021c8e46d92f56dee43c266453679839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/40d7d6d0021c8e46d92f56dee43c266453679839"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/af6b547b4aa29add7a5ad0e4bf48e0c828f3108e","verification":{"payload":"tree 40d7d6d0021c8e46d92f56dee43c266453679839\nparent aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43\nauthor XYR0$ <pctarvis@gmail.com> 1788177976 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788177976 +0530\n\nFeature/issue 5308 fda blockchain audit (#5388)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## 🚀 Description\nThis PR solves a critical institutional liability issue where Computer\nVision and IoT temperature safety systems were running successfully, but\nthe raw data was inaccessible during unexpected Health Department\naudits. We have introduced a 1-click **FDA HACCP Compliance Audit\nExport** tool. By querying our underlying Web3 infrastructure, it\nretrieves immutably signed safety logs and packages them into a highly\nprofessional, legally admissible PDF report for inspectors.\n\nfixes #5308 \n\n## 🛠 Changes Made\n- Installed `jspdf` and `jspdf-autotable` to enable complex, client-side\nPDF document generation.\n- Added a new migration (`20260906000000_fda_audit_logs.sql`) to track\n`fda_haccp_audit_logs`. Every time an admin runs a report, it securely\nlogs the targeted Vendor, the Polygon TX Hash, and the Computer Vision\nMerkle root for internal accountability.\n- Built the `generate-fda-audit-report` Edge Function:\n  - Validates Admin MFA / Authorization logic.\n- Queries the underlying Web3 RPC nodes (mocked) to extract the\nimmutable IoT Cold Storage temperature arrays and the Computer Vision\nSpoilage Intervention records.\n- Built the `FdaHealthAuditExport.tsx` frontend component:\n- A highly professional UI for Super Admins to input Vendor Contract\nIDs.\n- Generates a fully formatted FDA HACCP-compliant PDF document instantly\nin the browser.\n- Mathematically stamps the PDF footer with the cryptographically\nverified Transaction Hashes, proving absolute chain-of-custody to the\nHealth Inspector.\n\n## 🧪 Testing\n- Executed the `generate-fda-audit-report` function to verify the mock\nRPC latency and data payload structure.\n- Generated the PDF through the UI. Verified that `jspdf-autotable`\ncorrectly rendered both the IoT Table and the Computer Vision Action\nTable, and confirmed the Polygon cryptographic hashes were prominently\ndisplayed for legal verification.\n\n## 📖 Issue Closes\n\nCloses #5308 \n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an FDA/HACCP audit export tool for compiling vendor audit data.\n* Added blockchain verification, temperature monitoring, and spoilage\ndetails to audit reports.\n* Added PDF report downloads with formatted audit tables and\nverification information.\n* Added secure audit record storage and access controls for authorized\nadministrators.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlW44CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJf0QAAZBi49RjsCek9KemaJ6uRtc\nrAidlpOOKyieBnvVlTu5nunVtnwuJfhnmPC75c8/QT3SdxKYfmeUCP2woBVyco/J\nuHp/Lf1jMsqtu1Jep260/s9QmYWnZuwqypU8SvPa9nTBvoPYM+2pZBE88e2ukGD4\noMOR3Gqh9diw/3T3t3QF7P2dX9gEVSttkbOSxC3qrv6/sd8/CN7cgmHfmuSjA35I\nkiGLUel5AR4ovo0E5iwPeiGbD+FF3uLI1j8iOO9+AD4IAjgwQthma/1weZ1vA5Yq\nvEatAu0bGXziF9inS2QwpaPhKvg/lwAmgO+BnSHAGBwwJngeRAAz3+GywyvHbLvR\n4uqhY0T+BmB6RDtRTIyjICW4VTCcxxM82KKB3piu4+6BNGVTLygiAnht4wqOnbP1\nzaSkXBrB15K5ngupmMmT4Phn7FKwhQRkxjNcz3OLQpyBC3wNhQPrdKclXzVtnT2e\nvmPlJD+SGacn3Gpn/5fIqbnVCnpVKkt5RIQe0g/9FMBAgxjIsutXemJfJG/awCRg\ncF/KKuZtSmoYytux9gWkWLLRAnPfFVmRWdbgVWmNVp5E7vcouMUKRIGsLYUKAPQK\n9b0y7stYK2OcEyiN3rToHs6hTjFDBrRS8aUgp1YnKs+F6VIpE5IzCu9dELL4Qf4x\nV0vQCSYSTvRXd94ypDTL\n=nX1C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:06:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/af6b547b4aa29add7a5ad0e4bf48e0c828f3108e","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGFmNmI1NDdiNGFhMjlhZGQ3YTVhZDBlNGJmNDhlMGM4MjhmMzEwOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43","sha":"aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43"}],"sha":"af6b547b4aa29add7a5ad0e4bf48e0c828f3108e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/af6b547b4aa29add7a5ad0e4bf48e0c828f3108e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225343394?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vachhani-Tapan","id":225343394,"login":"Vachhani-Tapan","node_id":"U_kgDODW53og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vachhani-Tapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:03:41Z","email":"tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com","name":"Vachhani Tapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:03:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: implement TWAP Oracle architecture for Parametric Insurance (#5374) (#5389)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR replaces the hard time-lock mechanism with a Time-Weighted\nAverage Price (TWAP) architecture for weather probabilities in the\nDecentralized Insurance Pool.\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Smart Contract (`ParametricInsurance.sol`)**:\n- Implemented Uniswap V2/V3 style cumulative math to calculate the TWAP\nprobability of rain.\n- Replaced the hard time-lock, allowing clubs to purchase insurance up\nto 1 hour before the event.\n- Added dynamic premium calculation: the premium dynamically scales\nbased on the current 24-hour TWAP probability.\n- Changed payout logic to evaluate the 24-hour TWAP probability rather\nthan instantaneous precipitation. This mathematically dilutes high-speed\nflash loan arbitrage to guarantee a $0 payout for attackers simulating\nsudden weather spikes.\n- **Oracle Integration (`insuranceOracle.ts`)**:\n- Updated the backend mock to fetch a simulated 24-hour TWAP probability\n(75%) rather than instantaneous inches of precipitation.\n- Adjusted the autonomous payout trigger to evaluate if the TWAP\nprobability > 60%.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5374\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified the math logic for calculating TWAP using binary search and\nlinear interpolation. Checked edge cases for observation arrays and\ndynamically adjusted premium ranges.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"302359d9791038071950bbe55a052d5fae2ff0fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/302359d9791038071950bbe55a052d5fae2ff0fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43","verification":{"payload":"tree 302359d9791038071950bbe55a052d5fae2ff0fa\nparent a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1\nauthor Vachhani Tapan <tapan.vachhani.cg@gmail.com> 1788177821 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788177821 +0530\n\nfeat: implement TWAP Oracle architecture for Parametric Insurance (#5374) (#5389)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR replaces the hard time-lock mechanism with a Time-Weighted\nAverage Price (TWAP) architecture for weather probabilities in the\nDecentralized Insurance Pool.\n\n**Key Implementations:**\n- **Smart Contract (`ParametricInsurance.sol`)**:\n- Implemented Uniswap V2/V3 style cumulative math to calculate the TWAP\nprobability of rain.\n- Replaced the hard time-lock, allowing clubs to purchase insurance up\nto 1 hour before the event.\n- Added dynamic premium calculation: the premium dynamically scales\nbased on the current 24-hour TWAP probability.\n- Changed payout logic to evaluate the 24-hour TWAP probability rather\nthan instantaneous precipitation. This mathematically dilutes high-speed\nflash loan arbitrage to guarantee a $0 payout for attackers simulating\nsudden weather spikes.\n- **Oracle Integration (`insuranceOracle.ts`)**:\n- Updated the backend mock to fetch a simulated 24-hour TWAP probability\n(75%) rather than instantaneous inches of precipitation.\n- Adjusted the autonomous payout trigger to evaluate if the TWAP\nprobability > 60%.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5374\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified the math logic for calculating TWAP using binary search and\nlinear interpolation. Checked edge cases for observation arrays and\ndynamically adjusted premium ranges.\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlW2eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKUYQAJ7XxNPNfJRvCNKOPGMpya9F\nQQYje5coqoxpwh0NZqekJf0UE5ckRKBD+nvtSRN5654NB8wmd/QnIcAhcvqDxemp\nIO9mOJyR5GKrSQgIsK9wDrbRJI2N/inr3bANHVZyeSrtMwdxP/N601f/8QsL1Kxr\nb2DL2pF9BNVvXF2vG1zG9ogdmD8M7T2YFrvNuWar65BMKdb9gCbUAt06fb6hfRyX\nM9dp9Qfl84t5/ma+PkKDcJvjOT4CuAfMfAPK8ACT+dfIBwLWa9HrfJunZcIi8SXi\ncGGISVMx4tWme1AzA0M+2cXL0vJ6auGyfi9CAZGKekR8s8z/Lv470e7FXzKBgg60\n7hwvtLB/HMixRom0OpDysFH9rJi1cln+IuCSah0L2hZJNgvtntiiVyFZxstmELlY\nHd+i6HaBw1eRh7WHYT8/hQIiEzyylqdYVpp8+7SvEFqf/ekmzGzNpHS86xXiNA1I\nIcLW3Xr2MIDQ36VMChTTL6P1Cu0Zh6iZNsbJbzSK7LS/xvZrfqnd7OnpaFb5jikW\nSYz4mEr8VqxRXVk1gIqKsxEf9lZd67HVTiIKDrKEW1453jE5qZKy0YGQOG930zkN\nKOEskeuPT+qZdOAPQgoOeMDkG/HN0Okie4qFLjtWI7mFMG3NIyTizGnx43Kc1WTD\nccZIFsz9fEuuQMxGB2h4\n=TSCo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:03:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGFhOWRmNjJiNDAwMmY2YzNmNjM2MjU2Zjk0N2VjNDJkNTI4MmJmNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1","sha":"a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1"}],"sha":"aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/aa9df62b4002f6c3f636256f947ec42d5282bf43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224525950?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rishab11250","id":224525950,"login":"rishab11250","node_id":"U_kgDODWH-fg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:25:16Z","email":"rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com","name":"Rishab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:25:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tickets): add fractional ticket time-slices with Dutch auction market (#5386)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements time-sliced ticket fractionalization with a real-time\ndynamic-pricing Dutch auction secondary market (#5375). A monolithic\nevent ticket can be split into N time slices; each slice carries its own\nentry window, owner, and regenerated QR credential. Slices can be listed\non a secondary market where the price decays over time via a Dutch\nauction clock, and at the door the bouncer burns the slice only when its\nentry window is active — so a buyer who acquires \"Hour 3\" cannot enter\nduring \"Hour 1\".\n\nThe implementation:\n- Adds `ticket_slices` (lifecycle: available → listed → sold/burned),\n`ticket_slice_auctions` (Dutch price clock mirroring the existing\n`dutch_auctions` model), and `ticket_slice_purchases` tables with RLS +\nrealtime publication.\n- Adds RPCs: `fractionalize_ticket`, `list_ticket_slice_auction`,\n`get_slice_auction_current_price`, `purchase_slice_auction`\n(slippage-guarded, `FOR UPDATE` locks, ownership transfer with\nslice_token regeneration), `burn_ticket_slice` (window-gated,\nexactly-once), `get_user_ticket_slices`.\n- Adds the `verify-slice-ticket` edge function for the bouncer QR burn\nflow.\n- Adds `TicketSliceService` and a `TicketSliceMarketplace` UI: wallet\n(\"My Slices\"), live secondary-market catalog with a 1s price ticker,\nSupabase realtime updates, list-for-auction modal, and purchase with a\nmax-price slider.\n- Mounts the marketplace on the event ticket-pricing section.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5375\n\n## Testing\n\n- Deno handler tests for `verify-slice-ticket`: 7/7 passing (OPTIONS,\nmissing/malformed token, success → 200, window rejection → 409, RPC\ntransport error → 500, event cross-check).\n- Existing shared `auth-middleware` Deno tests: 9/9 passing.\n- SQL lifecycle test\n(`supabase/tests/ticket_fractionalization.test.sql`): 13 pgtap\nassertions covering fractionalization, listing, price decay, purchase,\nslippage, and burn gating.\n- ESLint: clean on new client files.\n- Prettier: clean on all new files. Note:\n`src/routes/events.$eventId.tsx` has a pre-existing syntax error on\nupstream main (verified via stash) — my change there is 2 additive lines\n(import + mount) that don''t touch the broken region.\n- TypeScript: zero errors in the new files (repo-wide `tsc` has\npre-existing errors elsewhere).\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — the marketplace renders in the existing event ticket-pricing\nsection; no static screenshots captured.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added fractional ticket slices for eligible event tickets.\n- Added a marketplace to view, list, and purchase ticket slices through\ndescending-price auctions.\n  - Added live pricing updates and real-time marketplace activity.\n- Added slice-based ticket verification and redemption during the valid\nentry window.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n- Improved validation and error handling for invalid, unavailable, or\nmismatched ticket slices.\n\n- **Tests**\n- Added coverage for fractionalization, auctions, purchases, pricing,\nand slice redemption.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"e9d1b99b089bf685ca8e2b9103524f9095574dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/e9d1b99b089bf685ca8e2b9103524f9095574dac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1","verification":{"payload":"tree e9d1b99b089bf685ca8e2b9103524f9095574dac\nparent 1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94\nauthor Rishab <rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com> 1788175516 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788175516 +0530\n\nfeat(tickets): add fractional ticket time-slices with Dutch auction market (#5386)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements time-sliced ticket fractionalization with a real-time\ndynamic-pricing Dutch auction secondary market (#5375). A monolithic\nevent ticket can be split into N time slices; each slice carries its own\nentry window, owner, and regenerated QR credential. Slices can be listed\non a secondary market where the price decays over time via a Dutch\nauction clock, and at the door the bouncer burns the slice only when its\nentry window is active — so a buyer who acquires \"Hour 3\" cannot enter\nduring \"Hour 1\".\n\nThe implementation:\n- Adds `ticket_slices` (lifecycle: available → listed → sold/burned),\n`ticket_slice_auctions` (Dutch price clock mirroring the existing\n`dutch_auctions` model), and `ticket_slice_purchases` tables with RLS +\nrealtime publication.\n- Adds RPCs: `fractionalize_ticket`, `list_ticket_slice_auction`,\n`get_slice_auction_current_price`, `purchase_slice_auction`\n(slippage-guarded, `FOR UPDATE` locks, ownership transfer with\nslice_token regeneration), `burn_ticket_slice` (window-gated,\nexactly-once), `get_user_ticket_slices`.\n- Adds the `verify-slice-ticket` edge function for the bouncer QR burn\nflow.\n- Adds `TicketSliceService` and a `TicketSliceMarketplace` UI: wallet\n(\"My Slices\"), live secondary-market catalog with a 1s price ticker,\nSupabase realtime updates, list-for-auction modal, and purchase with a\nmax-price slider.\n- Mounts the marketplace on the event ticket-pricing section.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5375\n\n## Testing\n\n- Deno handler tests for `verify-slice-ticket`: 7/7 passing (OPTIONS,\nmissing/malformed token, success → 200, window rejection → 409, RPC\ntransport error → 500, event cross-check).\n- Existing shared `auth-middleware` Deno tests: 9/9 passing.\n- SQL lifecycle test\n(`supabase/tests/ticket_fractionalization.test.sql`): 13 pgtap\nassertions covering fractionalization, listing, price decay, purchase,\nslippage, and burn gating.\n- ESLint: clean on new client files.\n- Prettier: clean on all new files. Note:\n`src/routes/events.$eventId.tsx` has a pre-existing syntax error on\nupstream main (verified via stash) — my change there is 2 additive lines\n(import + mount) that don''t touch the broken region.\n- TypeScript: zero errors in the new files (repo-wide `tsc` has\npre-existing errors elsewhere).\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — the marketplace renders in the existing event ticket-pricing\nsection; no static screenshots captured.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added fractional ticket slices for eligible event tickets.\n- Added a marketplace to view, list, and purchase ticket slices through\ndescending-price auctions.\n  - Added live pricing updates and real-time marketplace activity.\n- Added slice-based ticket verification and redemption during the valid\nentry window.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n- Improved validation and error handling for invalid, unavailable, or\nmismatched ticket slices.\n\n- **Tests**\n- Added coverage for fractionalization, auctions, purchases, pricing,\nand slice redemption.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlWScCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAydEQAErksKbN2hr756IWj1YOsLPX\n6E99vEeUWUXPonnC3niPltzEniK2hR0GXXJ2DF0J/i+pxZefomVZmBUjZJCcG2H4\nQ0rErlUUVkqsRn6l0aflOxCzFJpVBnyg8kkJz49PaCndjZs1x6yhYejWdUhS5aGQ\nJMUjR98dH+L4AWU352v+3/+BJGxRh48ELW6fUgOblUFDGAhUFi1CA3ECEpSsvDUY\n5NE6KtcYWqZsQhninpwNThRFU8SxFVPdhjom+/WJGxNSSPVBJPBb95GLoFO5y6Hf\nZfbUKSVY2BqhVZF3e/DSr3U+a4bWk+O7FgycVoZF/qxyAhtH2y0wuidYMAsrniUW\nG9OjT33wDmkLPcnfKMit8I174qC+aV+E69agOPIWuKj4OnMCSM5CPRfd/6tH8cTz\nihKpcIo0dyADjnI0g4OzApharvhdUFnbiRx8WFRfIcB0ayxutqsODLO0BAQpv2an\nEkqfk6MfYnatJw1nLvG4/qJxdeKASpg7Lo7LLASk7bzZGQBFEPw9mM9ig8+MI+XA\nUhdekOWQL7w5gBd4Perl0RgCn3BDIKOgN9V5mLgX+LE70IshsIvWcd1fmXFmkxRD\nuD2EneFMhndIVX3uogecLj+bFvqM+GEXuwIaNElgDlVTKIH4VTTmx8V7LvkgvPIN\n25sVYUrxYeH/lUDugC1G\n=9OoJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T11:25:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGE0N2NjYmRjZTY5N2YxZmFlNDgzNTk1ZjI1N2Y4Y2NiYjRmMmQzYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94","sha":"1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94"}],"sha":"a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/a47ccbdce697f1fae483595f257f8ccbb4f2d3b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224525950?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rishab11250","id":224525950,"login":"rishab11250","node_id":"U_kgDODWH-fg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:18:14Z","email":"rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com","name":"Rishab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:18:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): add token replay detection via session binding (#5385)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements automated token replay detection (SSO token replay attack\nsimulation). Since Supabase Auth mints the JWTs, each authenticated\ndevice session is bound to the browser fingerprint and /24 IP subnet\nthat minted it. When a JWT is presented from a different context (a\nconfirmed mismatch on both dimensions), the underlying auth session is\nrevoked and the request is rejected, forcing a global logout.\n\nThe implementation:\n- Adds `fingerprint_hash` + `ip_subnet_hash` columns to\n`device_sessions` (HMAC-SHA256 digests only — raw fingerprints and IPs\nare never persisted).\n- Adds a `detect_session_replay` RPC that compares a request''s context\nagainst the session binding and revokes the session on confirmed replay.\n- Captures the fingerprint and IP subnet in the\n`register-device-session` edge function.\n- Adds `verifyAuthWithReplayDetection` to the shared auth middleware,\nthrowing `SessionReplayError` on a confirmed replay. The check is\nfail-open: sessions minted before this feature, or requests lacking\nfingerprint/subnet data, are never locked out.\n- Sends `x-device-fingerprint` from the client when registering a device\nsession.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5376\n\n## Testing\n\n- Deno tests for the shared auth middleware: 9/9 passing (4 existing + 5\nnew replay-detection cases covering ok pass-through, confirmed-replay\nrejection, RPC failure fail-open, and missing fingerprint/IP fail-open).\n- ESLint: clean on the changed client file.\n- Prettier: clean on all changed files.\n- TypeScript: `src/lib/deviceSession.ts` typechecks clean.\n\nNote: the full edge test suite and repo-wide `tsc` have pre-existing\nfailures on upstream main (e.g.\n`supabase/functions/_shared/academicCalendar.ts` syntax error, unrelated\nJSX errors) that are outside this change.\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — backend/security change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"ad33992f4adfa9d9e585812734c108f25af5a854","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/ad33992f4adfa9d9e585812734c108f25af5a854"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94","verification":{"payload":"tree ad33992f4adfa9d9e585812734c108f25af5a854\nparent df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac\nauthor Rishab <rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com> 1788171494 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788171494 +0530\n\nfeat(security): add token replay detection via session binding (#5385)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements automated token replay detection (SSO token replay attack\nsimulation). Since Supabase Auth mints the JWTs, each authenticated\ndevice session is bound to the browser fingerprint and /24 IP subnet\nthat minted it. When a JWT is presented from a different context (a\nconfirmed mismatch on both dimensions), the underlying auth session is\nrevoked and the request is rejected, forcing a global logout.\n\nThe implementation:\n- Adds `fingerprint_hash` + `ip_subnet_hash` columns to\n`device_sessions` (HMAC-SHA256 digests only — raw fingerprints and IPs\nare never persisted).\n- Adds a `detect_session_replay` RPC that compares a request''s context\nagainst the session binding and revokes the session on confirmed replay.\n- Captures the fingerprint and IP subnet in the\n`register-device-session` edge function.\n- Adds `verifyAuthWithReplayDetection` to the shared auth middleware,\nthrowing `SessionReplayError` on a confirmed replay. The check is\nfail-open: sessions minted before this feature, or requests lacking\nfingerprint/subnet data, are never locked out.\n- Sends `x-device-fingerprint` from the client when registering a device\nsession.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5376\n\n## Testing\n\n- Deno tests for the shared auth middleware: 9/9 passing (4 existing + 5\nnew replay-detection cases covering ok pass-through, confirmed-replay\nrejection, RPC failure fail-open, and missing fingerprint/IP fail-open).\n- ESLint: clean on the changed client file.\n- Prettier: clean on all changed files.\n- TypeScript: `src/lib/deviceSession.ts` typechecks clean.\n\nNote: the full edge test suite and repo-wide `tsc` have pre-existing\nfailures on upstream main (e.g.\n`supabase/functions/_shared/academicCalendar.ts` syntax error, unrelated\nJSX errors) that are outside this change.\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — backend/security change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [ ] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlVTmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADc4QAJDYBkOyTjaGhiTkSkY6vmRV\nN6IwtzpfvHGSontSkKPuFI95WbxMp4x8KtPOZcE7hBDo97QWM2nLSxDbG6JqMKkA\nBLhvtGviRKbGvNgbGKOKr1zQWCTJh683ciIJOp9PeBWjISYOSY0F48X2fToTfPux\nnNZMWAkaDv62YIbeTg4cHN3Ign3t8YYXIQx5Xvg3FAE2Mu62iCBpEr7erkEqS4C5\nVYBDZ21HXRiT4JQ80U24BTuZcxryPEPP017bjob1qEGdbjD2sLRo5uda0bQb5dI6\n/fRUlBPpYJcGBAbgAMEczuW7Yl33iyWda9vQIT4XtJWeFFxt+cmZM3eq02NuKx5u\n5430Wwsj6PxJjRmGX+BffDH9/9VlnTlVphQEHRjLGJo4t0xvmqd2MUMtaB7WB35q\nF0R7GdTHCFl6/GdKxvXYhW6EpFPK+TTsQop+iCbhm448nsSyX5Qz8v/i5kKEZqrg\nKMzHf44xA88tIJLIuggxODmGYebJMWg2l0qCMpWT04rN8lbvwTEUWBURpajYbj2D\ne3tRz7xSc1dlzdWKZFP/gVEoin+Hc2aHAuf95unIlrsqIpQKzyLXPDBdxnJ4VRNF\nW0DXlAftShDRJSjXydqDdyW+XF+2v4PYVc723j1B2gRsRYNWREDAqBXbi6Putg8U\nqb/pJvSl0AItNHQjnrm/\n=4Kof\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T10:18:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDEzMjljMTQzYjY4YzgxZTE5YTEyNTZiZmY5YTY3MDZmMDA1MTljOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac","sha":"df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac"}],"sha":"1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/1329c143b68c81e19a1256bff9a6706f00519c94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261348571?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/revatikadam0607","id":261348571,"login":"revatikadam0607","node_id":"U_kgDOD5Pc2w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:17:58Z","email":"revatikadam0607@gmail.com","name":"Revati Kadam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:17:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: enforce attendance verification state machine (#5384)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplement a formal attendance state machine for event participation so\nRSVP,\ncheck-in, and attendance states cannot be modified arbitrarily.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add attendance_state to event RSVPs.\n- Define explicit attendance transitions:\n  RSVP -> Confirmed -> Checked-In -> Attended.\n- Add cancellation and invalidation transitions.\n- Add immutable attendance state transition history.\n- Add a centralized transactional attendance transition RPC.\n- Lock RSVP rows during transitions to prevent concurrent state\ncorruption.\n- Make duplicate check-ins idempotent.\n- Validate RSVP eligibility and current event state before check-in.\n- Require organizer authorization for privileged attendance transitions.\n- Update organizer check-in to use the centralized transition RPC.\n- Update geofenced check-in to use the same state machine.\n- Keep waitlist promotion synchronized with the confirmed state.\n- Keep RSVP cancellation synchronized with the cancelled state.\n- Add tests for valid, invalid, duplicate, and state-machine\ntransitions.\n\n## Concurrency\n\nAttendance transitions use row-level locking on the RSVP record,\nensuring that\nsimultaneous check-in requests cannot both create separate successful\ntransitions for the same attendee.\n\n## Auditability\n\nEvery successful state transition is recorded with the previous state,\nnew\nstate, actor, timestamp, and reason.\n\nExisting RSVP and waitlist behavior remains compatible with the new\nattendance\nstate machine.\n\nI''ve resolved the issue. Kindly review it, and if everything looks good,\nplease consider merging the corresponding PR.\n\nCloses #5225","tree":{"sha":"dea4a07454d82d7451ae298a858432f79e8529f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/dea4a07454d82d7451ae298a858432f79e8529f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac","verification":{"payload":"tree dea4a07454d82d7451ae298a858432f79e8529f4\nparent 48a5ed65c7162073aa883f198b97e33cc2c8fc90\nauthor Revati Kadam <revatikadam0607@gmail.com> 1788171478 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788171478 +0530\n\nfix: enforce attendance verification state machine (#5384)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplement a formal attendance state machine for event participation so\nRSVP,\ncheck-in, and attendance states cannot be modified arbitrarily.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add attendance_state to event RSVPs.\n- Define explicit attendance transitions:\n  RSVP -> Confirmed -> Checked-In -> Attended.\n- Add cancellation and invalidation transitions.\n- Add immutable attendance state transition history.\n- Add a centralized transactional attendance transition RPC.\n- Lock RSVP rows during transitions to prevent concurrent state\ncorruption.\n- Make duplicate check-ins idempotent.\n- Validate RSVP eligibility and current event state before check-in.\n- Require organizer authorization for privileged attendance transitions.\n- Update organizer check-in to use the centralized transition RPC.\n- Update geofenced check-in to use the same state machine.\n- Keep waitlist promotion synchronized with the confirmed state.\n- Keep RSVP cancellation synchronized with the cancelled state.\n- Add tests for valid, invalid, duplicate, and state-machine\ntransitions.\n\n## Concurrency\n\nAttendance transitions use row-level locking on the RSVP record,\nensuring that\nsimultaneous check-in requests cannot both create separate successful\ntransitions for the same attendee.\n\n## Auditability\n\nEvery successful state transition is recorded with the previous state,\nnew\nstate, actor, timestamp, and reason.\n\nExisting RSVP and waitlist behavior remains compatible with the new\nattendance\nstate machine.\n\nI''ve resolved the issue. Kindly review it, and if everything looks good,\nplease consider merging the corresponding PR.\n\nCloses #5225","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlVTWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAazwQABInBCSqr+hrPZmmcynHmNMo\nItBoLm1j63U1kkqF8euHKKdb218YkPSy4jjSmm+cHfDmYIa7tEkcDlnaZmkvcnke\n6VNkN93/Sf3Qb81IEgbotppOV/BLGqH7dUSmzPTg1J9rV6VS/dncSDnrPqzF13DV\n7VZEGP/CrRzJYKBv1dd81gcST3Wiuda6YtUfLMMRK3QOSPJs1JMcSxfJnwobK4mL\nKstWMicTjNBkXFYVe6WKqx39zvVbKR6RS+GqZhPJlWNGXO9PwRhHfUuELJI0o7vb\n0hGu89cakOwppRO1q+Ty4aRpgRPEQuuowr973wrIYlJvS2ozQZfaO9rJt5pZASSI\nhEH+MdNkcCN3zdvaM5XOhqgqoasj4Co4bdhLrQ7g0UVo+jCTMmaQQyPQ8nG5Vitj\nMBP4gaBIgnXjHE7BQQfaB2ZMylINZiVENSbHKmMSwA/a+KhKe46QHJKQP7Jj8wKK\n84W7U7333wpwVY6xlNADJjjISQikw8jXmvLOINqZufm/n9UyklxPAADYyn61hexF\nfQnTlKeWSSnR/NuMmgxyvHzLSnyAGPk9sBGtTOVbIBJdNHfgcqO8JccfdVa4GnPX\nJUPn2yQJ8aXQQb35bcA4bfYwtaZ/esGZYIgV5UeiXuRRB1E6m+CXcsuaOOyC+aOI\nDnkJEp9gMmgn7CkF+E1d\n=ZuXV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T10:17:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKGRmOWRiMDc5OGI5NmM4YWQ5ZTExYjE3YzJlMTI3NzM5YjkwZTFjYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/48a5ed65c7162073aa883f198b97e33cc2c8fc90","sha":"48a5ed65c7162073aa883f198b97e33cc2c8fc90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/48a5ed65c7162073aa883f198b97e33cc2c8fc90"}],"sha":"df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/df9db0798b96c8ad9e11b17c2e127739b90e1cac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261348571?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/revatikadam0607","id":261348571,"login":"revatikadam0607","node_id":"U_kgDOD5Pc2w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/revatikadam0607","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/48a5ed65c7162073aa883f198b97e33cc2c8fc90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:43:55Z","email":"revatikadam0607@gmail.com","name":"Revati Kadam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:43:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: keep event search index synchronized with event versions (#5383)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix event search index synchronization so event discovery remains\nconsistent\nwhen events are created, updated, cancelled, deleted, or when\nsynchronization\nrequests are retried out of order.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add event search synchronization version tracking.\n- Reuse the existing event OCC version for search ordering.\n- Store synchronization versions in the Meilisearch DLQ.\n- Prevent duplicate DLQ entries for the same event version.\n- Ignore stale event synchronization requests.\n- Prevent stale DLQ retries from overwriting newer event data.\n- Include deleted_at and synchronization version in event search\ndocuments.\n- Exclude cancelled, archived, and soft-deleted events from active\nsearch.\n- Update bulk synchronization to include the new event search state.\n- Add tests covering create/update synchronization, cancellation,\ndeletion,\n  failed synchronization, retries, and out-of-order updates.\n\n## Result\n\nNew event records are synchronized through the existing database webhook\npipeline.\n\nUpdated event records cannot be overwritten by older synchronization\nevents.\n\nCancelled and soft-deleted events are excluded from active search\nresults.\n\nFailed synchronization remains retryable through the existing DLQ\nmechanism,\nwhile stale retries are safely ignored.\n \nI''ve resolved the issue. Kindly review it, and if everything looks good,\nplease consider merging the corresponding PR.\n\nCloses #5224 \n@krushit1307","tree":{"sha":"962ffdd8c9f89b405f380c32a87be215bf3b0a6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/962ffdd8c9f89b405f380c32a87be215bf3b0a6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/48a5ed65c7162073aa883f198b97e33cc2c8fc90","verification":{"payload":"tree 962ffdd8c9f89b405f380c32a87be215bf3b0a6b\nparent 64f96069d03d3ec1ae3c13a34e188cda8269fd6a\nauthor Revati Kadam <revatikadam0607@gmail.com> 1788169435 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788169435 +0530\n\nfix: keep event search index synchronized with event versions (#5383)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix event search index synchronization so event discovery remains\nconsistent\nwhen events are created, updated, cancelled, deleted, or when\nsynchronization\nrequests are retried out of order.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add event search synchronization version tracking.\n- Reuse the existing event OCC version for search ordering.\n- Store synchronization versions in the Meilisearch DLQ.\n- Prevent duplicate DLQ entries for the same event version.\n- Ignore stale event synchronization requests.\n- Prevent stale DLQ retries from overwriting newer event data.\n- Include deleted_at and synchronization version in event search\ndocuments.\n- Exclude cancelled, archived, and soft-deleted events from active\nsearch.\n- Update bulk synchronization to include the new event search state.\n- Add tests covering create/update synchronization, cancellation,\ndeletion,\n  failed synchronization, retries, and out-of-order updates.\n\n## Result\n\nNew event records are synchronized through the existing database webhook\npipeline.\n\nUpdated event records cannot be overwritten by older synchronization\nevents.\n\nCancelled and soft-deleted events are excluded from active search\nresults.\n\nFailed synchronization remains retryable through the existing DLQ\nmechanism,\nwhile stale retries are safely ignored.\n \nI''ve resolved the issue. Kindly review it, and if everything looks good,\nplease consider merging the corresponding PR.\n\nCloses #5224 \n@krushit1307","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUzbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIpUQAEpJ9oYn1QMDnotwP/NGowk4\nCmgyY+A8iYqjL/0+4zZuMQmaWKx/e5l4GxM8808J+ymkCCyGK+0ZRmYZoboASdmL\nmM7O561aNS+TFdxYpFN0MBqMNvutvD5hMDg06diGRi2hijojEESHL4o6AV8q6NL7\n0q7f3KzYKODVqaSb0G5mPUxa5vutlg9gatsT6fZfLVRq5D8q6mleF4tXPwfzp39s\nR9dRna/IH/dAd2VQMjfkriBBSgBlDXPDWxEHcOYrR/LzzLBHwHBboDOt0XvEZVNP\nRObDjYyHxrg6qbUvEQ7TKf3nCbFd9BIBNgeSFHmfMIPml7tkRW+kcqyX0/W3uM/p\ntzIJPkLsNGYNlKwIG+4ysGEYgYDFn/+DaOXFjDcIe3gdlD48PS4XcYqx6bfhZG/f\nLVAfvuiOFAphA/r2x43+CfY9G2w6UoAWGcagyA+yqiwlsGxMb/Dpewvdo3FyT+0k\ni7u9Ou294KkN4vFER4xl3f0s1/3BPFL7TOcmXEAtQcyj4yskUfYyaqJAm+xDcWLo\np0C7/EuQo