_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/7b7d455155ebe39f87bfc9f7bebae503a3d02f5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:14:54Z","email":"revatikadam0607@gmail.com","name":"Revati Kadam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:14:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make event RSVP capacity enforcement transactionally consistent (#5350)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix event RSVP capacity races by making capacity reservation and RSVP\ncreation\nuse a single transactional PostgreSQL path.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Serialize RSVP capacity decisions using `SELECT FOR UPDATE` on the\nevent row.\n- Prevent concurrent RSVP requests from exceeding `max_attendees`.\n- Make duplicate RSVP requests idempotent.\n- Serialize cancellation with new RSVP requests.\n- Preserve automatic waitlist promotion after cancellation.\n- Route API and offline RSVP creation through the atomic RSVP RPC.\n- Replace the legacy toggle-RSVP deletion path with the transactional\ncancellation RPC.\n- Add integration coverage for simultaneous RSVP requests.\n- Add coverage ensuring duplicate RSVP requests consume only one\ncapacity slot.\n\n## Result\n\nA failed RSVP transaction cannot leave a phantom capacity reservation,\nand\nconcurrent RSVP requests cannot temporarily or permanently exceed event\ncapacity.\n\nCloses #5221 \n@krushit1307","tree":{"sha":"7daa028ae11d0e083ccff541943599960dc3a433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/7daa028ae11d0e083ccff541943599960dc3a433"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/7b7d455155ebe39f87bfc9f7bebae503a3d02f5e","verification":{"payload":"tree 7daa028ae11d0e083ccff541943599960dc3a433\nparent 9923f1f41962876edb7fed89a59674e7e0a30742\nauthor Revati Kadam <revatikadam0607@gmail.com> 1788167694 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788167694 +0530\n\nfix: make event RSVP capacity enforcement transactionally consistent (#5350)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix event RSVP capacity races by making capacity reservation and RSVP\ncreation\nuse a single transactional PostgreSQL path.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Serialize RSVP capacity decisions using `SELECT FOR UPDATE` on the\nevent row.\n- Prevent concurrent RSVP requests from exceeding `max_attendees`.\n- Make duplicate RSVP requests idempotent.\n- Serialize cancellation with new RSVP requests.\n- Preserve automatic waitlist promotion after cancellation.\n- Route API and offline RSVP creation through the atomic RSVP RPC.\n- Replace the legacy toggle-RSVP deletion path with the transactional\ncancellation RPC.\n- Add integration coverage for simultaneous RSVP requests.\n- Add coverage ensuring duplicate RSVP requests consume only one\ncapacity slot.\n\n## Result\n\nA failed RSVP transaction cannot leave a phantom capacity reservation,\nand\nconcurrent RSVP requests cannot temporarily or permanently exceed event\ncapacity.\n\nCloses #5221 \n@krushit1307","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUYOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQu8QAGYZnBbfjD6AuGk3vpxp5AcW\nUlUsPA/7y6/R875meByrNYAZmA/fOm8W06jd+Kwlj3b3PVIFFT4uFRSno4YYp3+F\nk3+gM0T4gwmL4qUyZFWt0WCTdinRQuN8pNE3MD8gHgnLbmQreruptSKnvbv1tBH5\nHZdKxKP8ZQm1RxeOAn6LIgQf3yGa9UEOSg/o4E/G7TIfY8VS1k57XgdfF+V1AfP2\nyFI8TKUjPnjxdvsvvngJQGKKABvWwSioUjMUBb9qucBvRvXqcv0N3citLdva/MXX\nL7BkSDz4LYl4Tey8m4qQKsAUuYF0OU8Rs8bVhQYPOsaeFtZOK3J3BuylyhzuGRAd\nANzCITDxOPMw8Esb/MR8tpRoTUW2XyVT6xVWeM9B+2QybT4ATv7Uce8TkQrk6sJS\n5ZjJhgC5q73aDRVJWoJ0NsN8EavylSXSjxCpNbn2EZIPAlpkQKtIjcQd6AnGVAxY\nhf/vCTsnhjRqq3V0/s97Nq1L0U8S3hpAIFhtm7iBKhtrQmtsuL+CgwNCcKZQbeLT\ne4AzQ1OxmFttDf3AVaTJg4h2PCgm7k8rcdmymFyMibXlOe4vFgviipJM1PrKUyQM\n7yHTqboAtGIDfpEFIai9aBZ1CtZ3HZ2T9HEUYh3wgyiSGMz9t88TJCZlnhMAVnYK\ndLkSl5iQrr1ypPvZrv7e\n=gRAZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:14:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/7b7d455155ebe39f87bfc9f7bebae503a3d02f5e","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDdiN2Q0NTUxNTVlYmUzOWY4N2JmYzlmN2JlYmFlNTAzYTNkMDJmNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/9923f1f41962876edb7fed89a59674e7e0a30742","sha":"9923f1f41962876edb7fed89a59674e7e0a30742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/9923f1f41962876edb7fed89a59674e7e0a30742"}],"sha":"7b7d455155ebe39f87bfc9f7bebae503a3d02f5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/7b7d455155ebe39f87bfc9f7bebae503a3d02f5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/231409700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nayanraj864-cmyk","id":231409700,"login":"nayanraj864-cmyk","node_id":"U_kgDODcsIJA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/9923f1f41962876edb7fed89a59674e7e0a30742/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:14:34Z","email":"nayanraj864@gmail.com","name":"nayanraj864-cmyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:14:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resources): Develop a ''Dynamic \"Resource Constraint\" Overbooking Margin Algorithm'' (#4984) (#5349)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements the ''Dynamic \"Resource Constraint\" Overbooking Margin\nAlgorithm'' (`resource_overbooking_configs`, `resource_standby_queues`,\n`resourceOverbookingMargin.ts`, and `ResourceOverbookingMarginWidget`),\nmaximizing campus hardware asset utilization by applying airline-style\nyield management (110% overbooking capacity based on 15% historical\nno-show rates) and automatically promoting standby clubs when primary\nreservations miss their 15-minute RFID pickup window.\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Database Schema\n(`20260871000000_resource_overbooking_margin.sql`)**: Created\n`public.resource_overbooking_configs` and\n`public.resource_standby_queues` tables logging historical no-show\nrates, overbooking capacity limits, and standby queue promotion\nstatuses.\n- **Yield Management & Standby Promotion Engine\n(`resourceOverbookingMargin.ts`)**: `calculateOverbookingCapacity`\ncomputes overbooking capacity limits; `evaluateNoShowStandbyPromotion`\nevaluates 15-minute RFID pickup grace periods, cancels no-show primary\nreservations, and dispatches push notifications to Standby Club\nofficers.\n- **Hardware Yield & Standby Portal UI\n(`ResourceOverbookingMarginWidget.tsx`)**: Features yield metric cards\n(Historical No-Show Rate & Overbooking Margin), primary reservation RFID\npickup status, standby queue list, 15-minute grace period simulator, and\npush notification dispatch card.\n\n---\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [x] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] UI/UX Enhancement\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Other\n\n---\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #4984\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed:\n\n- [x] Tested locally via `npx vitest run\nsrc/lib/resourceOverbookingMargin.test.ts\nsrc/components/resources/ResourceOverbookingMarginWidget.test.tsx`\n(**6/6 passed**)\n- [x] Verified overbooking capacity yield calculations (10 units + 15%\nno-show rate -> 11 units / 110%)\n- [x] Verified 15-minute RFID pickup window no-show evaluation\n- [x] Verified standby club promotion notification dispatch\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n---\n\n## Screenshots\n\n*N/A — Dynamic Resource Constraint Overbooking Margin Algorithm added to\nHardware Resource Inventory Management view.*\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"757bf2d50ee6ad7770f7b346a46bfdbb554bec8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/757bf2d50ee6ad7770f7b346a46bfdbb554bec8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/9923f1f41962876edb7fed89a59674e7e0a30742","verification":{"payload":"tree 757bf2d50ee6ad7770f7b346a46bfdbb554bec8d\nparent 6d74d9b5d3c18f9fcbc7c256272d13b26ff84c1a\nauthor nayanraj864-cmyk <nayanraj864@gmail.com> 1788167674 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788167674 +0530\n\nfeat(resources): Develop a ''Dynamic \"Resource Constraint\" Overbooking Margin Algorithm'' (#4984) (#5349)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements the ''Dynamic \"Resource Constraint\" Overbooking Margin\nAlgorithm'' (`resource_overbooking_configs`, `resource_standby_queues`,\n`resourceOverbookingMargin.ts`, and `ResourceOverbookingMarginWidget`),\nmaximizing campus hardware asset utilization by applying airline-style\nyield management (110% overbooking capacity based on 15% historical\nno-show rates) and automatically promoting standby clubs when primary\nreservations miss their 15-minute RFID pickup window.\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Database Schema\n(`20260871000000_resource_overbooking_margin.sql`)**: Created\n`public.resource_overbooking_configs` and\n`public.resource_standby_queues` tables logging historical no-show\nrates, overbooking capacity limits, and standby queue promotion\nstatuses.\n- **Yield Management & Standby Promotion Engine\n(`resourceOverbookingMargin.ts`)**: `calculateOverbookingCapacity`\ncomputes overbooking capacity limits; `evaluateNoShowStandbyPromotion`\nevaluates 15-minute RFID pickup grace periods, cancels no-show primary\nreservations, and dispatches push notifications to Standby Club\nofficers.\n- **Hardware Yield & Standby Portal UI\n(`ResourceOverbookingMarginWidget.tsx`)**: Features yield metric cards\n(Historical No-Show Rate & Overbooking Margin), primary reservation RFID\npickup status, standby queue list, 15-minute grace period simulator, and\npush notification dispatch card.\n\n---\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [x] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] UI/UX Enhancement\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Other\n\n---\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #4984\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed:\n\n- [x] Tested locally via `npx vitest run\nsrc/lib/resourceOverbookingMargin.test.ts\nsrc/components/resources/ResourceOverbookingMarginWidget.test.tsx`\n(**6/6 passed**)\n- [x] Verified overbooking capacity yield calculations (10 units + 15%\nno-show rate -> 11 units / 110%)\n- [x] Verified 15-minute RFID pickup window no-show evaluation\n- [x] Verified standby club promotion notification dispatch\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n---\n\n## Screenshots\n\n*N/A — Dynamic Resource Constraint Overbooking Margin Algorithm added to\nHardware Resource Inventory Management view.*\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUX6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmUEQAJ+MAmFUCVAS51d1sYYUXQHF\nV8+mzrjJxYIA312fwgGKYCoK8EB3IbzxZ9wiHws5cjKWZi+eDm/B1CJwV3MDWHGq\n6gNbdMiWB9u/82DxToKEXnyW6PSdMt+AtndRKG2/Yt5ogYsGF6UhIWFj34fOKw4X\nRjzxd0/qEhM7CNF+JfgrYX0j6cR8wRnPrWhN5WEsOwc3OBApsHZGb1TuJac3FOip\naPnUW6uQqNgBRSN4lRHlvi/UpeHxuP8hUBCJqveBDQrnB+RdGSqilV/uQ4fqZr1P\nK7S86rLn2d2HvyaHSF9UYqilShQdA2J2QMb7vN8a+Fma+h1/OF3EE7tMkCvpO6uF\nW4ivRz04t2wJa/sD0ovR3GOGduDAwB4onZYG+HKoNtkXt5+86oWGl8FH3DwV2T0u\n6bQSNaGDOOlObhMRjJUAafSBhohbdJJS22tCMGBDCP1O18T+rTQnp+qFijQO6YlS\n1tle6Bq9CB1sVHh6eI6wPMU8uwae+rDuEqCxA8yy0hJ8Y87SwArTtuKp20ikWrOB\ntMM6qEKJnTnGSO21zNYNeVMwG1xgD/9sdClWXSGTmrr94jNTQD0l+ilP0gpHq1z5\nebfBuYEG5r0EJFK2AY9fqPcNEyweiTEOvpW+CW0jtGMlPgyemQL2OrTq3w0veFh1\nA6ty0j1IsnKre/IxKQNU\n=jQhe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:14:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gi