d_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayanraj864-cmyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/6d74d9b5d3c18f9fcbc7c256272d13b26ff84c1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:03:45Z","email":"nayanraj864@gmail.com","name":"nayanraj864-cmyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:03:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(donations): Build a ''Real-Time \"Donation Goal\" Predictive Slippage Alert'' (#4983) (#5348)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements the ''Real-Time \"Donation Goal\" Predictive Slippage\nAlert'' (`crypto_donation_slippage_audits`, `cryptoDonationSlippage.ts`,\nand `CryptoDonationSlippageAlertWidget`), protecting Web3 donors from\nunexpected AMM liquidity losses when donating volatile altcoins by\npre-calculating slippage via 1inch/Uniswap DEX aggregator APIs and\nrendering prominent pre-signing warnings when slippage exceeds 2.0%.\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Database Schema\n(`20260870000000_crypto_donation_slippage_alert.sql`)**: Created\n`public.crypto_donation_slippage_audits` table logging DEX router\nestimates, slippage percentages, and donor acknowledgments.\n- **Predictive Slippage Engine (`cryptoDonationSlippage.ts`)**:\n`calculateSlippage` computes slippage percentage and dollar loss;\n`evaluateCryptoDonationSlippage` flags high-risk transactions (> 2.0%\nthreshold) and recommends zero-slippage USDC stablecoin alternatives.\n- **Web3 Slippage Alert Portal UI\n(`CryptoDonationSlippageAlertWidget.tsx`)**: Features crypto asset\nselection form, DEX router audit card, urgent red warning box\n(`\"WARNING: Low liquidity. You will lose approximately $2,000.00 in\nslippage\"`), 1-click \"Switch to USDC Stablecoin\" button, and manual\noverride checkbox.\n\n---\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [x] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] UI/UX Enhancement\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Other\n\n---\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #4983\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed:\n\n- [x] Tested locally via `npx vitest run\nsrc/lib/cryptoDonationSlippage.test.ts\nsrc/components/donations/CryptoDonationSlippageAlertWidget.test.tsx`\n(**6/6 passed**)\n- [x] Verified DEX aggregator slippage calculation math ($10,000 ->\n$8,000 = 20.00% loss)\n- [x] Verified 2.0% warning threshold evaluation\n- [x] Verified 1-click USDC stablecoin switch action\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n---\n\n## Screenshots\n\n*N/A — Real-Time Donation Goal Predictive Slippage Alert added to Web3\nCrypto Donation view.*\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"ef5079c30692ad2207394ec2d4295b51cc03e756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/ef5079c30692ad2207394ec2d4295b51cc03e756"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/6d74d9b5d3c18f9fcbc7c256272d13b26ff84c1a","verification":{"payload":"tree ef5079c30692ad2207394ec2d4295b51cc03e756\nparent 9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95\nauthor nayanraj864-cmyk <nayanraj864@gmail.com> 1788167025 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788167025 +0530\n\nfeat(donations): Build a ''Real-Time \"Donation Goal\" Predictive Slippage Alert'' (#4983) (#5348)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR implements the ''Real-Time \"Donation Goal\" Predictive Slippage\nAlert'' (`crypto_donation_slippage_audits`, `cryptoDonationSlippage.ts`,\nand `CryptoDonationSlippageAlertWidget`), protecting Web3 donors from\nunexpected AMM liquidity losses when donating volatile altcoins by\npre-calculating slippage via 1inch/Uniswap DEX aggregator APIs and\nrendering prominent pre-signing warnings when slippage exceeds 2.0%.\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Database Schema\n(`20260870000000_crypto_donation_slippage_alert.sql`)**: Created\n`public.crypto_donation_slippage_audits` table logging DEX router\nestimates, slippage percentages, and donor acknowledgments.\n- **Predictive Slippage Engine (`cryptoDonationSlippage.ts`)**:\n`calculateSlippage` computes slippage percentage and dollar loss;\n`evaluateCryptoDonationSlippage` flags high-risk transactions (> 2.0%\nthreshold) and recommends zero-slippage USDC stablecoin alternatives.\n- **Web3 Slippage Alert Portal UI\n(`CryptoDonationSlippageAlertWidget.tsx`)**: Features crypto asset\nselection form, DEX router audit card, urgent red warning box\n(`\"WARNING: Low liquidity. You will lose approximately $2,000.00 in\nslippage\"`), 1-click \"Switch to USDC Stablecoin\" button, and manual\noverride checkbox.\n\n---\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [x] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] UI/UX Enhancement\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Other\n\n---\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #4983\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe the testing performed:\n\n- [x] Tested locally via `npx vitest run\nsrc/lib/cryptoDonationSlippage.test.ts\nsrc/components/donations/CryptoDonationSlippageAlertWidget.test.tsx`\n(**6/6 passed**)\n- [x] Verified DEX aggregator slippage calculation math ($10,000 ->\n$8,000 = 20.00% loss)\n- [x] Verified 2.0% warning threshold evaluation\n- [x] Verified 1-click USDC stablecoin switch action\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n---\n\n## Screenshots\n\n*N/A — Real-Time Donation Goal Predictive Slippage Alert added to Web3\nCrypto Donation view.*\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUNyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZIIQABZ256se/kjFATJNOsMW0qDf\nD6miF1CHiNbBNI2sF8xHld21EWvglNLszU7iAlwMamxddrVrVxBTYhYwCp1GzkHL\nIifDc/hssm0csi3wipzpUufH69drb1BO5NUtzaecm0efYjw79rjm1Xvmv/MO8FCm\nUGIS0ZMs3ParFooewmqU6fpBMPyHfcSNZfaUziY/nmko1eoMS1R2jRlyxFvXkdPX\nOBSncndRvj3VILjcfADdRv3Bdddxt5EhWRvzh1wT/KCkOyhvetRmJn6FeeW2N3AT\n5j8sGlVBF+AwJLHvl0S8c/1cyL3YkVJysZ7958GCCqUjzLvjPb7SoMN0S6kedyWD\n9aa/YjjCJIEU8ohsBvepuZ+k8eG8Q3rDqwRGVsf4VdRiDIoAq9Qc9iYfbj3k0Q4Z\nkXclH0qicV7oTbo9HSylgQclw3Mo0gLQoVLD98sTFEha8oEtdOevD4ke3B+a9uVP\nBCRvUhsj6dEmu/f0V1evd1vtl1SmPhSvPIKNf2t5VTw0rMIM8KxByUJfmV29grT/\n33TjTlMoGHlubSqvS7x/o9IiIXpdYp+t2bdwMl3sIp/dAmp366/9ksXxK4QgcZ6e\nFSSOgG//KV+idF2wf1Oq01GgW9NAwC1/o7/1PCkMd3wh0A3qhInwkPjet0v+vk6m\nzvcl0cCL0eW+AMNq4juO\n=mBu3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:03:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/6d74d9b5d3c18f9fcbc7c256272d13b26ff84c1a","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDZkNzRkOWI1ZDNjMThmOWZjYmM3YzI1NjI3MmQxM2IyNmZmODRjMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95","sha":"9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95"}],"sha":"6d74d9b5d3c18f9fcbc7c256272d13b26ff84c1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/6d74d9b5d3c18f9fcbc7c256272d13b26ff84c1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224525950?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rishab11250","id":224525950,"login":"rishab11250","node_id":"U_kgDODWH-fg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:03:29Z","email":"rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com","name":"Rishab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:03:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(safety): implement fire alarm audio fingerprinting with T3 detection and emergency evacuation (#5347)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements **Interactive \"Campus Safety\" Fire Alarm Audio\nFingerprinting** (Closes #5279) to connect physical fire alarms to\ndigital turnstiles and prevent deadly crush bottlenecks during mass\nindoor concert evacuations.\n\n**Solution:** Localized acoustic fingerprinting on Bouncer/Check-in\niPads — a highly optimized background audio thread continuously runs FFT\non microphone input to detect the standardized ISO 8201 Temporal-Three\n(T3) pattern (0.5s tone / 0.5s silence ×3 + 1.5s pause, fingerprinting\n520Hz low-frequency and 3100Hz legacy bands). If T3 is detected\ncontinuously for >5 seconds, the iPad immediately fires a high-priority\n`EMERGENCY_EVACUATION` payload to the backend, which instantly commands\ndigital turnstiles to drop magnetic locks for frictionless free-flow\nevacuation.\n\n**Key changes:**\n- `src/lib/audio/fireAlarmFingerprint.ts` — dual-band FFT detection\n(`magnitude>-45dB` + `SNR>12dB`), `T3Detector` (sliding 6s window, 80%\nduty fallback + strict T3 correlation with 3+ onsets and long-pause\ncheck), `FireAlarmDetector` (FFT+T3 + 30s cooldown), payload builder and\n`computeMagnitudesNaive` fallback.\n- `src/hooks/useFireAlarmMonitor.ts` — `requestAnimationFrame` audio\nthread using `AudioContext`/`AnalyserNode` (`FFT_SIZE 2048`, `smoothing\n0.15`, `48kHz`), handles permission denial and calls\n`fireEvacuationWithRetry`.\n- `src/lib/turnstile/turnstileControl.ts` — RPC + Next.js API fallback\nwith retry handling for `EMERGENCY_EVACUATION`.\n-\n`supabase/migrations/20280922000000_fire_alarm_fingerprint_evacuation.sql`\n— extends `events` with evacuation columns\n(`emergency_evacuation_active`, `turnstile_magnetic_locks_dropped`,\netc.), creates `turnstile_devices` and `emergency_evacuation_events`\ntables with RLS/realtime, and idempotent `trigger_emergency_evacuation`\nRPC that drops locks atomically and audit-logs to `club_audit_logs`.\n- `supabase/functions/emergency-evacuation/index.ts` +\n`src/app/api/bouncer/emergency-evacuation/route.ts` — high-priority\ningestion with JWT validation and RPC delegation.\n- `src/app/bouncer/[eventId]/page.tsx` — integrates monitor, shows\nevacuation banner (`EMERGENCY EVACUATION — TURNSTILES UNLOCKED` with\n`peakFreqHz`/`fireAlarmStatus`).\n- Tests for full T3 detection including 520Hz/3100Hz tones, silence\nrejection, and temporal logic.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5279\n\n## Testing\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n**Automated:**\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/audio/fireAlarmFingerprint.test.ts` — 12\npassed (hz/bin roundtrip, magnitudeToDb, 520Hz/3100Hz detection,\nsilence/noise rejection, T3 >5s continuous vs <5s burst vs 80% duty,\nFireAlarmDetector cooldown, payload clamping, empty magnitudes)\n- `npx eslint` on 5 new files — 0 errors after `no-empty` fix; `npx tsc\n--noEmit` filtered for `fireAlarm|turnstile|emergency` → 0 new errors\n(full repo has pre-existing `EventSeriesAnalyticsDashboard` JSX errors\nunrelated)\n- Manual bouncer flow: microphone permission → `listening` → `detecting`\n(inject 520Hz tone) → 5s continuous → `evacuating` banner +\n`emergency_evacuation_events` row + `turnstile_devices.locked=false`\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — Background audio thread is headless; evacuation banner appears on\nBouncer iPad (`bg-red-600` alert with `role=alert` and peak frequency).\nNo static UI change to screenshot.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","tree":{"sha":"23644c7f4efe607b1afbe64c3fb380c7a8fb335c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/23644c7f4efe607b1afbe64c3fb380c7a8fb335c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95","verification":{"payload":"tree 23644c7f4efe607b1afbe64c3fb380c7a8fb335c\nparent cbd19e95c4a014aaaefe248b5eeb239d353332a0\nauthor Rishab <rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com> 1788167009 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788167009 +0530\n\nfeat(safety): implement fire alarm audio fingerprinting with T3 detection and emergency evacuation (#5347)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements **Interactive \"Campus Safety\" Fire Alarm Audio\nFingerprinting** (Closes #5279) to connect physical fire alarms to\ndigital turnstiles and prevent deadly crush bottlenecks during mass\nindoor concert evacuations.\n\n**Solution:** Localized acoustic fingerprinting on Bouncer/Check-in\niPads — a highly optimized background audio thread continuously runs FFT\non microphone input to detect the standardized ISO 8201 Temporal-Three\n(T3) pattern (0.5s tone / 0.5s silence ×3 + 1.5s pause, fingerprinting\n520Hz low-frequency and 3100Hz legacy bands). If T3 is detected\ncontinuously for >5 seconds, the iPad immediately fires a high-priority\n`EMERGENCY_EVACUATION` payload to the backend, which instantly commands\ndigital turnstiles to drop magnetic locks for frictionless free-flow\nevacuation.\n\n**Key changes:**\n- `src/lib/audio/fireAlarmFingerprint.ts` — dual-band FFT detection\n(`magnitude>-45dB` + `SNR>12dB`), `T3Detector` (sliding 6s window, 80%\nduty fallback + strict T3 correlation with 3+ onsets and long-pause\ncheck), `FireAlarmDetector` (FFT+T3 + 30s cooldown), payload builder and\n`computeMagnitudesNaive` fallback.\n- `src/hooks/useFireAlarmMonitor.ts` — `requestAnimationFrame` audio\nthread using `AudioContext`/`AnalyserNode` (`FFT_SIZE 2048`, `smoothing\n0.15`, `48kHz`), handles permission denial and calls\n`fireEvacuationWithRetry`.\n- `src/lib/turnstile/turnstileControl.ts` — RPC + Next.js API fallback\nwith retry handling for `EMERGENCY_EVACUATION`.\n-\n`supabase/migrations/20280922000000_fire_alarm_fingerprint_evacuation.sql`\n— extends `events` with evacuation columns\n(`emergency_evacuation_active`, `turnstile_magnetic_locks_dropped`,\netc.), creates `turnstile_devices` and `emergency_evacuation_events`\ntables with RLS/realtime, and idempotent `trigger_emergency_evacuation`\nRPC that drops locks atomically and audit-logs to `club_audit_logs`.\n- `supabase/functions/emergency-evacuation/index.ts` +\n`src/app/api/bouncer/emergency-evacuation/route.ts` — high-priority\ningestion with JWT validation and RPC delegation.\n- `src/app/bouncer/[eventId]/page.tsx` — integrates monitor, shows\nevacuation banner (`EMERGENCY EVACUATION — TURNSTILES UNLOCKED` with\n`peakFreqHz`/`fireAlarmStatus`).\n- Tests for full T3 detection including 520Hz/3100Hz tones, silence\nrejection, and temporal logic.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [x] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5279\n\n## Testing\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\n**Automated:**\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/audio/fireAlarmFingerprint.test.ts` — 12\npassed (hz/bin roundtrip, magnitudeToDb, 520Hz/3100Hz detection,\nsilence/noise rejection, T3 >5s continuous vs <5s burst vs 80% duty,\nFireAlarmDetector cooldown, payload clamping, empty magnitudes)\n- `npx eslint` on 5 new files — 0 errors after `no-empty` fix; `npx tsc\n--noEmit` filtered for `fireAlarm|turnstile|emergency` → 0 new errors\n(full repo has pre-existing `EventSeriesAnalyticsDashboard` JSX errors\nunrelated)\n- Manual bouncer flow: microphone permission → `listening` → `detecting`\n(inject 520Hz tone) → 5s continuous → `evacuating` banner +\n`emergency_evacuation_events` row + `turnstile_devices.locked=false`\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — Background audio thread is headless; evacuation banner appears on\nBouncer iPad (`bg-red-600` alert with `role=alert` and peak frequency).\nNo static UI change to screenshot.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUNhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvecQAACQ/b2fYwTTIpgUclPuh5ji\nnGq8nRocRfB7Nv5fsnsnQ8+kIy/3ZWIUcvlhXpd4BAAfknttkdYMU3dRHGksce7b\nP8Ie5QWJpNQfizVmMWVuGMxqY8vSA9WXbl62eCgRvdkMNcJx+bJqMpMcjPhXGKh8\n+SYDdxp+HpxY8JkZ14nmZrZO06w5asMnHTthcLw9VjlH1ABLXFXd5rbH5+lL3BNo\n/ismHu+n3ZWp4Ziaib7CjlqOCHhfpl4JhXkUVHdd3H0WdIy9PsQzp27K9pZyJF6n\njfGKEhJMpzaSrDGuqRToyMAsXxNEL/lpWokDiywjoA+2EKYz+75UGC+qoHh4CfHc\nvqLJ7/6h+rBQvhejfg92l/SL19wxZXKpYppg1hRgRFJ8AYOJ1ba5/1lNhUbsoPEL\n408MoBWxxIdAnV18Ou3cm6VIbAlP11rlKUrIytuv28KT9mkT+yz/bk9naoOSqVoU\n9Z3usL7euGYGoNj6O1+C7Jc442KUG+zWHcNLD6mzbdBxOrh3ums0npbzB9wYD4hT\nHFrDKa/19ecclD8l+tJ9JZx2y3186P3v3UTfB4sZ8th02AuVRROOkdT7McR+9iQD\nonsXDsEj8tHnLP3rSsfi27Z7S8zlo4onDKbg0TRGtZgv3S3ar+wqtJxbO6Tmtr/P\nSxMeABzfBnpm/UupvDmf\n=zcrW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:03:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95","node_id":"C_kwDOTPF5RdoAKDlkNDIzY2EwZjY0MzRlYzFiYzUxZWE3NmQ4ZTU2NTQ0MmQzOTRlOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commit/cbd19e95c4a014aaaefe248b5eeb239d353332a0","sha":"cbd19e95c4a014aaaefe248b5eeb239d353332a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/cbd19e95c4a014aaaefe248b5eeb239d353332a0"}],"sha":"9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/9d423ca0f6434ec1bc51ea76d8e565442d394e95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224525950?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rishab11250","id":224525950,"login":"rishab11250","node_id":"U_kgDODWH-fg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rishab11250","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/commits/cbd19e95c4a014aaaefe248b5eeb239d353332a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:29:11Z","email":"rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com","name":"Rishab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:29:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(events): implement dynamic alumni speaker live translation earpiece routing (#5345)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements Dynamic \"Alumni Speaker\" Live Translation Earpiece Routing\n(#5285) to stream near-real-time AI-translated keynote audio to\nstudents'' AirPods/headphones via WebRTC. Adds Deepgram WebSocket\ntranscription → DeepL neural translation (default Mandarin `zh`) → AWS\nPolly/ElevenLabs TTS → WebRTC pipeline with Supabase Realtime signalling\nand speaker-cadence synchronization. Includes organiser-owned live\nsessions and per-student earpiece routing with latency budgeting, plus\nUI for organisers (start live session, view routes) and checked-in\nattendees (select target language/device, join WebRTC route).\n\nKey changes:\n- **DB:** `alumni_speaker_live_sessions` (one live per event) and\n`earpiece_translation_routes` (unique per session/user/language) tables,\nRLS, triggers, realtime publication, and SECURITY DEFINER RPCs\n(`create_live_translation_session`, `join_earpiece_route`,\n`update_earpiece_webrtc_signal`, `get_live_translation_routes`) in\n`20261233000000_alumni_speaker_live_translation_earpiece_routing.sql`.\n- **Lib:** `src/lib/liveTranslationEarpieceRouting.ts` — pure, testable\npipeline helpers (Deepgram extraction, deterministic DeepL/TTS mocks,\nlatency/cadence estimation, WebRTC offer/answer builders, eligibility\nevaluation, full orchestration).\n- **Edge Function:**\n`supabase/functions/live-translation-router/index.ts` — JWT-verified\n`verifyAuth` flow that validates route ownership/live status, runs real\nvendor calls when keys present (fallback mocks), persists\n`audio_buffer_url`/`latency_ms`, and updates session `pipeline_stage` to\n`streaming`.\n- **UI:** `LiveTranslationEarpiecePanel` integrated into\n`events.$eventId.tsx` for live/connected states, language/device\nselectors, and cadence offset preview.\n- **Tests:** 11 vitest cases covering languages, pipeline stages,\nlatency, WebRTC signals, and orchestration.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5285\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified live translation pipeline and earpiece routing end-to-end\nwithout vendor keys using deterministic mocks.\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\nDetails:\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/liveTranslationEarpieceRouting.test.ts` —\n11/11 passed.\n- `npx eslint --fix` on new TS files — 0 errors (pre-existing\n`src/App.tsx` duplicate `Leaderboard`/`LibraryBookFinder` parse errors\nremain on `main`, 0 new TS errors for our files).\n- Manual smoke: organiser creates live session (`webrtc_room_id`,\n`pipeline_stage`), checked-in student joins route with `airpods`/`zh`,\nWebRTC offer persisted via `update_earpiece_webrtc_signal`, latency\n`~600ms` within `1200ms` budget, cadence offset preview rendered.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — UI is brutalist `border-4`/`shadow-[8px_8px_0_0]` panel with\nlive/idle badge, language/device selects, and realtime cadence preview;\nno visual regression beyond new panel in event detail page.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows project conventions\n- [x] Documentation updated where required\n- [x] No unnecessary files included\n- [x] Changes have been tested\n- [x] Ready for review\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added live translation earpiece support to event detail pages.\n* Organizers can start translation sessions and select target languages.\n* Checked-in attendees can choose a language and device, then join or\nleave translation routes.\n* Added real-time connection status, latency previews, and session\nupdates.\n* Added live translation processing for transcript, translation, audio\nsynthesis, and delivery.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Added validation for supported languages, devices, connection states,\nand route eligibility.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added comprehensive automated coverage for routing, latency,\nsignaling, and pipeline behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"9a8a6fd4d6585390c0d0207a2c9f20c2236973b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/trees/9a8a6fd4d6585390c0d0207a2c9f20c2236973b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/krushit1307/CampusConnect/git/commits/cbd19e95c4a014aaaefe248b5eeb239d353332a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a8a6fd4d6585390c0d0207a2c9f20c2236973b3\nparent 6be1b8c4b85779369abb47b6d967ca7b513f4f0b\nauthor Rishab <rishab.chandgothia.cg@gmail.com> 1788164951 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788164951 +0530\n\nfeat(events): implement dynamic alumni speaker live translation earpiece routing (#5345)\n\n# Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements Dynamic \"Alumni Speaker\" Live Translation Earpiece Routing\n(#5285) to stream near-real-time AI-translated keynote audio to\nstudents'' AirPods/headphones via WebRTC. Adds Deepgram WebSocket\ntranscription → DeepL neural translation (default Mandarin `zh`) → AWS\nPolly/ElevenLabs TTS → WebRTC pipeline with Supabase Realtime signalling\nand speaker-cadence synchronization. Includes organiser-owned live\nsessions and per-student earpiece routing with latency budgeting, plus\nUI for organisers (start live session, view routes) and checked-in\nattendees (select target language/device, join WebRTC route).\n\nKey changes:\n- **DB:** `alumni_speaker_live_sessions` (one live per event) and\n`earpiece_translation_routes` (unique per session/user/language) tables,\nRLS, triggers, realtime publication, and SECURITY DEFINER RPCs\n(`create_live_translation_session`, `join_earpiece_route`,\n`update_earpiece_webrtc_signal`, `get_live_translation_routes`) in\n`20261233000000_alumni_speaker_live_translation_earpiece_routing.sql`.\n- **Lib:** `src/lib/liveTranslationEarpieceRouting.ts` — pure, testable\npipeline helpers (Deepgram extraction, deterministic DeepL/TTS mocks,\nlatency/cadence estimation, WebRTC offer/answer builders, eligibility\nevaluation, full orchestration).\n- **Edge Function:**\n`supabase/functions/live-translation-router/index.ts` — JWT-verified\n`verifyAuth` flow that validates route ownership/live status, runs real\nvendor calls when keys present (fallback mocks), persists\n`audio_buffer_url`/`latency_ms`, and updates session `pipeline_stage` to\n`streaming`.\n- **UI:** `LiveTranslationEarpiecePanel` integrated into\n`events.$eventId.tsx` for live/connected states, language/device\nselectors, and cadence offset preview.\n- **Tests:** 11 vitest cases covering languages, pipeline stages,\nlatency, WebRTC signals, and orchestration.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] New Feature\n- [ ] Bug Fix\n- [ ] Documentation Update\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Performance Improvement\n- [ ] Security Improvement\n- [ ] Other\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #5285\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified live translation pipeline and earpiece routing end-to-end\nwithout vendor keys using deterministic mocks.\n\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] Existing functionality verified\n- [x] No new warnings or errors\n\nDetails:\n- `npx vitest run src/lib/liveTranslationEarpieceRouting.test.ts` —\n11/11 passed.\n- `npx eslint --fix` on new TS files — 0 errors (pre-existing\n`src/App.tsx` duplicate `Leaderboard`/`LibraryBookFinder` parse errors\nremain on `main`, 0 new TS errors for our files).\n- Manual smoke: organiser creates live session (`webrtc_room_id`,\n`pipeline_stage`), checked-in student joins route with `airpods`/`zh`,\nWebRTC offer persisted via `update_earpiece_webrtc_signal`, latency\n`~600ms` within `1200ms` budget, cadence offset preview rendered.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nN/A — UI is brutalist `border-4`/`shadow-[8px_8px_0_0]` panel with\nlive/idle badge, lang