60b203b385571f8733fc01f4925d5e8519ac7e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/460b203b385571f8733fc01f4925d5e8519ac7e6"}],"sha":"4045f9852e20513186ab3ca80d88edfbd3b6b21a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/4045f9852e20513186ab3ca80d88edfbd3b6b21a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/460b203b385571f8733fc01f4925d5e8519ac7e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:30:11Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:30:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(twenty-front): show only failing unit tests in CI (#22345)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a custom Jest reporter to **twenty-front** that, in CI, suppresses\npassing-test output and surfaces only failures — mirroring what we\nalready do for **twenty-server**.\n\n## How\n\n- New `packages/twenty-front/jest-failures-only-reporter.cjs` — a\nverbatim port of\n`packages/twenty-server/jest-failures-only-reporter.js`. It prints a\n`FAIL` block per failing suite plus a final \"FAILED TEST SUITES\nSUMMARY\", and otherwise emits only the suite/test totals.\n- Wired into `packages/twenty-front/jest.config.mjs` via `...(isCI && {\nreporters: [''./jest-failures-only-reporter.cjs''] })`, gated on `CI ===\n''true''` exactly like twenty-server.\n\n### Note on the `.cjs` extension\n\ntwenty-front''s `package.json` sets `\"type\": \"module\"`, so a `.js`\nreporter is parsed as ESM and `module.exports` throws. Renaming to\n`.cjs` keeps the file as CommonJS (Jest requires CJS reporters).\ntwenty-server is not an ESM package, hence its `.js` extension.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Passing suite (`CI=true npx jest <file>`): output reduced to the\ntotals summary only.\n- Temporary failing suite: shows the `FAIL` block, failure message, and\nthe failed-suites summary.\n\nLocal dev runs (no `CI` env) are unaffected — the default reporter is\nused.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22345?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"73e52ad4b8d47066bc4aeb64fbe8adf68ebb014b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/73e52ad4b8d47066bc4aeb64fbe8adf68ebb014b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/460b203b385571f8733fc01f4925d5e8519ac7e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 73e52ad4b8d47066bc4aeb64fbe8adf68ebb014b\nparent 1055764fff209fc95fa87917d92810b92d274d79\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.