_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51697796?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ijreilly","id":51697796,"login":"ijreilly","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNjk3Nzk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/4eb28b73c776b7f56fac5fea2d7b7d1a39b6d0ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T14:04:40Z","email":"51697796+ijreilly@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T14:04:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): normalize legacy index names (command) (#22053)\n\n## TL;DR\n\nAdds a workspace upgrade command that normalizes index names to the\ncurrent v2 deterministic naming convention (IDX_ prefix). This will\nclose https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/issues/21383 : uniqueness\nconstraint cannot be disabled (for users who set it before v2\ndeterminist naming is enforced).\n\n### Background\n\nThe deterministic index name embeds the table name, columns, uniqueness\nand where clause. The naming convention changed on **2025-09-23**\n(#14567 - added the `IDX_`/`IDX_UNIQUE_` prefix and folded the table\nname into the hash). Index rows created before that kept their old name\nin `core.\"indexMetadata\"`, and nothing rewrites it (only targeted\nphone/relation rebuilds got new names).\n\nCode paths that locate an index by recomputing its expected name then\nmiss these legacy-named rows. The most visible symptom is #21383:\ntoggling a field''s `isUnique` from `true` → `false` recomputes the\nexpected unique-index name, fails to find the legacy-named index, and\nsilently no-ops — so uniqueness can''t be disabled.\n\n### What the command does\n\nPer workspace, for each index:\n- recomputes the expected name with the same generator the app uses\n(`generateFlatIndexMetadataWithNameOrThrow`);\n- if the stored name differs → **rename** it (metadata `UPDATE` + a new\nmetadata-only `ALTER INDEX … RENAME`, which preserves the unique\nconstraint with no rebuild/lock);\n- if a correctly-named twin already exists (the legacy +\nfreshly-generated duplicate case) → **drop the redundant** one (physical\n+ metadata, field rows cascade) and keep the canonical;\n- invalidates the metadata cache so the running app + `isUnique`\nderivation reflect the new names.\n\nHonors `--dry-run`, wraps writes in a transaction (rolls back on error),\nand skips (with a warning) any single index whose name can''t be\nrecomputed so it can''t abort the whole workspace.\n\n### Notable changes\n- New `renameIndex` on `WorkspaceSchemaIndexManagerService` (`ALTER\nINDEX IF EXISTS … RENAME`).\n- Planning logic extracted into a pure, unit-tested util\n(`planIndexNameNormalization`).","tree":{"sha":"32897189795a0e12ba4ebe2de2037383928b1a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/32897189795a0e12ba4ebe2de2037383928b1a9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/4eb28b73c776b7f56fac5fea2d7b7d1a39b6d0ab","verification":{"payload":"tree 32897189795a0e12ba4ebe2de2037383928b1a9b\nparent 6fa803edc2914889dd1de0d171423b83cc80e9ab\nauthor Marie <51697796+ijreilly@users.noreply.github.com> 1782741880 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782741880 +0000\n\nfix(server): normalize legacy index names (command) (#22053)\n\n## TL;DR\n\nAdds a workspace upgrade command that normalizes index names to the\ncurrent v2 deterministic naming convention (IDX_ prefix). This will\nclose https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/issues/21383 : uniqueness\nconstraint cannot be disabled (for users who set it before v2\ndeterminist naming is enforced).\n\n### Background\n\nThe deterministic index name embeds the table name, columns, uniqueness\nand where clause. The naming convention changed on **2025-09-23**\n(#14567 - added the `IDX_`/`IDX_UNIQUE_` prefix and folded the table\nname into the hash). Index rows created before that kept their old name\nin `core.\"indexMetadata\"`, and nothing rewrites it (only targeted\nphone/relation rebuilds got new names).\n\nCode paths that locate an index by recomputing its expected name then\nmiss these legacy-named rows. The most visible symptom is #21383:\ntoggling a field''s `isUnique` from `true` → `false` recomputes the\nexpected unique-index name, fails to find the legacy-named index, and\nsilently no-ops — so uniqueness can''t be disabled.\n\n### What the command does\n\nPer workspace, for each index:\n- recomputes the expected name with the same generator the app uses\n(`generateFlatIndexMetadataWithNameOrThrow`);\n- if the stored name differs → **rename** it (metadata `UPDATE` + a new\nmetadata-only `ALTER INDEX … RENAME`, which preserves the unique\nconstraint with no rebuild/lock);\n- if a correctly-named twin already exists (the legacy +\nfreshly-generated duplicate case) → **drop the redundant** one (physical\n+ metadata, field rows cascade) and keep the canonical;\n- invalidates the metadata cache so the running app + `isUnique`\nderivation reflect the new names.\n\nHonors `--dry-run`, wraps writes in a transaction (rolls back on error),\nand skips (with a warning) any single index whose name can''t be\nrecomputed so it can''t abort the whole workspace.\n\n### Notable changes\n- New `renameIndex` on `WorkspaceSchemaIndexManagerService` (`ALTER\nINDEX IF EXISTS … RENAME`).\n- Planning logic extracted into a pure, unit-tested util\n(`planIndexNameNormalization`).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQnt4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsbIQAALAjbj97/nGts1NIAboJhsl\nd8zgxOGX/EfTaY8Eca4mZtoXOITbfkkzTDB4KRnsQczQS7q2zvpDLHt91OWu8asv\navLYkSxxSTiCsg8929wrjErMYQw57iql/FOYEsPxkRi/p0A5bQbzFaIdO28Jk21U\n67jdPjxOkXckQkILlHl32GsgSffLNjprY0wP+DIZWtPwXA+uZbWsre54Mi3ZrEVB\n4/bLdTBVDzvYe3ZrdK0/rJjhb8pnVObmznnUZhixOek0yPuESzj4WFF6xP0pgQo7\nCIZRg+nZybiwuNgA3urkCGmEAb1+w9HprgEQof8O6jum9CTno+M6FH/v2R0/O7S1\nyUdY1mxg7uW9OB1wf/e5YWY8OVoxKO/TpoSxr7ybMh1c/3p2HJ7hXiREtIK+hfxu\nBSFW6QjdpQTThI2IBbz3thZG/Hxlr2N140itYrjINNBPRN1+Cx71AyOzBrHitNm8\n2OvfgKgGM7FSUww8zofeQebGigvJUV9fYbxkQo5r1ZZeO4BXOObANLf+c2qGQy4F\nCeLm+cRWz+hMRgbi8nstdpJTGfooVcRyo2VaQlmAlgGkT8G05M4rQXoMCfUqzalx\n3Eq7T56uQeZJPXzZAGjGC8Oo+sxjDAgF5/HzAT0ONQ2j+Hc4FueQ16G5WY4JRcHb\nk12yceK8kSk+NQX8zlrc\n=bN4D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T11:43:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type