/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commit/db7d8172f7ebad82abcc3e06b11dff6d3e73979c","node_id":"C_kwDOTPIvWNoAKGRiN2Q4MTcyZjdlYmFkODJhYmNjM2UwNmIxMWRmZjZkM2U3Mzk3OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commit/921c528cc3b86aa08ef19a8bc2dd04a6df5fc385","sha":"921c528cc3b86aa08ef19a8bc2dd04a6df5fc385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/921c528cc3b86aa08ef19a8bc2dd04a6df5fc385"}],"sha":"db7d8172f7ebad82abcc3e06b11dff6d3e73979c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/db7d8172f7ebad82abcc3e06b11dff6d3e73979c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176405802?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhorcajada","id":176405802,"login":"mhorcajada","node_id":"U_kgDOCoO9Kg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhorcajada","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/921c528cc3b86aa08ef19a8bc2dd04a6df5fc385/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T11:00:42Z","email":"miguel.horcajada.oliva@gmail.com","name":"Miguel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T11:00:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(helm): add nodeSelector, tolerations and DNS overrides to server and worker (#22233)\n\nCloses #22250\n\n## What\n\nAdds four standard pod spec fields to both server and worker Deployments\nof the Helm chart, exposed under `server.*` and `worker.*` in\n`values.yaml`:\n\n- `nodeSelector`\n- `tolerations`\n- `dnsPolicy`\n- `dnsConfig`\n\n## Why\n\nSelf-hosters who run Twenty on clusters with dedicated nodes, taints, or\ncustom DNS requirements currently need to fork the chart or patch\nrendered manifests with Kustomize. These are the standard pod spec\nfields supported by virtually every other community chart (Bitnami,\nprometheus-community, cert-manager, etc.) and are commonly needed in\nproduction setups.\n\n## How\n\nUses the same `{{- with }}` pattern already present in the chart (e.g.\n`extraEnv`, `extraVolumeMounts`), so empty defaults skip rendering\nentirely:\n\n```yaml\n{{- with .Values.server.nodeSelector }}\nnodeSelector:\n  {{- toYaml . | nindent 8 }}\n{{- end }}\n```\n\n## Backward compatibility\n\nFully backward compatible. Defaults are empty:\n\n```yaml\nserver:\n  nodeSelector: {}\n  tolerations: []\n  dnsPolicy: ~\n  dnsConfig: {}\n```\n\n`helm template` output is bit-identical to the previous version for any\nexisting install.\n\n## Schema note\n\n`dnsPolicy` is typed as `[string, null]` and the enum includes `null` so\nthe empty default (`dnsPolicy: ~`) passes validation. The `{{- with }}`\nguard treats null as falsy and renders nothing.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `helm lint` passes\n- `helm template` with default values produces bit-identical output to\nbefore this PR\n- `helm template` with values set renders the four fields correctly on\nboth server and worker\n- Live install validated on a multi-node Kubernetes cluster, pinning\nTwenty to a dedicated tainted node with custom DNS (`ndots: 1`); server\nand worker scheduled and started successfully\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22233?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Charles Bochet <charles@twenty.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb1fa4ce2f38590086985a22ddf20e34bcd35f1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/bb1fa4ce2f38590086985a22ddf20e34bcd35f1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/921c528cc3b86aa08ef19a8bc2dd04a6df5fc385","verification":{"payload":"tree bb1fa4ce2f38590086985a22ddf20e34bcd35f1a\nparent 6e319283c4749daaba74eeea2b6b8b14ca4d453f\nauthor Miguel <miguel.horcajada.oliva@gmail.com> 1782730842 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782730842 +0200\n\nfeat(helm): add nodeSelector, tolerations and DNS overrides to server and worker (#22233)\n\nCloses #22250\n\n## What\n\nAdds four standard pod spec fields to both server and worker Deployments\nof the Helm chart, exposed under `server.*` and `worker.*` in\n`values.yaml`:\n\n- `nodeSelector`\n- `tolerations`\n- `dnsPolicy`\n- `dnsConfig`\n\n## Why\n\nSelf-hosters who run Twenty on clusters with dedicated nodes, taints, or\ncustom DNS requirements currently need to fork the chart or patch\nrendered manifests with Kustomize. These are the standard pod spec\nfields supported by virtually every other community chart (Bitnami,\nprometheus-community, cert-manager, etc.) and are commonly needed in\nproduction setups.\n\n## How\n\nUses the same `{{- with }}` pattern already present in the chart (e.g.\n`extraEnv`, `extraVolumeMounts`), so empty defaults skip rendering\nentirely:\n\n```yaml\n{{- with .Values.server.nodeSelector }}\nnodeSelector:\n  {{- toYaml . | nindent 8 }}\n{{- end }}\n```\n\n## Backward compatibility\n\nFully backward compatible. Defaults are empty:\n\n```yaml\nserver:\n  nodeSelector: {}\n  tolerations: []\n  dnsPolicy: ~\n  dnsConfig: {}\n```\n\n`helm template` output is bit-identical to the previous version for any\nexisting install.\n\n## Schema note\n\n`dnsPolicy` is typed as `[string, null]` and the enum includes `null` so\nthe empty default (`dnsPolicy: ~`) passes validation. The `{{- with }}`\nguard treats null as falsy and renders nothing.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `helm lint` passes\n- `helm template` with default values produces bit-identical output to\nbefore this PR\n- `helm template` with values set renders the four fields correctly on\nboth server and worker\n- Live install validated on a multi-node Kubernetes cluster, pinning\nTwenty to a dedicated tainted node with custom DNS (`ndots: 1`); server\nand worker scheduled and started successfully\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22233?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Charles Bochet <charles@twenty.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQlBaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdz4QAA23UD4d7K2xHsp4JcSQyqIX\n4vNWouXP7HVmRzJAFaETnZpqo2B70WYlbBeJPOuvG1cs/PjvOrFquB1HbOa9vZ/d\nTHq4291bpfyej/AEYg/1UtcqGoRiemsXCVhfb1LEzj2YKj8mNpDNInwDc5WkA/Pd\nHkJXeSUbCPRC8zPxqGRRc9vdU