s","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commit/56deba351b79c05b84434703629f40cfe43909e9","node_id":"C_kwDOTPIvWNoAKDU2ZGViYTM1MWI3OWMwNWI4NDQzNDcwMzYyOWY0MGNmZTQzOTA5ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commit/02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c","sha":"02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c"}],"sha":"56deba351b79c05b84434703629f40cfe43909e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/56deba351b79c05b84434703629f40cfe43909e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T09:03:16Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T09:03:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai-tools): make navigate_app tool schema a valid object root for direct model binding (#22284)\n\n## Problem\n\nUsing an AI Agent step in a workflow fails with:\n\n> Invalid schema for function ''navigate_app'': schema must be a JSON\nSchema of ''type: \"object\"'', got ''type: \"None\"''.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `navigate_app` tool declared its `inputSchema` as a top-level\n`z.discriminatedUnion(''type'', [...])`. When serialized via\n`toToolJsonSchema`, a discriminated union produces a **root-level\n`anyOf`** with no top-level `\"type\"`:\n\n```json\n{ \"anyOf\": [ { \"type\": \"object\", ... }, ... ] }\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22284?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"bf121f2380e84783ea2e667a9c7c0b74e469f547","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/bf121f2380e84783ea2e667a9c7c0b74e469f547"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c","verification":{"payload":"tree bf121f2380e84783ea2e667a9c7c0b74e469f547\nparent 71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1782723796 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782723796 +0000\n\nfix(ai-tools): make navigate_app tool schema a valid object root for direct model binding (#22284)\n\n## Problem\n\nUsing an AI Agent step in a workflow fails with:\n\n> Invalid schema for function ''navigate_app'': schema must be a JSON\nSchema of ''type: \"object\"'', got ''type: \"None\"''.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `navigate_app` tool declared its `inputSchema` as a top-level\n`z.discriminatedUnion(''type'', [...])`. When serialized via\n`toToolJsonSchema`, a discriminated union produces a **root-level\n`anyOf`** with no top-level `\"type\"`:\n\n```json\n{ \"anyOf\": [ { \"type\": \"object\", ... }, ... ] }\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22284?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQjTUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOVIQAKJVnuhk8RIQuc/qA/pWL4Hi\nzow7JKRe+VF64iq0Rm5HHrwmBzbOKeioob+8Dvkwmi1xi2mlJCqwSw+O+/YlC9WP\nK0tWqLxAAGf8SuPgIhYF6efl9MC9josXq3pzNXnQ7aqitJ8CrzAfo45l9OjJ90k8\no+bDaBQznViTmHP6CduI0VK0lSwNIZj1xL9rbreRaotTsNYR846+P1fp9+xect9h\nZEZl3qIRT1KEfb+lfJuKzUe18g76SRrO+bz8f4oVZ9drgJcRSOsKxNVHWSgiylxw\nhS348Q88WGXnKdi/gC4u4ATsCWpWV7lNRJPw9UOU6t9vm+ar2IG02cFENYz7yAHX\n56fzb036LYMA6zF8yBzsXVZT8e3McnFac5/4xYk2Y0j/z7r6Qyx/LJDIfoCY6UdP\nPEyyRXYfZ+52iQpQ2mQXdels9521lbwVCBtXPVTMBNK5D3nXJIwch9ycnvPaY03n\nyxVD4jLQyVWqYt30qIm6Meg1FGk5HOuZHhfzvRk7Iyx4OHTcvkO7UzCn/TawzN28\n0+ZFXxEPnNdZugkF+Oy7V7/OYtG6CsZqmVupdQC+x8bHTt6rzdQWViYAh9howUkf\n377nXXCfjsBVwc5pWTIT7lmaYbUv8FgjPyik8azSrgyx8GKi0jJMJcolJ3r7lA3P\n4ch69SYeQt7omxNODe6O\n=jGcM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T11:43:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commit/02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c","node_id":"C_kwDOTPIvWNoAKDAyZDYyYzQxNzU4OWU2MDU4YzA5ZjA2ZDlhNDk1ZmM5Yjc5YTA3NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commit/71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561","sha":"71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561"}],"sha":"02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/02d62c417589e6058c09f06d9a495fc9b79a075c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T08:08:40Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T08:08:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): dedupe in-flight application translation catalog loads (#22285)\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter v2.17.0 shipped app-owned metadata translations (#22235), `POST\n/metadata` got slower for workspaces with translation-carrying apps\ninstalled. Sentry flagged it as an N+1\n(`performance_n_plus_one_db_queries`): a single request fires **many**\nconcurrent identical queries:\n\n```sql\nSELECT … FROM \"core\".\"applicationTranslation\" WHERE \"applicationRegistrationId\" = $1 AND \"deletedAt\" IS NULL\n```\n\nSpan aggregates since the deploy: **272** such spans, **avg 74 ms**,\n**p95 556 ms**, **max 694 ms**, all on `POST /metadata`. HTTP stays 200\n— it''s latency, not errors.\n\nReported via Sentry `TWENTY-SERVER-HQY` (`twenty-v7`).\n\n## Root cause\n\n`ApplicationTranslationCacheService` kept a TTL value cache but had **no\nin-flight de-duplication**. The object/field metadata resolvers call\n`getCatalog` directly, per record. On a cold/expired (30 s TTL) cache,\nmany fields of the same app resolve concurrently, all miss, and each\nfires its own `repository.find` — a classic cache **stampede**, which\nqueues on the connection pool and produces the 556–694 ms tail. Each\nread also pulls the full per-locale `messages` JSON, so the redundant\nreads aren''t free.\n\n## Fix\n\nRebuild the service on the shared **`PromiseMemoizer`** primitive — the\nsame one `WorkspaceCacheService` and `CoreEntityCacheService` already\nuse. It pairs the 30 s TTL value cache with a `pending` promise map, so\nconcurrent callers for the same registration **share a single in-flight\nquery** instead of stampeding. Per-request query count for a given app\ngoes from N → 1.\n\n- Public API (`getCatalog` / `invalidate`) is unchanged — no caller\ntouched.\n- `invalidate` now clears via `memoizer.clearKeys(...)` (clears both the\ncached value and any in-flight read), matching `WorkspaceCacheService`.\n- Adds a unit test asserting 10 concurrent `getCatalog` calls trigger\nexactly **one** `repository.find`, plus cache-hit / empty-locale /\npost-invalidation reload cases.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Process-local 30 s TTL behaviour is unchanged (deliberate; no\ncross-process invalidation), this only removes the redundant concurrent\nreads.\n- Verified formatting with oxfmt locally; couldn''t run the server test\nsuite in this environment, so relying on CI for typecheck/test.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01NiE7o3cd3zCLZarVkJa6UA\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01NiE7o3cd3zCLZarVkJa6UA)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22285?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"2cc144ecd12b551f7aca5dbe1cae594ca598e3c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/2cc144ecd12b551f7aca5dbe1cae594ca598e3c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cc144ecd12b551f7aca5dbe1cae594ca598e3c0\nparent 13f80f0d95f734e41f25b698ed79d87fb0bc2741\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1782720520 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782720520 +0200\n\nfix(server): dedupe in-flight application translation catalog loads (#22285)\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter v2.17.0 shipped app-owned metadata translations (#22235), `POST\n/metadata` got slower for workspaces with translation-carrying apps\ninstalled. Sentry flagged it as an N+1\n(`performance_n_plus_one_db_queries`): a single request fires **many**\nconcurrent identical queries:\n\n```sql\nSELECT … FROM \"core\".\"applicationTranslation\" WHERE \"applicationRegistrationId\" = $1 AND \"deletedAt\" IS NULL\n```\n\nSpan aggregates since the deploy: **272** such spans, **avg 74 ms**,\n**p95 556 ms**, **max 694 ms**, all on `POST /metadata`. HTTP stays 200\n— it''s latency, not errors.\n\nReported via Sentry `TWENTY-SERVER-HQY` (`twenty-v7`).\n\n## Root cause\n\n`ApplicationTranslationCacheService` kept a TTL value cache but had **no\nin-flight de-duplication**. The object/field metadata resolvers call\n`getCatalog` directly, per record. On a cold/expired (30 s TTL) cache,\nmany fields of the same app resolve concurrently, all miss, and each\nfires its own `repository.find` — a classic cache **stampede**, which\nqueues on the connection pool and produces the 556–694 ms tail. Each\nread also pulls the full per-locale `messages` JSON, so the redundant\nreads aren''t free.\n\n## Fix\n\nRebuild the service on the shared **`PromiseMemoizer`** primitive — the\nsame one `WorkspaceCacheService` and `CoreEntityCacheService` already\nuse. It pairs the 30 s TTL value cache with a `pending` promise map, so\nconcurrent callers for the same registration **share a single in-flight\nquery** instead of stampeding. Per-request query count for a given app\ngoes from N → 1.\n\n- Public API (`getCatalog` / `invalidate`) is unchanged — no caller\ntouched.\n- `invalidate` now clears via `memoizer.clearKeys(...)` (clears both the\ncached value and any in-flight read), matching `WorkspaceCacheService`.\n- Adds a unit test asserting 10 concurrent `getCatalog` calls trigger\nexactly **one** `repository.find`, plus cache-hit / empty-locale /\npost-invalidation reload cases.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Process-local 30 s TTL behaviour is unchanged (deliberate; no\ncross-process invalidation), this only removes the redundant concurrent\nreads.\n- Verified formatting with oxfmt locally; couldn''t run the server test\nsuite in this environment, so relying on CI for typecheck/test.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01NiE7o3cd3zCLZarVkJa6UA\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01NiE7o3cd3zCLZarVkJa6UA)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22285?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQigICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAznYQAEqQaLSRdoWPvJUZLIsCrgKz\nGFqSi1A0wHx2e9aHGwjoBGN//BGngFxzi40iR1dnrf2isL7R/0QeUUsjrwH