,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/13f80f0d95f734e41f25b698ed79d87fb0bc2741"}],"sha":"71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/71370d9e66d14782b52b9df52f27bb42c39a8561"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246701683?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahirhir","id":246701683,"login":"mahirhir","node_id":"U_kgDODrRecw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahirhir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/13f80f0d95f734e41f25b698ed79d87fb0bc2741/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T06:08:11Z","email":"m.hirakawa07@icloud.com","name":"greymoth"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T06:08:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ignore IME composition Enter in chat-thread and attachment rename inputs (#22270)\n\n## What''s this PR doing?\n\nTwo inline rename inputs run their action on `Enter` without ignoring\nthe `Enter` that confirms an IME composition:\n\n- `AiChatThreadListItem` (renaming an AI chat thread). It also calls\n`preventDefault()`, so the composition-commit `Enter` is swallowed and\nthe half-typed title gets saved.\n- `AttachmentRow` (renaming an attachment). The same `Enter` saves the\nunfinished name.\n\nWhen you type with an IME (Japanese, Chinese, Korean), the first `Enter`\nafter typing confirms the candidate text rather than submitting, so\nthese handlers fire with text the user hasn''t finished entering.\n\n## Why\n\nThe codebase already guards this where keyboard handling goes through\n`useHotkeysOnFocusedElement` (`if (keyboardEvent.isComposing ||\nkeyboardEvent.keyCode === 229) return`), and the inline inputs that\ndon''t use that hook add the same check themselves: see\n`SettingsAccountsBlocklistInput`, `SettingsDevelopersApiKeysNew`, and\nthe sign-up workspace forms. These two rename inputs were just missing\nit.\n\n## How\n\nAdd the same `isComposing || keyCode === 229` guard before the `Enter`\nbranch. For input without an IME, `isComposing` is `false` and `keyCode`\nis `13`, so the rename-on-Enter behavior stays the same. This only skips\nthe action on the composition-commit key.\n\nI checked the change against the repo''s Prettier config locally. I\ncouldn''t add a unit test because jsdom doesn''t dispatch real composition\nevents (`isComposing` stays `false`), so it can''t reproduce the\nkeystroke. Happy to add an e2e test if that''s preferred.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22270?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"b5f16faaa102ca31f1975cf418e2372db808f5cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/b5f16faaa102ca31f1975cf418e2372db808f5cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/13f80f0d95f734e41f25b698ed79d87fb0bc2741","verification":{"payload":"tree b5f16faaa102ca31f1975cf418e2372db808f5cc\nparent 68f4cf269d1c50adc1eb42c9358790b316c166a3\nauthor greymoth <m.hirakawa07@icloud.com> 1782713291 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782713291 +0200\n\nfix: ignore IME composition Enter in chat-thread and attachment rename inputs (#22270)\n\n## What''s this PR doing?\n\nTwo inline rename inputs run their action on `Enter` without ignoring\nthe `Enter` that confirms an IME composition:\n\n- `AiChatThreadListItem` (renaming an AI chat thread). It also calls\n`preventDefault()`, so the composition-commit `Enter` is swallowed and\nthe half-typed title gets saved.\n- `AttachmentRow` (renaming an attachment). The same `Enter` saves the\nunfinished name.\n\nWhen you type with an IME (Japanese, Chinese, Korean), the first `Enter`\nafter typing confirms the candidate text rather than submitting, so\nthese handlers fire with text the user hasn''t finished entering.\n\n## Why\n\nThe codebase already guards this where keyboard handling goes through\n`useHotkeysOnFocusedElement` (`if (keyboardEvent.isComposing ||\nkeyboardEvent.keyCode === 229) return`), and the inline inputs that\ndon''t use that hook add the same check themselves: see\n`SettingsAccountsBlocklistInput`, `SettingsDevelopersApiKeysNew`, and\nthe sign-up workspace forms. These two rename inputs were just missing\nit.\n\n## How\n\nAdd the same `isComposing || keyCode === 229` guard before the `Enter`\nbranch. For input without an IME, `isComposing` is `false` and `keyCode`\nis `13`, so the rename-on-Enter behavior stays the same. This only skips\nthe action on the composition-commit key.\n\nI checked the change against the repo''s Prettier config locally. I\ncouldn''t add a unit test because jsdom doesn''t dispatch real composition\nevents (`isComposing` stays `false`), so it can''t reproduce the\nkeystroke. Happy to add an e2e test if that''s preferred.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22270?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQgvLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6Q8QACtlwkKDpcFlJjAnsNJg1PzM\nnRbBj1QjkhPgk/zf7TOriI7xleUiEE9NNfjAmzrVp4a2FsCCJwKaR85OTKvERpKZ\n+3QiiyNKiOdbp90fqBmzDhJAKgwZ2B6ijTdgnA6Pj2AV7k3lCWWQlzlT+LsOGdjK\nFb2o36YAQmNIovjJLuhcwqEmoSB3NJ9kl4XNIrcQEwoJE8cuimcn7ashrVbllYh8\njyDFJeK9p2tE3bVxWrkasLr2+EcsYIXVHCwZRNC3UNKBx55OeOaoQsCNiGgicE+v\n2I7x64PCZxBAgQQ4UfIYYQjsIJ2VbfGHfqI3VRXaEAtA+gE4DJ7nzvI2OrGNhYXZ\nfndhxinRCA71guIwJTUplnK21NMrTSgoyvIs0GxdpwmqZ6mJ4rPx+j2gDoq518Q+\nkkUPhNHqjZ44S81cUwODQ9El00FraFzBXhQdAwX0nV/90YNxlZrVXHw2TtodLGe+\nZFGuw6W9E66LrpaLYA92TSG7W+woCMjrD6OY/SmCWqDiXdKcqT8CZc+EySRehIXQ\nHu8RROoawgmzfRZ0bWEJC603EE7eDc0T8Cgn4TGGxSLZNXBrXSkdI4wfUXnTxcze\no3MIzN7V/Epmjzjczu1kJecEHBGovft0ELd0JnGJJyvA3Eo1fzU6RYkSU0k05o+7\nDeyY6KC4oYQjQ3bzhl3k\n=KD6p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T11:43:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow"