abdullahabaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mabdullahabaid","id":125115953,"login":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/commits/012af11d77f6c63d0791d78496eee096a22be222/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T09:39:59Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T09:39:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(website): ship all documentation locales (multi-locale site) (#22257)\n\n## What\n\nThe marketing site now serves every language the **documentation** ships\n— 14 locales (`en, fr, ar, cs, de, es, it, ja, ko, pt, ro, ru, tr, zh`),\nup from 3 (`en, es, fr`).\n\n## How\n\n- **Single source of truth.** `WEBSITE_LOCALE_LIST` derives directly\nfrom `DOCUMENTATION_SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES` (`twenty-shared/constants`).\nAdd a documentation language → it flows to the website automatically.\n- **Off `APP_LOCALES` entirely.** The website locale type is now\n`DocumentationSupportedLanguage` (short codes), so a locale **is** its\nURL segment — no short↔full mapping, and no `pt-BR`/`zh-CN` ambiguity to\nresolve.\n- **Removed the indirection this exposed** (it only existed because\n`AppLocale` was a superset of the deployed set):\n- `locale-to-url-segment` / `locale-by-url-segment` (locale == segment)\n- `get-locale-messages` pass-through → callers read `MESSAGES_BY_LOCALE`\ndirectly\n- the `messages-by-locale` runtime guard → a total\n`Record<DocumentationSupportedLanguage, Messages>` (a missing catalog is\nnow a **compile** error, not a runtime throw)\n- `isWebsiteLocale` → a `string → DocumentationSupportedLanguage` type\nguard\n  - the vestigial language-code `split(''-'')` in `locale-display-name`\n\n## Catalogs\n\n- Renamed `es-ES → es`, `fr-FR → fr`; added 11 new locales (untranslated\nfor now → **English fallback**).\n- `crowdin-website.yml` switched to `%two_letters_code%`.\n- Regenerating catalogs also synced `en.po` with current source\n(`Boolean` / `Date & Time` / removed `Fields widget` from the\nalready-merged #22249).\n- `ci-website` is unchanged — no `lingui:compile` step added; catalogs\nstay committed.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `typecheck` · `lint` (check-conventions + oxlint + oxfmt) · 347/347\ntests — all green. PR CI runs exactly lint + typecheck + test.\n\n## Follow-up (out of repo)\n\nEnable the 11 languages on **Crowdin project 4** so `website-i18n-pull`\nbackfills real translations. Until then, the new locales render with\nEnglish fallback (correct behavior).","tree":{"sha":"31fd44c39a96ff891a975ddcd80e9e41dec1f3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/trees/31fd44c39a96ff891a975ddcd80e9e41dec1f3df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ogSulem/KarkasCRM/git/commits/012af11d77f6c63d0791d78496eee096a22be222","verification":{"payload":"tree 31fd44c39a96ff891a975ddcd80e9e41dec1f3df\nparent d81b3c3fa3d6bbecfaf17fc7e3dbc23d73d94fbe\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1782639599 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782639599 +0500\n\nfeat(website): ship all documentation locales (multi-locale site) (#22257)\n\n## What\n\nThe marketing site now serves every language the **documentation** ships\n— 14 locales (`en, fr, ar, cs, de, es, it, ja, ko, pt, ro, ru, tr, zh`),\nup from 3 (`en, es, fr`).\n\n## How\n\n- **Single source of truth.** `WEBSITE_LOCALE_LIST` derives directly\nfrom `DOCUMENTATION_SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES` (`twenty-shared/constants`).\nAdd a documentation language → it flows to the website automatically.\n- **Off `APP_LOCALES` entirely.** The website locale type is now\n`DocumentationSupportedLanguage` (short codes), so a locale **is** its\nURL segment — no short↔full mapping, and no `pt-BR`/`zh-CN` ambiguity to\nresolve.\n- **Removed the indirection this exposed** (it only existed because\n`AppLocale` was a superset of the deployed set):\n- `locale-to-url-segment` / `locale-by-url-segment` (locale == segment)\n- `get-locale-messages` pass-through → callers read `MESSAGES_BY_LOCALE`\ndirectly\n- the `messages-by-locale` runtime guard → a total\n`Record<DocumentationSupportedLanguage, Messages>` (a missing catalog is\nnow a **compile** error, not a runtime throw)\n- `isWebsiteLocale` → a `string → DocumentationSupportedLanguage` type\nguard\n  - the vestigial language-code `split(''-'')` in `locale-display-name`\n\n## Catalogs\n\n- Renamed `es-ES → es`, `fr-FR → fr`; added 11 new locales (untranslated\nfor now → **English fallback**).\n- `crowdin-website.yml` switched to `%two_letters_code%`.\n- Regenerating catalogs also synced `en.po` with current source\n(`Boolean` / `Date & Time` / removed `Fields widget` from the\nalready-merged #22249).\n- `ci-website` is unchanged — no `lingui:compile` step added; catalogs\nstay committed.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `typecheck` · `lint` (check-conventions + oxlint + oxfmt) · 347/347\ntests — all green. PR CI runs exactly lint + typecheck + test.\n\n## Follow-up (out of repo)\n\nEnable the 11 languages on **Crowdin project 4** so `website-i18n-pull`\nbackfills real translations. Until then, the new locales render with\nEnglish fallback (correct behavior).","r