691635+zyonlab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zyonlab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:52:22Z","email":"272691635+zyonlab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zyonlab"},"message":"docs: 按 artemis 版式重写中文 README\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea46ab1303d5960dc8f14cca9396b616d8685e60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/ea46ab1303d5960dc8f14cca9396b616d8685e60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/ac0b4307c2cd2614b6d4d879ffdf5aaee5cdf06d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272691635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab","id":272691635,"login":"zyonlab","node_id":"U_kgDOEEDxsw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/ac0b4307c2cd2614b6d4d879ffdf5aaee5cdf06d","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGFjMGI0MzA3YzJjZDI2MTRiNmQ0ZDg3OWZmZGY1YWFlZTVjZGYwNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/a55881f30b7c735390c885bed642116f85411209","sha":"a55881f30b7c735390c885bed642116f85411209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/a55881f30b7c735390c885bed642116f85411209"}],"sha":"ac0b4307c2cd2614b6d4d879ffdf5aaee5cdf06d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/ac0b4307c2cd2614b6d4d879ffdf5aaee5cdf06d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272691635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab","id":272691635,"login":"zyonlab","node_id":"U_kgDOEEDxsw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/a55881f30b7c735390c885bed642116f85411209/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T13:19:50Z","email":"support@appidge.com","name":"zyonlab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T13:19:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix CI: the pipeline had never run, and what it found when it did\n\nThe repo had 100+ workflow runs and 0 successes. This branch makes the pipeline\nparse, execute, and pass end to end — and fixes the defects it surfaced once it\nwas actually looking.\n\n## Why nothing ran\n\n`secrets` in a step-level `if:`. GitHub rejects the whole workflow at validation\ntime, which surfaces as a 0-second run with no jobs and no logs. Hoisted to a\njob-level `env`. Found by elimination: a minimal probe ran in 8s on the same push.\n\nSeparately, `on: pull_request:` carried no `types`, so the `e2e` label could be\napplied and would never trigger anything — the documented escape hatch was inert.\n\n## What it found once it ran\n\nSix of these are product defects, not CI configuration:\n\n- **/markets answered 503 to every visitor.** markets-table inlines a rule that\n  styles its own degraded state, so `data-fallback=\"true\"` appeared in every\n  healthy response and the runtime''s deprecated HTML sniff misclassified each\n  one. Required slot \"failed\" -> page unhealthy -> gateway 503, every layer\n  behaving exactly as specified. The sniff is now removed entirely; metadata is\n  the only signal.\n- **Every product page requested an image that does not exist** — `<Image>` built\n  a path from the product id and `apps/page-product` has no `public/`.\n- **CLS 0.2027 against a 0.1 budget**, from diagnostics rendered above content\n  (578px) plus streamed slots with no reserved space. Slots can now declare\n  `reserveHeightPx`; CLS is 0 on four routes and 0.0075 on the fifth.\n- **Two pages imported a workspace package they never declared**, invisible to a\n  whole-repo build and fatal to the per-unit build each Dockerfile runs. A new\n  `undeclared-workspace-import` audit rule closes the class.\n- **The runtime gate''s every `page.evaluate` was dead** (`__name`, esbuild''s\n  keepNames helper) and it never exited after failing — one CI job held a runner\n  for 2h29m.\n- **`key={hint.kind}` duplicated React keys** on page-product, the one page that\n  had not moved to the composite key the other four use.\n\n## What the gates could not tell us\n\nThree fixes were about diagnosability, and each paid for itself within one run:\nthe failing gate''s own output, the URL behind a bare \"Failed to load resource\",\nand the elements behind a bare CLS number.\n\n`docker-smoke` checked 2 of 7 composed routes while deriving its health checks\nfrom the registry — that gap is why the /markets 503 went unseen. Now all seven,\nderived, which also absorbs each page''s first render before the runtime gate runs.\n\n## Claims corrected to match reality\n\n- The smoke suite required a `data-shell-gateway` marker that three other tests\n  assert is ABSENT (the gateway became a transparent proxy in 058f13b).\n- `E2E_STRICT=1` was applied to a JavaScript-disabled browser, where live\n  composition provably cannot complete.\n- page-home''s no-JS claim said \"fully readable\", which streaming cannot deliver.\n  It now states what is guaranteed, and asserts each part.\n\n## Verification\n\n14/14 gates, 22 images built, 22 containers up, smoke 29/29, runtime gate 5/5,\nPlaywright 35 passed / 5 skipped / 0 failed under `E2E_STRICT=1`.\n\nThe `docker` job is skipped on PRs and will execute for the first time on this\nmerge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"6ef70fe27aab1ce7109554d4a1aa35a41d7351aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/6ef70fe27aab1ce7109554d4a1aa35a41d7351aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/a55881f30b7c735390c885bed642116f85411209","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ef70fe27aab1ce7109554d4a1aa35a41d7351aa\nparent 4a458114294e14c36ec1573b6498ca42ebb436de\nparent ce5b73a85a727e5a2c88dfe4e9a9efa2e2480c99\nauthor zyonlab <support@appidge.com> 1789996790 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789996790 +0800\n\nFix CI: the pipeline had never run, and what it found when it did\n\nThe repo had 100+ workflow runs and 0 successes. This branch makes the pipeline\nparse, execute, and pass end to end — and fixes the defects it surfaced once it\nwas actually looking.\n\n## Why nothing ran\n\n`secrets` in a step-level `if:`. GitHub rejects the whole workflow at validation\ntime, which surfaces as a 0-second run with no jobs and no logs. Hoisted to a\njob-level `env`. Found by elimination: a minimal probe ran in 8s on the same push.\n\nSeparately, `on: pull_request:` carried no `types`, so the `e2e` label could be\napplied and would never trigger anything — the documented escape hatch was inert.\n\n## What it found once it ran\n\nSix of these are product defects, not CI configuration:\n\n- **/markets answered 503 to every visitor.** markets-table inlines a rule that\n  styles its own degraded state, so `data-fallback=\"true\"` appeared in every\n  healthy response and the runtime''s deprecated HTML sniff misclassified each\n  one. Required slot \"failed\" -> page unhealthy -> gateway 503, every layer\n  behaving exactly as specified. The sniff is now removed entirely; metadata is\n  the only signal.\n- **Every product page requested an image that does not exist** — `<Image>` built\n  a path from the product id and `apps/page-product` has no `public/`.\n- **CLS 0.2027 against a 0.1 budget**, from diagnostics rendered above content\n  (578px) plus streamed slots with no reserved space. Slots can now declare\n  `reserveHeightPx`; CLS is 0 on four routes and 0.0075 on the fifth.\n- **Two pages imported a workspace package they never declared**, invisible to a\n  whole-repo build and fatal to the per-unit build each Dockerfile runs. A new\n  `undeclared-workspace-import` audit rule closes the class.\n- **The runtime gate''s every `page.evaluate` was dead** (`__name`, esbuild''s\n  keepNames helper) and it never exited after failing — one CI job held a runner\n  for 2h29m.\n- **`key={hint.kind}` duplicated React keys** on page-product, the one page that\n  had not moved to the composite key the other four use.\n\n## What the gates could not tell us\n\nThree fixes were about diagnosability, and each paid for itself within one run:\nthe failing gate''s own output, the URL behind a bare \"Failed to load resource\",\nand the elements behind a bare CLS number.\n\n`docker-smoke` checked 2 of 7 composed routes while deriving its health checks\nfrom the registry — that gap is why the /markets 503 went unseen. Now all seven,\nderived, which also absorbs each page''s first render before the runtime gate runs.\n\n## Claims corrected to match reality\n\n- The smoke suite required a `data-shell-gateway` marker that three other tests\n  assert is ABSENT (the gateway became a transparent proxy in 058f13b).\n- `E2E_STRICT=1` was applied to a JavaScript-disabled browser, where live\n  composition provably cannot complete.\n- page-home''s no-JS claim said \"fully readable\", which streaming cannot deliver.\n  It now states what is guaranteed, and asserts each part.\n\n## Verification\n\n14/14 gates, 22 images built, 22 containers up, smoke 29/29, runtime gate 5/5,\nPlaywright 35 passed / 5 skipped / 0 failed under `E2E_STRICT=1`.\n\nThe `docker` job is skipped on PRs and will execute for the first time on this\nmerge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsS72CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9J0QAFtZxbPODhYAfeoMzYaI7GCl\nBIJ1i2XdFyFb64UGegh/0GhAY+v5NgyIkTk8JG4FhdCk3GkgRIiJWkK5QwBskQUM\napg1TBGzOEaXtX7DC7W8S5ifRQGUgYhudi2HKPKD5NYISrEqBOAhmnybekxzEDlc\nhjYIbcCTLxSNVPqNHt6Ja4Vtn8jXELJB3W1RgFr8xsPTRajHp6OaPQBCSskGOQO1\naw8qYTnawOnWWHkGGcPFeIxtfMivTqe0olVcIxOb9v64aaQSkW7VEn8iKY60ZtHH\njoxNsTkXfjVe6phMNRjhK2X5bC0VdR3Rae/6dZ9ujbCrBmt0yrP8C1AE3nTTaX3X\nDB8juVY5uWNRIeSXYTElfR7P0xGcFhGKdMRyEcNQuODZsQoi/9TUx7dsQCvZtJtR\nm/9X4fr9I7gxOMM6HXNJ/gZZEB2duy2WVJLkbhbwb2lrVoUzxEcQbJnD8PW4ndDr\nloNg2SISONmQv5GdSbvzn127fYphTm4uGmM1IXrOlu+r9sIlApbzSBUKyfNMi7RP\nhCV4CRnqijmXvkvBOPFl6SucHRN4rjuFCwGW90JAo4YCn9OpxD44EW9a+kWe/Z5J\nLWSS1TD/8KhqmpxBRwWaLh/JLZKTyRuak9tl6lgOXr5M7iayTCBmJE6QGGJOe1hf\ncO1VJG503b2Az06rrQEl\n=jA0o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T13:19:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.githu