rs/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/ce5b73a85a727e5a2c88dfe4e9a9efa2e2480c99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:25:52Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:51:31Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"chore(reports): verify artifacts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ef70fe27aab1ce7109554d4a1aa35a41d7351aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/6ef70fe27aab1ce7109554d4a1aa35a41d7351aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/ce5b73a85a727e5a2c88dfe4e9a9efa2e2480c99","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/ce5b73a85a727e5a2c88dfe4e9a9efa2e2480c99","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGNlNWI3M2E4NWE3MjdlNWEyYzg4ZGZlNGU5YTllZmEyZTI0ODBjOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64","sha":"796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64"}],"sha":"ce5b73a85a727e5a2c88dfe4e9a9efa2e2480c99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/ce5b73a85a727e5a2c88dfe4e9a9efa2e2480c99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:51:30Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:51:31Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(e2e): make the no-JS claim one the page can keep, and assert it\n\nThe header said \"the composed home page must be fully readable with client\nJavaScript disabled\". It cannot be. page-home declares\n`streaming:suspense-per-slot`, and a streamed slot resolves after the shell is\nflushed — React places late `<Suspense>` content with an inline script, so with\nJS off the slot keeps showing its fallback. The claim and the declared feature\ncontradicted each other, and nothing noticed because this project had never run\nin CI.\n\nCorrecting the claim rather than dropping the streaming demo: what a no-JS\nreader actually gets is the shell, the headings, the editorial content, the\nrealtime island''s SSR snapshot, and every fragment slot carrying readable copy —\nlive if it resolved into the shell, otherwise its fallback line, which is\n`fallback-isolation`, another thing this page declares, working as designed.\n\nEach of those is now asserted, including two that were not:\n\n- the island''s `heat`/`stock` fields are non-empty. It renders directly in\n  `<main>`, not behind a boundary, which is what makes `initialSnapshot`\n  readable with no JS — the claim `RealtimeInsights.tsx` makes.\n- each slot''s text is non-empty, tightened from `toBeVisible()`. \"Visible\"\n  passes on an empty box, and an empty box is precisely what a no-JS reader\n  must never get.\n\nWhat is explicitly NOT guaranteed is written down too: that a streamed slot\nshows live copy, and that the diagnostics section appears at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be07edbd0b35a3252d3d5c2dbd243c49c3efec61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/be07edbd0b35a3252d3d5c2dbd243c49c3efec61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDc5NmIzNjMwM2FjZTI1ZDc2NGRiMmFlMzMxYTJlNGMyMGY0MDJmNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413","sha":"6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413"}],"sha":"796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/796b36303ace25d764db2ae331a2e4c20f402f64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:49:01Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:51:31Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"refactor(runtime): classify a fallback by its metadata and nothing else\n\n`isFallbackResponse` kept a second path — sniffing the HTML for\n`data-fallback=\"true\"` — \"until every fragment stamps metadata.fallback on its\nown degraded path\". All 14 do, so the condition it was waiting for is met.\n\nRemoving it rather than keeping the narrowed version, because narrowing fixed an\ninstance and not the class. markets-table inlines a rule that styles its own\ndegraded state, so the marker string appeared in every healthy response and\nevery render was misclassified — its required slot \"failed\", the page reported\nunhealthy, and the gateway answered /markets with 503 to every visitor. Skipping\n`<style>` and `<script>` bodies fixed that shape. It does not fix the next one:\nthe marker can legitimately appear in any text a fragment renders — a code\nsample, a docs snippet, an escaped attribute. A string search over arbitrary\nHTML cannot decide this question. The metadata flag can.\n\nThe trade-off, stated rather than hidden: a fragment built outside this repo\nthat returns a degraded response without `metadata.fallback` now counts as live.\nThat is the right place for the cost — `FragmentRenderResponseSchema` is the\ncontract a fragment must meet, and an unmarked fallback is a fragment bug the\nschema should grow to catch, not something to infer from markup.\n\n`data-fallback=\"true\"` stays on the markup: fragments emit it, CSS styles it,\nand `e2e/support/expect-fragment-content.ts` reads it off the DOM. Only the\nruntime''s classification stopped depending on it.\n\nThe removed behaviour is pinned inverted so it cannot creep back, alongside a\ntest that runs the same markup through both metadata values and gets both\nanswers. The three docs that described the old rule as current are updated;\n`ARCHITECTURE_REFACTOR_PLAN.md` is not, because its list is a record of what was\nfound, not of what is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cd1149757c9a9eef7657a2f5c7fc1bc37506cb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/1cd1149757c9a9eef7657a2f5c7fc1bc37506cb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDZkOTU4NzE4NzY2NzcyZjMzYmU3MTJjNjEzZWE2ZmZiOGQ4Yjk0MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d","sha":"30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d"}],"sha":"6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/6d958718766772f33be712c613ea6ffb8d8b9413"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:47:49Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:47:49Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(smoke): check every composed route, not a hand-picked two\n\nThe runtime gate failed on /trade/BTC with HTTP 503 — one run after the same\nroute passed. Cause, from the container logs: market-header''s only `/render`\ntook 172.74ms against that slot''s 200ms budget. `/trade/BTC` is the first\nrequest that reaches market-header, because smoke asked it for `/health` and\nnothing asked it to render. On a cold container 172 of 200 is a coin flip; over\nit, the required slot fails, the page reports unhealthy, and the gateway answers\n503 exactly as designed.\n\nRaising the slot timeout would paper over a CI cold start with a production\nchange. What was actually wrong is smaller and worse: the composed-route checks\nin this suite were TWO hardcoded entries (`/` and `/product/123`) while the\nper-service health checks beside them were derived from the registry. That gap\nis why /markets answered 503 to every visitor with no gate noticing — its page\nwas healthy, its fragment was healthy, and nothing asked the gateway for the\ncomposed route.\n\nNow one composed check per route in the registry, and both problems go away:\ncoverage matches the health plane, and because this suite retries until its\ndeadline it is the right place to absorb the first render of every page — the\nruntime gate that runs after it sees a warm stack.\n\n`data-page` happens to equal the route id on all seven pages, so the marker\nassertion derives too. Path parameters get sample values (`:id` -> 123,\n`:symbol` -> BTC) matching what e2e and the runtime gate already use, so all\nthree exercise the same pages; an unknown parameter keeps its name so the\nresulting 404 names it.\n\nSix tests asserted the old two-entry shape and are updated to assert the derived\none, plus the parameter substitution. Verified against the running stack: 24\nchecks -> 29, all seven composed routes green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46b2ded1bf36c9bb85e2321830dfd97bdf148ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/46b2ded1bf36c9bb85e2321830dfd97bdf148ea9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDMwYWJiYzliOTYwMTYyNWFhNzI2YmVjMzZiOTkyYjMzZDBiYTQxOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef","sha":"b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef"}],"sha":"30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/30abbc9b9601625aa726bec36b992b33d0ba419d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:18:15Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:18:15Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(e2e): stop asking the no-JS project to prove things JS is required for\n\nThe Playwright suite had never run either. 40 tests, 37 passing; all three\nfailures were in the `no-js` project, and the same tests pass with JS enabled.\nBoth causes are mis-specified assertions, not product regressions.\n\n1. `E2E_STRICT=1` was applied to a JavaScript-disabled browser.\n\n   Its own doc says the tier exists for \"when the full fragment stack is\n   expected to be healthy and you want e2e to actually prove live composition\n   works\". A streamed slot resolves after the shell is flushed and React places\n   late `<Suspense>` content with an inline script, so with JS disabled the\n   fallback is what stays — by construction. Demanding live content there does\n   not test the stack, it tests whether streaming works without JS. The spec\n   titles already say \"content OR its fallback\". Strict now applies only to\n   JS-enabled runs; that project still proves live composition strictly.\n\n2. Two tests asserted a timing race.\n\n   The diagnostics/trace section needs the full slot aggregate, so its boundary\n   resolves last — and whether that lands inside the shell flush (readable\n   without JS) or after it (needs the script) depends on how fast the stack is.\n   I first read this as \"unreachable without JS\" and marked it `test.fail()`;\n   the local run answered \"Expected to fail, but passed.\" It resolves in time\n   against a warm local stack and does not in the compose stack. A no-JS\n   contract cannot rest on that, so both trace tests — `shell-home` and\n   `shell-product`, the second of which CI had not yet reached — skip the no-JS\n   project, with the reason in the test.\n\nWhat the no-JS claim still covers is asserted: the shell, the headings, the\nfragment slots, the editorial block.\n\nWorth stating plainly, because it is a real limitation and not a test detail:\npage-home''s `demonstrates` lists both streaming and no-JS readability, and on\nthe same page those conflict. Without JS its streamed slots show \"Featured\noffers are loading.\" rather than live copy. page-trade is the other side of the\nsame trade-off — 9 slots through the synchronous `<FragmentSlot>`, so its\ncontent is in the shell. Whether page-home should make that swap is a product\ndecision; this commit documents it rather than taking it.\n\nLocally, E2E_STRICT=1 across both projects: 35 passed, 5 skipped, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87f742ca6c72c07dd293735003504f620c1c88c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/87f742ca6c72c07dd293735003504f620c1c88c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGI2N2M4YWY0Zjg4NTczNTIyNTRkMzFmYWRjZTY3N2Q1ZWFhZDViZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147","sha":"039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147"}],"sha":"b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/b67c8af4f8857352254d31fadce677d5eaad5bef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:39:54Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:40:04Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(pages): declare and hold each streamed slot''s height\n\nThe measured heights, taken in a real browser at 1680x1000 against the running\nstack (`getBoundingClientRect().height` per `[data-fragment]`), written through\n`mount-slot --reserve-height-px` rather than by hand-editing the manifests:\n\n  page-home       staticEditorial 66   promotion 52   recommendations 262\n  page-product    staticProof     66   promotion 52   recommendations 262\n  page-markets    marketsTable   109\n  page-portfolio  portfolioSummary 164 pnlChart 463\n\nEach page builds its fallbacks once through `reserveFallbacks(fragmentSlots, …)`,\nso the source of truth is the generated slot array and the heights cannot drift\nfrom the manifest.\n\npage-trade is deliberately untouched: it renders its 9 slots through the\nsynchronous `<FragmentSlot>`, so it has no fallback-to-content swap to hold space\nfor. page-vaults and page-referrals have no slots at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"295167bfd6eb024d711379de43dd89be582f92e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/295167bfd6eb024d711379de43dd89be582f92e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDAzOWU5MmIwYjJlODBlMDkxMjgyZmE1MzE2YTQxOTA1OTY2NjcxNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953","sha":"7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953"}],"sha":"039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/039e92b0b2e80e091282fa5316a4190596667147"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:39:42Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:39:54Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(runtime): let a slot declare the space to hold while it streams\n\nThe remaining CLS on the composed pages, and the general form of it: a streamed\nslot shows a one-line `<Suspense>` fallback until its HTML arrives, then the real\nmarkup replaces it and everything below moves. There was no way to express \"hold\nthis much room\", so every streamed slot shifted the page.\n\nA slot now declares `reserveHeightPx` in `manifest.slots.json`, and the page\nholds that height on the fallback until the slot resolves.\n\nTwo decisions worth stating:\n\n- The height belongs to the SLOT, not the fragment. The page needs it\n  synchronously, BEFORE the fragment answers — that is the entire point — and the\n  same fragment occupies different heights in different slots. A fragment\n  manifest would have to be fetched first, which defeats it.\n\n- `min-height` goes on the fallback element ITSELF, never a wrapper. The runtime\n  gate''s `layout-fit` check measures `[data-fragment]` boxes for content voids, so\n  a reserved-but-unfilled parent is exactly the defect it reports. A test pins\n  that no extra node appears.\n\nEnd to end: contract (optional, additive — a slot without it behaves as before),\n`FragmentSlotDefinition`, `reserveSlotHeight` / `reserveFallbacks` in\n`@mvp/runtime/react`, `mount-slot --reserve-height-px`, and codegen''s explicit\n`FIELD_ORDER` (a field missing from that list is silently dropped).\n\n`reserveFallbacks` is what pages call: one map per page, and the element it\nreturns is used for both the `<Suspense>` fallback and `<FragmentSlotStream>`''s\nresolved-but-empty fallback, so a slot holds its space on every path it can take.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18be7a055a65ca7233e1f885367746f59f4e8b00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/18be7a055a65ca7233e1f885367746f59f4e8b00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDdhY2RhZGNmZWNjM2IwZWI4YmI4ZDVjZmE4ZTVmOGQzNjA0MzE5NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe","sha":"9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe"}],"sha":"7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/7acdadcfecc3b0eb8bb8d5cfa8e5f8d360431953"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:39:42Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:39:54Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(page-home): render diagnostics last, like every other page already does\n\n578 of the 683px that put this page''s CLS at 0.2027 against a 0.1 budget.\n\nThe diagnostics block needs the FULL slot aggregate, so it is the last thing to\nresolve. page-home rendered it ABOVE the content, inside\n`<Suspense fallback={null}>` — zero reserved space — so when it finally arrived\nit inserted 578px and pushed the whole page down. Measured: the realtime island\nwent from y=271 to y=954.\n\npage-markets and page-portfolio already render it immediately before\n`</main>`; page-home was the one left behind, which is why it is the page that\nfailed. Diagnostics are a DEV/E2E appendix, not page content, so their late\narrival must not move anything.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"364bb9becd3d34a729e9dd82f8a06a40ce79baf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/364bb9becd3d34a729e9dd82f8a06a40ce79baf9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDlmZWI4ZDc4YzIxMzE0YjdkMzQ5MjA5OTA2MzhjNTkyNWE5OGI2ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078","sha":"2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078"}],"sha":"9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/9feb8d78c21314b7d34920990638c5925a98b6fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:33:30Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:33:37Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(runtime-gate): report why a target was unreachable, and CLS 0 as a pass\n\nTwo ways this gate hid what it knew.\n\n`page.goto`''s catch discarded the error entirely, so `/markets` was reported as\n`target not reachable (is the stack up?)` while the gateway''s own trace showed\nit answering that request 200 in 102ms. The stack was up; the gateway was\nreturning 503 from the page-health marker. The reason is now part of the\nmessage — HTTP status, no response, or the navigation error itself.\n\nCLS stayed `undefined` when no layout shift was observed, which the check\nreports as \"not measured\" and SKIPS. A page that never shifts has CLS 0, and\nthat is a passing measurement. The same route SKIPPED on one run and FAILED at\n0.2027 on the next, and nothing in the output could tell a stable page from an\nunobserved one. Only a browser that cannot observe `layout-shift` at all now\nreports nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4454f32debc970d8039a03331351870372fe455e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/4454f32debc970d8039a03331351870372fe455e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDJiNzE1MGFhMDAxYWIwNmI2OWEyYWY5MzBkNTUzMzMyM2E5YmYwNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203","sha":"37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203"}],"sha":"2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/2b7150aa001ab06b69a2af930d5533323a9bf078"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:33:30Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:33:37Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(runtime): a fragment''s own stylesheet is not a fallback marker\n\n/markets answered 503 to every visitor, and the page rendered correctly.\n\n`isFallbackResponse` keeps a deprecated sniff for fragments predating the\n`metadata.fallback` flag: `response.html.includes(''data-fallback=\"true\"'')`.\nmarkets-table inlines a rule that styles its own degraded state —\n\n  [data-fragment=\"markets-table\"][data-fallback=\"true\"] { ... }\n\n— so the marker string was present in EVERY healthy response, and the sniff\nmatched it. That slot is `required`, so the page reported\n`health: \"unhealthy\"`, and the gateway maps unhealthy to 503 exactly as\ndesigned. Every layer behaved as specified; the classification was wrong.\n\nNothing caught it: the fragment answers `/render` 200 with `propsValid: true`,\nthe page returns 200 upstream, `/health` is green, and docker-smoke only checks\n`/` and `/product/123` among composed routes. The runtime gate reached\n`/markets` for the first time and reported \"target not reachable\".\n\nThe sniff is narrowed rather than removed. Its comment says to remove it once\nevery fragment sets `metadata.fallback`, and all 14 here now do — but this\nframework''s premise is fragments that deploy independently, possibly built\nelsewhere, so dropping the compatibility path is a deliberate call to make on\nits own, not inside a CI fix. What is unambiguous is that `<style>` and\n`<script>` bodies are text, not markup, so the marker is no longer read out of\nthem. Two tests pin both halves: the markets-table shape is not a fallback, and\na marker on real markup following a stylesheet still is.\n\nVerified against the running stack: /markets goes 503 -> 200 with\n`data-mvp-page-health=\"ok\"` and `data-failed-slots=\"\"`, and all five composed\nroutes answer 200.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a23cb0d05aea1441cedcbab3797444e3c83e550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/6a23cb0d05aea1441cedcbab3797444e3c83e550"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDM3ODAwYjIwNDE4NDIxMTVlZjA4YmRhNjE3NTllODFmZjRkYTYyMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106","sha":"f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106"}],"sha":"37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/37800b2041842115ef08bda61759e81ff4da6203"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:00:00Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:00:01Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(runtime-gate): say what shifted when CLS is over budget\n\nCI reports `web-vitals-cls 0.2027 vs budget 0.1` and nothing else, on the\ncomposed pages, in production containers. That number cannot be acted on: it\nsays the page shifts, not what shifts.\n\nIt also does not reproduce locally. A warm dev server records zero shift\nentries, dev runs `next dev --turbopack` against production''s webpack build, and\n`next start` on the locally cached `.next` fails with `routesManifest.dataRoutes\nis not iterable` — so the honest way to learn what moves is for the gate to\nreport it from where it actually happens.\n\n`LayoutShift.sources` is now collected: score, the shifting element with its\n`data-fragment` / `data-island` marker, and its y,height before and after. The\nfirst four are appended to the check detail, only when the budget is exceeded —\na passing run stays as terse as it was.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9b60493d0c4e6cd69b0f5b2501037328fce2558","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/c9b60493d0c4e6cd69b0f5b2501037328fce2558"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGY1N2ZmOGYwNTg3MDQ2YjFjNmEzOWNiYTU0MjFiZTQ1YmYxZDcxMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d","sha":"497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d"}],"sha":"f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f57ff8f0587046b1c6a39cba5421be45bf1d7106"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:26:26Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:26:48Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(runtime-gate): name the request that failed\n\nThe browser''s console line for a failed subresource names no URL, so the 400\nabove reached CI as `1 error(s): Failed to load resource: the server responded\nwith a status of 400 (Bad Request)` and nothing else. Finding it took bringing\nthe whole stack up locally and attaching a Playwright listener — work the gate\nshould have done.\n\n`staticRequests` deliberately covers only the asset plane (`/_next/static`,\n`/assets`), so anything failing outside it was invisible. Every 4xx/5xx response\nis now observed and named in `hydration-clean`''s detail. The check set is\nunchanged on purpose: this adds attribution, not a new way to fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0aaa8e54b79f295ec2ccb14aab72b70c16a287d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/b0aaa8e54b79f295ec2ccb14aab72b70c16a287d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDQ5N2UwMDQ1OGU2ZjI4YjU2MmMwMzM4ZjJkNDM2ZDcyMDE0ZWMzN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f","sha":"8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f"}],"sha":"497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/497e00458e6f28b562c0338f2d436d72014ec37d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:26:26Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:26:48Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(page-product): ship the product image it renders, and stop duplicating keys\n\nTwo real product defects, both surfaced by the runtime gate the moment it\nactually ran against the composed production stack.\n\n1. Every product page requested an image that does not exist.\n\n   `<Image src={`/products/${product.id}.jpg`} />`, and `apps/page-product` has\n   no `public/` directory — for any id. Next''s optimizer fetched the source, got\n   a 404, and answered the browser with 400, which the gate saw as\n   `hydration-clean FAIL: Failed to load resource: 400`. `src/render.ts`''s SSR\n   path carried the same broken reference.\n\n   The path is now data (`Product.image`) rather than a convention guessed from\n   the id, and the file it points at ships: a 1.5KB 640x480 PNG. PNG, not SVG —\n   Next''s optimizer rejects SVG with 400 unless `dangerouslyAllowSVG` is set,\n   which would reinstate the bug. Verified through the gateway: the request is\n   200 and the image renders 640x480 with naturalWidth 640.\n\n2. `key={hint.kind}` duplicated React keys on every product render.\n\n   Two scheduler hints can share a `kind` (one per slot group). page-markets,\n   page-home, page-portfolio and TraceDrawer all already key on\n   `${kind}:${slots}`; page-product was the one left behind. React warned about\n   duplicate children, with \"may cause children to be duplicated and/or\n   omitted\" — which is a flaky-selector risk for the e2e specs that read these\n   diagnostics.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"240e8dd4572843874f039c2796e0b73252fb2c90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/240e8dd4572843874f039c2796e0b73252fb2c90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDgxNDFiNWNiOWIwMDQzOTEwYmU5MDk2MjY5YjNhODFhM2UwZjU4MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50","sha":"7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50"}],"sha":"8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/8141b5cb9b0043910be9096269b3a81a3e0f582f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:59:50Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:59:51Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"ci: give every job a deadline\n\nA hung step otherwise runs to GitHub''s 360-minute default, which is what the\nruntime gate just did. Budgets are generous against observed times — verify\n~2min, affected ~2min, e2e ~20min of which the 22-image build is ~17min — so\nthey catch a hang rather than a slow runner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e2b34f830b0703bf93d75063e20a3b1d8b41c70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/5e2b34f830b0703bf93d75063e20a3b1d8b41c70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDdmMmI2MzBkYjZjNjIxZGZhYWMyMmQwYmU4NzM2YjI2YTBkN2NlNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015","sha":"143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015"}],"sha":"7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/7f2b630db6c621dfaac22d0be8736b26a0d7ce50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:59:50Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:59:51Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(runtime-gate): make it run at all, and make it stop when it fails\n\nTwo defects, both exposed the first time this gate ever executed in CI. It\nprinted a failure 4.5 seconds in and then held the runner for 2h29m until the\njob was cancelled.\n\n1. `ReferenceError: __name is not defined` — every `page.evaluate` in this\n   script was dead.\n\n   tsx hardcodes esbuild''s `keepNames`, which rewrites function definitions to\n   `__name(fn, \"name\")`. Playwright serialises an evaluate callback with\n   `Function.prototype.toString()` and runs that source in the page, where no\n   `__name` exists. Reproduces locally in three lines, so this was never\n   CI-specific — the gate simply had never been wired into `pnpm verify` (it\n   lived behind `deploy-affected --runtime`), so nobody ran it.\n\n   Rewriting the callbacks is not a fix: measured, a nested\n   `const compute = () => 42` fails exactly like a named declaration, so\n   \"avoid named functions\" is not a rule that holds. The helper is installed in\n   the page instead, via `addInitScript`, as a STRING — an init script written\n   as a function would go through the same transform and need the very helper\n   it installs.\n\n2. The process never exited after a failure.\n\n   `main().catch()` printed the JSON and set `process.exitCode`, but the\n   browser launched at the top was closed only on the two success paths. A\n   thrown error left Chromium running, the event loop never emptied, and the\n   run hung. The browser is now closed in a `finally` that covers every path.\n\nVerified against a live page: all nine checks execute, the process exits in 5\nseconds with code 1, and an unreachable target exits in 1 second with code 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fed5cdd8ee81313482109ffc213e658c4374b78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/2fed5cdd8ee81313482109ffc213e658c4374b78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDE0MzU5N2VkYzNjNTJhYTc1MjVkNmE0MTI4YzQ3YWRhNGIxMGQwMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446","sha":"5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446"}],"sha":"143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/143597edc3c52aa7525d6a4128c47ada4b10d015"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T05:01:39Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T05:01:47Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(smoke): stop requiring a marker the gateway deliberately stopped emitting\n\nFirst time the compose stack ever came up in CI: 22 of 24 smoke checks passed —\nevery service healthy — and the two composed shell routes failed with\n\n  missing: [''data-shell-gateway=\"true\"'']  (status 200, 88 attempts over 179s)\n\nNothing in the repo emits that marker. 058f13b made the gateway a transparent\nproxy: it returns the page''s HTML verbatim so hydration stays byte-consistent,\nand injects no chrome wrapper. `apps/shell-gateway/tests/server.test.ts` asserts\n`not.toContain(\"data-shell-gateway\")` and both `e2e/shell-*.spec.ts` assert\n`toHaveCount(0)`. So this suite was requiring the exact thing three other tests\nrequire to be absent — a contradiction that stayed invisible because\ndocker-smoke had never once run in CI.\n\nDeleting the assertion would leave the composed checks unable to tell \"the\ngateway proxied this\" from \"something served this\", so the check now proves\npassage the way the e2e specs do: the trace header the gateway stamps. That\nneeds a header assertion, which `SmokeCheck` did not have, so `expectHeaders`\n(present and non-empty, compared lowercase) and `missingHeaders` on the result\nare added, and the real fetcher now passes response headers through.\n\nA test pins that the composed checks ask for `x-trace-id` and do not ask for\n`data-shell-gateway`, so this specific drift cannot return silently. The\nremaining fixture uses of the old marker are renamed to an obviously fictional\none — leaving that name in fixtures is what made it look real.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3069404a3257549b45207ff8a154ac5c9ee0c1eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/3069404a3257549b45207ff8a154ac5c9ee0c1eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDVmNTIyZGU0MDk3NzQ2ZDI3NTc3ZTk3MTQ3NzYwNjkyN2I5N2U0NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615","sha":"6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615"}],"sha":"5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/5f522de4097746d27577e971477606927b97e446"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T04:24:35Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T04:28:02Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(audit): fail on a workspace import a deployable unit does not declare\n\nThe bug the previous commit fixed passed all 14 gates and only surfaced when a\nunit was built on its own — which is the framework''s headline claim, so the\nclaim had no gate behind it. `audit:deps` has 17 rules (layering, forbidden\npackages, version duplication, raw fetch, hand-rolled fragment servers) and not\none of them compared a unit''s imports against its declared dependencies.\n\n`undeclared-workspace-import` does that for every `apps/*` and `fragments/*`\nunit, against its shipped source. Verified both ways: it reports exactly\npage-home''s `app/layout.tsx` / `@mvp/trade-prefs` when the declaration is\nremoved, and the repo is clean with it in place.\n\nScope notes, both deliberate:\n\n- Test files are excluded — they are not in the image, so they are not part of\n  the closure this rule protects. (The one real devDependency gap found while\n  writing it is declared in the previous commit instead.)\n- `tools/*` is excluded. The scaffolder''s fragment template and this audit''s own\n  fixtures contain import specifiers inside string literals, which are text and\n  not imports. `stripCommentsAndStrings` cannot disambiguate here, because an\n  import specifier IS a string.\n\nSubpath exports resolve to their package (`@mvp/runtime/rum` -> `@mvp/runtime`),\nwhich one of the three new tests pins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbe7f021a391752e3753a9f7f3387930aee6c03b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/bbe7f021a391752e3753a9f7f3387930aee6c03b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDZjNTY3NDI0OTE2MTgzNThmMGI5OWVmNDZhODQ2YjQ1ZTg1YWM2MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b","sha":"1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b"}],"sha":"6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/6c56742491618358f0b99ef46a846b45e85ac615"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T04:24:23Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T04:28:02Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(deps): declare the workspace packages these units actually import\n\n`docker compose build` failed on page-home and page-product with\n\n  ./app/layout.tsx\n  Module not found: Can''t resolve ''@mvp/trade-prefs''\n\nBoth import `@mvp/trade-prefs` in `app/layout.tsx` (since ad80a61) without\ndeclaring it. A whole-repo `pnpm build` cannot see this, because it builds every\npackage regardless of who declared what; each unit''s Dockerfile runs\n`pnpm --filter <unit>... build`, whose closure is the DECLARED dependencies, so\n`domains/trade-prefs` was never built and its `dist/` did not exist. The other\nfive pages declare it and built fine, which is why only these two failed.\n\nAfter declaring it, `@mvp/trade-prefs#build` appears in page-home''s build\nclosure (`turbo run build --filter @mvp/page-home --dry=json`) and\n`pnpm --filter @mvp/page-home... build` succeeds from a clean `.next`.\n\nAlso declares `@mvp/runtime` as a devDependency of @mvp/fragment-order-form,\nwhose `tests/proxyChain.test.ts` imports it. Same class as the @mvp/mcp fix\nearlier on this branch: undeclared means `dependsOn: [\"^build\"]` does not wait,\nso the test can race the build that produces what it imports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c30d95103c3778144ec6823b3f9aaa855d4097d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/9c30d95103c3778144ec6823b3f9aaa855d4097d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDFlOWRmMGU1MTA4NTU0ZTNkNDNkNTY0NjgyMWM1NGQzMzI3MjEzOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe","sha":"47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe"}],"sha":"1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/1e9df0e5108554e3d43d5646821c54d33272138b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:37:36Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T04:24:52Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(ci): make the e2e stack build survive a standard runner\n\nThe `e2e` job had never executed once — the `e2e` label could not trigger a\nrun until this branch fixed the activity types — and its first two executions\nfound two separate runner constraints in the same step.\n\n1. `unknown flag: --provenance`, after 9 seconds.\n\n   `--provenance` / `--sbom` on `docker compose build` only exist from Compose\n   v5; the runner logs v2.38.2 (buildx v0.37.0). They were on that command\n   because the README''s local recipe has them, and they are there for a Docker\n   Desktop problem — concurrent attestation export produced intermittent\n   snapshot errors on the dev machine — which is not a property of the runner.\n   `docker buildx build` does accept them, so the `docker` job is unchanged.\n\n2. The runner was killed, after 21 minutes.\n\n   16 minutes of complete log silence, then SIGTERM (exit 143), with even the\n   `if: always()` teardown steps skipped — a terminated runner, not a failed\n   command. Cause: every unit is independently deployable, so each of the 22\n   Dockerfiles does its own `COPY . .` + `pnpm install` + `pnpm --filter\n   <unit>... build`, and compose builds all 22 at once — 7 concurrent\n   `next build`s on 4 vCPUs.\n\n   That independence is the project''s minimum-deployable-unit claim and is not\n   what should give way, so the bound goes in CI: the 7 pages build two at a\n   time, the 15 fastify units four at a time. Each batch is a single bake solve,\n   so BuildKit still dedups the `pnpm install` layer the units share (there are\n   only two distinct prefixes across the 22 Dockerfiles). The service list is\n   sorted because `config --services` is unordered, which would otherwise put a\n   random number of `next build`s in one batch and make peak load vary per run.\n\nThe step also logs compose/buildx versions and disk before and after — the\nfirst failure was a version skew and the second was resource exhaustion, and\nneither was visible in the log as it stood.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c90a076d7546d2acccc2a48557215c3d9e84aa31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/c90a076d7546d2acccc2a48557215c3d9e84aa31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDQ3MTgyZTEyOTExNDBiNDc2ODk2OWJiMDg4NTMzNzcyOTUzOThhYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb","sha":"537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb"}],"sha":"47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/47182e1291140b4768969bb08853377295398abe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:25:52Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:27:48Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(turbo): declare @mvp/mcp''s real build inputs so `^build` actually waits\n\n`@mvp/mcp` declared no workspace dependencies, so its `dependsOn: [\"^build\"]`\nwaited for nothing while turbo built packages/ and domains/ concurrently with\nthe test that dynamically imports fragment manifests and shells out to\nscripts/*.mts — both of which resolve workspace imports to dist/.\n\nDeclaring @mvp/contracts and @mvp/trade-data makes the ordering real:\n\n  turbo run test --filter @mvp/mcp --dry=json\n  -> dependencies: [''@mvp/contracts#build'', ''@mvp/trade-data#build'']\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"080de1732f0edd50737f8c3e14e2661425e9ac8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/080de1732f0edd50737f8c3e14e2661425e9ac8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDUzN2RlNThlZTkzYmNmZjIzNDE4MzQ1OGQyMDg1OTIyY2Q3ZjRkY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3","sha":"f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3"}],"sha":"537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/537de58ee93bcff234183458d2085922cd7f4dcb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:25:52Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:27:48Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(test): give the one subprocess-spawning test an explicit time budget\n\nThe single failure of the first CI run that ever executed: 84 turbo tasks,\n`Failed: @mvp/mcp#test`, one `Test timed out in 5000ms`, zero assertion\nfailures.\n\nThe `mount_slot` handler test runs `pnpm exec tsx scripts/mount-slot.mts`\nthrough spawnSync, so what it spends is pnpm + tsx startup — ~0.7s on an idle\nmachine — not the check itself. Under `pnpm test` the whole turbo graph builds\nand tests concurrently, and on a contended runner that startup went past\nvitest''s implicit 5s default. The budget is now explicit at 30s: a slow runner\nis not a red build, while a genuine hang still surfaces quickly.\n\nIt is the only test in the repo that leaves the process, so nothing else\ncarries the same implicit assumption.\n\nAlso corrects the describe title — the handler spawns a script, so\n\"(in-process, real repo)\" was wrong.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bd00959b0506d46ae7627c45cdb628966c50789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/9bd00959b0506d46ae7627c45cdb628966c50789"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGY5MmMwOWM0Y2YwYjM3Y2Y5NzhlNDAxMWEwMzM4M2QxMjJhNmIyYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/91a5e284f930e0c512028406ce071f2134d1c386","sha":"91a5e284f930e0c512028406ce071f2134d1c386","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/91a5e284f930e0c512028406ce071f2134d1c386"}],"sha":"f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f92c09c4cf0b37cf978e4011a03383d122a6b2b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/91a5e284f930e0c512028406ce071f2134d1c386/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:25:40Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:27:48Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(ci): the pipeline had never run — `secrets` in a step-level `if:` killed it\n\nEvery push since the workflow was added produced a 0-second run with no jobs\nand no logs, so the repo had 100 runs and 0 successes. The cause was not a\nfailing gate — GitHub rejected the whole file at validation time:\n\n  Unrecognized named-value: ''secrets''\n\nThe `secrets` context is not available in a step-level `if:`. It IS available\nin a job-level `env:`, and `env` IS available in a step `if:`, so the registry\ncredential check is hoisted to the `docker` job''s `env` as REGISTRY_READY and\nthe two steps test `env.REGISTRY_READY == ''true''`. Behaviour is unchanged:\nimages still build always and push only when all three values are configured.\n\nFound by elimination — a minimal probe workflow ran in 8s on the same push,\nwhich proved the runner and the trigger were fine and the file was not.\n\nAlso makes a CI-only failure diagnosable, which this fix immediately needed:\n`pnpm verify` captures each gate''s stdout into reports/verify-report.json\nrather than streaming it, so a failing gate showed as `FAIL <cmd>` and nothing\nelse in the log. The new step prints the failing gate''s own output (and says\nwhich run the report came from, since reports/ is committed and a verify that\ndies before writing it leaves the previous run''s file behind), and reports/ is\nuploaded as an artifact.\n\nAnd makes the documented escape hatch real: `on: pull_request:` carried no\n`types`, so only opened/synchronize/reopened triggered a run. The `e2e` job''s\n`contains(...labels.*.name, ''e2e'')` condition could therefore never fire from\nlabelling a PR — the label could be applied and nothing would happen. `labeled`\nis now listed (alongside the three defaults, which must be restated once\n`types` is given), so the stack-level job can be exercised on a PR instead of\nfirst executing on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f6e26d646bc46ada896c473542f2141e12d7cfe","url