 inside one page''s feature island, so six of seven pages\nreported nothing — including `page-trade`, the nine-slot realtime terminal, the\npage where jank and interaction latency are the things anyone would actually\nwant measured. Ingestion was per-app with a process-local registry, so samples\nneither survived a restart nor aggregated across pages.\n\nBoth halves move to where they are shared.\n\n**`<RumBeacon />`** (`@mvp/runtime/rum`) is one line in each app''s\n`layout.tsx`, so it covers every route in that app rather than one component —\n`page-product` gets both its routes for free. Browser-only, so it is a separate\n`\"use client\"` entry beside `@mvp/runtime/live`, and a server bundle never pulls\nit in. It renders `null`.\n\n**`POST /_shell/rum`** on the gateway replaces the per-app route. The gateway is\nthe single public origin every page already talks to, so one endpoint serves all\nseven, and samples land in the registry `/metrics` already exposes — aggregated\n*and* scrapeable, rather than stranded in one app''s memory.\n\nThe generalisable part is not the measurement: **telemetry that has to be\nhand-wired per page ends up wired on the page that needed it least.** The fix\nwas moving the wiring somewhere a page cannot forget it.\n\nIngestion also now rejects a non-finite value. JSON has no `Infinity`, but a\nclient-side computation can produce one, and a histogram that ingests it is\nruined for every later reader.\n\nThe four route tests moved with the endpoint rather than being deleted, and the\npage-home test file says where they went.\n\nVerified in the browser on the page that previously reported nothing: loading\n`/trade/BTC` and backgrounding it produces two beacons to `/_shell/rum`\n(LCP 600 ms, CLS 0.034), both carrying the same `traceparent` as that load''s\nserver spans. `/metrics` then carries `web_vitals_*` series for `/trade/BTC`,\n`/markets`, `/portfolio`, `/vaults` and `/referrals` in one registry.\n\nF17 is marked FIXED in both editions; struck headings are normalised to `<s>`\n(\"no longer accurate\") rather than `<del>` (\"removed content\"), which the\nMarkdown conversion had left inconsistent between the two languages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7dd933634f8e583fb0ea7cbdc8561e14fc3d2c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/f7dd933634f8e583fb0ea7cbdc8561e14fc3d2c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/cda638590ca484b1b015be6521a61ced0885da26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/cda638590ca484b1b015be6521a61ced0885da26","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGNkYTYzODU5MGNhNDg0YjFiMDE1YmU2NTIxYTYxY2VkMDg4NWRhMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807","sha":"c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807"}],"sha":"cda638590ca484b1b015be6521a61ced0885da26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/cda638590ca484b1b015be6521a61ced0885da26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:39:35Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:39:35Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"docs: record what the observability work found and what it left open\n\nTwo new findings in both editions, and one existing entry corrected.\n\n**F16 (fixed)** — the trace id was a hardcoded constant. Recorded not because\nit is still broken but because of *why it survived*: correlation that always\n\"works\" is indistinguishable from correlation that works. No test failed, no\nerror fired, no report flagged it — every span carried a trace id, and it was\nthe wrong one. The generalisation is worth keeping in front of a reader: any\nidentifier that is generated rather than observed can be a constant and nothing\nwill complain, which is a question still owed to `requestId`, cache keys and\nidempotency keys.\n\n**F17 (open)** — RUM measures properly now but reaches one page of seven, and\n`page-trade` — the nine-slot realtime terminal, where jank and interaction\nlatency actually matter — reports nothing. The ingestion endpoint is per-app\nand in-process, so samples neither survive a restart nor aggregate. Stated as\nreplacing a worse problem rather than as an achievement: one page reporting\nreal numbers beats seven reporting a confident wrong one, but it is not\ncoverage.\n\n**F11 corrected.** It claimed `maxINPMs` was declared while INP went unmeasured.\nINP is now genuinely measured in the browser, so that half is no longer true —\nbut the runtime gate still has no INP check, so the declared ceiling is still\nnot a ceiling. Measured-and-ungated is a different problem from unmeasured, and\na smaller one; the page now says which it is.\n\nCounts updated to 17 findings / 4 fixed. Verified: both editions render the new\nanchors, and every internal link and in-page anchor across all 70 pages still\nresolves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"49f0a41950071ef1d2acc02e7fa5bb50f32aa3ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/49f0a41950071ef1d2acc02e7fa5bb50f32aa3ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGMzMTIyYThjOTVlNzA3MGMxYjc2ZTEwZDJkZjIxMTVhNzA5NTY4MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28","sha":"4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28"}],"sha":"c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/c3122a8c95e7070c1b76e10d2df2115a70956807"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T16:18:05Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T16:18:05Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(observability): real web vitals, long tasks, and a browser↔server trace join\n\nThe only RUM sample this repository produced was\n`{ name: \"INP\", value: performance.now() }`, reported at island mount on one\npage. That is elapsed time since navigation. It is not Interaction to Next\nPaint, and it never observed an interaction at all — a dashboard fed by it\nwould have shown a confident, precise, wrong number, which is worse than an\nempty panel.\n\n`@mvp/observability/rum` replaces it with measurement. A separate entry\ncarrying `\"use client\"`, the same shape as `@mvp/runtime/live`, because it\nreads `performance` and installs `PerformanceObserver`s and the package''s main\nentry must stay server-safe.\n\n- **TTFB** from the navigation entry — and deliberately *not* reported when\n  `responseStart` is 0, because that means \"not measured\", not \"instant\". The\n  alternative puts a 0 ms bar in a dashboard for every browser that withheld it.\n- **LCP** and **CLS** flushed on `visibilitychange`, since neither is final\n  until the page is backgrounded. CLS excludes shifts within 500 ms of input —\n  those are the user''s doing, not the page''s.\n- **INP** from `event` entries that carry an `interactionId`, tracked as the\n  running worst case. Entries without one are event timings the metric\n  deliberately excludes.\n- **Long tasks**, kept separate from the vitals on purpose: a vital says the\n  page was slow, a long task says which script to look at.\n\nEvery observer is installed inside a try/catch, so a browser that does not\nimplement an entry type degrades to *not reported* rather than to a wrong\nvalue — the same failure mode the old code got wrong.\n\n**The correlation.** The gateway now publishes its `traceparent` as a\n`Server-Timing` entry, so the browser reads the server''s trace id straight off\n`PerformanceServerTiming` — no extra markup, no extra request, reusing the\nchannel the previous commit built. Every beacon carries it, and the ingestion\nendpoint preserves it rather than dropping it at the door: an endpoint that\naccepts a field and forgets it is indistinguishable from one that never\nreceived it.\n\nThat closes the loop the capability audit found open. A Chrome DevTools session\ncan now read per-fragment server durations *and* the trace id that joins them\nto the server''s span tree, which is the prerequisite for driving load, first-\npaint and jank work from the browser side.\n\nVerified from inside the browser, not asserted: `PerformanceServerTiming`\nreturns six entries including\n`traceparent;desc=\"00-79d950b5…-81e71841ed34c394-01\"` plus three per-slot\ntimings with their source; all four observer types are supported; and a beacon\nposted in the real payload shape round-trips its trace id through the endpoint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1edae9f2ef4b0e3ed8af0f9d2050901b0d445d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/1edae9f2ef4b0e3ed8af0f9d2050901b0d445d3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDRiYjdhYzkyZTgxZDg0OWZhZGMwMDcxMmMyMWY4YWNkMDk2ZWVkMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792","sha":"9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792"}],"sha":"4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/4bb7ac92e81d849fadc00712c21f8acd096eed28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T15:59:21Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T15:59:21Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(observability): W3C trace context, replacing a trace id that was a constant\n\n`createTraceId()` in the gateway returned the literal string\n`\"trace_0000000000000000\"`. Every request in the system therefore shared one\ntrace id: spans from unrelated page loads collapsed into a single trace, and\nnothing complained, because correlation that always \"works\" looks the same as\ncorrelation that works. Every trace exported from this repository so far has\nbeen one indistinguishable blob.\n\n`@mvp/observability/traceContext` replaces it with real W3C Trace Context:\n`createTraceId`, `createSpanId`, `formatTraceparent`, `parseTraceparent` and\n`continueTrace`. The format matters beyond hygiene — `traceparent` is what\nChrome DevTools, OpenTelemetry collectors and commercial APMs read, so this is\nthe difference between a browser timeline and a server span tree referring to\nthe same request rather than merely happening at the same time.\n\nPropagation is now end to end: the gateway continues an incoming `traceparent`\nor mints one, forwards it to the page app, `serializeContext` carries it from\nthe page to each fragment, and the gateway echoes it on the response so the\nbrowser can read it back. `RequestContextSchema` gains an optional\n`traceparent` — framework vocabulary, not business vocabulary, which is why it\nbelongs in the schema rather than in `ctx.extensions`.\n\nTwo decisions worth stating. A malformed `traceparent` starts a NEW trace\nrather than being partially adopted, because spans attached to a trace nobody\ncan query are worse than a clean one. And the legacy `x-trace-id` still wins\nfor `ctx.traceId`, since upstreams and tests pin it; when it is also valid\n32-hex the two headers name the same trace, and when it is not (`trace-home`)\nit simply cannot be carried into `traceparent`, so the standard header names a\nfresh trace and the legacy one is echoed unchanged beside it.\n\n20 tests cover the spec''s own example vector, the sampled bit, all-zero\nrejection (which the spec requires and which is exactly the shape of the bug\nbeing fixed), unknown-version rejection, and uniqueness across 500 ids.\n\nVerified against a live stack rather than asserted: three requests produce three\ndistinct trace ids; an incoming `traceparent` keeps its trace-id and gets a\nfresh span-id; a malformed one yields a new trace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0eb5fcd078c62d008ecb184538572aca95388045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/0eb5fcd078c62d008ecb184538572aca95388045"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDlmMjhjN2YwM2JlOGU3N2ZjNTJhOTkzOGUzZTgwMmZlNjgwNzk3OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc","sha":"3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc"}],"sha":"9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/9f28c7f03be8e77fc52a9938e3e802fe68079792"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T15:36:21Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T15:36:21Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(observability): emit real Server-Timing instead of a hardcoded placeholder\n\nThe gateway sent `server-timing: shell;dur=1` — a constant. The real span\ndurations were sitting on the trace object in the same function and never left\nthe process. This makes them reach the browser.\n\n`Server-Timing` matters here specifically because it is the one standard\nchannel that puts server-side durations into the browser''s own timeline:\nChrome shows each entry per request in the network panel and exposes it on\n`PerformanceServerTiming`, so \"which fragment made this page slow\" becomes\nanswerable from a devtools session rather than from a trace export nobody\nopens during a page load.\n\nTwo sources are merged. The gateway contributes what it actually knows —\n`shell` (total) and `upstream` (page app fetch). The per-slot entries come from\nthe page, which cannot set a response header in the App Router; it stamps them\ninto the markup and the gateway promotes them, the same mechanism and for the\nsame reason as the page-health marker. `PAGE_TIMING_ATTR` sits next to\n`PAGE_HEALTH_ATTR` deliberately.\n\n`FragmentSlotResult` gains `durationMs`, measured through a single exit point in\n`fetchFragmentSlot` so that a cache hit, a timeout and a fallback substitution\nare all timed and no future branch can forget to be.\n\n`desc` carries the slot''s `source`, which is the second question a reader asks\nafter \"how long\": a 2 ms slot is a cache hit, not a fast fragment, and the two\ncall for opposite actions. Verified live against the composed home page:\n\n    shell;desc=\"gateway total\";dur=65.3, upstream;desc=\"page app\";dur=65.2,\n    staticEditorial;desc=\"static\";dur=0, recommendations;desc=\"network\";dur=11,\n    promotion;desc=\"cache\";dur=0\n\nand read back through Chrome''s own API rather than assumed:\n`performance.getEntriesByType(''navigation'')[0].serverTiming` returns all five\nentries with name, duration and description intact.\n\nThe header grammar is unforgiving — one stray `;` or `,` in a name silently\ntruncates every entry after it — so names are sanitised to the allowed token\ncharacters and descriptions are stripped of quotes. A slot name is authored\ndata, so that is a correctness concern rather than defensive habit. Nine tests\ncover the escaping, the entity round-trip React applies to the attribute, and\nthe \"page does not participate\" case, which must read as no opinion rather than\nas zero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a603e29ff10ae6a6edd0963731bf83ad877d27aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/a603e29ff10ae6a6edd0963731bf83ad877d27aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDNlNjdjNDY2MGFiNmZiMmY3NWViNWYyOTg3MGFiOTMzN2Y3YzE0ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1","sha":"e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1"}],"sha":"3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/3e67c4660ab6fb2f75eb5f29870ab9337f7c14fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T14:17:43Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T14:17:43Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"docs(en): bring the English pages to the same editorial density as 中文\n\nThe English set was the converted baseline: correct prose, correct figures,\nbut a wall of paragraphs. The Chinese edition had been written with the\neditorial components — eyebrow, lede, fact rows, cards, graded callouts,\nchips — and the two read as different products. This closes that.\n\nCoverage across the 35 English pages, up from eyebrow 0 / lede 0 / facts 0 /\ncards 0 / notes 0 / chips 0:\n\n    eyebrow  35    lede  35    notes  27\n    cards     7    facts  2    chips   2    figures 9\n\n**The mechanical half was done mechanically.** Every page''s eyebrow comes from\n`_nav.json`, and the first paragraph after `<h1>` was promoted to a lede by\nscript — 32 and 28 pages respectively, with the four pages that open straight\ninto an `<h2>` given a lede written for them.\n\n**The editorial half was done per page**, mirroring where the Chinese edition\nhad a component and why. The callout grade carries meaning rather than\ndecoration: `note good` for \"this is the mechanism that makes the rest\ntrustworthy\" and \"skipping hydration IS the success case\"; `note warn` for\n\"never hand-edit the generated file\" and \"pnpm only\"; `note bad` for the\nfindings a reader can act on wrongly — F1''s confidently wrong optimizer advice,\nF11''s ungated budget fields, F14''s discarded contract tier.\n\nTwo prose blocks became cards because they were parallel choices being read as\na list: `dependsOn` vs `dataDependencies` on slot scheduling, and\n`executeFragmentSlots` vs `streamFragmentSlots` on page composition. One code\nblock became chips: the four enums on contracts-first are a vocabulary to\nrecognise, not a snippet to copy.\n\nTwo asymmetries are deliberate and remain. `introduction/glossary` has a note in\n中文 only — it explains the translation convention, which has no English\ncounterpart. `concepts/contracts-first` gained an English note that the Chinese\nlacked, so the Chinese page got the same wrapping back; every other page now\nmatches component for component.\n\nVerified: all 70 pages return 200, no page reports a missing figure, every\n`<div>` balances, 0 broken internal links, `pnpm verify` 14/14.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e40dd506c43cb7970e5d5262a8609aa21627c45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/7e40dd506c43cb7970e5d5262a8609aa21627c45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGUzMTIwNzc3NzJmMGU4Y2ZhN2IyNjZiNTc2MDMwMTMyNDdjMDliZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba","sha":"d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba"}],"sha":"e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/e312077772f0e8cfa7b266b57603013247c09bd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272691635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab","id":272691635,"login":"zyonlab","node_id":"U_kgDOEEDxsw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyonlab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T13:38:18Z","email":"support@appidge.com","name":"zyonlab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T13:38:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #50 from zyonlab/fix/framework-hardening\n\nFramework hardening: one fragment host, fragment-declared realtime, React 19, and bilingual outward docs","tree":