id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGQxYjRiMmVmZjg4ODMwMWJiODE3ZjQxMDNjZTZlYjBlOWNlNGZmYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/420f04372cd4cd6975247499a43fb400b43b030a","sha":"420f04372cd4cd6975247499a43fb400b43b030a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/420f04372cd4cd6975247499a43fb400b43b030a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f","sha":"d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f"}],"sha":"d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/d1b4b2eff888301bb817f4103ce6eb0e9ce4ffba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:17:12Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:17:12Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"docs: complete the Chinese edition and place the figures\n\nAll 35 pages now exist in both languages (70 total), every figure is placed,\nand every nav entry, internal link and page renders — checked, not assumed.\n\n**中文 is a translation of the argument, not of the words.** Technical\nidentifiers stay in English throughout: `dependsOn` is `dependsOn`, not 「依赖\n于」. They are strings you type into a terminal and into JSON, and translating\nthem manufactures ambiguity in the one place a reader can least afford it. The\nsame rule governs the figures, which is why one SVG serves both languages —\nnode labels are `POST /render`, `canary`, `dynamic-ssr`.\n\nThe pages that carry a figure carry it in both editions, with the caption\nsaying what the reader should take from it rather than restating the diagram:\ncomposition topology and the story map on the index, request lifecycle on\n\"what is it\", the slot DAG, the page-health decision, the island handshake, the\nrealtime ownership split, release channels, and the three-layer rule.\n\nTwo things this pass fixed rather than shipped around:\n\n- The on-page table of contents and the `<title>` were escaping text a second\n  time, so a heading documenting `<FRAGMENT>_URL` rendered as the entities\n  themselves. Heading text is lifted out of already-escaped authored HTML; it\n  must not be escaped again.\n- Empty `<a id=\"fN\"></a>` anchor targets became ids on the headings they label,\n  which is better HTML and puts all 15 findings in the generated contents.\n\nChecked before committing: all 70 pages return 200, no page reports a missing\nfigure, every nav entry resolves to a file in both languages, and all internal\nlinks resolve (0 broken). `pnpm verify` 14/14.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6b534cd34e0b81f78e674f99e99b45d82bdda0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/f6b534cd34e0b81f78e674f99e99b45d82bdda0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGQ1MjE5YWNkNjZiYThiN2E4ZmY4Mjc5MDQxMWRhNDFhMjIyNTY2OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9","sha":"86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9"}],"sha":"d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/d5219acd66ba8b7a8ff82790411da41a2225668f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:45:36Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:45:36Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(docs): designed HTML pages, shared SVG figures, and a Chinese edition\n\nMarkdown rendered by a minimal renderer produced walls of text. This replaces\nthat with hand-authored HTML on a shared design system, and adds 中文.\n\n**Pages are content fragments; the server injects the chrome.** Each page is\nplain HTML — no `<html>`, no `<head>`, no navigation — and `serve-docs.mts`\nwraps it with the sidebar, language switch, on-page table of contents and\nprev/next links. Authoring stays \"write the article\", with full control of\nlayout, cards and figures, while the chrome and stylesheet live in one place\nrather than being copy-pasted across 70 files. The Markdown renderer and its\ntests are removed: with every page authored as HTML it was dead code, and the\none-time conversion it performed is already in the result.\n\n**The design system is the reports'', not a new one.** `assets/docs.css` reuses\nthe exact token names and values from `docs/reports/` so the long-form reports\nand the docs read as one product. The CJK fallbacks (PingFang SC, Hiragino Sans\nGB, Microsoft YaHei) are first-class — a stack that degrades to a generic sans\nfor 中文 looks broken, and half of these pages are Chinese.\n\n**Nine inline SVG figures**, following the diagram skill''s rules: ≤9 nodes,\northogonal connectors with rounded elbows, arrow labels masked with a 6–10px\ngap so the connector stays traceable, accent colour on at most two elements,\n4px grid on all rect geometry, legend as a bottom strip, and `<title>`/`<desc>`\nfor assistive technology.\n\nThey are *inline*, expanded from `_diagrams/*.svg` by a `<!--@figure:name-->`\ndirective, rather than `<img src>`. That is what lets one file paint with the\npage''s own CSS variables and therefore serve light theme, dark theme, English\nand Chinese without a second export. Node labels stay in the technical\nvocabulary (`POST /render`, `canary`, `dynamic-ssr`) precisely so the figures\nare language-neutral.\n\nFigures: composition topology · request lifecycle (sequence) · slot DAG ·\npage-health decision · island handshake · three-layer rule · release channels ·\nrealtime ownership split · developer story map.\n\n**Bilingual.** `website/docs/{en,zh}/`, following Module Federation''s `docs/en`\nconvention — which this documentation already cited when describing competitor\nstructure. `_nav.json` carries both languages'' labels; the switcher preserves\nthe current page. Technical identifiers are deliberately NOT translated: they\nare strings you type into a terminal, and translating them manufactures\nambiguity.\n\nTwo things the gates caught and improved rather than suppressed: empty\n`<a id=\"fN\"></a>` anchor targets became ids on the headings they label (better\nHTML, and they now appear in the generated table of contents), and the\nstylesheet''s base element rules moved above the component rules that also\ntarget those elements — `noDescendingSpecificity` was pointing at a genuinely\nfragile cascade, not being pedantic.\n\nEnglish pages are the converted baseline; their editorial pass and the\nremaining Chinese pages follow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb4bd934dca92c2acde64c6548d43e09e090ceb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/eb4bd934dca92c2acde64c6548d43e09e090ceb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDg2ZDkyNmVkMmNhOWM2Mzk2NDRjNTIxYzc5MGNmNjcxOTJlOWU4ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529","sha":"c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529"}],"sha":"86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/86d926ed2ca9c639644c521c790cf67192e9e8e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:20:07Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:20:07Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(docs): serve website/docs in a browser with no build step\n\nThe outward-facing docs were Markdown with no way to read them as a site.\nMarkdown is the right source form — reviewable in a diff, greppable, and what\nany docs framework would consume — and the wrong reading form.\n\n`pnpm docs:serve` renders them on request at http://localhost:4301. One file,\nzero dependencies, no build step, sidebar built from `_nav.json`, light and\ndark themes from `prefers-color-scheme`.\n\nA real docs framework (VitePress, Rspress, Docusaurus) would do this better\nand cost a large dependency plus a build step for something nothing in\n`pnpm verify` depends on. `scripts/serve-reports.mts` already set the\nprecedent for the cheap version, and its path-safety logic is reused rather\nthan copied — `resolveRequestPath` is imported, not reimplemented.\n\nURLs mirror file paths **including** the `.md` suffix, so every relative link\nin the source resolves in the browser with no rewriting.\n\nThe renderer covers the Markdown these docs actually use and is explicit that\nit is not CommonMark. Three cases a naive renderer gets wrong, all pinned by\ntests in `e2e/unit/serve-docs.test.ts` (17 of them):\n\n- HTML is escaped before inline formatting, so a documented `<head>` renders\n  as text rather than opening an element;\n- code spans are extracted to placeholders first, so `` `**a**` `` survives as\n  literal asterisks instead of becoming bold;\n- `**bold**` is consumed before `*emphasis*`, so the former is not misread as\n  two emphasis markers.\n\nTwo rendering bugs were found by looking at the output rather than by\nreasoning about it: `*do*` was rendering as literal asterisks (no single-\nasterisk emphasis), and the sidebar read \"Ai setup\" because capitalisation\nwas naive. Both fixed; the second via an acronym set, since \"ai-setup\" is not\nthe last slug that will hit this.\n\nVerified across all 35 pages: tag balance for every block and inline element,\ntables with code spans in cells, fenced blocks containing HTML, the explicit\n`<a id=\"fN\">` anchors `known-limitations.md` links to, relative cross-page\nlinks, and no placeholder sentinel leaking into the output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ecfa3b7e2cf308c366f95af7e6814275d61a028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/9ecfa3b7e2cf308c366f95af7e6814275d61a028"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGM3YjQ5ODJiOTEwY2E5ODk4ZDUyYzdkZTY2NjU0NGJjYzEyZGM1Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044","sha":"5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044"}],"sha":"c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/c7b4982b910ca9898d52c7de666544bcc12dc529"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:18:05Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:18:05Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"chore: refresh tracked generated output\n\n`reports/*` (audit output, rewritten by every `pnpm verify`) and the per-app\n`tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` files are tracked in this repository, so they churn on\nevery run and would otherwise add noise to each of the preceding commits.\nCollected here instead, regenerated against the final tree so the committed\n`bundle-report.json` numbers match the code beside them — which is what makes\nthat file usable as a bundle-size baseline, as the React 19 commit relies on.\n\nThese arguably do not belong in version control at all. Keeping them tracked\nis a pre-existing decision, not one made here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"84a4bf6768b369de6c2c73bb9a08ac277524cc18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/84a4bf6768b369de6c2c73bb9a08ac277524cc18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDViNDY2MGM5YTQ4NjJhMjM1ZjYyNTNkYTU5YmRjOGJkYzcwNDYwNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a","sha":"140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a"}],"sha":"5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/5b4660c9a4862a235f6253da59bdc8bdc7046044"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:12:54Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:16:53Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"docs: outward-facing documentation set, with its findings fixed\n\n35 pages under `website/docs/`, structured on what the three competitors\nwhose docs were actually fetched converge on: Podium\n(`introduction/` · `guides/` · `api/`), Nx (`getting-started/` · `features/` ·\n`concepts/` · `reference/` · `troubleshooting/`) and Module Federation\n(`guide/` · `configure/` · `ai/`). Both Nx and Module Federation now ship a\nfirst-class AI section, which is the axis this project is strongest on, so\n`getting-started/ai-setup.md` is a top-level page rather than an appendix.\n\nWritten against the source tree rather than the internal docs. Every count\nand flag list was extracted from code — CLI flags from each script''s own\n`unknownFlagError` allowlist, routes from the Fastify registrations, env vars\nfrom the reads, rule codes from the audit sources, budget numbers from the\ngenerated report. Four numbers I had written from inference were wrong and\nwere corrected by checking: 41 Zod schemas (really 35 Zod + 6 JSON Schema),\n`data-mvp-page-health-failed` (really `data-failed-slots`), \"40 executable\nblocks, 0 skipped\" (really 41 executable + 7 no-run), and 12 shadcn\nprimitives (really 11).\n\nOne claim was corrected by probing rather than reasoning: a `curl` example\nwas expected to fail validation because `RequestContextSchema` requires\n`traceId`, `requestId`, `featureFlags` and `timestamp`. It returns 200 with\nreal HTML — `parseFragmentRenderRequest` is two-tier, strict then lenient.\nThat is now documented, along with the fact that the tier signal is discarded.\n\n`known-limitations.md` is a first-class page holding 15 findings, each with\nthe file that proves it, because a docs set that only describes the intended\ndesign is not usable for evaluation. The three that would change a decision:\nthe advisory optimizer recommends statically rendering the realtime order\nbook on 10 of 19 slots (its freshness guard reads an input the audit never\npasses, and the surviving condition keys on `dependsOn`, which is slot\nordering, not a data signal); 5 of 11 performance-budget fields have no gate\nanywhere, including the per-fragment latency and render ceilings every\nfragment declares; and the render contract''s strict/lenient tier is computed\nand then read by nothing, so a page that quietly stopped propagating\n`traceId` is indistinguishable from one that works.\n\nTwo findings are fixed here rather than only recorded:\n\n- The `scaffold_component` MCP tool description said \"9 files\" while the\n  scaffolder emits 11 — and the tool description is the one thing an agent\n  reads by default, while `CLAUDE.md` defines the accept criterion as\n  `files.length === 11`. Corrected in the tool and in the two internal docs\n  that also said 9. The comment in `fragmentTemplate.ts` still says 9 and is\n  left alone deliberately: it narrates the old broken scaffold.\n- `turbo.json` declared `REGISTRY_URL`, `REGISTRY_USERNAME` and\n  `REGISTRY_PASSWORD` in `globalPassThroughEnv`, which nothing in the\n  repository reads. Removed rather than left to imply an integration that\n  does not exist.\n\nBoth stay on the limitations page marked FIXED, because the mechanism that\nallowed each one is still there: nothing warns when a passthrough env\ndeclaration stops being used, and no test compares a documented file count\nagainst what the scaffolder writes.\n\nAlso ignores per-unit `reports/traces/` output. The existing pattern has a\nslash and is therefore anchored to the repo root, so each service''s own trace\ndirectory was showing up untracked after any `pnpm dev`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34686d683d2d95ff95b0ff908a15cab580af69cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/34686d683d2d95ff95b0ff908a15cab580af69cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDE0MDIyNmMwZTUxZWQ5OGFiYzc1MWU0NDczYTQ4NGRmNzYyOGY0OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f","sha":"f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f"}],"sha":"140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/140226c0e51ed98abc751e4473a484df7628f48a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:10:18Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:10:18Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"chore(deps): React 18.3 -> 19.3\n\nNext stays on 15.3: its peer range already reads\n`^18.2.0 || 19.0.0-rc-… || ^19.0.0`, so nothing about the upgrade required\ntouching it. Next 15 -> 16 is a separate migration.\n\nThe blocker recorded earlier — page-trade''s `react-dom/server` test strategy\n— turned out not to exist. `renderToStaticMarkup` is still exported from\n`react-dom/server` and resolves correctly under vitest in all 11 test files\nthat use it, verified by probe rather than by reasoning:\n\n    REACT_VERSION= 19.3.0\n    ✓ renderToStaticMarkup still served from react-dom/server\n    ✓ createRoot available from react-dom/client\n\nTypecheck is clean across all 54 projects with `@types/react` 19, and the\nclean pass was checked for coverage holes rather than trusted: no bare\n`JSX.Element`, no no-argument `useRef<T>()`, no `propTypes`/`defaultProps`/\n`findDOMNode`/`ReactDOM.render`. `forwardRef` (used by the shadcn components)\nis still fully supported.\n\nAll 55 test tasks ran fresh — `Cached: 0` for every `#test` task, since the\nlockfile change invalidates the whole cache — so the green is real and not a\ncache artifact. The Playwright suite was also run against a live stack with a\nreal Chromium: 37 passed, 3 skipped, 0 failed, including `trade-hydration`\n(island hydration, order-book row click driving the order form through the\nshared store, and the trades feed ticking live).\n\n**Bundle cost: effectively zero.** Measured against the committed\n`reports/bundle-report.json` baseline, restricted to the six pages that this\nbranch did not otherwise change, so the delta is React and nothing else:\npage-home −129 B, page-product +19 B, and −1 B on markets, portfolio,\nreferrals and vaults (gzipped first-load JS). page-trade''s +2,456 B and\norder-form''s +491 B come from this branch''s own feature work, not from React.\n\nPeer ranges are `^19.3.0` rather than a looser `^19.0.0` because\n`audit:deps`'' `duplicated-package-version` rule requires a single declared\nrange per package name across the workspace — a peer/dependency split fails\nthe build. The repo-wide constraint wins over the usual library convention,\ndeliberately.\n\nFour now-false claims that React 18 could not hoist `<meta>` out of a\ncomponent are corrected. React 19 does hoist it — confirmed by SSR probe —\nbut the page-health marker stays a hidden `div`, and the reason is restated:\nit is a gateway signal, not document metadata, and `<head>` is the document''s\npublic metadata surface. The workaround became a deliberate choice rather\nthan a limitation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42024476505a6901be18b302b88e3911f278183d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/42024476505a6901be18b302b88e3911f278183d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGYyNjI0ZjNlMGNkMGJhYjQ1OTQ1YTgyZjFiN2IwNDRjMWE3ZjUxM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5","sha":"953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5"}],"sha":"f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/f2624f3e0cd0bab45945a82f1b7b044c1a7f513f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:05:21Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:05:21Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(runtime): fragments declare their own realtime subscriptions\n\nBefore this, `apps/page-trade/src/realtime.ts` was the realtime layer: 542\nlines in which the PAGE knew which fragments were live, which source id each\none needed, and how to patch each one''s DOM. A fragment therefore could not\nbecome live — or change what it listens to — without a page edit, which\ncontradicts the claim that a fragment is the unit of deployment.\n\nThe declaration moves to where the fact lives. A fragment declares source-id\n**templates** in its own manifest, reusing the `<param>` vocabulary that was\nalready in the tree and had never been consumed by anything:\n\n    dataDependencies: [\"book.l2.<symbol>\"],   // what SSR reads once\n    subscriptions:    [\"book.l2.<symbol>\"],   // what the browser holds open\n\nThese are deliberately separate rather than one field: `order-form` reads\n`account` at render time and subscribes to nothing, so driving subscriptions\noff `dataDependencies` would have opened a stream it never had.\n`GET /manifest` publishes `subscriptions`, so a new fragment version can\nchange what it listens to and ship on its own.\n\nThe browser half ships from the fragment too, behind a `./live` export: a\n`LivePanel` with `mount(ctx) -> { onFrame, stop? }`. `@mvp/runtime/live`\nprovides the generic driver — discovery, template resolution, subscribe,\nre-subscribe, teardown, fallback skipping, per-panel error isolation.\n\nThe page keeps only what it alone knows: the panel list, the parameter\nvalues, and a `subscribe` adapter onto its data client. The driver never\nsees the client, only resolved source ids. `realtime.ts` goes 542 → 124\nlines, half of it comment, with no fragment-specific code left in it.\n\nThe nicest consequence is that a hand-written rule became a derivation.\n`ctx.remounted` is true only when a parameter THAT PANEL binds changed, so\n\"the order book and the tape rebuild on a symbol switch but open positions\nkeep their rows\" now follows from the declarations instead of from a\n`rebuild: true` argument threaded through the page. Behaviour is unchanged —\nall 43 page-trade tests pass untouched, including the symbol-switch and\nteardown cases.\n\nTwo checks keep the seam honest. 16 driver tests in `packages/runtime` use\nfake panels and a fake bus, so the driver is tested without the trade domain\nat all. `apps/page-trade/src/liveContract.test.ts` fails the build if a panel\ndeclares a template that does not resolve to a known source id, or binds a\nparameter the page cannot supply — either of which would otherwise mount a\npanel that silently never receives a frame.\n\nRemaining coupling, stated plainly: the page still statically imports each\npanel and lists it, because there is no runtime module loading here. Adding a\nNEW live fragment is two lines in the page. Changing what an existing one\nsubscribes to is zero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51120727b193440127805bfed7cffbf6785600dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/51120727b193440127805bfed7cffbf6785600dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDk1MzgyNWYxYTgzODYyNWFmNDY1NjczNmJiNThhZDQxNDYyNDFlZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9","sha":"77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9"}],"sha":"953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/953825f1a838625af4656736bb58ad4146241ed5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:02:43Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:02:43Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"feat(trade): enforce instrument constraints before an order reaches the engine\n\nThe order form could submit an order that violated the instrument''s own\nlimits — off-grid price, off-grid size, below minimum, over the leverage\nladder''s tier cap — and find out from the exchange''s rejection. This puts\nthe check in front of the mutation.\n\n`domains/trade-contracts/src/orderConstraints.ts` is a pure validator with\n14 violation codes. Two deliberate properties:\n\n- It collects **all** violations in one pass rather than throwing on the\n  first, because a trader fixing one field at a time is a worse experience\n  than seeing every problem at once.\n- It reports `unchecked` rules explicitly. A market order with no reference\n  price cannot have its notional — and therefore its leverage tier — checked.\n  The validator does not pretend it passed; the caller decides whether to\n  reject or proceed, but is never misled into thinking every rule ran.\n\n`submitOrder` now calls `assertOrderAgainstSymbol` BEFORE\n`placeOrder.execute`, and `tests/placeOrderGuard.test.ts` asserts\n`mutate` was never called — the guard is proven to sit in front of the\nmatching engine, not beside it.\n\nThe instrument limits (tick size, lot size, decimals, max leverage, minimum\nsize, the leverage ladder, mark price) are loaded during SSR and carried\ninto the island snapshot, so the browser enforces the same numbers the\nserver rendered.\n\nOne real bug found and fixed while writing this: `isMultipleOf` scaled to\nthe instrument''s DECLARED precision, which rounded the non-conformance away.\nA size of `0.0015` at 3 declared decimals became `round(1.5) = 2`, which\ndivides cleanly by a lot size of 1 — so an off-grid size was reported as\nvalid. Now it scales to `max(declared, countDecimals(step), countDecimals(value))`,\nwith a regression test. Float modulo cannot answer \"is this divisible\".\n\nAdding three required fields to `OrderFormIslandPropsSchema` makes older SSR\nsnapshots fail the M3 props handshake, so those islands stop hydrating. That\nis the designed behaviour and the reason the handshake exists: an order form\nmust never mount without the limits it is supposed to enforce. The trade\npage''s hydration fixture is updated accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5cb9ae3d6e151e3750ddc2c6adbfae382554817","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/a5cb9ae3d6e151e3750ddc2c6adbfae382554817"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDc3ODkwYjI0NDNlMDUxMjM0MGVjNjY4M2FiNjZmNGVlMGU2ZTNiYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb","sha":"a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb"}],"sha":"77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/77890b2443e0512340ec6683ab66f4ee0e6e3ba9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:00:12Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T05:00:12Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"perf(build): Turborepo task caching for build and test\n\n`pnpm verify` went from ~165s to ~31.6s warm (build 100.3s → 0.2s,\ntest 24.5s → 0.2s). Turborepo also restores deleted `dist/`/`.next/` from\ncache instead of rebuilding them.\n\nCache correctness was verified in three dimensions rather than assumed:\na source change propagates to dependents, a `globalDependencies` change\ninvalidates all 55 packages, and a cross-package input change invalidates\nexactly the task that reads it (editing a page manifest makes\n`@mvp/mcp#test` MISS while `@mvp/request-context#test` stays HIT).\n\nTwo rules the config encodes, both correctness rather than style:\n\n- Anything a task reads from OUTSIDE its own package must be declared or the\n  cache serves a stale pass. `packages/mcp/turbo.json` is the worked example:\n  its tests shell out to `scripts/*.mts` which read `registry/*.json` and the\n  page manifests, so those are `$TURBO_ROOT$` inputs.\n- Env vars that change what a task does go in `globalEnv`; values that only\n  address an external environment (`*_URL`, secrets) go in\n  `globalPassThroughEnv` so they never enter a cache key. Biome''s\n  `noUndeclaredEnvVars` starts enforcing this once `turbo.json` exists, which\n  is how four undeclared vars surfaced.\n\n`scripts/ensure-workspace-build.mts` now ALWAYS delegates to turbo rather\nthan short-circuiting when a `dist/` merely exists — a present-but-stale\n`dist/` is exactly the failure that check exists to prevent, and the\nshort-circuit defeated the cache it was supposed to cooperate with. The\npreamble is still needed with turbo because `^build` covers only DECLARED\ndeps, and `@mvp/mcp` declares none while its tests need the workspace built.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36f69961e8994f6017c355bdfef6cc7dc6f89643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/36f69961e8994f6017c355bdfef6cc7dc6f89643"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKGE2NTRlMmFiYzEyMDhmMzg5MmQ1YTNhNzE2M2M5OWFkOTk5NTcyY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/ad80a61b28b39a3f31686d64125ce3e34a2f6fa0","sha":"ad80a61b28b39a3f31686d64125ce3e34a2f6fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/ad80a61b28b39a3f31686d64125ce3e34a2f6fa0"}],"sha":"a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/a654e2abc1208f3892d5a3a7163c99ad999572cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/ad80a61b28b39a3f31686d64125ce3e34a2f6fa0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:57:42Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:57:42Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"refactor(framework): one fragment host, backend proxy, honest page health\n\nThe largest structural change on this branch. Five things that were each\na hole in the \"a fragment is the minimum deployable unit\" claim.\n\n**@mvp/fragment-host** — all 14 fragment services now run on one HTTP host\nthat owns `GET /` · `/health` · `/ready` · `/metrics` · `/manifest` ·\n`/assets` · `/budget` · `POST /render`, plus metrics and trace export.\nReplaces 1,902 lines of per-service `server.ts` and 816 lines of duplicated\n`observability.ts` with 655 + 285. `/health` and `/ready` now report the\ndeployed manifest **version**, which is what makes \"deploy, verify which\nbuild answered, then promote\" a procedure rather than an act of faith.\n`audit:deps` gains `fragment-server-not-hosted` so a hand-rolled server\nfails the build.\n\n**Fragment backend proxy** — a fragment declares\n`proxy: { <target>: <url | /path> }` and the gateway mounts it at\n`/_fragment/<fragment>/<target>/*`. Closes a structural gap: a fragment\ncould reach its backend during SSR but its hydrated island had no channel\nat all. Modelled on `@podium/proxy`; the root-relative form is a deliberate\ndeparture, because a fragment''s own endpoint lives at a different host per\nenvironment. Pure resolution in `packages/runtime/src/fragmentProxy.ts` —\nthe declared base is the boundary, and a remainder that would escape it is\nrejected. Bodies are forwarded as-is rather than re-serialized as JSON.\n\n**Page health → HTTP status** — a composed page stamps `ok`/`degraded`/\n`unhealthy` into the markup and the gateway maps a failed **required** slot\nto `503` + `retry-after` while returning the body unchanged. This is\nTailor''s `primary` semantic: before it, a page whose main content was dead\nstill answered `200`, so crawlers indexed degraded markup as real content.\nThe marker is a hidden `div`, not a `<meta>` — it is a gateway signal, not\ndocument metadata.\n\n**`ctx.extensions`** — an open, validated extension slot for context\ndimensions the framework must not know about (A/B bucket, tier), propagated\nas `x-mvp-ctx-<name>`. Without it, adding a business dimension meant\nediting `@mvp/contracts`, which the layering rule forbids product code from\ntouching. The schema-validated equivalent of `@podium/context`''s\n`.register(name, parser)`.\n\n**Declarative layering + executable single-unit proof** —\n`dependency-audit.json` carries `tags` + `depConstraints` (modelled on\n`@nx/enforce-module-boundaries`), and `pnpm verify:unit --name <f>` builds\none unit''s closure, boots the artifact and asserts `/health`, `/ready` and\n`/manifest` agree on the version.\n\nAlso: SEO metadata helpers with canonical/hreflang/OG (`@mvp/runtime/seo`),\n`robots.txt` + `sitemap.xml` on the gateway, bounded fragment cache with\ntag invalidation, web-vitals checks in the runtime gate that skip rather\nthan silently pass, `docs/reports/` long-form reports served by\n`pnpm reports`, and `AGENTS.md` as a symlink to `CLAUDE.md` so the two\ncannot drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e964e432fd59941c6728d8f638c1bddd584b1dbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/e964e432fd59941c6728d8f638c1bddd584b1dbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/ad80a61b28b39a3f31686d64125ce3e34a2f6fa0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.c