hub.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/40adc082fef1ec9ee5a8e63eb00e32ae8d302602/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T08:44:36Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T08:44:36Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"fix(delivery): freshness gates for docs/DEMOS.md and the manifest-gen discovery hole\n\nTwo related declarative-surface freshness gaps from the 2026-07-11\nre-audit — the repo''s recorded meta-lesson is that hand-maintained\nsurfaces rot within one merge cycle; only generated-or-executed\nsurfaces stay true.\n\n- scripts/verify-manifest-gen.mts discovered pages by the PRESENCE of\n  fragmentSlots.gen.ts, so a deleted gen file (or a page whose slots\n  were never generated) silently dropped out of the drift gate.\n  Discovery is now every apps/<page> with a manifest.slots.json (same\n  rule load-graph.ts uses): a non-empty slots array without a fresh\n  gen file is ''stale'' (exit 1); an empty slots array (page-vaults,\n  page-referrals — slotless by design, PR #34) is ''exempt'' and\n  reported as such, not silently skipped. A gen file that DOES exist\n  alongside an empty manifest (a page whose last slot was unmounted)\n  is still checked, not exempted.\n- New scripts/verify-demos.mts (--check | --write) generates the\n  demonstrates capability table in docs/DEMOS.md from every page\n  manifest, inside clearly-delimited <!-- BEGIN/END GENERATED -->\n  markers; --check fails loudly on drift instead of the table quietly\n  going stale (as it already did once, same-day, before PR #15).\n  Wired into pnpm verify as verify:demos (14th gate).\n- Every doc naming ''13 gates'' updated to 14: CLAUDE.md, README.md,\n  docs/DELIVERY.md, docs/OPERATIONS.md (two spots), docs/RELEASE_MODEL.md,\n  llms.txt. docs/GAP_ANALYSIS.md''s historical point-in-time ''13'' left\n  untouched (describes a past merge state, not a live invariant).\n\npnpm verify: REAL_EXIT=0, 14/14.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0277d83bd23126fbd7b13868fe03586a4e99577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/e0277d83bd23126fbd7b13868fe03586a4e99577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/40adc082fef1ec9ee5a8e63eb00e32ae8d302602","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/40adc082fef1ec9ee5a8e63eb00e32ae8d302602","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDQwYWRjMDgyZmVmMWVjOWVlNWE4ZTYzZWIwMGUzMmFlOGQzMDI2MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/3c2409a608c6855460e405f045e67a4e53b57df1","sha":"3c2409a608c6855460e405f045e67a4e53b57df1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/3c2409a608c6855460e405f045e67a4e53b57df1"}],"sha":"40adc082fef1ec9ee5a8e63eb00e32ae8d302602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/40adc082fef1ec9ee5a8e63eb00e32ae8d302602"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/0987a922954b4e6999bceaf64e10779a2d59d8f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T08:38:40Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T08:38:40Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"refactor(runtime): extract shared page-wrapper scaffolding, piloted on page-home\n\nSecond half of the fragmentSlots hygiene pass (audit M4): the five pages''\nsrc/fragmentSlots.ts wrappers repeat identical per-request scaffolding\naround their generated slot arrays. Extract only the genuinely identical\npieces into @mvp/runtime — applySlotRequestOverrides (the {...slot,\ntimeoutMs, props} merge every non-static slot needs),\ncollectSlotDiagnostics/toSlotDiagnostic (map slot results to their\ndiagnostic slice, generic over the page''s own diagnostic shape),\nPageFragmentStream/resolveFragmentStream (the barrier that awaits every\nslot promise into the resolved-HTML map, built ON the stream so barrier\nand streaming stay behaviorally identical by construction).\n\nPiloted on page-home only — the same pilot-then-rollout pattern this repo\nalready used for A1 (PR #18 piloted on page-home, PRs #20-22 rolled out to\nproduct/markets/portfolio). page-home''s fragmentSlots.ts now visibly reads\nas \"generated slots + page-specific glue (data resolvers, featured-content\naggregation) + shared helper calls\" instead of re-deriving the same\nscaffolding. Rendered output, diagnostics shape, and every existing test\nare unchanged (verified: 82/82 runtime+page-home tests green). Rollout to\nproduct/markets/portfolio (page-trade stays on the barrier API by design,\nper its own documented executeFragmentSlots constraint) is a natural,\nlow-risk follow-up now that the pattern is proven — not done here, same\nscoping discipline as the A1 precedent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"563062e9029b55e5b5cb67266311a8d1a47d511a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/563062e9029b55e5b5cb67266311a8d1a47d511a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/commits/0987a922954b4e6999bceaf64e10779a2d59d8f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/0987a922954b4e6999bceaf64e10779a2d59d8f7","node_id":"C_kwDOTPTVXtoAKDA5ODdhOTIyOTU0YjRlNjk5OWJjZWFmNjRlMTA3NzlhMmQ1OWQ4Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commit/53ef167473b8ad109abc383c092bdf7815701da4","sha":"53ef167473b8ad109abc383c092bdf7815701da4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/53ef167473b8ad109abc383c092bdf7815701da4"}],"sha":"0987a922954b4e6999bceaf64e10779a2d59d8f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/0987a922954b4e6999bceaf64e10779a2d59d8f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20755029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zyoncode","id":20755029,"login":"zyoncode","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzU1MDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zyoncode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/commits/53ef167473b8ad109abc383c092bdf7815701da4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T01:23:47Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T01:23:47Z","email":"joewong7321@gmail.com","name":"Joe Wong"},"message":"refactor(pages): unify fragmentSlots vocabulary — html: for resolved HTML, slotPromises: for pending promises\n\nThe five pages'' fragmentSlots.ts wrappers had drifted into one-concept-two-\nnames and one-name-two-concepts: the resolved-HTML map was `html:` on\npage-home/product/markets but `slots:` on page-portfolio/page-trade, while\nhome/product/markets used `slots:` for a different thing entirely (the\nper-slot pending-promise map on the stream handle).\n\nOne vocabulary everywhere now:\n- `html:` — the per-slot resolved-HTML map on every *FragmentHtml barrier\n  result (page-portfolio and page-trade renamed from `slots:`).\n- `slotPromises:` — the per-slot pending-promise map on every\n  *FragmentStream handle (page-home/product/markets/portfolio renamed from\n  `slots:`), so the overloaded `slots:` field name disappears from the\n  page wrappers entirely.\n\nMechanical consumer updates only: each page''s page.tsx lookups and the test\nassertions that named the renamed fields. No behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac30862cff0c84c109016faabd5676a444e495c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/git/trees/ac30862cff0c84c109016faabd5676a444e495c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zyonlab/ai-first-web-frame/g